_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e6d551e2c48d805bb12077491b4eb9ece69d524c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:30:49Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:30:49Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Document local OAuth portless DNS\n\nLocal OAuth needs a provider-valid domain because common providers reject .localhost subdomains. Add a recipe for using an owned public DNS wildcard with portless custom TLDs, including Cloudflare DNS-only records and project-scoped host patterns.\n\nConstraint: Local DNS overrides are intentionally excluded from this path; provider validation and team onboarding should use public DNS records under a domain the team owns\nRejected: Keep only the default .localhost guidance | Google and Apple OAuth redirects commonly reject that shape\nRejected: Use one wildcard for every project host | DNS wildcards only match one label, so project-scoped hosts need records such as *.billing.local.example.com\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Use owned public DNS wildcards for OAuth local-dev domains; keep .localhost for normal non-OAuth dev\nTested: pnpm exec prettier --check README.md docs/recipes/README.md docs/recipes/local-oauth-with-portless.md; git diff --check\nNot-tested: Runtime OAuth provider flow","tree":{"sha":"df34ed20d48616768070b9ee18be6d99f3812d75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/df34ed20d48616768070b9ee18be6d99f3812d75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/e6d551e2c48d805bb12077491b4eb9ece69d524c","verifica