st_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/ddca0d1e39e68632883e00e84e622fb7235c9658/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:06:52Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T05:06:52Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Add global portless setup\n\nGlobal portless is the upstream-recommended day-to-day install, but the template only had repo-local scripts and manual docs. Add an explicit setup helper plus bootstrap opt-in flags so forks can choose global install, CA trust, and proxy startup without hiding system prompts in the default bootstrap path.\n\nConstraint: Global npm install and CA trust must be explicit because they can prompt for system credentials\nRejected: Pin global portless to the workspace catalog | global tooling should follow latest while the repo-local devDependency remains the reproducible fallback\nRejected: Run global portless setup during bootstrap by default | would make bootstrap unexpectedly prompt for npm/global trust credentials\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep pnpm dev:portless:setup installing portless@latest; keep repo scripts usable via local devDependency\nTested: pnpm dev:portless:setup -- --skip-install --skip-trust; pnpm test:scripts; pnpm check; pnpm syncpack:check; pnpm audit --json; git diff --check\nNot-tested: Full pnpm build after this docs/scripts-only change","tree":{"sha":"84ae5c14848454568a47a6614e0ba5e94996c1b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/84ae5c14848454568a47a6614e0ba5e94996c1b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/ddca0d1e39e68632883e00e84e622fb7235c9658","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/ddca0d1e39e68632883e00e84e622fb7235c9658","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGRkY2EwZDFlMzllNjg2MzI4ODNlMDBlODRlNjIyZmI3MjM1Yzk2NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8","sha":"3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8"}],"sha":"ddca0d1e39e68632883e00e84e622fb7235c9658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/ddca0d1e39e68632883e00e84e622fb7235c9658"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:49:06Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:49:06Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Document portless proxy setup\n\nThe portless integration worked after CA trust, but non-interactive terminals cannot answer the sudo prompt needed for a privileged 443 proxy. Add explicit scripts and onboarding docs for CA trust, privileged proxy startup, unprivileged :1355 fallback, and proxy shutdown so downstream forks have a copy-safe path.\n\nConstraint: Local dev setup should explain both clean HTTPS URLs and non-interactive fallback behavior\n\nRejected: Leave portless startup as implicit first-run behavior | non-TTY agents and CI-like shells cannot answer sudo prompts\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: narrow\n\nDirective: Use pnpm dev:trust once, pnpm dev:proxy for privileged 443, or pnpm dev:proxy:unprivileged when sudo prompts are unavailable\n\nTested: pnpm dev:proxy; pnpm dev:api; pnpm dev:proxy:stop; pnpm format; pnpm check; pnpm test:scripts; pnpm syncpack:check; pnpm audit --json; git diff --check\n\nNot-tested: Privileged 443 proxy success path because this non-TTY session cannot provide sudo credentials","tree":{"sha":"8973a3a90fafc53eeaf178e3648caa00cba89796","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/8973a3a90fafc53eeaf178e3648caa00cba89796"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDM2MjFlMDUwMDRmYjQyYjY2MTU2ODczZTJmNjZhNzMzMjdhYTk3ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935","sha":"e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935"}],"sha":"3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/3621e05004fb42b66156873e2f66a73327aa97e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:42:55Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:42:55Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Resolve template audit findings\n\nAudit still reported low and moderate transitive advisories after the portless integration. Pin patched transitive versions through pnpm overrides, keep filtered portless app starts copy-safe with package-level portless metadata, and block Metro from scanning sibling app build output during monorepo builds.\n\nConstraint: Template security gates should report zero audit advisories without weakening runtime package boundaries\n\nRejected: Ignore low and moderate advisories | leaves a known noisy baseline for downstream forks\n\nRejected: Rely only on root portless.json | pnpm --filter runs from package context and can recurse into the dev script without package-level metadata\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: medium\n\nDirective: Keep transitive security overrides explicit and revisit them when upstream packages ship patched dependency ranges\n\nTested: pnpm install; pnpm check; pnpm test; pnpm build; pnpm audit --json; git diff --check; pnpm exec portless trust; pnpm exec portless proxy start --port 1355 --https; pnpm --filter @repo/api dev\n\nNot-tested: Privileged portless proxy on port 443 because this non-TTY session cannot answer sudo prompts","tree":{"sha":"8f6bb14fc780248389bd7d705bd5eb0d0df20438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/8f6bb14fc780248389bd7d705bd5eb0d0df20438"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGU5ZTRhM2ZjZjA5MmQ1ODUxZTJlNmNmYTI2MWVlNDdhMDA0NzU5MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934","sha":"6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934"}],"sha":"e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e9e4a3fcf092d5851e2e6cfa261ee47a00475935"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:37:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T04:37:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Add portless dev URLs\n\nLocal dev still assumed fixed localhost ports in scripts, env defaults, and docs, which makes multi-surface template work prone to port conflicts and inconsistent URLs. Adopt portless for browser-facing HTTP surfaces while keeping raw dev:app fallbacks for automation, Playwright, and Tauri native boot.\n\nConstraint: Template dev URLs should be stable for humans and agents without hard-coding framework ports as the primary contract\n\nRejected: Run Expo mobile through portless by default | native QR and LAN workflows remain Expo-managed and should not be forced through the browser proxy\n\nRejected: Point Playwright webServer at portless | non-interactive runs can fail on first-use trust prompts, so E2E keeps the raw localhost fallback\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: medium\n\nDirective: Keep HTTP app dev scripts as portless, keep real framework commands in dev:app, and centralize names in portless.json\n\nTested: pnpm install; pnpm format; pnpm syncpack:check; pnpm check; pnpm test; pnpm build; pnpm licenses:check; pnpm audit --audit-level high; git diff --check\n\nNot-tested: Interactive first-run portless trust flow and live browser navigation because it may require local CA/sudo approval outside the repo gate","tree":{"sha":"b54a19468e787d1163c5b11cb512bab8fe9bb568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/b54a19468e787d1163c5b11cb512bab8fe9bb568"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDYzNzMyMzRmOWM0YTVmYTMxYmE2NWQ2YWYyYWIzOWFlYjlmZWY5MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a","sha":"f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a"}],"sha":"6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/6373234f9c4a5fa31ba65d6af2ab39aeb9fef934"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T07:02:44Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T07:02:44Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Preserve template activation contracts\n\nReview found that several activation recipes were easy to copy into invalid forks: pg-boss workers reached into a private field, provider examples bypassed the typed env adapter, and the in-memory queue surfaced missing-job errors as Effect defects instead of typed failures. Tighten the runtime contract and document the rules in AGENTS.md so future recipe work stays aligned with the template boundaries.\n\nConstraint: Template forks should be able to copy activation recipes without bypassing env validation or silently no-oping runtime methods\nRejected: Expose pg-boss internals directly | keeps examples coupled to one backend''s private client shape\nRejected: Leave missing-job queue errors as thrown defects | breaks Effect error-channel composition for library consumers\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep activation recipes copy-safe and route provider configuration through @repo/env or API_ENV, not broad process.env reads\nTested: pnpm check; pnpm test; pnpm build; pnpm --filter @repo/infrastructure test -- queue.test.ts; pnpm design:lint\nNot-tested: Real pg-boss, Resend, S3/R2, and CSP runtime integrations because recipes remain opt-in examples","tree":{"sha":"37386b9a1286e4e9ba3326a42cf5b6f7515c17f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/37386b9a1286e4e9ba3326a42cf5b6f7515c17f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGY2NjJlMjdiYmMwNzQwZmNiZmM1YmY1ZTdhNWFhYThhMDljY2Y1NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e","sha":"137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e"}],"sha":"f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/f662e27bbc0740fcbfc5bf5e7a5aaa8a09ccf54a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:42:31Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:42:31Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Wire 4 remaining contract modules + their activation recipes (close out A-group adoption)\n\nCloses the recipe set: every Group A contract now has a wired\nDI module + an activation guide that covers swap-the-provider →\nimplementation sketch → test against the memory adapter → verify.\nMirrors the PolicyModule + AuditModule pattern from commit d44fe39.\n\nOutboxModule (apps/api/src/outbox/{outbox.tokens,outbox.module}.ts):\nprovides OUTBOX_RELAY = noopOutboxRelay. Recipe enable-outbox-relay\ncovers Postgres polling worker (recommended) + LISTEN/NOTIFY +\nDebezium CDC alternatives, ships the canonical SELECT FOR UPDATE\nSKIP LOCKED claim implementation, walks through Option A\n(@nestjs/schedule @Interval in-process worker) vs Option B\n(separate apps/worker/ deploy) for production. Domain-side: the\nhandler inserts into the outbox table inside its existing DB\ntransaction; the relay forwards asynchronously.\n\nQueueModule (apps/api/src/queue/{queue.tokens,queue.module}.ts):\nprovides JOB_QUEUE = noopJobQueue. Recipe enable-job-queue covers\nBullMQ+Redis / pg-boss+Postgres / Inngest / SQS / Cloud Tasks /\nTemporal alternatives, picks pg-boss as the default (reuses\nPostgres, no new infra). Handler-side enqueue with idempotencyKey\nfor \"user double-clicked signup\" recovery; worker-side can run\nin-process (Option A) or separate deploy (Option B, recommended for\nprod). The recipe is explicit that pg-boss handlers run inside\nboss.work() rather than the JobQueue port''s claimNext/ack/nack —\nthose exist for memory-mock testing and would matter for backends\nwithout a built-in subscribe pattern.\n\nNotifierModule (apps/api/src/notifier/{notifier.tokens,notifier.module}.ts):\nprovides NOTIFIER = noopNotifier. Recipe enable-notifier covers\nResend / SES / Postmark / SendGrid / Twilio / FCM alternatives,\nships a Resend implementation (the recommended default for new\nforks — cheap, great DX, handles DKIM/SPF), shows the composite-\nnotifier pattern for multi-channel dispatch, and walks through the\nqueue-mediated send (handler enqueues, worker calls notifier.send)\nthat''s the production-recommended wiring. Pairs with enable-job-\nqueue and enable-multi-tenancy.\n\nStorageModule (apps/api/src/storage/{storage.tokens,storage.module}.ts):\nprovides OBJECT_STORAGE = noopObjectStorage. Recipe enable-object-\nstorage covers S3 / R2 / GCS / Azure Blob / MinIO / Backblaze\nalternatives, ships the canonical S3 SDK v3 implementation (works\nunchanged on R2 and MinIO via S3_ENDPOINT), shows direct-upload\n(small files, server proxies) vs presigned-URL (large files,\nbrowser uploads directly to storage) handler patterns. Common\npitfalls section calls out filesystem-by-accident, public-bucket\nmistakes, missing per-tenant prefixes, and lifecycle policy.\n\nUpdated:\n- apps/api/src/app.module.ts: imports OutboxModule + QueueModule +\n  NotifierModule + StorageModule. The four new modules join\n  TenantModule + PolicyModule + AuditModule for a total of seven\n  noop-default DI surfaces; activation = swap the provider value in\n  the matching module file (one-line change per contract).\n- docs/capabilities.md apps/api row Notes column: extends the wired-\n  modules sentence to list all 7 tokens (TENANT_RESOLVER /\n  POLICY_EVALUATOR / AUDIT_SINK / OUTBOX_RELAY / JOB_QUEUE / NOTIFIER\n  / OBJECT_STORAGE) with the matching recipe names.\n- docs/recipes/README.md: 4 new recipe rows (outbox-relay, job-queue,\n  notifier, object-storage) — total recipe count now 13, every Group\n  A contract has its activation guide.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, same baseline), pnpm test (28/28\nturbo tasks, no new test surface — the new modules are pure DI\nwiring matching the PolicyModule/AuditModule pattern), pnpm build\n(18/18). Each new module adds ~30 lines (token + module). The lane\nis inert until handlers call the injected port; solo deploys pay\nzero runtime cost beyond the Nest DI graph node.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf4a5e9e639bafe5117cab564eefea0718899f05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/cf4a5e9e639bafe5117cab564eefea0718899f05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDEzN2Y4NmEwNjk4MjhhZDBmYTU2ZThiNzA1MDFjYjhkNTRkODRhNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0","sha":"d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0"}],"sha":"137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/137f86a069828ad0fa56e8b70501cb8d54d84a4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:54:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:54:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Wire PolicyModule + AuditModule + their activation recipes (integration round 2)\n\nMirrors the tenant pattern from commit 17ba006 at the DI-token layer\nonly — no middleware. Both modules expose a wired DI token with a noop\ndefault, so future handlers can `@Inject(POLICY_EVALUATOR)` /\n`@Inject(AUDIT_SINK)` today and a fork activates by swapping the\nprovider value. Recipes walk through the activation end-to-end.\n\nPolicyModule (apps/api/src/policy/{policy.tokens.ts,\npolicy.module.ts}) provides POLICY_EVALUATOR with useValue:\nallowAllPolicyEvaluator. The application-level default is allowAll\n(distinct from createMemoryPolicyEvaluator''s fail-closed deny inside\nthe rule loop) — reasoning: the lane is inert until handlers actually\ncall evaluator.evaluate(), and a denyAll default would break every\nunprotected route the moment a handler is wrapped. No middleware:\npolicy is consumer-pull (a service @Injects and calls evaluate),\nnot middleware-push like tenant. Mixing the two would force every\nroute through a policy gate even when there is no policy-relevant\ndecision to make.\n\nAuditModule (apps/api/src/audit/{audit.tokens.ts, audit.module.ts})\nprovides AUDIT_SINK with useValue: noopAuditSink. Same consumer-pull\npattern — handlers call sink.record() at forensic-relevant points\n(signin, mutation, denied policy decision, data export) rather than a\nmiddleware recording every request.\n\ndocs/recipes/enable-policy.md (8-step guide): pick an engine\n(rule-list / CASL / Cedar / OPA / custom service), write the rules\nor adapter, swap the provider, inject and call evaluate from\nhandlers, test with denyAllPolicyEvaluator or createMemoryPolicyEvaluator,\nupdate API docs with FORBIDDEN error code + auth posture, remove the\ndeferred-capabilities entry, verify with a curl. Common pitfalls\ncovered: forgetting to call evaluate (allowAll default lets\neverything through silently — flip to denyAll in dev for a sanity\ncheck), conflating roles with policy actions, calling evaluate per-row\nin a list (filter at query layer instead), skipping the audit pairing\non denials.\n\ndocs/recipes/enable-audit.md (8-step guide): pick a persistence story\n(Drizzle audit_events table / SIEM forwarding / outbox-backed async /\nWORM / composite), write the sink (full DrizzleAuditSink example with\nthe schema + Effect.tryPromise pattern), swap the provider, inject\nand call record from handlers (canonical sites: mutations, auth\nevents, denied policy decisions, sensitive reads), test with\ncreateMemoryAuditSink + entries() snapshot, update API docs, remove\nthe deferred entry, verify with a curl + psql lookup. Common pitfalls\ncovered: recording before DB commit (use post-commit or outbox-backed\nvariant), PII in details, skipping denied policy decisions, missing\nretention policy, missing tenantId once multi-tenancy is activated.\n\nBoth recipes pair with each other and with enable-multi-tenancy\n(denied decisions get tenantId-scoped audit entries; the three\ncontracts compose without further wiring).\n\nUpdated:\n- apps/api/src/app.module.ts: imports PolicyModule + AuditModule.\n- docs/capabilities.md apps/api row Notes column: notes that the\n  three modules (TenantModule + PolicyModule + AuditModule) are\n  wired with noop defaults so handlers can @Inject the tokens\n  today; activation = swap the provider value.\n- docs/recipes/README.md: enable-policy + enable-audit rows added.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, same baseline), pnpm test (28/28,\napps/api stays at 21 — no new test surface; the modules are pure\nDI wiring and the recipes show how consumers test them), pnpm build\n(18/18). The lane is inert until handlers call the injected\nevaluator/sink — solo deploys pay zero runtime cost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3bed35151e620a3cf2fc839026e5939bdf9e6627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/3bed35151e620a3cf2fc839026e5939bdf9e6627"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGQ0NGZlMzk1NzViMDYyZWI4MDU2ODlkOGVkN2YwNzE5ZTkyNGY2ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f","sha":"17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f"}],"sha":"d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d44fe39575b062eb805689d8ed7f0719e924f6f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:39:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:39:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Wire tenant resolver + middleware into apps/api (ADR 0013, integration round 1)\n\nActivates the multi-tenancy contract from ADR 0004 inside the API\napplication. The contract pieces (TenantContext schema in @repo/contracts,\nwithTenantContext ALS in @repo/platform, TenantResolver port in\n@repo/infrastructure) all shipped weeks ago — this commit lands the\nglue: a global Express middleware that consults a DI-provided resolver\nand seeds withTenantContext + withLoggerContext({ tenantId }) when a\ntenant is resolved.\n\napps/api/src/tenant/tenant.tokens.ts: TENANT_RESOLVER DI token.\napps/api/src/tenant/tenant.module.ts: provides TENANT_RESOLVER with\nuseValue: noopTenantResolver as the default. A fork swaps the provider\nvalue for a real resolver (header / subdomain / JWT claim / membership\nlookup) — see docs/recipes/enable-multi-tenancy.md.\n\napps/api/src/tenant/tenant.middleware.ts: createTenantMiddleware(resolver)\nfactory returns the Express middleware function. The factory pattern\nkeeps the middleware pure and testable — no Nest DI inside the\nmiddleware itself. On a non-null resolution the middleware wraps next()\nin withTenantContext(ctx, () =&gt; withLoggerContext({ tenantId }, () =&gt;\nnext())). On Effect.fail(AppError) the error flows through next(err)\nand the global AppErrorFilter handles it. Resolver returns null →\nmiddleware just calls next() with no scope opened.\n\napps/api/src/tenant/tenant.middleware.test.ts: vitest unit tests cover\nthe four cases — noop resolver (no scope opened), success\n(withTenantContext + LoggerContext.tenantId both seeded), failure\n(AppError forwarded to next(err)), and nested-scope (tenant scope\nunder an existing requestId scope keeps both visible).\n\napps/api/src/main.ts: pulls TENANT_RESOLVER from DI and mounts the\nmiddleware between requestIdMiddleware and requestLoggerMiddleware.\nThe mount order is load-bearing: requestId → tenant → logger ensures\nthe per-request access log line carries tenantId in details\nautomatically (AppErrorFilter''s getLoggerContext() reads it). The ADR\nexplains why this order is the only one that produces fully-labeled\naccess logs.\n\napps/api/src/app.module.ts: imports TenantModule. apps/api/package.json:\nadds effect to devDeps so middleware tests can construct test\nresolvers via Effect.succeed / Effect.fail (apps/api previously got\neffect transitively through @repo/infrastructure but couldn''t import\nit directly under pnpm''s strict node_modules layout).\n\nADR 0013 (docs/adr/0013-tenant-middleware-wiring.md) builds on 0004\nand documents: global mount (not per-controller — tenancy is\ncross-cutting, opt-out is simpler than opt-in), resolver-pluggable\nvia DI (a fork swaps useValue, no middleware change required), noop\ndefault (solo deploys pay one Effect microtask per request, no scope\nopened). Rejected alternatives: per-controller @UseGuards (silent\nforgetting bug), reading the x-tenant-id header directly in middleware\n(forecloses on subdomain / JWT / membership-lookup strategies),\ndefer-until-tenant-aware-domain-module (the resolver shape is stable\nenough that shipping wiring now lets the next ADR skip relitigating\nmount order).\n\nRecipe (docs/recipes/enable-multi-tenancy.md): seven-step activation\nguide. Step 1 picks a resolution signal (header / subdomain / JWT /\nmembership) with trade-offs. Step 2 writes the resolver. Step 3 swaps\nthe TenantModule provider — *that''s the activation*. Steps 4-7 cover\ndomain-code awareness (strict vs cross-tenant-for-service-accounts vs\npublic-endpoint posture), per-route docs, removing the deferred-\ncapabilities entry, and verification curls. Common pitfalls section\ncalls out the four failure modes the integration round surfaced\n(forgetting strict-vs-soft, OTel span attributes, cache key prefixing,\nbackground job tenant scope).\n\ndocs/api/README.md grows a \"Tenancy\" section explaining the default\nbehavior (noop) and pointing at the recipe for activation.\ndocs/capabilities.md operational lanes table grows a \"Tenancy\" row.\nADR README index updated.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, 2 design.md warnings + 1 info — same\nbaseline), pnpm test (28/28 turbo tasks; apps/api grew 17 → 21 tests\nwith the four middleware cases), pnpm build (18/18). The middleware\nruns unconditionally on every request — including /health/* and\n/metrics — but with noopTenantResolver returning Effect.succeed(null),\nthe cost is one microtask per request and no scope is opened. Forks\nthat wire a real resolver can short-circuit on /health/* paths inside\nthe resolver (a per-request branch is cheaper than a per-route mount\nconfig).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97333b3f0bef31203eb2db97115b93377f47ea7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/97333b3f0bef31203eb2db97115b93377f47ea7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDE3YmEwMDYyNzJkNWI2MGMxNGU1NjMwMjUwNjM4OTc3MjBmZTNmMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a","sha":"5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a"}],"sha":"17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/17ba006272d5b60c14e563025063897720fe3f2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:24:42Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:24:42Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"B-group polish: CSP recipe, axe-core a11y gate, gitleaks, ADR 0012 (API versioning)\n\nCloses the four small B-group items left after the OpenAPI hard\npivot (commit 9e2852c).\n\nCSP recipe (docs/recipes/enable-csp.md): the conservative\nsecurityHeaders block in apps/web/next.config.ts intentionally omits\nContent-Security-Policy because Tailwind 4 + Next.js hydration both\nneed an inline-allowance strategy and the third-party catalog of the\nfirst product UI is the constraint that picks the policy. The recipe\nwalks through nonce-based-via-middleware (recommended), shows the\nexact apps/web/middleware.ts to drop in, references the nonce in\napp/layout.tsx via headers(), and prescribes Report-Only soak before\nflipping to enforce. Common gotchas (Tailwind 4 v4 utility-class\ninjection, Fast Refresh inline scripts, CSP report endpoints, older\nbrowsers) called out. No code change — pure docs. Index entry in\ndocs/recipes/README.md.\n\na11y gate: @axe-core/playwright added to apps/web devDeps + the\nworkspace catalog (4.10.2). New apps/web/e2e/a11y.spec.ts runs\nAxeBuilder over the home page scoped to WCAG 2.1 A + AA tags\n(wcag2a / wcag2aa / wcag21a / wcag21aa). AAA excluded — typically\ntoo strict as a default; forks with formal compliance posture re-add.\nRuns as part of `pnpm --filter @repo/web test:e2e`; no separate\nscript (a11y issues should fail the gate alongside functional ones).\ndocs/capabilities.md operational lanes table grew an \"a11y gate\" row.\n\ngitleaks workflow: extends .github/workflows/security.yml with a\ngitleaks job using gitleaks/gitleaks-action@v2 alongside the existing\nTrivy + CodeQL jobs. Checkout uses fetch-depth: 0 so the action can\nscan past commits, not just the current snapshot. Uploads SARIF to\nGitHub Security tab. Findings fail the workflow (gitleaks-action\nexits non-zero) so a leaked secret blocks merge. capabilities.md CI\nsecurity row updated to mention gitleaks.\n\nADR 0012 (docs/adr/0012-api-versioning.md): no /v1/ prefix today.\nIntroduce versioning only when the first breaking change requires\nit; when introduced, use URL versioning with a 90-day deprecation\noverlap (new path serves new shape, old path serves old shape, then\nremoved). Header versioning rejected (invisible to URL-aware tools),\nquery-param versioning rejected (breaks URL caching), date-based AWS-\nstyle versioning rejected for small teams. Mixed-cohort post-break\nstate (some resources at /, some at /v1) is acceptable — the prefix\ncommunicates \"this resource has been versioned at least once\". The\nADR is explicit that additive changes (new optional fields, new\nendpoints) don''t require versioning — bump only on actual breaking\nchanges. ADR README index updated.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, 2 design.md warnings + 1 info — same\nbaseline), pnpm test (28/28 turbo tasks), pnpm build (18/18). pnpm\ninstall added @axe-core/playwright as a devDep (no runtime impact).\nThe new a11y.spec.ts is included in the Playwright run when test:e2e\nis invoked locally; CI gates can opt in by running test:e2e in a\nseparate job (default CI doesn''t run e2e per docs/capabilities.md\ntesting baseline).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f3bcaaff7bc414823c3aad1d38db887dcea5047","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/0f3bcaaff7bc414823c3aad1d38db887dcea5047"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDVkZGViZTA2ZGJmNjM3MDc3NDcxYjNiMjE3Y2QzZDY0MjE1ODIzNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705","sha":"9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705"}],"sha":"5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5ddebe06dbf637077471b3b217cd3d642158234a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:19:55Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:19:55Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Replace OpenAPI surface with hand-authored Markdown docs (ADR 0011)\n\nHard pivot away from the runtime OpenAPI document and Scalar UI\nestablished by ADR 0003. The API surface is now documented in\ndocs/api/<resource>.md, hand-authored, reviewed in PRs alongside the\ncontroller it describes. ADR 0003 is marked Superseded by 0011 and\nkept for historical context. Net diff: -503 / +44 in code, plus the\nnew MD docs lane.\n\nRemoved:\n- apps/api/src/openapi/ (module, controller, generator, drift-guard\n  test). The Zod → JSON Schema generator is gone; the contracts\n  package''s tests still cover the schemas themselves.\n- @scalar/express-api-reference dep + its workspace catalog entry\n  (pnpm install dropped 5 packages from the lockfile).\n- The /docs Scalar UI mount in apps/api/src/main.ts.\n- EXPOSE_DOCS env key from packages/env/src/apps/api.ts (and from the\n  listening log payload in main.ts).\n- docs/recipes/generate-client-sdk.md (premise — read from\n  /openapi.json — no longer holds).\n\nAdded:\n- docs/api/README.md — index + format convention. Each resource file\n  is one paragraph + routes table + per-route errors + auth posture +\n  curl block, linked back to the @repo/contracts source as the\n  runtime source of truth.\n- docs/api/notes.md — reference for the canonical domain module.\n- docs/api/auth.md — Better Auth /api/auth/* surface (linked to\n  Better Auth''s docs rather than enumerated) plus the /me protected\n  reference route.\n- docs/api/health-and-metrics.md — /health/live, /health/ready,\n  /health, /metrics. Documents the Prometheus cardinality posture\n  (route templates, not URLs; <unmatched> bucket bounds attacker-\n  driven cardinality).\n- docs/recipes/document-an-api-route.md — the convention enforcement\n  recipe: change apps/api → update docs/api/<resource>.md in the same\n  PR. No automated drift gate; review is the mechanism.\n- docs/adr/0011-api-docs-in-markdown.md — the decision record. ADR\n  0003 marked Superseded by 0011 with a top-of-file note pointing\n  here. ADR README index updated.\n\nUpdated:\n- docs/recipes/add-api-domain-module.md (Step 6 swapped from\n  /openapi.json registration to docs/api/<resource>.md authoring),\n  docs/recipes/protect-an-api-route.md (Step 4 swapped same way),\n  docs/recipes/production-checklist.md (EXPOSE_DOCS row + the\n  /openapi.json smoke step removed), docs/recipes/README.md (drop\n  generate-client-sdk row, add document-an-api-route row).\n- docs/capabilities.md apps/api row Notes column rewritten — drops\n  /openapi.json + /docs (Scalar) + EXPOSE_DOCS=false references,\n  points at docs/api/ + ADR 0011. The Deferred section''s stale\n  @nestjs/swagger entry is replaced with a single OpenAPI/Swagger/\n  Scalar entry pointing at ADR 0011 and the zod-openapi escape\n  hatch for forks that need codegen.\n\nADR 0011''s \"Costs\" section is explicit about the trade-offs:\nreview-only drift enforcement (no lint gate), no browsable Scalar UI\nin dev (curl + the MD docs replace it), and forks targeting public\nconsumer-facing APIs should re-introduce zod-openapi at build time.\nThe decision is biased toward the early-stage end of the\nsolo→enterprise spectrum that this template targets.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, 2 design.md warnings + 1 info — same\nbaseline), pnpm test (28/28 turbo tasks; apps/api dropped from 21 to\n17 tests reflecting the 4 removed openapi.test.ts cases), pnpm build\n(18/18). pnpm install -5 packages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a555f3a58e752b56202c5148910e5598e0080ccc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/a555f3a58e752b56202c5148910e5598e0080ccc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDllMjg1MmNkNTEwMWM1OTMxZjM1M2I0MTYwM2JlNzdkNDhiMzA3MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932","sha":"2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932"}],"sha":"9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/9e2852cd5101c5931f353b41603be77d48b30705"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:59:47Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:59:47Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Enterprise contracts: object storage, audit sink (close out group A)\n\nCloses the seven-contract enterprise lane this template promises:\nmulti-tenancy (ADR 0004), outbox (0005), policy (0006), job queue\n(0007), notifier (0008), and now object storage + audit sink. Same\nADR-0001 pattern: pure Zod contracts in @repo/contracts, Effect-typed\nports + memory/noop adapters in @repo/infrastructure, ADRs explaining\nwhat''s shipped vs. fork choice, capabilities-doc deferred entries,\nADR README index.\n\nObject storage (ADR 0009): @repo/contracts/storage ships\nStorageObjectKey (slash-delimited path with a regex + traversal refine\nthat blocks `..` segments and `//` empty segments at the type-system\nboundary — the canonical upload-handler bug class fails before reaching\nthe storage layer), StorageObjectMetadata (key, contentType, sizeBytes,\noptional etag, lastModified, optional tenantId), SignedUrlRequest (key,\noperation: get/put, expiresInSeconds capped at 7 days, optional\ncontentType + contentLength for PUT pre-signing), SignedUrl (url,\nexpiresAt, optional headers). @repo/infrastructure/storage ships\nObjectStorage (put, get → bytes + metadata, head, delete, signUrl —\nEffect-typed) plus noopObjectStorage (UNAVAILABLE/NOT_FOUND failures\non reads, silent delete) and createMemoryObjectStorage (in-process Map,\nmonotonically incrementing mem-N etag, signUrl returns mem:// URL so\ntests can assert \"a signed URL was issued\" without a real signer).\n\nBody is Uint8Array (universal — Node Buffer extends, browsers native).\nThe ADR is explicit that real adapters extend with their own stream\nmethods for multi-GB uploads (S3 multipart, GCS resumable, Azure block\nblob have meaningfully different ergonomics) — the contract covers the\nsmall-file 90% pattern.\n\nAudit sink (ADR 0010): @repo/contracts/audit ships AuditOutcome\n(success/failure/denied — denied is first-class, not a sub-case of\nfailure, since \"denied\" is the most-queried filter for compliance\nreview), AuditActor (optional userId + optional serviceName + roles +\noptional tenantId — service-initiated actions like a scheduled-job\ntick set serviceName), AuditEntry (server-assigned id+occurredAt plus\nactor/action/resource/outcome/requestId/correlationId/details), and\nNewAuditEntry (omits the server-assigned fields).\n@repo/infrastructure/audit ships AuditSink (one method:\nrecord(entry) → Effect<AuditEntry, AppError>) plus noopAuditSink\n(stamps id:\"noop\" but stores nothing) and createMemoryAuditSink\n(appends to internal list, exposes entries() snapshot + clear() for\ntests).\n\nThe ADR is explicit that audit is distinct from system_events\n(operational telemetry — different retention, different access\ncontrol) and from outbox (audit can *ride* the outbox for durable async\nforwarding to a SIEM, but the audit entry shape is the source of truth\n— the outbox row is the transport). Composes naturally with the policy\nport: every denied policy decision is an audit candidate, and the\n\"denied\" outcome is the contract''s first-class shape for it.\n\nBoth lanes carry tenantId optionally so multi-tenancy activation\n(ADR 0004) does not require contract follow-up. Capabilities-doc\npackage rows for @repo/contracts and @repo/infrastructure pick up the\nnew responsibilities; deferred-capabilities entries point at the new\nADRs (real object storage provider: AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / Google\nCloud Storage / Azure Blob / MinIO / Backblaze B2; real audit\npersistence: DB-backed audit_events table / SIEM forwarding to\nSplunk / Datadog / CloudWatch / immutable WORM via S3 Object Lock or\nGCS Bucket Lock). ADR README index updated for 0009 + 0010.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, 2 design.md warnings + 1 info — same\nbaseline), pnpm test (28/28 turbo tasks: contracts grew 30 → 45 tests,\ninfrastructure 28 → 40), pnpm build (18/18). PutOptions.tenantId now\nreferences the branded TenantId type from @repo/contracts so passing a\nraw string into storage.put fails typecheck — caught one fixup of the\ninfrastructure test fixture during the build cycle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d4bca390c9a4849af7c9e8bd377b73ddc113180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/6d4bca390c9a4849af7c9e8bd377b73ddc113180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDJkMWY0Nzk2NzZmNWQyOTQxMzU5M2U2MGExZTM2YTVlNWJiMmM5MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d","sha":"e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d"}],"sha":"2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/2d1f479676f5d29413593e60a1e36a5e5bb2c932"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:48:10Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:48:10Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Enterprise contracts: job queue, notifier (memory adapters + ADRs)\n\nTwo more opt-in lanes following the same ADR-0001 pattern as the\ntenant/outbox/policy round (dcdd7ca): pure Zod contracts in\n@repo/contracts, Effect-typed ports + memory/noop adapters in\n@repo/infrastructure, ADRs explaining what is shipped vs. what stays a\nfork choice, capabilities-doc deferred entries, and ADR README index.\n\nJob queue (ADR 0007): @repo/contracts/job ships JobDescriptor (producer:\nname + payload + optional idempotencyKey + optional scheduledFor +\nmaxAttempts default 3 + optional tenantId), JobRecord (queue-side\nruntime fields: id, status, attempt, enqueuedAt, optional lastError),\nand JobStatus (pending/running/succeeded/failed). @repo/infrastructure/\nqueue ships JobQueue (enqueue, claimNext, ack, nack, sizeByStatus —\nEffect-typed) plus noopJobQueue (silent enqueue, never produces work)\nand createMemoryJobQueue() which honors idempotencyKey dedup,\nscheduledFor wall-clock deferral, and maxAttempts retry exhaustion. The\nADR makes explicit that JobQueue is for *demand-driven deferred work*,\ndistinct from @nestjs/schedule (cron/time-driven) and from the outbox\nrelay (event publish, no per-message retry budget). enqueue lives on\nthe port (unlike OutboxRelay.enqueue) because job enqueue is not\ntransactional with any specific DB write — dedup via idempotencyKey is\nthe recovery story.\n\nNotifier (ADR 0008): @repo/contracts/notification ships a discriminated\nNotificationRecipient (email/push/sms/webhook, each with the right\nfield — address/deviceToken/phone/url, so cross-channel mistakes fail\nat compile time), NotificationMessage (recipient + optional subject +\nbody + structured data + optional tenantId), and NotificationResult\n(delivered + optional providerMessageId + optional error).\n@repo/infrastructure/notification ships Notifier (one method:\nsend → Effect<NotificationResult, AppError>) plus noopNotifier\n(returns delivered:false silently) and createMemoryNotifier() (records\nsent messages and exposes drain() for tests). The ADR is explicit that\nthe contract does not enforce inline-vs-queued — the typical production\nwiring enqueues a notification job (per ADR 0007) and lets a worker\ncall send, isolating the request path from third-party network latency\nand getting retries for free.\n\nBoth lanes carry tenantId optionally so multi-tenancy activation\n(ADR 0004) does not require a contract follow-up. Capabilities-doc\npackage rows for @repo/contracts and @repo/infrastructure pick up the\nnew responsibilities; deferred-capabilities entries point at the new\nADRs (real job queue backend: BullMQ/Inngest/SQS/Cloud Tasks/pg-boss;\nreal notification provider: Resend/SES/Postmark/Twilio/Firebase). ADR\nREADME index updated for 0007 + 0008.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (0 errors, 2 design.md warnings + 1 info — same\nbaseline as last commit), pnpm test (28/28 turbo tasks: contracts grew\n17 → 30 tests, infrastructure 17 → 28), pnpm build (cached). Lint fix\non queue.test.ts replaced non-null assertions on optional claim returns\nwith explicit if-throw narrowing so biome''s noNonNullAssertion stays\nclean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"808d66f146290af6f8f5dfd4743a6fc088d19f99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/808d66f146290af6f8f5dfd4743a6fc088d19f99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGU1ZDhjZmY5YzZiNjA2OWRmNGY3ZDRmYTk2YjQ3MGViYzU5OWMwOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82","sha":"dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82"}],"sha":"e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/e5d8cff9c6b6069df4f7d4fa96b470ebc599c09d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:39:27Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:39:27Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Enterprise contracts: tenant, outbox, policy (memory adapters + ADRs)\n\nThree new opt-in lanes scaffolded as pure contracts + memory/noop adapters,\nfollowing ADR-0001 (avoid day-one overreach). Each lane lets a fork that\nneeds the capability activate it as a wiring change, and a fork that doesn''t\npay zero runtime cost — the no-op default returns immediately and seeds no\nALS scope.\n\nMulti-tenancy (ADR 0004): @repo/contracts/tenant adds a branded TenantId,\nTenantContext schema, and the conventional `x-tenant-id` header constant.\n@repo/platform gains a tenant-context AsyncLocalStorage (parallel to\nwithLoggerContext) and an optional `tenantId` field on LoggerContext so log\nlines emitted inside a tenant scope are auto-labeled. @repo/infrastructure\nships the Effect-typed TenantResolver port + noopTenantResolver. The\nresolver lives in @repo/infrastructure (not @repo/auth) because @repo/auth\nstays pure-schema (no Effect dep). organizationId from @repo/auth/identity\nremains a separate concept (membership / billing) — the ADR is explicit\nthat they are not the same axis.\n\nOutbox (ADR 0005): packages/db/src/schema/outbox.ts adds the transactional-\noutbox Drizzle table with a `(published_at, created_at)` index for the\nrelay''s pending-claim query and a `(tenant_id)` index for tenant-scoped\ndiagnostics. drizzle/0002_quiet_dark_beast.sql is the generated migration.\n@repo/contracts/outbox is the Zod row contract (metadata reuses\neventMetadataSchema, so an outbox row carries the same provenance as a\nDomainEvent). @repo/infrastructure/outbox ships the Effect-typed\nOutboxRelay port (claimBatch / markPublished / markFailed) plus\ncreateMemoryOutboxRelay for testing the relay loop in isolation. enqueue\nis intentionally NOT on the port — outbox writes happen inside the\napplication''s existing DB transaction alongside the business mutation, not\nthrough the relay.\n\nPolicy (ADR 0006): @repo/contracts/policy ships the authorization data\nshapes (PolicyDecision, PolicySubject, PolicyResource, PolicyAction,\nPolicyQuery) where the subject carries optional tenantId so per-tenant\nrules work day one. @repo/infrastructure/policy ships PolicyEvaluator (one\nmethod: evaluate(query) → Effect<PolicyDecision, AppError>) plus three\nadapters: allowAllPolicyEvaluator, denyAllPolicyEvaluator, and\ncreateMemoryPolicyEvaluator(rules) which evaluates a rule list of (query)\n=> allow|deny|abstain predicates in order with a fail-closed deny default.\nDecisions are binary at the contract level — abstain is internal to the\nrule loop, callers always get a definitive answer. CASL / Cedar / OPA\nplug in by implementing the port.\n\nAll three lanes carry tenantId optionally so multi-tenancy activation does\nnot require schema or contract follow-up changes. Capabilities doc gains\nthree deferred-capabilities entries (real tenant resolution, real outbox\nrelay, real policy engine), each pointing at the respective ADR; the\npackage rows for @repo/contracts, @repo/db, @repo/platform, and\n@repo/infrastructure pick up the new responsibilities; ADR README index\nbackfilled for 0003-0006.\n\nVerified: pnpm check (30/30 turbo tasks, 0 errors), pnpm test (28/28 —\n17 contracts, 17 infrastructure, 14 platform, 2 db), pnpm build (18/18).\nDrizzle migration generated cleanly without a live DB.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3060c5b460fccca18fa0cf3dc65789e792f0f34d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/3060c5b460fccca18fa0cf3dc65789e792f0f34d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGRjZGQ3Y2FjNjQ2NDA5YWZkMWFlNzk3NWMzNjMxZGYyYmVkNDNjODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e","sha":"020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e"}],"sha":"dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/dcdd7cac646409afd1ae7975c3631df2bed43c82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T14:08:06Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T14:08:06Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"README badges + repo description + topics (final polish)\n\nAdds five status badges at the top of the README — CI, Security, latest\nrelease, Node 24, pnpm 10 — so the GitHub landing page leads with the\ngreen-build signal and the version pin instead of just the H1. The badges\nall hot-link back to the relevant artifact (Actions tab, releases page,\n.nvmrc, package.json).\n\nSets the GitHub repo description (one sentence covering the surface set +\nthe production-hardened API defaults) and 18 topics so the template surfaces\nin `gh search repos` and the topic-tag pages: typescript, turborepo,\nmonorepo, template, pnpm, nextjs, nestjs, react, react-native, expo, tauri,\ndrizzle-orm, better-auth, biome, vitest, opentelemetry, openapi, scaffold.\n\nThese were the last items still degrading the first impression of the\nlanding page; closing them is the natural stopping point for this round of\nwork.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a650b76e94b1935569dd1adc8e131091c4668f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/a650b76e94b1935569dd1adc8e131091c4668f39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDAyMDU4M2M4ZGJjNTIxZTEwY2Y1ZjE0NjA0MzU4MDRiNGQ2MjMwOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d","sha":"5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d"}],"sha":"020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/020583c8dbc521e10cf5f1460435804b4d62308e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:49:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:49:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Cross-platform clean + .gitattributes + Tauri honesty\n\n`pnpm clean` was POSIX-only — `rm -rf` and `find -exec` don''t run under\nWindows cmd or PowerShell. Replaced with `scripts/clean.mjs` (Node fs\nAPIs), so the workflow runs the same on macOS / Linux / Windows. The new\nscript removes the same surfaces as before (root .turbo, coverage,\nplaywright-report, test-results; per-package dist, .next, .turbo,\ncoverage, .expo; all .tsbuildinfo files) and reports a single completion\nline. Verified: clean → build (18/18 turbo tasks) → test (28/28) all\ngreen.\n\nAdds `.gitattributes` enforcing `* text=auto eol=lf` so a Windows clone\ndoesn''t silently CRLF-corrupt POSIX shebangs in scripts/*.mjs (which\nwould break `node scripts/preflight.mjs` and friends). Keeps .cmd/.bat/\n.ps1 at CRLF since their tooling expects it; marks common image/binary\nformats as binary; flags pnpm-lock.yaml as linguist-generated so PR diffs\ncollapse it.\n\nUpdates capabilities.md to be honest about the desktop and mobile\nsurfaces:\n- `apps/desktop` ships `tauri.conf.json` only, no Rust shell. The note now\n  tells fork users to run `pnpm tauri init` inside `apps/desktop` before\n  `pnpm tauri build`, and flags bundle id / IPC / signing as fork\n  decisions.\n- `apps/mobile` ships eas.json with credential placeholders (Apple +\n  Google fields are null); the note now calls that out plus the\n  scaffold-only state of auth + API client wiring.\n\nBoth surfaces still build today; the doc just stops over-promising.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42aef5cc6ffed0b765a64ae3383cf52d2cca9dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/42aef5cc6ffed0b765a64ae3383cf52d2cca9dd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKDVkNTU4NjljNGM0N2Q3YmQyMTkxNjAzZWExNWY4NzBiMWQ2NzczN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59","sha":"d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59"}],"sha":"5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/5d55869c4c47d7bd2191603ea15f870b1d67737d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:33:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:33:25Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"v0.1.1 doc sync + production-checklist recipe + pnpm clean\n\nCHANGELOG: cuts the v0.1.1 entry covering the six commits since v0.1.0 —\nrequest-logger middleware, HTTP request metrics, pino-pretty in dev,\nMermaid diagram, CORS_ORIGINS / EXPOSE_DOCS / SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS env knobs,\nthe Better Auth per-route rate limit, AppErrorFilter HttpException\ntranslation, prod stack-trace scrub, graceful shutdown drain, lint:fix +\ntest:watch scripts, and the lint-info drain.\n\ncapabilities.md: refreshes the apps/api row to mention the new env-controlled\nknobs, the access log middleware, the metrics histogram + counter, the auth\nrate limit, and the /me reference module. \"Last checked\" pushed to today.\n\ndocs/recipes/production-checklist.md (new): a one-page go-live walkthrough —\nrequired env vars table (with which ones requireInProduction enforces), auth\nposture, DB / observability / CORS / container / shutdown items, plus a 4-\nstep `docker run` smoke. Linked from the recipes index.\n\npnpm clean: removes .turbo, coverage, playwright-report, test-results, every\napps/packages dist|.next|.turbo|.expo, and stale .tsbuildinfo files so a\nfollow-up `pnpm build` actually re-emits. Verified: clean + build cycles\nthrough 18/18 turbo tasks; full test + lint + format + env:check all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df0b37ed46d4860d4562b9744e320570287f9002","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/df0b37ed46d4860d4562b9744e320570287f9002"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59","node_id":"C_kwDOSLiwcdoAKGQ3ZWRmZjA4NTMxZTBkYTdhNGVjYmU2NGEzZDI3MTk0OGVkNThkNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo/turbo-template/commit/002cda4b93d338acb2cd811c5622642e9e41af82","sha":"002cda4b93d338acb2cd811c5622642e9e41af82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/002cda4b93d338acb2cd811c5622642e9e41af82"}],"sha":"d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/d7edff08531e0da7a4ecbe64a3d271948ed58d59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","id":63547292,"login":"de-novo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTQ3Mjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/002cda4b93d338acb2cd811c5622642e9e41af82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:16:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T13:16:33Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"DX + cleanup: scripts, CONTRIBUTING, drain lint backlog\n\nAdds two root scripts the prior workflow lacked:\n  pnpm lint:fix    biome lint --write\n  pnpm test:watch  vitest (no `run`, so it watches)\n\nUpdates CONTRIBUTING.md''s Local setup to use `pnpm bootstrap` instead of the\nmanual `cp env/local/*.example` pair — bootstrap landed earlier and is now\nthe documented onboarding path everywhere else.\n\nDrains the three piled-up lint infos:\n  - apps/api/src/db/db.module.ts: empty constructor (`noUselessConstructor`)\n  - scripts/bootstrap.mjs:121: `lines.join + \"\\n\"` → template literal\n  - scripts/rename-template.test.mjs:24: `JSON.stringify + \"\\n\"` → template literal\n\n`pnpm lint` now reports zero warnings AND zero infos, so future regressions\nwill surface immediately rather than hide in a noisy baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"47d3642875612e72041854e3dcb43e1d5b95b989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/47d3642875612e72041854e3dcb43e1d5b95b989"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/002cda4b93d338acb2cd811c5622642e9e41af82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63547292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/de-novo","i