nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/de-novo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/commits/78ec503c2aede455b3269e70384b9c0b8bbe9b90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T08:46:58Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T08:46:58Z","email":"vo0v0000@naver.com","name":"de-novo"},"message":"Polish: pino-pretty in dev + Mermaid dependency-direction diagram\n\napps/api dev script now pipes JSON through pino-pretty (catalog 13.1.3,\nlocal devDep) so console output is colorized + indented in local dev:\n\n  [17:45:43.700] INFO: API listening on http://localhost:4200\n      serviceName: \"fullstack-typescript-template\"\n      database: \"not-configured\"\n      auth: \"memory\"\n\nProduction deploys (`node dist/main.js`) are untouched and continue emitting\nstructured JSON for log shippers. Pipe (rather than pino''s in-process\ntransport) chosen because tsx + ESM silently breaks pino''s worker-thread\ntransport resolution; piping is the reliable belt-and-suspenders path.\n\nREADME''s \"Core dependency direction\" replaces the ASCII tree with a Mermaid\ngraph that GitHub renders inline. Same content, faster to scan, harder to\nlet drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"293649b0ef5c02ce9d9b6dce87a8b5c97a992eeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/trees/293649b0ef5c02ce9d9b6dce87a8b5c97a992eeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/de-novo/turbo-template/git/commits/78ec503c2aede455b3269e70384b9c0b8bbe9b90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,