ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teseo-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teseo-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teseo-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/teseo-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teseo-bot/multitenant-admin-panel/commits/40ebb850996c417fafffe31cf418081e2a72b627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:39:54Z","email":"teseo@teseo.lat","name":"Teseo Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:39:54Z","email":"teseo@teseo.lat","name":"Teseo Agent"},"message":"chore(ts): activar allowUnreachableCode — trinquete contra los fallbacks muertos\n\nUn `return` incondicional al inicio de una funcion deja el resto del cuerpo\ninalcanzable y tsc no dice nada mientras la bandera este en su default. Ese es\nexactamente el patron que dejo dos tools de Calendar rotuladas \"FALLBACK DE\nSUPERVIVENCIA\" devolviendo `success` durante meses: CI en verde y el agente\nprometiendo citas que nunca se creaban.\n\nYa estaba puesta en context-kdb-orchestrator. Esto la extiende al resto.\n\nMedido antes de tocar nada, con y sin la bandera sobre este mismo commit: el\nconteo de errores de `tsc --noEmit` no cambia. Es gratis hoy y solo muerde\ncuando alguien vuelva a escribir codigo inalcanzable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7b706acafaff315f59a85f15d14419c59ef6647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teseo-bot/multitenant-admin-panel/git/trees/c7b706acafaff315f59a85f15d14419c59ef6647"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teseo-bot/multitenant-admin-panel/git/commits/40ebb850996c417fafffe31cf418081e2a72b627","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262443783?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/u