he tint (#1021)\n\nOwner decision (#1021, 2026-09-23): fix the colour at the token layer\ninstead of patching ~200 call sites. The #1189 test now also measures\n--state-danger-text on the plain surface and on the composited tint.\nRed in :root, serban-light, serban-compact (3.76 / 3.19) and serban-dark\n(tint 3.63); serban-hc and the extension dark blocks already pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): danger text meets WCAG AA at the token layer (#1021)\n\n--state-danger-text: serban-light and serban-compact use palette\ndanger.700, serban-dark uses danger.400; serban-hc and the extension dark\nblocks already pass and are untouched. Regenerated theme.css; the dark-mode\naliases generated from the serban-dark token (--text-danger,\n--state-error-text, --state-danger in [data-mode=dark] and system-dark)\nfollow automatically.\n\nFirst v2 decision danger-text-contrast-1021: 3 token targets, the 10\nchanged generated declarations, and 8 measurements the gate recomputes\n(plain 6.47 / tint 5.49 light, plain 7.28 / tint 4.94 serban-dark).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e7c1b7412fb00b324884593aac05d74bbeeceb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/6e7c1b7412fb00b324884593aac05d74bbeeceb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/5e40e082da4bee753aa340e684524c60c642b787","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e7c1b7412fb00b324884593aac05d74bbeeceb6\nparent f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1790951466 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790951466 +0300\n\nfix(theme): danger text meets WCAG AA at the token layer (#1021) (#1205)\n\n* test(theme): the danger text itself must reach 4.5 on the plain surface and the tint (#1021)\n\nOwner decision (#1021, 2026-09-23): fix the colour at the token layer\ninstead of patching ~200 call sites. The #1189 test now also measures\n--state-danger-text on the plain surface and on the composited tint.\nRed in :root, serban-light, serban-compact (3.76 / 3.19) and serban-dark\n(tint 3.63); serban-hc and the extension dark blocks already pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): danger text meets WCAG AA at the token layer (#1021)\n\n--state-danger-text: serban-light and serban-compact use palette\ndanger.700, serban-dark uses danger.400; serban-hc and the extension dark\nblocks already pass and are untouched. Regenerated theme.css; the dark-mode\naliases generated from the serban-dark token (--text-danger,\n--state-error-text, --state-danger in [data-mode=dark] and system-dark)\nfollow automatically.\n\nFirst v2 decision danger-text-contrast-1021: 3 token targets, the 10\nchanged generated declarations, and 8 measurements the gate recomputes\n(plain 6.47 / tint 5.49 light, plain 7.28 / tint 4.94 serban-dark).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv8AqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiksQAF7OZEmCRrv4YHC9AoQiQDdi\nj/tr+T6hq5zni5f71B2yBRcLCkSYdf79XykKPtHH8/0B39SU1GsTUXNGsLzF2Pop\n4rYl2UgUSoPmFGIj7FgsGQJuRQSrfqJThwzq89RzQGilZCo4FT14ELoefiRTcE4W\n5WtB05AKm84B3WMoxZh5uS1N20GXSeC8PdlPYBXT7nCWfs5thE+rzQMxfECSMuyd\n80DsnYaoAFmSeNuuT8GEr0PbQl9QzoOQvrC9DSfZCrP8R6e5FSDxMmz7EuWyNd9V\nAxD2CMkx0tXc0E94YGVnEjTVRJz7DAUk2EqxEWpZcShvs/4eVsQmlHBnoKGo192z\nTIX40vAgn4VsbIdR4OU3ph4f5bTjDZ5+LhSpSphkOiedMgn75aGA3cukf7ZGPCu3\nfdeDySWMor/KC3dvRTmuvshamb4ygG3H4PYgQA0HDt0Z4/6sjz/DU4GqebNbSDod\nGWEm0uJcI+k6wrR6Mu6g5xTE5NxUR/2zv2p82WCdO7FvhlcbHrzKKDaTHTTCUBlf\nsRQr2O0+89y1/dU0kd6p/yHD3x0CRR8M/Lol9WA+JEnVZRaH39IBGahjMPQKZnJt\nuLDtc2m85EKwXqXzx