owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:01:45Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:01:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(endpoint-admin): group the six software tabs of the device drawer under one \"Yazılımlar\" tab (#1213)\n\nThe device detail drawer rendered 18 top-level tabs in one row (1323 px of\ntabs in a 672 px drawer at 1440 px). Six of them were software views\nscattered across the row: Envanter, Güncel Olmayan Yazılım, Yazılım\nDeğişimleri, Güncel Olmayan Değişimler, Yasaklı Yazılım, Yazılım Kataloğu.\n\nThey now live behind a single \"Yazılımlar\" tab (at the old Envanter\nposition) with a secondary switcher: Yüklü · Güncel Olmayan · Yasaklı ·\nDeğişimler · Güncel Olmayan Değişimler · Katalog. The top-level row drops\nto 13 tabs (939 px).\n\n- No view is rewritten; each keeps its lazy chunk, and the switcher mounts\n  only the selected section, so opening Yazılımlar still loads one chunk\n  and runs one view''s queries (WEB-014D cold-path budget).\n- The section is drawer state: it survives a trip to another top-level\n  tab and resets with the top-level tab on open / device change.\n- Section labels drop the \"Yazılım\" prefix the parent tab carries; the\n  three i18n tests that pin those labels follow the new copy.\n- TabFallback moves to its own module so both levels share it.\n\nTests: new DeviceDetailDrawer.software-tab test (real Tabs, both\ntablists) fails 5/5 against the old drawer and catches both removed\nbehaviours (reset on device change, persistence across tabs) under\nmutation. mfe-endpoint-admin: 83 files / 1323 tests pass; tsc error set\nidentical to origin/main (133 pre-existing, 0 new); eslint clean.\n\nTracked by #1212\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9afdb7e06785c80ae4f364435546d4f8a7662508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/9afdb7e06785c80ae4f364435546d4f8a7662508"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b","verification":{"payload":"tree 9afdb7e06785c80ae4f364435546d4f8a7662508\nparent fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1790748105 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790748105 +0300\n\nfeat(endpoint-admin): group the six software tabs of the device drawer under one \"Yazılımlar\" tab (#1213)\n\nThe device detail drawer rendered 18 top-level tabs in one row (1323 px of\ntabs in a 672 px drawer at 1440 px). Six of them were software views\nscattered across the row: Envanter, Güncel Olmayan Yazılım, Yazılım\nDeğişimleri, Güncel Olmayan Değişimler, Yasaklı Yazılım, Yazılım Kataloğu.\n\nThey now live behind a single \"Yazılımlar\" tab (at the old Envanter\nposition) with a secondary switcher: Yüklü · Güncel Olmayan · Yasaklı ·\nDeğişimler · Güncel Olmayan Değişimler · Katalog. The top-level row drops\nto 13 tabs (939 px).\n\n- No view is rewritten; each keeps its lazy chunk, and the switcher mounts\n  only the selected section, so opening Yazılımlar still loads one chunk\n  and runs one view''s queries (WEB-014D cold-path budget).\n- The section is drawer state: it survives a trip to another top-level\n  tab and resets with the top-level tab on open / device change.\n- Section labels drop the \"Yazılım\" prefix the parent tab carries; the\n  three i18n tests that pin those labels follow the new copy.\n- TabFallback moves to its own module so both levels share it.\n\nTests: new DeviceDetailDrawer.software-tab test (real Tabs, both\ntablists) fails 5/5 against the old drawer and catches both removed\nbehaviours (reset on device change, persistence across tabs) under\nmutation. mfe-endpoint-admin: 83 files / 1323 tests pass; tsc error set\nidentical to origin/main (133 pre-existing, 0 new); eslint clean.\n\nTracked by #1212\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvKXJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeGcQAEWr8VHi6cdYA9+hssA+d4f5\n2MVW2JgHivGBzs8XsC5t4qJvEdZiIDN311ZNlnAXgGMdsjEflUJssJuRLDV5Ke3k\nB5IaWIQ1OrypESuzb0CHll9Bu24WwXANogdQMCgNCNBMEJyn3X6dlimv3anvZ3cG\noLbFhYZxSNAnnErnZbqguJRmU+SxaMMmFtExCyfX0o/9iJAhKJpf5N0ru9cCsX0C\nsgc34Rz+m6jZqEDkiOazjmlhDqxAF3wEo8BOvPYIFa1xQNURNVZ8V7WJZ9Eze8Yl\n4cHYmP4TXr7l5M6r0cP/qzv5K6sxK8ZDHjJbLGTfyKcEGe+iHXZFp8BrYJXObS2d\nXrxq3sKGuSr2BabKE45B2FxzICBQhUD4uHkeriGKbiXmg/QjmLMTtvdFg2PP3OCf\ndCzpIESFtNCLZZxQvsXXaGl4LePp02or7SaczIemAObul2GAZ4yIgAy50gfpGEe6\nfc0QEC1cVYT7meeWwypY7TMHCgP76i0bZrwQax5+I0HrSvcXyTc4HIl5qrsCADMU\nCqKrWDPaADDMAnOG4mf4oaBjCuV6WZOIz7Fll4wFyAr202UtAoH+2yiwXBanlckT\nfXhb4fBu5OmWsY1yonibZN9XOta8sy79dpd+AmSeHBtRNSz/lS+VBiCCGc+f9K3N\njxuwEjsRgnGgxT/A9a/T\n=G4uD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T06:01:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKGY2NDAwODdiMDkxYTY2YWM0ZTkwNDZiNzVjOTk0OTc2NGQzNTA0NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32","sha":"fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32"}],"sha":"f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f640087b091a66ac4e9046b75c9949764d35046b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:16:22Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:16:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(theme): chain an append-only v2 remediation ledger after the frozen v1 (#1021) (#1203)\n\n* test(theme): pin the v2 remediation ledger gate and the shared colour math (#1021)\n\nOwner-approved design (#1021, 2026-09-25): v1 is frozen at its own result\ncommit, v2 chains after it and only grows, contrast claims are recomputed\nby the gate, and the gate and the #1189 test share one colour module.\n\nThis commit carries the tests, the strict v2 JSON Schema and the empty v2\nledger (predecessor = main at authoring time), plus a scaffold with no\nbehaviour: color-contrast.mjs throws, the remediation gate accepts\neverything. 19 new tests are red until the gate lands; the empty-ledger\ntest is green, and the existing v1 gate and --check are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): chain an append-only v2 remediation ledger after the frozen v1 (#1021)\n\n- theme-ownership-remediation-contract.mjs: validates v2 against its\n  strict schema (only enforced keywords, every object closed), freezes v1\n  at predecessor.commit (same bytes, verified there from Git objects),\n  keeps merge-base decisions immutable, partitions every token and theme\n  change into exactly one reviewed decision, requires alias bridges to be\n  complete, recomputes each contrast measurement (tolerance 0.01) and\n  binds the five result digests.\n- color-contrast.mjs: the single colour-math module; translucent layers\n  are composited in gamma-encoded sRGB, as the browser paints them. The\n  #1189 shell contrast test now measures through it.\n- generate-theme-css.mjs --check answers to v2; the v1 tests read their\n  inputs from the predecessor commit.\n- CODEOWNERS: the ledger, its schema, the gates and the colour math.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): bind the v2 ledger digest false positive to its exact finding (#1021)\n\ngitleaks generic-api-key flags \"tokenSourceSha256\" in the v2 ledger, the\nsame content-addressed SHA-256 already reviewed for v1. Like the v1 entry,\nthe exemption is bound to the exact commit, file, rule and line; any later\nchange to the digest is scanned again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): build gate scenarios from the frozen predecessor, not the working tree (#1021)\n\nThe gate tests assumed the repository ledger was empty, so the first real\ndecision would have broken them. Synthetic scenarios now start from the\npredecessor commit with an empty ledger; a separate test checks that the\nrepository ledger itself passes. Found while preparing the first decision\n(the --state-danger-text token PR).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): scope the ledger digest exemption to one rule, path and line shape (#1021)\n\nOwner decision (#1205 review, 2026-09-25): commit-bound .gitleaksignore\nlines do not survive a squash merge and would be needed for every new\nledger decision. .gitleaks.toml now allows, for the generic-api-key rule\nonly, a line in design-tokens/migrations/theme-ownership-decisions.v<N>.json\nthat is exactly one \"...Sha256\": \"<64 hex>\" field (condition AND). The\ncommit-bound v2 line is removed; the historical v1 entry is left as is.\n\nMeasured with gitleaks 8.24.3 (the CI version, checksum-verified):\n- a global [[allowlists]] block is not applied in that version, so the\n  rule-scoped [[rules.allowlists]] form is used;\n- this branch and the #1205 branch scan clean without commit-bound lines;\n  the #1205 ledger file scanned as a plain file (squash-merge case) is\n  clean with the new config and still flagged with main''s config;\n- still reported: another field in a ledger file, a digest line in any\n  other file, and a digest line that also carries another key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09177b73f10e48a0d2bcb9a76b0ffc4a6482a51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/09177b73f10e48a0d2bcb9a76b0ffc4a6482a51b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32","verification":{"payload":"tree 09177b73f10e48a0d2bcb9a76b0ffc4a6482a51b\nparent 917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1790525782 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790525782 +0300\n\nfeat(theme): chain an append-only v2 remediation ledger after the frozen v1 (#1021) (#1203)\n\n* test(theme): pin the v2 remediation ledger gate and the shared colour math (#1021)\n\nOwner-approved design (#1021, 2026-09-25): v1 is frozen at its own result\ncommit, v2 chains after it and only grows, contrast claims are recomputed\nby the gate, and the gate and the #1189 test share one colour module.\n\nThis commit carries the tests, the strict v2 JSON Schema and the empty v2\nledger (predecessor = main at authoring time), plus a scaffold with no\nbehaviour: color-contrast.mjs throws, the remediation gate accepts\neverything. 19 new tests are red until the gate lands; the empty-ledger\ntest is green, and the existing v1 gate and --check are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): chain an append-only v2 remediation ledger after the frozen v1 (#1021)\n\n- theme-ownership-remediation-contract.mjs: validates v2 against its\n  strict schema (only enforced keywords, every object closed), freezes v1\n  at predecessor.commit (same bytes, verified there from Git objects),\n  keeps merge-base decisions immutable, partitions every token and theme\n  change into exactly one reviewed decision, requires alias bridges to be\n  complete, recomputes each contrast measurement (tolerance 0.01) and\n  binds the five result digests.\n- color-contrast.mjs: the single colour-math module; translucent layers\n  are composited in gamma-encoded sRGB, as the browser paints them. The\n  #1189 shell contrast test now measures through it.\n- generate-theme-css.mjs --check answers to v2; the v1 tests read their\n  inputs from the predecessor commit.\n- CODEOWNERS: the ledger, its schema, the gates and the colour math.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): bind the v2 ledger digest false positive to its exact finding (#1021)\n\ngitleaks generic-api-key flags \"tokenSourceSha256\" in the v2 ledger, the\nsame content-addressed SHA-256 already reviewed for v1. Like the v1 entry,\nthe exemption is bound to the exact commit, file, rule and line; any later\nchange to the digest is scanned again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): build gate scenarios from the frozen predecessor, not the working tree (#1021)\n\nThe gate tests assumed the repository ledger was empty, so the first real\ndecision would have broken them. Synthetic scenarios now start from the\npredecessor commit with an empty ledger; a separate test checks that the\nrepository ledger itself passes. Found while preparing the first decision\n(the --state-danger-text token PR).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): scope the ledger digest exemption to one rule, path and line shape (#1021)\n\nOwner decision (#1205 review, 2026-09-25): commit-bound .gitleaksignore\nlines do not survive a squash merge and would be needed for every new\nledger decision. .gitleaks.toml now allows, for the generic-api-key rule\nonly, a line in design-tokens/migrations/theme-ownership-decisions.v<N>.json\nthat is exactly one \"...Sha256\": \"<64 hex>\" field (condition AND). The\ncommit-bound v2 line is removed; the historical v1 entry is left as is.\n\nMeasured with gitleaks 8.24.3 (the CI version, checksum-verified):\n- a global [[allowlists]] block is not applied in that version, so the\n  rule-scoped [[rules.allowlists]] form is used;\n- this branch and the #1205 branch scan clean without commit-bound lines;\n  the #1205 ledger file scanned as a plain file (squash-merge case) is\n  clean with the new config and still flagged with main''s config;\n- still reported: another field in a ledger file, a digest line in any\n  other file, and a digest line that also carries another key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquUFWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdqEQABcrEHHlp2kSgZRmtp+vdj1F\nB3SowqtBV8tH2UBL4+vfDtURe1jgRvM+bK09ykp0vMWJVrgM32YM8ObojTDquzT+\nDWF+5OiMfLbiCEGsqeA8AiGhUEx//d/dK7sFT/5bnqf3fEBXi0waF/YP6q+uTap0\nj2fzhCKtZGGloNmaZX8eHCotUJRObgmyG5N4uwDy2Vh3Q9zH0KH8i5UYjO0N+55h\neQSCJXnw9PujzJSAUiZCEF8Q7FAP63S9udjKtF9skyKyqAPLMoh2G7faageLkhey\nwvdjy6XmmTiDBevf9numIkR0f6kGCRuowXdFzQMmSq4i/czio24FQz6oUVPlJrWC\nSlk425LXnzuiyR+d9DYb/sP+DgdtV2SbBwHRrUBV/wqH797SHLFwD8FV969S9ZQ+\nqzrErw0iw9JdqWE1CUKWALspMQsMKs46dVPKT6LiNfC2BWQrtvVMj57OPZtyHvtU\nxr6hRYNYt4jYkHqlmVlNiCLfkkqY8o27LDU2zPKls26XzR+y331mMpawR4D0jE/P\n/H3yGj8eSTPS3l3cmr+E3ik/FcZBtwr7UOTcwIs9WeaUy8AygLxx6fna6u6bgaRc\nd+reOheI+pWsEBSgpcyabEvpvX7XQTC76sOL/vjAELs1+PvyvndlB3TBr0ZK564W\n0KmmBBDsvtU/GY8rwLAF\n=5zRb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T16:16:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKGZjNGNlNjIyMWVmZDEwOGZjMWRmNWQ5ZDlkYmJhOGFmZDlhOGVhMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060","sha":"917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060"}],"sha":"fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/fc4ce6221efd108fc1df5d9d9dbba8afd9a8ea32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:14:38Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:14:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review) (#1207)\n\n* test(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review)\n\nOwner decision (#1193 review, 2026-09-25): move the five local recruiter\nformatDate copies to a shared helper with the same \"—\" behaviour and the\nsame tests as the candidate portal, so the invalid-date crash cannot come\nback through a copy.\n\nScaffold only: format-date.ts has the final signature but no guard yet,\nand the panels still use their own copies. Red until the fix:\n- formatDateSafe writes \"—\" for \"abc\", \"\", \"not-a-date\", \"2026-13-45\",\n  null and undefined;\n- each recruiter surface imports the helper and builds no\n  Intl.DateTimeFormat of its own;\n- the recruiter inbox stays on screen with createdAt \"abc\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review)\n\nformatDateSafe(value, { withTime?, timeZone? }) writes \"—\" for an invalid\nor missing date and keeps today''s formatting otherwise. The five recruiter\nsurfaces drop their local Intl.DateTimeFormat copies; call signatures stay\n(the offer panel keeps withTime, the interview panel its time zone).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8591f05f5286cb4483b3b33017d9234930617cee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/8591f05f5286cb4483b3b33017d9234930617cee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/917181bc4d9f4f45be7ba421918a0133f5878060","verification":{"payload":"tree 8591f05f5286cb4483b3b33017d9234930617cee\nparent b9fd690f575dbd4834754b996336c8d979b88522\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1790525678 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790525678 +0300\n\nfix(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review) (#1207)\n\n* test(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review)\n\nOwner decision (#1193 review, 2026-09-25): move the five local recruiter\nformatDate copies to a shared helper with the same \"—\" behaviour and the\nsame tests as the candidate portal, so the invalid-date crash cannot come\nback through a copy.\n\nScaffold only: format-date.ts has the final signature but no guard yet,\nand the panels still use their own copies. Red until the fix:\n- formatDateSafe writes \"—\" for \"abc\", \"\", \"not-a-date\", \"2026-13-45\",\n  null and undefined;\n- each recruiter surface imports the helper and builds no\n  Intl.DateTimeFormat of its own;\n- the recruiter inbox stays on screen with createdAt \"abc\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): recruiter surfaces format dates through one invalid-safe helper (#1193 review)\n\nformatDateSafe(value, { withTime?, timeZone? }) writes \"—\" for an invalid\nor missing date and keeps today''s formatting otherwise. The five recruiter\nsurfaces drop their local Intl.DateTimeFormat copies; call signatures stay\n(the offer panel keeps withTime, the interview panel its time zone).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquUDuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+gQQAEasRaVedg7Lp7UKkgPmhGxT\nX1eYLmDJe+wXbG4FDQkDr8b1HXFidfYfrmS8C0YopQpfKceLbvckXQqf/GR+hc2K\nnZxXlU+W2WfGCv+TlZ+dw8rmtnXezv00qL03175GzSkRVzPmHrLzMNK7GnPv20wF\nU9625Sb9Hu+vH1ds9xP/7lwIS8MiuJKAC4KcQTEsC7wnqPMtxcdFLz97g4J8pdSP\nYYPZR9El3bI6aUhel4ESwtTgmDlispCbquK9HaI3Ux6x+6WX4OjFNVkxYp8FhfAW\nPr9HuTMCGd+sGoMvudgMm9TtCe+9beYX3T9tK9VINFovSDnDkM0PCDZtXrLjbS+3\nzIgGntmN9gVE9tDInpQcdiWgg2tsOggVZap+SS73/FXrE2Zk9lKN2NwyVYrbwNDQ\n4kIduZlnKqJbfYswTPnw60hJ7cLPdl10AXQpDg6fgPdSC7ExbfJRZhcPOaoTIVWd\n9JwbRKphIUB+xdzHe2MIV6ooAGhyj53LxSuiUIgJRGpczxW0zdYzyg2bwqprd62P\nres3xbLmF0koEchUzpTzgJ8Utf1sekSqk+Oj0NxFegIHZdTCT4H+Hq8upL5RDuHT\nkMdYeQyqBY8JunSCkjitc7PPjcGhQ8Rxc5Sc446aAc/oD7z6fda3iYMLuEozGh2L\nXdp8AFe2m5eK/70EYmnD\n=LYlK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T16:14:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow