m/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e"}],"sha":"109a75467fe6c2596ccf2a200e54e0e6ae28ae47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/109a75467fe6c2596ccf2a200e54e0e6ae28ae47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T08:18:03Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T08:18:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): release the callback hold from the live URL, not the router snapshot (#1204)\n\nFollow-up to 110d48e (#1201). Live verification on testai showed the new\n\"hold while an unconsumed Keycloak callback is in the URL\" guard never\nreleased for a stale callback: keycloak-js strips the fragment with\nhistory.replaceState, which React Router does not observe, so\n`location.hash` kept the stale `#state=…&code=…` and ProtectedRoute kept\nrendering null — shell chrome visible, <main> empty. The old behaviour on\nthat URL was an infinite login loop; a blank page is not an acceptable\nreplacement.\n\nRead window.location.hash (what keycloak-js actually mutates) instead of\nthe router''s location.hash. AuthBootstrapper always dispatches a final\nphase after kc.init, so the re-render that sees the clean hash is\nguaranteed; with no token it then redirects to a fragment-free\n/login?redirect=… and Keycloak (SSO alive) issues a fresh code.\n\nTests: the hold test now drives window.location via replaceState (the\nMemoryRouter entry never reaches window). New test pins the release path:\nrender under the poisoned URL → empty; strip the fragment the way\nkeycloak-js does → rerender → Login Page with a clean return-to and no\n\"%23\". Both tests fail when the hold reads the router snapshot again and\nwhen the hold is removed (negative verification, 2 mutations). 39/39\nacross the three auth suites.\n\nRefs #1200\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e188a6dcffe84b044f768778034fb3bb74965108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/e188a6dcffe84b044f768778034fb3bb74965108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e","verification":{"payload":"tree e188a6dcffe84b044f768778034fb3bb74965108\nparent 110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1790324283 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790324283 +0300\n\nfix(auth): release the callback hold from the live URL, not the router snapshot (#1204)\n\nFollow-up to 110d48e (#1201). Live verification on testai showed the new\n\"hold while an unconsumed Keycloak callback is in the URL\" guard never\nreleased for a stale callback: keycloak-js strips the fragment with\nhistory.replaceState, which React Router does not observe, so\n`location.hash` kept the stale `#state=…&code=…` and ProtectedRoute kept\nrendering null — shell chrome visible, <main> empty. The old behaviour on\nthat URL was an infinite login loop; a blank page is not an acceptable\nreplacement.\n\nRead window.location.hash (what keycloak-js actually mutates) instead of\nthe router''s location.hash. AuthBootstrapper always dispatches a final\nphase after kc.init, so the re-render that sees the clean hash is\nguaranteed; with no token it then redirects to a fragment-free\n/login?redirect=… and Keycloak (SSO alive) issues a fresh code.\n\nTests: the hold test now drives window.location via replaceState (the\nMemoryRouter entry never reaches window). New test pins the release path:\nrender under the poisoned URL → empty; strip the fragment the way\nkeycloak-js does → rerender → Login Page with a clean return-to and no\n\"%23\". Both tests fail when the hold reads the router snapshot again and\nwhen the hold is removed (negative verification, 2 mutations). 39/39\nacross the three auth suites.\n\nRefs #1200\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqti47CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANngQAErfVmm+TkONcEdZxFiW+yKT\n12Q8jxX51NNMlAC6z5JXDxOOd8Xiw41YLITL3fV+TgVpqju5qf/stV5KpzfqiCbp\n5r5w/cNeTnijRkQzKlpOBOs0+PeSXV4Q4zsSEgCPNrC5Ja+VDl8XbgHLOqfbj/B/\ntjaebmzFkMV/o6VZRPxg20w6L2iUwhkOsNoAdunKKSc16E2k+R8ReMxQzduY4qEF\no3a5S5pDBoJAdwctfrR3w6FiHgzEgESvHFSNAjSNUctRkGWDGZcrJo5rdf/1QmJl\nhbW7e2TPxpHdBooliwXjVXQrZpD1WTAWqP9WbsaG1EWQVdTTtP8gQuphBUiamn43\nHwti8mkUjTUifOQ7VXVWfF3VZLb1/yFD6oid01ilpZY2Oix7UX64htiQauGz2rFP\nPQ5w9DNBH2Ada7Ydvprtm4Nn6TXKWKb9y8tpvcel2BG4/cztmWZ2yQ8RXq3KAryS\nWj8jY1FVT+n5yNQiYlruUzuyy7/lQ8vv2y2Wh5+31onr5FkjGhCoIfUeCFeUxQHi\nmk+pk8voE6iNSqFzjvw/wl7g6Cggt6UjSr6pgnrOGlmkL2ySZu7lxlvgmEZCfv9o\nsK2EeGEQD6QSdSp473UQSjdlRa4jB8jcwyxG2vzPsP1Vi/VTG9u92wvemSdmedKP\nC/ICNd0yOa2Ro6naHFit\n=Jo1+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T08:18:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDliM2ZiYWQxMmJiMDAwYzEzYzUzNTlhMTg0YzY0NWZhYmQ0ZGI5NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d","sha":"110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d"}],"sha":"9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/9b3fbad12bb000c13c5359a184c645fabd4db95e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T06:51:27Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T06:51:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): never round-trip a Keycloak callback fragment into redirect_uri (#1201)\n\nLive incident (testai, 2026-09-25): after a successful Keycloak login the\napp bounced straight back to /login, indefinitely. Keycloak''s LOGIN event\nrecorded the redirect_uri the shell sent:\n\n  …/admin/reports/hr-demografik-yapi#state=…&session_state=jnqL…&iss=…&code=…\n\ni.e. the *previous*, unconsumed authorization-code callback. Keycloak\n(response_mode=fragment) appended a fresh callback onto it, keycloak-js\nmatched the stale `state` first, declared the user unauthenticated, and\nProtectedRoute redirected to /login with the same poisoned return-to.\nNo CODE_TO_TOKEN event was ever emitted for the user that day: the code\nwas lost, not rejected.\n\nTwo defects combined:\n\n1. ProtectedRoute composed the ?redirect= return-to from pathname + search\n   + hash, and LoginPage only stripped the hash for its /login* comparison\n   before returning the full value to buildAppRedirectUri. RFC 6749 §3.1.2\n   forbids a fragment in the redirection URI at all.\n2. On a deep route the guard could redirect away before keycloak-js had\n   parsed the callback fragment, discarding the code (the documented\n   auth-sync self-replay race, now reachable through other paths).\n\nFix (single source of truth: app/auth/redirect-target.ts):\n- ProtectedRoute: omit location.hash from the return-to; while an\n  unconsumed callback (`code` + `state`) is still in the URL and there is\n  no token, hold (render null) instead of redirecting — keycloak-js clears\n  that fragment on parse regardless of outcome, so the hold cannot stick.\n- LoginPage: strip the fragment from the redirect param before it becomes\n  redirect_uri (keeps the query).\n- auth-config.normalizeRedirectPath: strip the fragment at the redirect_uri\n  boundary so every present and future caller is covered.\n\nTests: 38/38 across the three suites (6 new). Every layer was negatively\nverified — reverting each strip/hold makes its test fail:\nProtectedRoute hash omission (1), callback hold (1), LoginPage strip (2),\nstripUrlFragment (3). The ProtectedRoute assertion uses exact textContent\nequality because toHaveTextContent(string) is a substring match and passed\nvacuously against the pre-fix value. tsc error set identical to main.\n\nRefs #1200\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a735ef2cc83236d01817416eba7e790369e4ea09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/a735ef2cc83236d01817416eba7e790369e4ea09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d","verification":{"payload":"tree a735ef2cc83236d01817416eba7e790369e4ea09\nparent e16e0784776dcfc74316187d35245e47e4216250\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1790319087 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790319087 +0300\n\nfix(auth): never round-trip a Keycloak callback fragment into redirect_uri (#1201)\n\nLive incident (testai, 2026-09-25): after a successful Keycloak login the\napp bounced straight back to /login, indefinitely. Keycloak''s LOGIN event\nrecorded the redirect_uri the shell sent:\n\n  …/admin/reports/hr-demografik-yapi#state=…&session_state=jnqL…&iss=…&code=…\n\ni.e. the *previous*, unconsumed authorization-code callback. Keycloak\n(response_mode=fragment) appended a fresh callback onto it, keycloak-js\nmatched the stale `state` first, declared the user unauthenticated, and\nProtectedRoute redirected to /login with the same poisoned return-to.\nNo CODE_TO_TOKEN event was ever emitted for the user that day: the code\nwas lost, not rejected.\n\nTwo defects combined:\n\n1. ProtectedRoute composed the ?redirect= return-to from pathname + search\n   + hash, and LoginPage only stripped the hash for its /login* comparison\n   before returning the full value to buildAppRedirectUri. RFC 6749 §3.1.2\n   forbids a fragment in the redirection URI at all.\n2. On a deep route the guard could redirect away before keycloak-js had\n   parsed the callback fragment, discarding the code (the documented\n   auth-sync self-replay race, now reachable through other paths).\n\nFix (single source of truth: app/auth/redirect-target.ts):\n- ProtectedRoute: omit location.hash from the return-to; while an\n  unconsumed callback (`code` + `state`) is still in the URL and there is\n  no token, hold (render null) instead of redirecting — keycloak-js clears\n  that fragment on parse regardless of outcome, so the hold cannot stick.\n- LoginPage: strip the fragment from the redirect param before it becomes\n  redirect_uri (keeps the query).\n- auth-config.normalizeRedirectPath: strip the fragment at the redirect_uri\n  boundary so every present and future caller is covered.\n\nTests: 38/38 across the three suites (6 new). Every layer was negatively\nverified — reverting each strip/hold makes its test fail:\nProtectedRoute hash omission (1), callback hold (1), LoginPage strip (2),\nstripUrlFragment (3). The ProtectedRoute assertion uses exact textContent\nequality because toHaveTextContent(string) is a substring match and passed\nvacuously against the pre-fix value. tsc error set identical to main.\n\nRefs #1200\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqthnvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI3cQACjd7LYwukfaJthPnHVWYvZ5\nL+VO0NFS7Nz2RKjlwJy3UXc8JfjfLwyk2W6IE5gmpWIW+TqQsjCv79/FFrzzgvnp\nWBPGZXaFjuUsl1YyRES8E09r1Wla27RXcxOKwwF7dkVQjNmqoKezcyQ9uU6yLRUq\nj85EL9LCfvPehtK61iID1FBvmSaPjzbUAVcP7xQuCEXXKC8XslyzrIWyHpqKOLt5\n6Vj2Em8gvmCHsZpLelg2PiA6e6mvLrNgeLVwnOmKnxhbTKZnJvmp7q1GsAsZsYMr\no7w2/pWYhQwQ39G1qxSgKfLc3tOomg137f5+UilJquXjNTlPbGrsez/Zjkz8h6/4\nA0Yg9FK16JQn4SxiHLK8BfZ93xhcnMll0GBhXeIhOwpy9URSVdzUqutB4vLsehAu\nngBguIP57BaFQmGwkPX5AwsKc82h6rU3QgQbyqUXCwwo/MP7VL7rtxheYOvDT4zG\n1pa52Qqqdxa2fbhgWM2RSU3Fq1qQZ9wf8kPiX780vf5NqWcPG2Di5rjo4zmhcnBP\nwjzEN94LU3W5pfgTzhpSPtD/4/C3BGi97eDC7vPBGt2a40oPwxJB46ATpkoTHCO6\npkq76lKgypAf+0QkJc1bgQ1/LUBKrHfgkCMWeM8Hx8xbj6JmFjFLUFKjmweT8rOc\n84UWG0NkS5a3qzdpU2Bv\n=tclJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T06:51:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/110d48ef840a1e5aa771a586abc804effe5cb72d","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwO