https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/4acbb3227d785733062ad9d751a959358df33c67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T12:37:22Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T12:37:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mfe-meeting): assign tasks via the meeting-scoped people picker (gitops#3834) (#1196)\n\n* fix(mfe-meeting): assign tasks via the meeting-scoped people picker (gitops#3834)\n\nThe \"Göreve ata\" picker searched the admin user grid (GET /v1/users),\nwhich requires USER_READ and answers 403 to every non-admin. The editor\ncaught the error and rendered it as \"sonuç yok\", so a permission failure\nlooked like \"nobody matches\".\n\nsearchAssignees(meetingId, query) now POSTs to\n/v1/admin/meetings/{id}/assignee-candidates/search (platform-backend\n#1186: gated like creating a task, returns only assignable people\nvisible to the caller; POST keeps the typed name out of URLs). Errors\npropagate; the editor shows them as an alert (\"Kişi araması\nyapılamadı: …\") and keeps \"sonuç yok\" for a real empty answer.\n\nTests: 4 new cases red on the old code, green now; mfe-meeting suite\n157/157, tsc and eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-meeting): show the assignee by name, not as an account id (gitops#3834)\n\nAn assigned task rendered task.assigneeSubject — a Keycloak UUID — as\nits assignee. MeetingTask now carries assigneeDisplayName (sent by\nmeeting-service, see platform-backend#1186 follow-up) and the row shows\nit; when the name cannot be resolved the row says \"Atanmış kişi\"\ninstead of exposing the id. Safe before the backend field ships: the\nfallback applies.\n\nTests: 2 new cases red on the old rendering/mapping, green now;\nmfe-meeting 159/159, tsc and eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88d91fa5a0f37da7244b0f43600fe539d7b5f3db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/88d91fa5a0f37da7244b0f43600fe539d7b5f3db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/4acbb3227d785733062ad9d751a959358df33c67","verification":{"payload":"tree 88d91fa5a0f37da7244b0f43600fe539d7b5f3db\nparent cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1790253442 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790253442 +0300\n\nfix(mfe-meeting): assign tasks via the meeting-scoped people picker (gitops#3834) (#1196)\n\n* fix(mfe-meeting): assign tasks via the meeting-scoped people picker (gitops#3834)\n\nThe \"Göreve ata\" picker searched the admin user grid (GET /v1/users),\nwhich requires USER_READ and answers 403 to every non-admin. The editor\ncaught the error and rendered it as \"sonuç yok\", so a permission failure\nlooked like \"nobody matches\".\n\nsearchAssignees(meetingId, query) now POSTs to\n/v1/admin/meetings/{id}/assignee-candidates/search (platform-backend\n#1186: gated like creating a task, returns only assignable people\nvisible to the caller; POST keeps the typed name out of URLs). Errors\npropagate; the editor shows them as an alert (\"Kişi araması\nyapılamadı: …\") and keeps \"sonuç yok\" for a real empty answer.\n\nTests: 4 new cases red on the old code, green now; mfe-meeting suite\n157/157, tsc and eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-meeting): show the assignee by name, not as an account id (gitops#3834)\n\nAn assigned task rendered task.assigneeSubject — a Keycloak UUID — as\nits assignee. MeetingTask now carries assigneeDisplayName (sent by\nmeeting-service, see platform-backend#1186 follow-up) and the row shows\nit; when the name cannot be resolved the row says \"Atanmış kişi\"\ninstead of exposing the id. Safe before the backend field ships: the\nfallback applies.\n\nTests: 2 new cases red on the old rendering/mapping, green now;\nmfe-meeting 159/159, tsc and eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtRmCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9jcQAFC46bEqpr0w5QDe4PmqmyGt\nH0EXif8UxxBJ3HMaugI5vrNkNUQ4tLJr9aeQpGgPJxkDmLd4LWBj3qcZk2Dk0YRk\naT2k34Sz81m+rwljBz/xAxndDrv6esI03XcRndSoFdK+VumSm4eMP7IFpKGoH8rT\nGZhAYisGzXC4Ezz3YkRf7lcdQG8U8zHB/9unbZLc3Q7awiVVXvG61ew03B8nEPI9\nACEe/ZXjT01/nGU+H6LcJBI6GfNv72IDxbQw5H68NblO8b7VLtTQ95mr3QkCCTFW\nMTyOZMtTO0niJbU1VSjLwljpvpI5hj0z90fpAsAtWWzIjJIQ/thNg+3ct2i7fOwl\nU3WjYAptmkUNIUN8c3OFVd6DOUObtaFPXz2QcE4gKWaMfpplN+b03KmWIWMgO/sY\n1uxAfHIsY20g75hJpd9lblUwy8wnlGXU0IiHV4Y2LFmsOygRZKOQ55PoJkFJJV/n\notIA58l+zkyqqBtFMSb7CqgJA3AFoW/l4P+P6twuow6/uTEBx3L7arvqGeVXnqlP\nYZk95j0VQxmLNFyag1DG/vRYTykUbfQKbvQOBy7v+6QWnVX/Xry7HtwcRAKCLRo8\nRFMAqcdaQGwOu1w8n3C4Izreczeg0xH5Gb9gkKbXzEdwrysuUuiXli2gGOBf3A81\nH9srak1w9aADNFHPI+lV\n=FG9z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T12:37:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/4acbb3227d785733062ad9d751a959358df33c67","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDRhY2JiMzIyN2Q3ODU3MzMwNjJhZDlkNzUxYTk1OTM1OGRmMzNjNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982","sha":"cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982"}],"sha":"4acbb3227d785733062ad9d751a959358df33c67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/4acbb3227d785733062ad9d751a959358df33c67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:58:17Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:58:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ats): show server rejections to the recruiter and the offer start date as a date (#963) (#1190)\n\n* test(ats): server rejections and the offer start date as the recruiter and candidate see them (#963)\n\nTests only. On TEST, an offer without a completed interview was rejected\nwith 409 INTERVIEW_NOT_COMPLETED but the recruiter saw nothing: every error\npath writes the message and then calls refresh(), which clears it. Six such\npaths across the offer and interview panels.\n\nThe candidate portal also shows the calendar start date 2026-10-06 as\n\"6 Eki 2026 03:00\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): keep server rejections on screen and show the offer start date as a calendar day (#963)\n\nError paths now refresh first and write the rejection afterwards, so the\nrefresh no longer wipes the reason (offer create/update/transition,\ninterview schedule/reschedule/complete/scorecard). The candidate portal\nformats the calendar start date without converting it through a time zone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3a0cff3eb2f26f55a8e175a15f9be7f169de168","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/b3a0cff3eb2f26f55a8e175a15f9be7f169de168"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/cf6628fcbddd90562746df94a72b15225eaf5982","verification":{"payload":"tree b3a0cff3eb2f26f55a8e175a15f9be7f169de168\nparent e432718aeb895129a76050c24ff0a40d585b125b\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1790153897 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790153897 +0300\n\nfix(ats): show server rejections to the recruiter and the offer start date as a date (#963) (#1190)\n\n* test(ats): server rejections and the offer start date as the recruiter and candidate see them (#963)\n\nTests only. On TEST, an offer without a completed interview was rejected\nwith 409 INTERVIEW_NOT_COMPLETED but the recruiter saw nothing: every error\npath writes the message and then calls refresh(), which clears it. Six such\npaths across the offer and interview panels.\n\nThe candidate portal also shows the calendar start date 2026-10-06 as\n\"6 Eki 2026 03:00\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): keep server rejections on screen and show the offer start date as a calendar day (#963)\n\nError paths now refresh first and write the rejection afterwards, so the\nrefresh no longer wipes the reason (offer create/update/transition,\ninterview schedule/reschedule/complete/scorecard). The candidate portal\nformats the calendar start date without converting it through a time zone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5SpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAppMQAKmSDX1nPU5av6kbLV4SOJbb\nlWh6PK+2mLmXBmEgdTzWNcycitto0acVh2LSYgMhy8o1cUpV3bbhZZocNVegP2ZC\nxgcYs1lvqC9wrukljEedrLVLqRsF42d/2Wh7vZ7G/LV3KiPCP9sP2vXx+nO2L8mj\nG2HLveVrPMP8gtAa1rHpRCkEHS6W3qD8hI/msOf/Lx5PVp1ymsNiCyN5vJz9FTA/\nzhv7vgcocvy/co8IroZZH5WNhj7ppWlCkmcljyPl88WPGFGmHJR5JULXir3NJKET\n+kK+1ojf2yUxADRgr1tQXfs9+70Hyxj1dDZabtkn2SQkW5muQj05khpMBqfmkrmw\nR3x43cMpkpEanJU9rg1xb2dDJzJiOEYA3NZGtLOoIfKtpNB/XI8iDCwp8HukJiGt\nQ5GmuvPWmgvgN85/IRHaWn6XF6T7vBd9qYrNZb7hVJsV7wQ73gG5dIuw6JD3B5Tw\n0G99xqOQcdVQTMG/50/8uZfDXTsyaK1zbNmC6GOmtAHS8I38ItzkEFbhCWGYSBvX\nHrAqsQDDDYK0Id97/6cii9FtYYwGh8bm0TxqmyGiDyoAFMqLM1ANs/jkYn1iAFWU\nft++DVLbbtrt7c4V3Yltvn