ub.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/e7640339295ecce6cf0d1fb0260ca34dbbdec57e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:01:05Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:01:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ats): plain candidate copy and focus after candidate actions (#992 C) (#1187)\n\n* test(ats): candidate actions need plain language and must keep focus\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#992 (slice 992-C). Tests only: candidate copy\nstill says \"terminal\" and points \"below\" to a status shown above; after\na withdrawal (success or A1 conflict) and after an offer response the\npressed control leaves the DOM and focus drops to body; the withdrawal\nconfirmation neither takes nor returns focus.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): plain candidate copy and focus after candidate actions\n\nCandidate copy used the technical word \"terminal\" and pointed \"below\" to\na status shown above; the wording is now plain (offered for product\nreview in the PR). After a withdrawal (success or A1 conflict) and after\nan offer response, focus moves to the outcome box next to the actions\ninstead of dropping to body; the withdrawal confirmation takes focus on\nopen and returns it on cancel. Focus requests respect the view epoch.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#992 (slice 992-C).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"efafeb3ecdaede5b812d7f7f7046df4c54544f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/efafeb3ecdaede5b812d7f7f7046df4c54544f0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/e7640339295ecce6cf0d1fb0260ca34dbbdec57e","verification":{"payload":"tree efafeb3ecdaede5b812d7f7f7046df4c54544f0c\nparent f6169a3569e010f6f637dcf3331f0ef44e09e6d7\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1790150465 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790150465 +0300\n\nfix(ats): plain candidate copy and focus after candidate actions (#992 C) (#1187)\n\n* test(ats): candidate actions need plain language and must keep focus\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#992 (slice 992-C). Tests only: candidate copy\nstill says \"terminal\" and points \"below\" to a status shown above; after\na withdrawal (success or A1 conflict) and after an offer response the\npressed control leaves the DOM and focus drops to body; the withdrawal\nconfirmation neither takes nor returns focus.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): plain candidate copy and focus after candidate actions\n\nCandidate copy used the technical word \"terminal\" and pointed \"below\" to\na status shown above; the wording is now plain (offered for product\nreview in the PR). After a withdrawal (success or A1 conflict) and after\nan offer response, focus moves to the outcome box next to the actions\ninstead of dropping to body; the withdrawal confirmation takes focus on\nopen and returns it on cancel. Focus requests respect the view epoch.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#992 (slice 992-C).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs4dBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk8IQAILtfBuGDjOhaj/k/J+Efulc\ne6SwWercudEwItl2WPMHM9Fpc+4HSdDiI3qiLj3GrVKFfsr4Qt+HvV19+Fdli+yZ\nRo+kU38UfoLt05PQvfO56lnBaI8hdzw0hkp61XdU3FbQZCtGfPGMT69RyLnusyfK\nFylFybisYGgVJaLQCrn4v