:"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/cc6ed8746962e0fd112990863bc6a99a9ca95aee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244165292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zeynep-serban","id":244165292,"login":"zeynep-serban","node_id":"U_kgDODo2qrA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeynep-serban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/8265db52089f979cd4e598c4428f95fb29b059e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:48:56Z","email":"zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr","name":"zeynep-serban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:48:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ats): candidate portal keeps several applications in one tab (#965 B) (#1180)\n\n* test(ats): candidate portal must survive an unknown application status\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-A). Test only: fails until the\nportal stops reading STATUS_COPY[x].label without a fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): show a neutral status instead of crashing on an unknown value\n\nThe candidate portal read STATUS_COPY[x].label unguarded in four places;\na status the web bundle does not know yet crashed the whole portal.\nUnknown status/nextAction now render neutral candidate copy; the raw\nserver code is never shown.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-A).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ats): candidate portal keeps several applications in one tab\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-B). Tests only: fail until the\ntab keeps a versioned list of application credentials instead of\noverwriting the single latest.v1 record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ats): keep several candidate applications in one tab\n\nThe tab stored a single latest.v1 credential, so a second application\noverwrote the first and the candidate could not return to it. Credentials\nnow live in a versioned sessionStorage list (ats.candidate.sessions.v2):\nlatest.v1 migrates without loss (removed only after v2 is written), the\nportal lists the applications of the tab with open/remove actions, and\nswitching resets per-application state so a confirmation never carries\nover. A late response for the application the candidate left is ignored.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-B).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ats): pending mutations must not leak into another application view\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 / #1180 review (P1). Tests only: a\nwithdrawal or offer response started on B that resolves or rejects after\nswitching to A currently replaces A''s view with B.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): isolate pending mutations when switching applications (#1182)\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Guard withdrawal and offer continuations with an application-view epoch; cover stale success, failure and busy-state completion.\n\n* fix(ats): retain the originating withdrawal summary (#1181) (#1183)\n\n* fix(ats): isolate pending mutations when switching applications\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Guard withdrawal and offer continuations with an application-view epoch; cover stale success, failure and busy-state completion.\n\n* fix(ats): refresh only the originating withdrawal summary\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Preserve concurrent author regressions and do not update removed or replaced credentials.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c2c3557d763e44c2824234c5a8a203f3ccb0fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/0c2c3557d763e44c2824234c5a8a203f3ccb0fb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/8265db52089f979cd4e598c4428f95fb29b059e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c2c3557d763e44c2824234c5a8a203f3ccb0fb5\nparent 21da64d878c5e259ace5dc8c5c13cb558e55efb0\nauthor zeynep-serban <zeynep.akkilic@serban.com.tr> 1789454936 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789454936 +0300\n\nfeat(ats): candidate portal keeps several applications in one tab (#965 B) (#1180)\n\n* test(ats): candidate portal must survive an unknown application status\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-A). Test only: fails until the\nportal stops reading STATUS_COPY[x].label without a fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): show a neutral status instead of crashing on an unknown value\n\nThe candidate portal read STATUS_COPY[x].label unguarded in four places;\na status the web bundle does not know yet crashed the whole portal.\nUnknown status/nextAction now render neutral candidate copy; the raw\nserver code is never shown.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-A).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ats): candidate portal keeps several applications in one tab\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-B). Tests only: fail until the\ntab keeps a versioned list of application credentials instead of\noverwriting the single latest.v1 record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ats): keep several candidate applications in one tab\n\nThe tab stored a single latest.v1 credential, so a second application\noverwrote the first and the candidate could not return to it. Credentials\nnow live in a versioned sessionStorage list (ats.candidate.sessions.v2):\nlatest.v1 migrates without loss (removed only after v2 is written), the\nportal lists the applications of the tab with open/remove actions, and\nswitching resets per-application state so a confirmation never carries\nover. A late response for the application the candidate left is ignored.\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 (slice 965-B).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ats): pending mutations must not leak into another application view\n\nRefs Halildeu/platform-web#965 / #1180 review (P1). Tests only: a\nwithdrawal or offer response started on B that resolves or rejects after\nswitching to A currently replaces A''s view with B.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ats): isolate pending mutations when switching applications (#1182)\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Guard withdrawal and offer continuations with an application-view epoch; cover stale success, failure and busy-state completion.\n\n* fix(ats): retain the originating withdrawal summary (#1181) (#1183)\n\n* fix(ats): isolate pending mutations when switching applications\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Guard withdrawal and offer continuations with an application-view epoch; cover stale success, failure and busy-state completion.\n\n* fix(ats): refresh only the originating withdrawal summary\n\nTracked by #1181 and #965. Preserve concurrent author regressions and do not update removed or replaced credentials.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeynep Nisa Akkılıç <zeynep.akkilic@acik.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqOpYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyBgQAFn2Suv2tKgFwIuu83lYNRnQ\nZs/pK1M3uB3yCMnNGxSpRDUu76lQB+ZBMJw8jDIqtiH/l5JJWZZQlbBlbHMLibTq\nrl0Z3ZLPDcX875ddHPKTV92DT5UB8QA5I/q4LiVp98okLH52a5FYrt7Fuzhe7yZM\ngUeh+sr/tQZzyVIxRFIiRWiG6WvrQbwUCuPM5CkHDDHm7Bqsh9CpX7NMQ7K7vFGu\nJrQ1ms6CQJElYK4Wgp8+ByClbrVCyTU28MGETGj61lXYn+WkKD7zhwrLd6x2qQ16\nr+D+sSiDnv+YyXkAFhJpV7RRc2b+l/LRZjwVEfiblx0+fxicS1pcyZKuihaMHiQw\n1fqTmRdBYH2QXsiKPtoMXvBGd+rkYR72HNWmc6V9kNotjKIxUPBuNb9bVXfa9vFA\npYXTooIsx9/d5TMslbnyVxidPtFDTngTl+iVgsqQYocTMLtXDcdJCpvKxjBScBF6\n9S/2cOBzSfQfuTfCCNc9UOSGuRl9dMQd8vdkj1dnQq/jrT6XT6K7jPXyz61Ur1Aa\nwYmcUEVQdvLYyXS4X5AzUzcS3Yxr+DEK45UqCb8GNuei1du5pLRr9q30afM2vLuE\n92XeDZ7JugJjbqmU+YXyG5mhMCq5OW+RCgjrVDIzoy2A+p2aGfnJwAtYRuYUHiU6\nFDc9gPlyYpIe15NylBs4\n=B9HR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T06:48:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/8265db52089f979cd4e598c4428f95fb29b059e3","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDgyNjVkYjUyMDg5Z