ations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/47ebe5bc2ba49dd08317adb7df3b5b6b0a48325a","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDQ3ZWJlNWJjMmJhNDlkZDA4MzE3YWRiN2RmM2I1YjZiMGE0ODMyNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35","sha":"14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35"}],"sha":"47ebe5bc2ba49dd08317adb7df3b5b6b0a48325a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/47ebe5bc2ba49dd08317adb7df3b5b6b0a48325a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:08:23Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:08:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mfe-schema-explorer): ER graph separation by construction — deterministic start + overlap resolution (gitops#3650) (#1163)\n\n* fix(mfe-schema-explorer): ER graph separation by construction — deterministic start and post-layout overlap resolution (gitops#3650)\n\nThe acceptance run on the merged build (sha-5c327d9) reported 1 overlapping\ntable box on one run and 0 on the next: fcose starts from random positions and\ndoes not guarantee separation, so the number the harness asserts (0) held by\nluck. Now the neighbourhood starts from deterministic positions (centre at the\norigin, the rest on a ring in id order; domain maps on a grid), fcose runs with\nrandomize:false, and once it stops any boxes that still intersect are pushed\napart along the axis of least penetration (the pinned centre never moves)\nbefore the view is fitted. data-overlaps is therefore 0 by construction.\n\nTests: initial positions deterministic and ring-shaped; resolveOverlaps clears\na crafted overlapping set without moving the pinned node, is a no-op on a\nseparated layout, separates twelve stacked boxes and is deterministic.\n\n* fix(mfe-schema-explorer): finite placement fallback after the push-apart pass; domain map keeps randomizing (Codex 01a08f35 REVISE)\n\n- resolveOverlaps pass 2: if the iterative push-apart leaves intersections\n  (30 identical boxes left 9 pairs within its budget), boxes are placed one by\n  one, ordered by distance from the pinned centre then id, each walked outward\n  along its own ray until it clears everything placed before it — finite by\n  construction, pinned node untouched. Regression tests: 30 and 60 identical\n  boxes, the 60-box diagonal stack, determinism across calls.\n- fcose 2.2 with quality ''draft'' and randomize:false throws (no spectral\n  start, no CoSE phase) and the domain map silently fell back to the grid; the\n  domain map keeps randomize:true as before, only the neighbourhood starts\n  deterministically. graphLayout.fcose.test.ts runs both option sets on the\n  installed fcose (compound domain graph; pinned centre stays at the origin).\n\n* test(mfe-schema-explorer): drop unused eslint-disable directives in the fcose test","tree":{"sha":"0bdea948c8b439eea78fb903eec8b31f9b24dec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/0bdea948c8b439eea78fb903eec8b31f9b24dec2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bdea948c8b439eea78fb903eec8b31f9b24dec2\nparent 747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1789110503 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789110503 +0300\n\nfix(mfe-schema-explorer): ER graph separation by construction — deterministic start + overlap resolution (gitops#3650) (#1163)\n\n* fix(mfe-schema-explorer): ER graph separation by construction — deterministic start and post-layout overlap resolution (gitops#3650)\n\nThe acceptance run on the merged build (sha-5c327d9) reported 1 overlapping\ntable box on one run and 0 on the next: fcose starts from random positions and\ndoes not guarantee separation, so the number the harness asserts (0) held by\nluck. Now the neighbourhood starts from deterministic positions (centre at the\norigin, the rest on a ring in id order; domain maps on a grid), fcose runs with\nrandomize:false, and once it stops any boxes that still intersect are pushed\napart along the axis of least penetration (the pinned centre never moves)\nbefore the view is fitted. data-overlaps is therefore 0 by construction.\n\nTests: initial positions deterministic and ring-shaped; resolveOverlaps clears\na crafted overlapping set without moving the pinned node, is a no-op on a\nseparated layout, separates twelve stacked boxes and is deterministic.\n\n* fix(mfe-schema-explorer): finite placement fallback after the push-apart pass; domain map keeps randomizing (Codex 01a08f35 REVISE)\n\n- resolveOverlaps pass 2: if the iterative push-apart leaves intersections\n  (30 identical boxes left 9 pairs within its budget), boxes are placed one by\n  one, ordered by distance from the pinned centre then id, each walked outward\n  along its own ray until it clears everything placed before it — finite by\n  construction, pinned node untouched. Regression tests: 30 and 60 identical\n  boxes, the 60-box diagonal stack, determinism across calls.\n- fcose 2.2 with quality ''draft'' and randomize:false throws (no spectral\n  start, no CoSE phase) and the domain map silently fell back to the grid; the\n  domain map keeps randomize:true as before, only the neighbourhood starts\n  deterministically. graphLayout.fcose.test.ts runs both option sets on the\n  installed fcose (compound domain graph; pinned centre stays at the origin).\n\n* test(mfe-schema-explorer): drop unused eslint-disable directives in the fcose test","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo6jnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASfEQAEphZlxkBQn//444F+fD6uJI\nhDN+X7M378h6EM2l2I10RDn1LkY4TzY77x58SOg5FvQJWhBo0AZkXKoaOTGqDg+r\n1Lfm76f0vfx0zKB05y6Nh5I252TxEFd2/oPjUutl2So13nXZ8WNxn1BvXTdgeBuf\nyra/wg6skrYb8Zq2BBBHxaMsr0ulf9TXZUUCZSo/s/Ag5j7teNw9R89PI4+2ULLM\nW0zoGIgPSqzQNSnx45YIi2hfUZGuApBxjAJzFGM61WGMnV0uvinJ22eEyublFOxZ\nn2wdjQkkWgbv7bCkdM7ENZlfCJ5Oi2a47dd0EKH+Nm/Z8J5hf3H0A2qbxBA+dH3Z\nOxpYn9OcvhsNtqb9iruFI+nprbjFPbsi+DrpzU/5NImwWtRug+OxBi2dT24J1H8p\nxAdsQ3Uby+is/fQfmpZNEGbOHdxRyMd2gujWgG9vR2vVkQp/cTXSgki9MAgQNDo0\nYW6fh5CByA4MxnVmhySAXxNB6ttJg01AIou9+6ccD7KlnwjK45ZblMD8G8siYX4m\ncoXPgA38DxkXj8daEluljkqjHP9dZS+Rk8PpEFo8BE2583uV1WVA7yhIyyryNZdi\nl7pvSV7fvcNjEFeJQmuqsudNfbUw+OgkPcfjkLykmPPi1BnwLAoxXRo8ZLDokjrw\nnZlObHmnzfoT6tYQuelm\n=uM0R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T07:08:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDE0YTNlMGUwYzI1ZGZmM2EwZTQ3NTZjN2RlNDljMGFkYTZlMGZhMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c","sha":"747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c"}],"sha":"14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/14a3e0e0c25dff3a0e4756c7de49c0ada6e0fa35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:06:33Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:06:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(etik-speak-manager): grid-variants calls carry the session token; AG Grid licence key reaches the manager bundle (#1155) (#1162)\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): grid-variants calls carry the session token; AG Grid licence key reaches the manager bundle (#1155)\n\nMeasured on testai 2026-09-11 (manager browser smoke with response headers):\nevery GET /api/v1/variants left the manager WITHOUT an Authorization header\n(hasAuthorization=false, no WWW-Authenticate) — not an audience problem.\nstandalone-http''s resolveAuthToken() invoked the async token provider and\nreturned null on its Promise (typeof !== ''string''), and the design-system\ngrid-variants client reads that resolver synchronously right before its\nfetch. auth.ts now registers a synchronous token snapshot next to the async\nprovider; scope, audience, PKCE, check-sso and the upgrade path are\nuntouched (behavioural tests unchanged), the auth contract anchor moves to\nthe new digest with the review recorded in ADR-0046.\n\nThe manager bundle never received VITE_AG_GRID_LICENSE_KEY (no build-arg,\nno Vite define), so every grid printed the Enterprise licence banner. Same\nsingle-source lane as the platform frontend: GitHub secret -> build-arg ->\nVite define(''process.env'') -> design-system ag-grid-license. The key is\npublic by design (client bundle).\n\nTests: standalone-http.test.ts (3, new), manager suite 22/22; tsc + eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): licence key via window.__env__ shim, release build-arg, keep HTTP boundary tests (Codex 01a08f1f REVISE)\n\n- The design-system licence reader guards its process.env branch with\n  typeof process !== ''undefined''; a Vite define of process.env never satisfies\n  that in a browser (Codex reproduced setupAgGridLicense() === false). The key\n  now reaches the page the way the platform shell does: an index.html\n  window.__env__ shim filled by an inject-runtime-env plugin, with an explicit\n  allowlist (VITE_AG_GRID_LICENSE_KEY only). Verified on a production build with\n  synthetic values: the key is in dist/index.html, an unrelated VITE_* sentinel\n  is nowhere in dist.\n- The release workflow builds its own candidate; it now passes the build-arg\n  and refuses to publish when the secret is empty (value never printed).\n- The ten pre-existing HTTP boundary tests were overwritten in the previous\n  commit; restored, with the three snapshot tests appended. The Keycloak\n  lifecycle test pins the snapshot end to end: null before ready, the live\n  token after ready, refreshed token visible at once, null on contract loss\n  and after invalidation while the Keycloak object still holds a token.\n- runtime-env.test.ts executes the injected shim in a process-less scope.\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): deliver the runtime env as a same-origin hashed asset — CSP script-src ''self'' forbids the inline shim (Codex 01a08f1f iter-2)\n\nThe manager serves script-src ''self''; an inline window.__env__ script never\nruns there. The inject-runtime-env plugin now emits assets/runtime-env-<hash>.js\n(content-hashed, so the immutable cache policy for /ethic/assets/ holds) and\nprepends <script src> to <head>, ahead of the deferred module entry; the dev\nserver serves the same path from memory. The candidate browser smoke asserts\nwindow.__env__ exists (asset ran under the CSP) and, when the build carried the\nsecret, that the licence key is in it; both workflows set that expectation\n(release: always; PR: only when the secret is available).\n\n* test(etik-speak-manager): record runtime-env evidence from the manager document before check-sso navigates away (Codex 01a08f1f iter-3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb53721535c6f5847b5b4d46adecbac39b62ae37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/bb53721535c6f5847b5b4d46adecbac39b62ae37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/747666b94ed5a01328fa991aaa4b5c95d485617c","verification":{"payload":"tree bb53721535c6f5847b5b4d46adecbac39b62ae37\nparent 2ee2a8aea390da617df21fe23b2a6c2e3215872e\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1789110393 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789110393 +0300\n\nfix(etik-speak-manager): grid-variants calls carry the session token; AG Grid licence key reaches the manager bundle (#1155) (#1162)\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): grid-variants calls carry the session token; AG Grid licence key reaches the manager bundle (#1155)\n\nMeasured on testai 2026-09-11 (manager browser smoke with response headers):\nevery GET /api/v1/variants left the manager WITHOUT an Authorization header\n(hasAuthorization=false, no WWW-Authenticate) — not an audience problem.\nstandalone-http''s resolveAuthToken() invoked the async token provider and\nreturned null on its Promise (typeof !== ''string''), and the design-system\ngrid-variants client reads that resolver synchronously right before its\nfetch. auth.ts now registers a synchronous token snapshot next to the async\nprovider; scope, audience, PKCE, check-sso and the upgrade path are\nuntouched (behavioural tests unchanged), the auth contract anchor moves to\nthe new digest with the review recorded in ADR-0046.\n\nThe manager bundle never received VITE_AG_GRID_LICENSE_KEY (no build-arg,\nno Vite define), so every grid printed the Enterprise licence banner. Same\nsingle-source lane as the platform frontend: GitHub secret -> build-arg ->\nVite define(''process.env'') -> design-system ag-grid-license. The key is\npublic by design (client bundle).\n\nTests: standalone-http.test.ts (3, new), manager suite 22/22; tsc + eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): licence key via window.__env__ shim, release build-arg, keep HTTP boundary tests (Codex 01a08f1f REVISE)\n\n- The design-system licence reader guards its process.env branch with\n  typeof process !== ''undefined''; a Vite define of process.env never satisfies\n  that in a browser (Codex reproduced setupAgGridLicense() === false). The key\n  now reaches the page the way the platform shell does: an index.html\n  window.__env__ shim filled by an inject-runtime-env plugin, with an explicit\n  allowlist (VITE_AG_GRID_LICENSE_KEY only). Verified on a production build with\n  synthetic values: the key is in dist/index.html, an unrelated VITE_* sentinel\n  is nowhere in dist.\n- The release workflow builds its own candidate; it now passes the build-arg\n  and refuses to publish when the secret is empty (value never printed).\n- The ten pre-existing HTTP boundary tests were overwritten in the previous\n  commit; restored, with the three snapshot tests appended. The Keycloak\n  lifecycle test pins the snapshot end to end: null before ready, the live\n  token after ready, refreshed token visible at once, null on contract loss\n  and after invalidation while the Keycloak object still holds a token.\n- runtime-env.test.ts executes the injected shim in a process-less scope.\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): deliver the runtime env as a same-origin hashed asset — CSP script-src ''self'' forbids the inline shim (Codex 01a08f1f iter-2)\n\nThe manager serves script-src ''self''; an inline window.__env__ script never\nruns there. The inject-runtime-env plugin now emits assets/runtime-env-<hash>.js\n(content-hashed, so the immutable cache policy for /ethic/assets/ holds) and\nprepends <script src> to <head>, ahead of the deferred module entry; the dev\nserver serves the same path from memory. The candidate browser smoke asserts\nwindow.__env__ exists (asset ran under the CSP) and, when the build carried the\nsecret, that the licence key is in it; both workflows set that expectation\n(release: always; PR: only when the secret is available).\n\n* test(etik-speak-manager): record runtime-env evidence from the manager document before check-sso navigates away (Codex 01a08f1f iter-3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo6h5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAce0QAKJ/4QTcY1lP/5CNoOA9hFh1\nuCzmFV6y86pyuL0JlF1Mvi42eWGAGuypwsSU2K2Of09h8AQbtvpHH3mtvyPd1cYl\nZIGfwgeHjyeeHSq1nCRDN8XNQUJv1tX1LH4vuakRE3vdSPbHKKd98IhSEqG6Wzk0\nqHxPjjlQdwz/IupkzRpEckj3dJvhEut1W26pUhYksFAqcLZ1KKxRUfbXdz025AbL\nZV7b2j0xUwLbBLnFhv28jSTtJGR/4oHT02AlDgIUJdxPGTypsUvYglJdG31iDRDp\n1pPLZSGebeAvmNsAQankLsF7LczVIChnu735dQOiEeo3Gu2PUxznOrw64Bq97Wro\nuRFTTFZJHVZO9QkohgGiU1ahYcoqb7io/pP/qvy2ANxBXPiSu5L2oYBA6JlyXGz/\nGEB8/lx0MF96OwK7xVt7Xz9Fwf9pacNzjmuVyg1TiNWk1MC4dX8M2jTZlYxdSsUD\n3wgDkNj1ZZThqGi6XJV5zGDAUGNRnmUPpRAedjcyjYPgA9eErfigBX4hfYj/zN91\nP1eqneJoCxnrvqh8lHB8pq6TRsKGKHoS/Ro5PnU8cJfE10f/yQA1ICrSHGwgtPlO\n2qSKWauokjqtZPTWz5JkYytV+Fs6IRilYVK5fUQVWKSAqckqv+6rHGpJaEyFmU4X\n8wP46rTeSQRFuldhbEH3\n=8Fty\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T07:06:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubu