plorer): keep the header and source picker usable while the snapshot loads (gitops#3605)\n\nThe whole page was a spinner until the default (Workcube) snapshot\narrived. On a fresh schema-service pod that build takes ~100 s\n(measured: \"Snapshot built in 106208ms\"), so an IFS user could not even\nreach the source picker, and the browser acceptance lane timed out at\n60 s waiting for it (run 34409951838).\n\nThe header (source + schema pickers, nav) now renders immediately; only\nthe snapshot-backed parts — stats, sidebar, main panel, table detail —\nshow the loading / error state. Two tests: picker present and usable\nwhile getSnapshot never resolves; error rendered inside the layout with\nthe picker still there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(schema-explorer): drop a stale schema-list reply after switching source; pin mid-load behaviour (Codex 01a0884d)\n\nWith the header usable before any snapshot, a slow reply for the\nprevious source could land after the user switched to IFS and offer a\nWorkcube schema under source=ifs. The list is cleared on change and a\nstale reply is ignored. Tests: reversed completion order, IFS result\nshown while the primary snapshot is still pending, panel switching\nwhile loading, error rendered inside main with recovery by switching\nsource (13/13).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <gladyatore@hotmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a1bb049b7244098ed740ac141775b4672265343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/2a1bb049b7244098ed740ac141775b4672265343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/f043d67711b9d3c7a4682adc42913abd35d2f460","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a1bb049b7244098ed740ac141775b4672265343\nparent 823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1788994353 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788994353 +0300\n\nfix(schema-explorer): keep the header and source picker usable while the snapshot loads (gitops#3605) (#1151)\n\n* fix(schema-explorer): keep the header and source picker usable while the snapshot loads (gitops#3605)\n\nThe whole page was a spinner until the default (Workcube) snapshot\narrived. On a fresh schema-service pod that build takes ~100 s\n(measured: \"Snapshot built in 106208ms\"), so an IFS user could not even\nreach the source picker, and the browser acceptance lane timed out at\n60 s waiting for it (run 34409951838).\n\nThe header (source + schema pickers, nav) now renders immediately; only\nthe snapshot-backed parts — stats, sidebar, main panel, table detail —\nshow the loading / error state. Two tests: picker present and usable\nwhile getSnapshot never resolves; error rendered inside the layout with\nthe picker still there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(schema-explorer): drop a stale schema-list reply after switching source; pin mid-load behaviour (Codex 01a0884d)\n\nWith the header usable before any snapshot, a slow reply for the\nprevious source could land after the user switched to IFS and offer a\nWorkcube schema under source=ifs. The list is cleared on change and a\nstale reply is ignored. Tests: reversed completion order, IFS result\nshown while the primary snapshot is still pending, panel switching\nwhile loading, error rendered inside main with recovery by switching\nsource (13/13).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <gladyatore@hotmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoeMxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVAIQAF4ozuUMAdFX51Od9KsdOSq6\nrBhJTELlYR1o+ns3BdpHlzZpH7V7EUuPWWnG+dpl7nDKuvqB2uk3wJ+ZBH3V6YtR\nZF8PaPLYu02hp4gQLxpMKqdHr5bKpa45XqFOjzjBAkXhivRVyQ37R8ZNtLEVQx8Q\n9xBQb3aP2shJ2lEMaGoW1IyO8uinNHt7nuKDRC2zGWtNSTmoGlS59l9