43d67711b9d3c7a4682adc42913abd35d2f460","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f043d67711b9d3c7a4682adc42913abd35d2f460"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:19:25Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:19:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): gate the Schema Explorer on REPORT, not THEME (#3605) (#1150)\n\n* fix(shell): gate the Schema Explorer on REPORT, not THEME\n\nThe Explorer browses catalog metadata of the reporting sources — table/view\nnames, columns, discovered relationships — and no row data. Its route has\nrequired the THEME module since the 2026-04-08 bulk module migration (#213);\nnothing in that commit motivates THEME (theme/design-lab management) for it,\nand the live permission data shows the practical effect: ADMIN is the only role\ncarrying THEME, so only admins could open the Explorer while an analyst with\nREPORT:MANAGE could not.\n\nREPORT is the module whose users already see the data these catalogs\ndescribe. Proxy decision (Codex thread 01a087c0): A now — gate on REPORT — with\na dedicated SCHEMA module tracked as the long-term model, and a P1 that the\nschema API itself must enforce the same boundary (tracked separately).\n\nTracked by Halildeu/platform-k8s-gitops#3605\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): move the Explorer''s nav and search entries to REPORT with the route\n\nThe route guard alone is not enough: header-navigation.config and\nheader-search.config carried module: THEME / permission: THEME for the same\nentry, so a REPORT user could reach /admin/schema-explorer by URL but never see\nit in the menu or the command palette. The header-search test that pinned THEME\nnow pins REPORT and says why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"374c382781eabdaada05bef6e7bce7b4addcf0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/374c382781eabdaada05bef6e7bce7b4addcf0e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909","verification":{"payload":"tree 374c382781eabdaada05bef6e7bce7b4addcf0e4\nparent b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1788985165 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788985165 +0300\n\nfix(shell): gate the Schema Explorer on REPORT, not THEME (#3605) (#1150)\n\n* fix(shell): gate the Schema Explorer on REPORT, not THEME\n\nThe Explorer browses catalog metadata of the reporting sources — table/view\nnames, columns, discovered relationships — and no row data. Its route has\nrequired the THEME module since the 2026-04-08 bulk module migration (#213);\nnothing in that commit motivates THEME (theme/design-lab management) for it,\nand the live permission data shows the practical effect: ADMIN is the only role\ncarrying THEME, so only admins could open the Explorer while an analyst with\nREPORT:MANAGE could not.\n\nREPORT is the module whose users already see the data these catalogs\ndescribe. Proxy decision (Codex thread 01a087c0): A now — gate on REPORT — with\na dedicated SCHEMA module tracked as the long-term model, and a P1 that the\nschema API itself must enforce the same boundary (tracked separately).\n\nTracked by Halildeu/platform-k8s-gitops#3605\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): move the Explorer''s nav and search entries to REPORT with the route\n\nThe route guard alone is not enough: header-navigation.config and\nheader-search.config carried module: THEME / permission: THEME for the same\nentry, so a REPORT user could reach /admin/schema-explorer by URL but never see\nit in the menu or the command palette. The header-search test that pinned THEME\nnow pins REPORT and says why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqob9NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPAwQAEcWppYxeR9XgDWXvhkzQ1/N\nUhrUvqYQpfp5g9lqThiFvd863z29a/WOYQv2a63NNIRZB1xTEH9n3WJMbI5NTrCW\n9lzBrGZp3bBngxROhMWUibS2gfBm44bxfhT/XXb4sKucIeXOMFeWJ3FWZmiKMe06\n51JoJDxD5l6roM6MfY69pQ0OLiqjE+SUWTTUZCD9sqC+f1tymE64/IEHXumr8woA\nlvzaCV44HOZ3tyYlDbd2Wqf5N3wariNWjhcWxb8EWZYHd6Bc794UegV8s+jLI0ib\nD9WQbdqh/B6ZoV+KAsEYIMqeo5LvjiAoZtIn1Rdj190P+5BjGBE1PIDIuqgbZb0C\nZvWPl5kBXBJwW14n2wcQ1CDYap+dkan7r/lkBsG0qccWQkTnXBTKeDLEGeDH8gLV\nSHaP+njY0dAyqd6IM1IJ9qv8JB82T79ks4iQT1Yjf2cPYYCrehVud/lP7j0evhrD\njPhg7VTEmMsNghzcby/qZFx24cDtTCpiq1ns8zpRrqF5Sd6Q5MylpY9CXW4Sjoip\nWN5thGd0pZBYWyX4qKgDp0sYXQAc/7xAQOaHWuyiLakynprpzE3MlFEntUQf9xtu\nH9RJ92sTc2RWAMvdAwMEw4RK2KtqjYseZphmTDBh4YoAhW0dZ5jSG8zH0b7A90UL\nvW6PWFvapqNs9P97W+wb\n=isJe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T20:19:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDgyMzI1MGI3OTU0YmZkNDZkYzIzMGMwNjk5NmJlMDY3ZTIyM2I5MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50","sha":"b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50"}],"sha":"823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/823250b7954bfd46dc230c06996be067e223b909"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:03:15Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:03:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema-explorer): source picker — browse the IFS ERP Oracle catalog beside Workcube (#1149)\n\nschema-service exposes more than one catalog since gitops#3594 (Workcube MSSQL\nand IFS ERP Oracle), but the Explorer only ever called /schemas and /snapshot\nwith no source, so the second catalog was reachable through the API and\ninvisible in the product.\n\nThe API layer now carries a scope — which source, which schema inside it — on\nevery call, and the header gains a source picker fed by /sources. Choosing a\nsource reloads the schema list from it and resets the schema, so the service\nresolves that source''s own default owner (IFSAPP for IFS) rather than carrying\na Workcube schema name across. The panels that used raw fetch() (health, drift,\nfind-path) go through scopedUrl(); column search and impact pass the scope to\ntheir hooks. An absent source is the primary lane, so a single-source\ndeployment renders exactly as before.\n\nThis app had no tests at all. vitest is wired up (jsdom + Testing Library,\nmirroring mfe-reporting), the root test chain and ci-web-check gain the run,\nand 7 tests pin the contract: source/schema on every call, scopedUrl keeping\nexisting query parameters, picker start state, switching to ifs reloading\nschemas and snapshot, picker hidden with no sources.\n\nServer side: platform-backend#1143 makes every snapshot-backed endpoint honour\nsource.\n\nTracked by Halildeu/platform-k8s-gitops#3605\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"94f8cb38bbb7b397a9632d48a4c2ed8a1738fe8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/94f8cb38bbb7b397a9632d48a4c2ed8a1738fe8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/b506f6411239203d403de86a5d1cdd6e45e10c50","verification":{"payload":"tree 94f8cb38bbb7b397a9632d48a4c2ed8a1738fe8e\nparent dce494d30051932cddcef7b1f99b97993adb61f8\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1788984195 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788984195 +0300\n\nfeat(schema-explorer): source picker — browse the IFS ERP Oracle catalog beside Workcube (#1149)\n\nschema-service exposes more than one catalog since gitops#3594 (Workcube MSSQL\nand IFS ERP Oracle), but the Explorer only ever called /schemas and /snapshot\nwith no source, so the second catalog was reachable through the API and\ninvisible in the product.\n\nThe API layer now carries a scope — which source, which schema inside it — on\nevery call, and the header gains a source picker fed by /sources. Choosing a\nsource reloads the schema list from it and resets the schema, so the service\nresolves that source''s own default owner (IFSAPP for IFS) rather than carrying\na Workcube schema name across. The panels that used raw fetch() (health, drift,\nfind-path) go through scopedUrl(); column search and impact pass the scope to\ntheir hooks. An absent source is the primary lane, so a single-source\ndeployment renders exactly as before.\n\nThis app had no tests at all. vitest is wired up (jsdom + Testing Library,\nmirroring mfe-reporting), the root test chain and ci-web-check gain the run,\nand 7 tests pin the contract: source/schema on every call, scopedUrl keeping\nexisting query parameters, picker start state, switching to ifs reloading\nschemas and snapshot, picker hidden with no sources.\n\nServer side: platform-backend#1143 makes every snapshot-backed endpoint honour\nsource.\n\nTracked by Halildeu/platform-k8s-gitops#3605\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobuDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm4cQAIdm7B3z/StTKCyNiTmkGK+/\nvIgDb5UVCFYX0hPrF0FgMF9TCu6Y1Oc5fev8p3G9JBQfXmenL49HNGGOpdzoGPkE\nWYUMA3PQYhaAo3j+vMUJZ5QZD2NOWQqjl2J+nPxpr6O82xxrDXQ/84/VlCc6YOV6\ntxrqUSkSeAPrGH6yKCR0IcQRBeBObdGn9ovnZY0Kj0vWEcLKhPpZIDPaaj58bJxu\nvfFYrXnYRblTaNNZK4OrMgQr0IQ720XSeL/N/v3KUitYiz2+Z8Q3a3Js+gtekeKO\n9nZAFfKwnvOmHN03BrMHoaZLNBYfTNp4UDVs5qiiTsmIyltwh6t9xmdDl/F47mGM\nyRiIOzLvv21L9klFe+TxM9vgoKkBmyR+F2VKSrWLunHLFhkoHsa92/RWDX9x7YwP\nuruAK4z+21SIzNayh3rH0FDf8oUgrVoPkjGZuhsoRUG5FjS2yIwcM0RRgIJGjObw\nMkFXzqRL2l6rMw4hQevtf21aA8ntsQiRCFO8rEU/kV61n2JQOmMag4AvSnY2UKSG\nvUJtewYqIfVaLGJkuBipCDJL1GoWGUgVryA2WfYl94g9yK0KGi5JDHn1WHvfnOUA\nSOqrQVdt7a1rCJin+8F9pkuY20/b6jgU3kcNDEjckyW8wmrkY9Mm8xdRV6VzjjwA\nTQ/n36PDO7VZ5uCpGxzB\n=IxqJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T20:03:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repo