om/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/0b9ac21fc53916fc42ac1139aa8c1b4b60819772/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:12:30Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:12:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(budget-workspace): Workcube plan import surface — trigger, draft view, submit (#3479) (#1126)\n\nBudget Workspace gains a plan-import section: the planner picks the fiscal\nyear (scenario plans stay out unless explicitly opted in), triggers\nPOST /api/v1/budgets/import/workcube, sees the import result\n(fetched/imported/merged/skipped + readable skip reasons and provider\nfailure codes), reviews the resulting versioned draft (annual-bucket\nperiods, line table, period net totals) and submits it for approval.\nErrors fail closed with the module''s BudgetApiError mapping; nothing is\nwritten to the ERP.\n\nBackend contract: gitops#3454 lane (budget-service import + BudgetController\nread/submit, all X-Company-Id scoped). 28/28 module tests, tsc clean for the\nnew files, eslint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"438028e951f9037ba2b7e8c02cc414df0a64bb7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/438028e951f9037ba2b7e8c02cc414df0a64bb7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/0b9ac21fc53916fc42ac1139aa8c1b4b60819772","verification":{"payload":"tree 438028e951f9037ba2b7e8c02cc414df0a64bb7f\nparent 2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1787083950 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787083950 +0300\n\nfeat(budget-workspace): Workcube plan import surface — trigger, draft view, submit (#3479) (#1126)\n\nBudget Workspace gains a plan-import section: the planner picks the fiscal\nyear (scenario plans stay out unless explicitly opted in), triggers\nPOST /api/v1/budgets/import/workcube, sees the import result\n(fetched/imported/merged/skipped + readable skip reasons and provider\nfailure codes), reviews the resulting versioned draft (annual-bucket\nperiods, line table, period net totals) and submits it for approval.\nErrors fail closed with the module''s BudgetApiError mapping; nothing is\nwritten to the ERP.\n\nBackend contract: gitops#3454 lane (budget-service import + BudgetController\nread/submit, all X-Company-Id scoped). 28/28 module tests, tsc clean for the\nnew files, eslint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhLyuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwsEQAHI6toKM0x3dpGv/VVf27ZwI\nuQKj4DTU/9fpWsjNIpM0uvaGBOCYfb+h/uRnq7452rk3NygtyWERxJGxBCEhSfLc\nZQilAgX1xJjag0wb+9jWhHsIj2aOUJLEoCg2Im1peQw6r5iDpkIUGl6nU/3Zugz3\n4IHy+wwyBX93h1n6nufmYGSYEPGcJ356XV2daFDqRRHsVBhzmKbRYVC3OZmx85NZ\nMNxMH8IXmZ/mduivp3FNjE+G2LkOYrsy/xNuh9iuh7KIShfvab+Y8UtjcmzgnJlA\n+N3Sqg9wEvFQ4LmSurc9mmlYT6CrRRhofYlaGqYw77owcS46Qx5xYX2VkyPonaEB\nMWYV8dwc56gaMkDHyXIe20D+PGuto6QZD55KvoWYYc58bPA6JEtUlM8qwvuvh/Ri\nigMC+quUEok4EkTqlyV3aHKsjefrc3k8ak5GVzhXLVWX1P7H2psB9o46bdawus+3\nKQjmDmfANUZ68NwPOHLllaK/nJSbDYNMdxbcRxoI173KoJmobXKQpxp1ufLpmkHv\nY3RJ0A38vuu9SIvRi7Rh1ij4VNMyPR6pLrhzX0k7o0NtoDlwDd+5zeFA++/+JaEq\nzdBq7LxvBz1Qle2X8ch09IxB0xb2l8/KTCIkNDeBgO9Co5zKylq6yGuhQ7iA8MME\n68q5U5PnRoLFgUujVXeE\n=Mozy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T20:12:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/0b9ac21fc53916fc42ac1139aa8c1b4b60819772","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDBiOWFjMjFmYzUzOTE2ZmM0MmFjMTEzOWFhOGMxYjRiNjA4MTk3NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372","sha":"2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372"}],"sha":"0b9ac21fc53916fc42ac1139aa8c1b4b60819772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/0b9ac21fc53916fc42ac1139aa8c1b4b60819772"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T17:20:31Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T17:20:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): complete case workspace to ModuleHome level — next-work banner, freshness row, four list states (#1125)\n\nCloses the three gaps the cross-AI review (#1120, Codex REVISE) left open\nafter the workspace landed in #1122:\n\n1. Next-work banner. The queue already ordered the visible list by urgency\n   (sortForQueue), but the answer to \"what needs me next\" still had to be\n   read out of row one. The banner says it: first visible case, subject\n   clipped to ~60 chars, and the WHY in words. The reason is derived by\n   nextWorkReason() in case-grid.ts from the same cell derivations the grid\n   renders (ackSlaFor / feedbackSlaFor / ownerFor) — no second SLA\n   arithmetic exists to drift from the first. \"Aç\" routes through the\n   existing onSelect path; an empty visible list renders no banner.\n\n2. Metric freshness. KPI numbers and SLA cells are clock arithmetic, so the\n   moment they were computed is part of their meaning: \"Son güncelleme\n   HH:MM\" records the last successful list load (page state only), and\n   Yenile rides the screen''s one existing refresh() — passed down as a\n   prop, no new fetch path — disabled and reading \"Yükleniyor…\" (aria-busy)\n   while it runs.\n\n3. State surfaces, all four owned by CaseListWorkspace now instead of the\n   shell swapping the workspace for a paragraph: an initial-load skeleton\n   (refresh over existing data keeps the grid), unfiltered-empty vs\n   filtered-empty with different words — the filtered one carries its own\n   \"Filtreleri temizle\" undo — and a load-failure surface that replaces the\n   grid (a stale grid rendered as current would be a quiet lie) with\n   \"Tekrar dene\" on the same reload path. The list-header Yenile button\n   moved into the freshness row rather than duplicating it.\n\nGrid, columns and the variant system are untouched; ethics.css grew an\nappend-only block on the existing --ethics-* tokens. case-grid.ts stays\nreal in tests (only transport and grid chrome are mocked).\n\nTests: mfe-ethic 90 → 104 (banner picks by queue order not payload order,\nAç selects, empty hides it; freshness clock + busy Yenile; filtered-empty\nundo; error retry; nextWorkReason/truncateSubject units pinned to the same\nderivations the grid uses). etik-speak-manager stays 29 green; tsc clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b4455da988b079a477e0938d2c165dbb2fb8a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/5b4455da988b079a477e0938d2c165dbb2fb8a5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b4455da988b079a477e0938d2c165dbb2fb8a5e\nparent 938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1786814431 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786814431 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): complete case workspace to ModuleHome level — next-work banner, freshness row, four list states (#1125)\n\nCloses the three gaps the cross-AI review (#1120, Codex REVISE) left open\nafter the workspace landed in #1122:\n\n1. Next-work banner. The queue already ordered the visible list by urgency\n   (sortForQueue), but the answer to \"what needs me next\" still had to be\n   read out of row one. The banner says it: first visible case, subject\n   clipped to ~60 chars, and the WHY in words. The reason is derived by\n   nextWorkReason() in case-grid.ts from the same cell derivations the grid\n   renders (ackSlaFor / feedbackSlaFor / ownerFor) — no second SLA\n   arithmetic exists to drift from the first. \"Aç\" routes through the\n   existing onSelect path; an empty visible list renders no banner.\n\n2. Metric freshness. KPI numbers and SLA cells are clock arithmetic, so the\n   moment they were computed is part of their meaning: \"Son güncelleme\n   HH:MM\" records the last successful list load (page state only), and\n   Yenile rides the screen''s one existing refresh() — passed down as a\n   prop, no new fetch path — disabled and reading \"Yükleniyor…\" (aria-busy)\n   while it runs.\n\n3. State surfaces, all four owned by CaseListWorkspace now instead of the\n   shell swapping the workspace for a paragraph: an initial-load skeleton\n   (refresh over existing data keeps the grid), unfiltered-empty vs\n   filtered-empty with different words — the filtered one carries its own\n   \"Filtreleri temizle\" undo — and a load-failure surface that replaces the\n   grid (a stale grid rendered as current would be a quiet lie) with\n   \"Tekrar dene\" on the same reload path. The list-header Yenile button\n   moved into the freshness row rather than duplicating it.\n\nGrid, columns and the variant system are untouched; ethics.css grew an\nappend-only block on the existing --ethics-* tokens. case-grid.ts stays\nreal in tests (only transport and grid chrome are mocked).\n\nTests: mfe-ethic 90 → 104 (banner picks by queue order not payload order,\nAç selects, empty hides it; freshness clock + busy Yenile; filtered-empty\nundo; error retry; nextWorkReason/truncateSubject units pinned to the same\nderivations the grid uses). etik-speak-manager stays 29 green; tsc clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgJ/fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjd8QABJ3Tr8Qpf4f4FDHCaIxbHjJ\nx/K7lfeDRIr//kA19P0QtSs1oHYHbDzrWdsfgaox0J4lX0G0iGdMbGdkV+idLCg9\nZadjWCtrQjQ+KXly3i/E9rjzxQrRC4SPsBHoVkBFB8/DLl1ynCka5f6Soo6qKEaq\nWHfj/FXOO15SNNsp2WaDwOMe0HsX7e9jZH27XZimGMX6hstL24iaRjgYb2wlVjnG\nyollJcbM/jWxEAY0I34QdbFR0//H4283WUox4VFZ1KBsb7j5+eBOmjIryayt+xZ4\ndbB+cYm4KbirVUSQs40xVkRjo2RmAVq380OAbRDfKJHVt1JjzhXNV2X4Q8NjvjAm\n9zao5gZtQ/un832dkoi4l0lcXdWYGJ++D4wWOJrZvk47DIuAOP23upVmYX49EtPf\npv7Lg5uIqk/8n3io+CJlkg2IrCRm24/npLbz3I7LqDpXy0VIGjYIJ0dgVePCaGMD\nd8BuHsjpVhXO/V+1rGchZm11mCmi4HljSuZPzuOR60A73AnJVbMkG4DGYn4leNjf\nvXbM1VmKAI+LtOhIxcyZA4Ckh6LPiS8PVrUVPniBlniE+7XhV5Naq97l5hC0MmgR\nS+vGz9y3pArd6ZtPWUsXmIEH2YgOnYlduQR0YPP3YvjumtSnL7MBekkiprptkVCy\n5yuFI+ywUvcneKrSes19\n=fGLn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-15T17:20:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDJkOWU3N2I2YjI0OGQzMTJjMGI2ZDllZGU4MWMyZjk1MWI2NDMzNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20","sha":"938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20"}],"sha":"2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/2d9e77b6b248d312c0b6d9ede81c2f951b643372"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:25:52Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T07:25:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-meeting): Akıcı transkript görünümü — cümle-sınırlı akış + satır-içi canlı kuyruk (#1123)\n\n* feat(mfe-meeting): fluent transcript view — sentence-bounded flow with inline live tail\n\nMirrors platform-desktop#117 on the web surface (Tracked by\nplatform-k8s-gitops#3419). The transcript timeline rendered one\nmetadata-laden card per 2-5s STT commit, fragmenting sentences across\nrows. Industry reference UIs (see gitops\ndocs/faz24-realtime-stt-industry-survey.md §7) flow committed text into\none paragraph until a sentence terminator is certain and keep the\nmutable partial tail updating in place at the end of the flow.\n\n- transcript-flow.ts: pure grouping — group per speaker, paragraph\n  closes ONLY on sentence-final punctuation (never on elapsed time),\n  trailing draft/stabilizing segments of the last group become the live\n  tail; mid-stream drafts stay in the flow so REST-fallback content is\n  never lost.\n- TranscriptTimeline: ''Akıcı | Satırlar'' toggle, fluent default; the\n  row view is unchanged. Citation deep links (#segment-{id}) keep\n  working — every segment renders inside its own span anchor in the\n  flow.\n- 8 new unit tests; mfe-meeting suite 55/55, eslint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe-meeting): load every session''s transcript in the meeting detail (gitops#3421)\n\nThe canonical intelligence result binds ONE session — the latest analysis\nrun''s. When a socket-close mid-meeting spawns a short tail session, the\nlatest run belongs to that tail, so the main session''s transcript (the\nuser''s actual meeting) never rendered — perceived as ''my recording did\nnot reach the web''. Evidence 2026-08-03: meeting e4163355, 27-min main\nsession (136 segments) invisible behind a 5-min tail session result.\n\nloadMeetingDetail now lists the meeting''s sessions and loads every\nsession''s transcript pages for DISPLAY, while citation resolution stays\non the analysis session''s segments (source_index contract unbroken —\nmerged display cannot shift citation indices). Session-list failure\ndegrades to the previous single-session behavior.\n\nTests: multi-session merge + citation stability + sessions-unavailable\nfallback; suite 90/90, eslint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0af7ad6b03ff518d46a7411b47fcc3e6fae88c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/0af7ad6b03ff518d46a7411b47fcc3e6fae88c63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20","verification":{"payload":"tree 0af7ad6b03ff518d46a7411b47fcc3e6fae88c63\nparent 0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785741952 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785741952 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-meeting): Akıcı transkript görünümü — cümle-sınırlı akış + satır-içi canlı kuyruk (#1123)\n\n* feat(mfe-meeting): fluent transcript view — sentence-bounded flow with inline live tail\n\nMirrors platform-desktop#117 on the web surface (Tracked by\nplatform-k8s-gitops#3419). The transcript timeline rendered one\nmetadata-laden card per 2-5s STT commit, fragmenting sentences across\nrows. Industry reference UIs (see gitops\ndocs/faz24-realtime-stt-industry-survey.md §7) flow committed text into\none paragraph until a sentence terminator is certain and keep the\nmutable partial tail updating in place at the end of the flow.\n\n- transcript-flow.ts: pure grouping — group per speaker, paragraph\n  closes ONLY on sentence-final punctuation (never on elapsed time),\n  trailing draft/stabilizing segments of the last group become the live\n  tail; mid-stream drafts stay in the flow so REST-fallback content is\n  never lost.\n- TranscriptTimeline: ''Akıcı | Satırlar'' toggle, fluent default; the\n  row view is unchanged. Citation deep links (#segment-{id}) keep\n  working — every segment renders inside its own span anchor in the\n  flow.\n- 8 new unit tests; mfe-meeting suite 55/55, eslint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe-meeting): load every session''s transcript in the meeting detail (gitops#3421)\n\nThe canonical intelligence result binds ONE session — the latest analysis\nrun''s. When a socket-close mid-meeting spawns a short tail session, the\nlatest run belongs to that tail, so the main session''s transcript (the\nuser''s actual meeting) never rendered — perceived as ''my recording did\nnot reach the web''. Evidence 2026-08-03: meeting e4163355, 27-min main\nsession (136 segments) invisible behind a 5-min tail session result.\n\nloadMeetingDetail now lists the meeting''s sessions and loads every\nsession''s transcript pages for DISPLAY, while citation resolution stays\non the analysis session''s segments (source_index contract unbroken —\nmerged display cannot shift citation indices). Session-list failure\ndegrades to the previous single-session behavior.\n\nTests: multi-session merge + citation stability + sessions-unavailable\nfallback; suite 90/90, eslint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcEKACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVSAQAI8AIKMekgs3z5Wxk7TMz1za\npactx2Ar+ChPhy+eSkDYxhtb7Zic/FC/SYEewVgGnIB+xq/8u2nC7qB0/SHe0qpw\niGxMitIhOxkjPvMZf+EpfTwAI9t8LjrqtGnQ46mJs1WtALgiO4lQs3k0vxWAgBdX\njZ/MsUKhfgFW8IfNRgkWop3o2SwZjHa9QcuMId5IPu/EaRTx2p54rZiczGwtLeAD\nUPp2RXXffEVrGebKTK01E1QypQ0TcMUR66gWgBnxv/y0DcAChEkiZ0T/SuOoEdeA\n6Rcz6RfdNWe3MiIeHstwn4Km3F6Fbn1qi9koBT0dpR6XTMez5G3W0nISBkrw5a/N\n2FmEDoqpLs48d0DKmGmewqVdMOGZGcQzyCuADNOCndZBL0CdFG9MQexNR4aTHcsW\nRouPAL03OgDfxJlzwFcC6BnS66SMorwlr3ZGogYQOHnZCva+afDgyboyXENXNmfr\nGV8i8jIdSwP+6NrdjeYOxbCwJHC46B+HjjvGU9WJfUlrm9fxEu079ADLXkqwNAiI\n5V4BvmKr2/r49z6LFQrxZrhn3XPlNz45EmzeMS7fjTTdQ3cg6BsMrKE81yMTs3ft\nmHs7gCkFJEt+NjqH7gQr1sMd0rmrXnaC0hEioZRQlOlWbUbV6sMCsGDu5+KpnJZc\ncRu2TyIetcf9F/sOXFyI\n=IcnS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T07:25:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDkzOGY5YjgxN2I5ZWI2ZGY5NmE4YmJhNDg2M2M5NDJhZWZjZThlMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917","sha":"0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917"}],"sha":"938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/938f9b817b9eb6df96a8bba4863c942aefce8e20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T22:10:41Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T22:10:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): case workspace — KPI row, filter toolbar, platform grid (#1120) (#1122)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): the case list becomes a workspace — KPIs, filters, entity grid\n\nThe manager screen answered \"which case needs me\" with a card list beside a\nnarrow detail pane: choosing between 200+ reports meant scrolling past all of\nthem, and the pane the choice opened into had a third of the panel. This\nrebuilds the LIST surface on the platform''s standard entity-grid composition\n(EntityGridTemplate, client mode — the whole list already arrives in one\nresponse) and gives the DETAIL the full panel width with an explicit way back.\n\nWhy each piece:\n\n- Four KPI cards (Açık vaka / Sahipsiz / Teyit süresi geçen / Geri bildirim\n  gecikmiş) lead the screen because they are the four questions triage exists\n  to answer. A card is a filter with a number on it: its count and its click\n  apply the same predicate, so the number can be trusted by construction.\n- The existing CaseFilter is EXTENDED, not replaced: mode / openOnly /\n  feedbackOverdue are additive fields with inert defaults, and the KPI cards\n  and toolbar write the same one filter object the screen always had. Nothing\n  imposes a filterModel on the grid — the variant system keeps owning it.\n- Feedback SLA is derived from the directive''s own rule (2019/1937 art.\n  9(1)(f): three months from acknowledgement, or from the seven-day window''s\n  expiry when none was sent; a CLOSED case has had its feedback — the closing\n  message is it). A frontend that cannot compute the deadline says \"Okunamadı\"\n  rather than printing a compliance claim.\n- Rows enter the grid in sortForQueue order, so the default reading order is\n  still \"what needs me next\", not recency; column sorting remains the\n  reader''s move on top of that.\n- Privacy: the subject stays the only free-text cell. Every other column is a\n  closed vocabulary — labels, counts, day arithmetic. No export config is\n  wired, and SLA/status tones always travel with words in the cell.\n- Selection rides the URL (?vaka=<id>, pushState/popstate), so browser\n  back/forward move between list and detail and a case link can be shared.\n- The detail JSX is unchanged content-wise (mailbox, evidence, sanctions,\n  retaliation, timeline — every data-testid intact); only the frame changed.\n\ncase-grid.ts holds the pure derivations (rows, KPIs, columns) outside both the\ntransport module (vi.mock must not erase them) and the component (they are\nfacts about data, not about React). Tests: 90 passing (69 preserved — grid\nchrome stubbed light, case-grid deliberately real — plus row/KPI/SLA/column\ncoverage and the back-button and KPI-filter flows).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): resolve the grid subpath in the standalone cell\n\nThe validate job compiles the standalone cell, whose module resolution is its\nown: the design-system package exports list only dist entries with no\n./advanced/*, so the platform grid import could not resolve there.\n\nONLY that subpath is mapped to src. The first attempt was the blanket\n@mfe/design-system/* map endpoint-admin uses — it dragged the whole\ndesign-system + x-charts source tree into this cell''s compilation and\nsurfaced eight pre-existing type debts that belong to those packages, not to\nthis cell.\n\nThe remaining errors were the cell''s own: standalone-http mirrors the real\nshared-http client but was missing put/delete and the timeout config field\nthat the grid-variant API uses. The stub now carries the full surface;\nvariant persistence in the cell degrades to the request''s natural failure and\nthe grid works without saved views.\n\nCell: tsc 0, 29 tests, production build green. mfe-ethic: 90 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6638ac3a4e868c2b1429dfb3143d87a6f3792f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/c6638ac3a4e868c2b1429dfb3143d87a6f3792f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917","verification":{"payload":"tree c6638ac3a4e868c2b1429dfb3143d87a6f3792f8\nparent f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785708641 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785708641 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): case workspace — KPI row, filter toolbar, platform grid (#1120) (#1122)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): the case list becomes a workspace — KPIs, filters, entity grid\n\nThe manager screen answered \"which case needs me\" with a card list beside a\nnarrow detail pane: choosing between 200+ reports meant scrolling past all of\nthem, and the pane the choice opened into had a third of the panel. This\nrebuilds the LIST surface on the platform''s standard entity-grid composition\n(EntityGridTemplate, client mode — the whole list already arrives in one\nresponse) and gives the DETAIL the full panel width with an explicit way back.\n\nWhy each piece:\n\n- Four KPI cards (Açık vaka / Sahipsiz / Teyit süresi geçen / Geri bildirim\n  gecikmiş) lead the screen because they are the four questions triage exists\n  to answer. A card is a filter with a number on it: its count and its click\n  apply the same predicate, so the number can be trusted by construction.\n- The existing CaseFilter is EXTENDED, not replaced: mode / openOnly /\n  feedbackOverdue are additive fields with inert defaults, and the KPI cards\n  and toolbar write the same one filter object the screen always had. Nothing\n  imposes a filterModel on the grid — the variant system keeps owning it.\n- Feedback SLA is derived from the directive''s own rule (2019/1937 art.\n  9(1)(f): three months from acknowledgement, or from the seven-day window''s\n  expiry when none was sent; a CLOSED case has had its feedback — the closing\n  message is it). A frontend that cannot compute the deadline says \"Okunamadı\"\n  rather than printing a compliance claim.\n- Rows enter the grid in sortForQueue order, so the default reading order is\n  still \"what needs me next\", not recency; column sorting remains the\n  reader''s move on top of that.\n- Privacy: the subject stays the only free-text cell. Every other column is a\n  closed vocabulary — labels, counts, day arithmetic. No export config is\n  wired, and SLA/status tones always travel with words in the cell.\n- Selection rides the URL (?vaka=<id>, pushState/popstate), so browser\n  back/forward move between list and detail and a case link can be shared.\n- The detail JSX is unchanged content-wise (mailbox, evidence, sanctions,\n  retaliation, timeline — every data-testid intact); only the frame changed.\n\ncase-grid.ts holds the pure derivations (rows, KPIs, columns) outside both the\ntransport module (vi.mock must not erase them) and the component (they are\nfacts about data, not about React). Tests: 90 passing (69 preserved — grid\nchrome stubbed light, case-grid deliberately real — plus row/KPI/SLA/column\ncoverage and the back-button and KPI-filter flows).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(etik-speak-manager): resolve the grid subpath in the standalone cell\n\nThe validate job compiles the standalone cell, whose module resolution is its\nown: the design-system package exports list only dist entries with no\n./advanced/*, so the platform grid import could not resolve there.\n\nONLY that subpath is mapped to src. The first attempt was the blanket\n@mfe/design-system/* map endpoint-admin uses — it dragged the whole\ndesign-system + x-charts source tree into this cell''s compilation and\nsurfaced eight pre-existing type debts that belong to those packages, not to\nthis cell.\n\nThe remaining errors were the cell''s own: standalone-http mirrors the real\nshared-http client but was missing put/delete and the timeout config field\nthat the grid-variant API uses. The stub now carries the full surface;\nvariant persistence in the cell degrades to the request''s natural failure and\nthe grid works without saved views.\n\nCell: tsc 0, 29 tests, production build green. mfe-ethic: 90 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb8BhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAggEQACIhs8aJgHbY90NSv93OeHBB\n5+q2CMKA3HZfoYJVOvcksP/rbWWDjg/NTKV54ofEwsrwdwkp1w8c4uGWPGuFsJ24\nKhOEUAwJq3+jxgJjVKeCnWpfn+3BptKOOvBdiOyQUe1zyBvSb7Xc3ofWuVm826u9\nRAmNnA124KtYvn4wH82VUVgf7OajNxpIWIQtDTB6wf2BoghpJTQeWj5QLhqYjLtz\no+54vgGBwmc3tKzBZaCgGcI2HlznEHoh5KmB6dAev/FKKhm5NTZszRe5VnNPDWhN\nGmCD2R5mYxwmQxBNflon1P2cpFjsVNDDPQ4WQfs9zcFXA/QYb+zs7NNCvHKVuP7c\nyFknw4ZU6jOvUkX3lirFg0t+DoYwCclyovqkY/qoMn+89s4YHOMt4yCOK94GMwYu\n8H8q2IAZJYkU5U5aHJ+RYI+umQMHPLT+bkSiY3j5N+Qj/UxsI835+a4DoRJ5V2da\nTiEXaZr4wTv4loO7WcJfexOO58smSYujITz9RWbbP+UH2yJWwjSrJSioNBoyQLpE\ncYP8ChZ7YG2s3MidXaNAjeewACS0jDrYsEoZRJ6lj78z5IJHNLSWvlykC2H/7IzN\ndjToQXZj36FWwyeAg4BRMU7Bl4i+PvnkhCyGDz+EhAd1+ldhI9M93GCdkTYyqm6T\nIDmDO56altBlalikn3Fw\n=FE3f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T22:10:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDA1ODZiN2Q3YmRmZTJhYzcxYzdhNWY2Y2VlMmE4NGJjOTc1YTI5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764","sha":"f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764"}],"sha":"0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/0586b7d7bdfe2ac71c7a5f6cee2a84bc975a2917"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:54:55Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:54:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): the sidebar answers \"where inside it\", not \"which product\" (#1120) (#1121)\n\n* feat(shell): the sidebar answers \"where inside it\", not \"which product\" (#1120)\n\nThe old sidebar was a flat list — Home, Dashboard, Projects, Meetings, Etik\nSpeak, ATS, Services, Schema Explorer on one level, plus an empty\n\"View all / Recent\" folders relic — while the header had already become\nmodule-grouped. Two navigations answering the same question differently.\n\nCross-AI review (REVISE, absorbed on the issue) rejected the obvious fix of\nmirroring the header in the sidebar: that duplicates one question and leaves\nthe other unanswered. The pattern that ships here: header = global module\nswitcher; sidebar = the ACTIVE module''s internal destinations, with one exit\nback to the hub. On /home (or inside a direct-path product with no internal\nnav yet) the sidebar is the module launcher instead.\n\nBoth modes are fed by useHeaderNavigation(), so entitlement filtering, remote\ngating, i18n and the initialized guard live in exactly one place. Fail-closed\nby construction: until entitlements initialize the hook returns no groups, so\nnothing privileged flashes and disappears. Sidebar items are static config\nlabels — an ethics case title can never reach the sidebar (confidentiality\nrequirement from the review, not styling).\n\nMeetings gets a header group it never had: it was reachable ONLY from the old\nflat sidebar, so the grouped navigation was silently incomplete. Access is\nany-of (MEETING or TRANSCRIPT), which the config and hook now support.\n\nThe ethics work queues share a pathname and differ only in query\n(?odak=sahipsiz / ?odak=teyit); active resolution tries pathname+search\nexactly first, then the longest query-less prefix, so \"Tüm vakalar\" does not\nstay lit while the reader is in \"Sahipsiz\".\n\nmfe-shell: 1690 tests pass. tsc: my files carry the same 2 pre-existing\nerrors as on main, zero new.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): deliver dataTestId to the DOM, and pin the e2e to the new IA\n\nThe e2e looked for a visible \"ATS Ürün Merkezi\" link on /home — the old flat\nsidebar''s row. Under the context-sensitive IA the launcher shows İK, whose\nlanding destination in the remote-off harness IS the ATS hub, so the spec now\nasserts the launcher entry by test id and keeps exercising product discovery\nthrough the command palette as before.\n\nWhich surfaced the real gap: ShellSidebar had been forwarding dataTestId into\na className ternary since the flat-sidebar days — the type promised a hook\nfor tests and the DOM never carried it, so every getByTestId against a nav\nitem silently matched nothing. The prop now travels ShellSidebar →\nAppSidebarNavItem → data-testid on both the anchor and button branches, and a\ntest pins the delivery on each so the gap cannot reopen.\n\nNoted, deliberately untouched: the anchor branch also ignores onClick, so\nsidebar navigation has been full-page all along. Separate concern.\n\nmfe-shell 1690 + design-system 8693 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"888d10deb1e0178778139d7cd1dbfc049ad2de93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/888d10deb1e0178778139d7cd1dbfc049ad2de93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764","verification":{"payload":"tree 888d10deb1e0178778139d7cd1dbfc049ad2de93\nparent 18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785704095 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785704095 +0300\n\nfeat(shell): the sidebar answers \"where inside it\", not \"which product\" (#1120) (#1121)\n\n* feat(shell): the sidebar answers \"where inside it\", not \"which product\" (#1120)\n\nThe old sidebar was a flat list — Home, Dashboard, Projects, Meetings, Etik\nSpeak, ATS, Services, Schema Explorer on one level, plus an empty\n\"View all / Recent\" folders relic — while the header had already become\nmodule-grouped. Two navigations answering the same question differently.\n\nCross-AI review (REVISE, absorbed on the issue) rejected the obvious fix of\nmirroring the header in the sidebar: that duplicates one question and leaves\nthe other unanswered. The pattern that ships here: header = global module\nswitcher; sidebar = the ACTIVE module''s internal destinations, with one exit\nback to the hub. On /home (or inside a direct-path product with no internal\nnav yet) the sidebar is the module launcher instead.\n\nBoth modes are fed by useHeaderNavigation(), so entitlement filtering, remote\ngating, i18n and the initialized guard live in exactly one place. Fail-closed\nby construction: until entitlements initialize the hook returns no groups, so\nnothing privileged flashes and disappears. Sidebar items are static config\nlabels — an ethics case title can never reach the sidebar (confidentiality\nrequirement from the review, not styling).\n\nMeetings gets a header group it never had: it was reachable ONLY from the old\nflat sidebar, so the grouped navigation was silently incomplete. Access is\nany-of (MEETING or TRANSCRIPT), which the config and hook now support.\n\nThe ethics work queues share a pathname and differ only in query\n(?odak=sahipsiz / ?odak=teyit); active resolution tries pathname+search\nexactly first, then the longest query-less prefix, so \"Tüm vakalar\" does not\nstay lit while the reader is in \"Sahipsiz\".\n\nmfe-shell: 1690 tests pass. tsc: my files carry the same 2 pre-existing\nerrors as on main, zero new.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): deliver dataTestId to the DOM, and pin the e2e to the new IA\n\nThe e2e looked for a visible \"ATS Ürün Merkezi\" link on /home — the old flat\nsidebar''s row. Under the context-sensitive IA the launcher shows İK, whose\nlanding destination in the remote-off harness IS the ATS hub, so the spec now\nasserts the launcher entry by test id and keeps exercising product discovery\nthrough the command palette as before.\n\nWhich surfaced the real gap: ShellSidebar had been forwarding dataTestId into\na className ternary since the flat-sidebar days — the type promised a hook\nfor tests and the DOM never carried it, so every getByTestId against a nav\nitem silently matched nothing. The prop now travels ShellSidebar →\nAppSidebarNavItem → data-testid on both the anchor and button branches, and a\ntest pins the delivery on each so the gap cannot reopen.\n\nNoted, deliberately untouched: the anchor branch also ignores onClick, so\nsidebar navigation has been full-page all along. Separate concern.\n\nmfe-shell 1690 + design-system 8693 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb66fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfdQQADWi37hcsrQx7K/kCy82d3sy\nsT2AJShF33Mh3eIdK7POd7uK1dOU/7rNxGEO9q2m/IxNFQMlTNGszd+AK1iPc38+\nnI551EvirgksNNfJ6QpXAi8VdkmHEjaHLw9Jb0pMZ067EWMylybHeCbC01aS3jSx\njFO6iBUkZ4Pks94t5WW0I66aBlVRK+6Av+lvLl4aXRuXE3/TT4SxZVr4TG1ohG0c\nIfMxVumyJlBCYaIDegicipxwaOh7Jb6hpsxsqspTV8pwCndvIG1Be/cet4mrkOpZ\nungf4dJL42+bxqIWiFTH/HB4ko27QVC91B8LaDdGQRHkUHe7FjqQlcWKsWsQPzUk\n6cbAVI+oJxD2Axxw79EwJEvX5XRAcfnJg/TsP534Quym36EEvuOX1ZO3KjnE3rhm\nepfVFyn2ycT06/fZV+ieBOi0/6kedRJFF5rLoxX1LVq+/8rNGgHw6eXZ0FLuSsvG\nzkJXaoPgKNuQrb1lP8LCx50zUsD+o0Ycf4R5d6aMY2fnfctfbIU5TJjz1QJuY7L0\ncyk+o83WItjjCsUcvB4xr3rAg28VeG1PeWORprftUIspSF5xKgUx8WmQLjzzbR8O\nG/rEweNSXRmcZ6O0mxdL+7wpQYnaPs8oY0Q94vSLR80CC1CK+uchSPA1cQLmVxnX\n4UtuhZvzjG8RW6J/eXdr\n=kzIV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T20:54:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKGY5MzMxZWQ4MDFlZTZkYTY2NDU3Mjg3NWRlMDg2OTI4ZTg2ZWE3NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658","sha":"18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658"}],"sha":"f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/f9331ed801ee6da664572875de086928e86ea764"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:41:21Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:41:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mfe-ethic): the lifecycle forms had a class and no rule behind it (#3375) (#1119)\n\n`.ethics-form` was applied to all three lifecycle forms — record a sanction,\napply it, conclude a retaliation check — and never styled. The labels kept\n`display: inline`, so each one flowed around its own control like running\ntext: in the detail pane \"Yaptırım türü\", \"Seçin\" and the next label''s\nopening words landed on one line. Wide enough it passes for deliberate,\nwhich is how it got through review.\n\nThe breakpoint was measured on the wrong thing. Inside the platform shell the\nsidebar and padding take ~170px, so `@media (width <= 800px)` was still\nwaiting while the pane had already dropped to 305px — measured live at an\n853px viewport. It is now a container query on the panel itself, so the\nlayout responds to the room it actually has. Same rule serves the standalone\ncell at /ethic, where the container is nearly the viewport.\n\n`width: 100%` on .ethics-manager is load-bearing and not obviously so.\nInline-size containment stops the contents contributing to the element''s own\nintrinsic width, and in the shell it is a flex item sized by exactly that\ncontribution — without the width the box collapses to its padding. I measured\n48px before adding it, i.e. the panel disappears. The comment says so.\n\nVerified by injecting the rules into the running page rather than by the\nsuite: vitest runs in jsdom, which computes no layout, so the 69 green tests\nsay nothing about any of this. Measured after: labels sharing a line 0 (was\nthe defect), detail pane 305px → 681px, no horizontal overflow, and the query\nflips both ways when the threshold is moved either side of the container''s\n681px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65ba93ca1c2fc572411323f8e0ce39d2727d29cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/65ba93ca1c2fc572411323f8e0ce39d2727d29cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658","verification":{"payload":"tree 65ba93ca1c2fc572411323f8e0ce39d2727d29cb\nparent 43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785681681 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785681681 +0300\n\nfix(mfe-ethic): the lifecycle forms had a class and no rule behind it (#3375) (#1119)\n\n`.ethics-form` was applied to all three lifecycle forms — record a sanction,\napply it, conclude a retaliation check — and never styled. The labels kept\n`display: inline`, so each one flowed around its own control like running\ntext: in the detail pane \"Yaptırım türü\", \"Seçin\" and the next label''s\nopening words landed on one line. Wide enough it passes for deliberate,\nwhich is how it got through review.\n\nThe breakpoint was measured on the wrong thing. Inside the platform shell the\nsidebar and padding take ~170px, so `@media (width <= 800px)` was still\nwaiting while the pane had already dropped to 305px — measured live at an\n853px viewport. It is now a container query on the panel itself, so the\nlayout responds to the room it actually has. Same rule serves the standalone\ncell at /ethic, where the container is nearly the viewport.\n\n`width: 100%` on .ethics-manager is load-bearing and not obviously so.\nInline-size containment stops the contents contributing to the element''s own\nintrinsic width, and in the shell it is a flex item sized by exactly that\ncontribution — without the width the box collapses to its padding. I measured\n48px before adding it, i.e. the panel disappears. The comment says so.\n\nVerified by injecting the rules into the running page rather than by the\nsuite: vitest runs in jsdom, which computes no layout, so the 69 green tests\nsay nothing about any of this. Measured after: labels sharing a line 0 (was\nthe defect), detail pane 305px → 681px, no horizontal overflow, and the query\nflips both ways when the threshold is moved either side of the container''s\n681px.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb1cRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsjkQAKV7h8lzFBhImBmOnDbm2Ktw\nIL37viM2zEeLf+f6DPTjbZSoolFGp8gCyKtvZnUoMfoR8mSO4xavNZV0aN5sqq8F\n2sSehUhLp/cm9JzHmvgYBF+x/HnmEIAQd3LAdk4BdOUlcCYO7fTxUSLaJrGFX2b5\nkkINB/G7JC7p8l73nVZXwFVXfDQm3Vy7FPXdV8WkA+s6XoGPrxxAJlAB/gy7YA3B\nKzQ7Fptzm0aesRUClzDcab5sRrmcahdBS0VvQT++KJcmIFsXaIYgArlgcw1JrSMM\nRv6h2hVMRyN266Gb5Rf7QdO6PW/LR44A+Z9XBvTU5rJkMN/JP5fPUzPGcduyG9cI\n+xErYz5fYfvM+IWoX7N89R87P+8AgF9USRyezVwgCWUDCQA6iwarg0K/UBZmOSzb\nwnsJctTs2F6VpLphiRV2Eev3mt9inm+/aRUrH91qnpf16VGMfXY9lpU1b+v6J69c\n2D0lYlMuVzH3O2sqFj/TKtwWa9MYzPWgqzDuqo7hqjMx4SuoB+PHriICg6Y8PRq9\n5kz4pAp+DBwUG3/B65WsYWU7CzJVL9YfqQhpXV06s5TIw+oIWzB9WwF8fe3dgjEi\n1Idh0e+Nwz/2popxGKHsZee3ZQsItn35rE8CtZFlOVG/fFTrZ9fsxDs0B67o8M+A\npgbxpMgVbN7OwtI3i+VG\n=9Cil\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T14:41:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDE4ZTllZDk2NzEyYzBhYjViOGUzYzdmYWFkYjgzMjRhY2JjYmU2NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6","sha":"43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6"}],"sha":"18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/18e9ed96712c0ab5b8e3c7faadb8324acbcbe658"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T13:37:23Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T13:37:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): the violation category, and a floor the form actually applies (#3375) (#1118)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): the violation category, and a floor the form actually applies (#3375)\n\nThe sanction form asked for a score, a type and a free-text \"escalation\nreason\" whose placeholder suggested typing \"kamu görevlisine rüşvet — cetvel\notomatik yükseltme listesi\". That was the whole of the automatic-escalation\nrule on this side: a hint, addressed to whoever was reading.\n\nThe category is now a field. Choosing one the scale escalates fixes the band\nat ÇOK AĞIR however the ten criteria totalled, and says so on the derived-band\nline rather than rejecting the handler on submit.\n\nTwo things the tests were hiding, both the same shape:\n\n- vi.mock empties exported constants, so AUTOMATIC_ESCALATIONS.has() would\n  have answered undefined and every assertion about the floor would have\n  passed for the wrong reason. Restored with getter spies.\n- bandForScore is auto-mocked too, and had been answering undefined all along:\n  the derived-band line read \"Puan 1–40 aralığında olmalı\" in every test that\n  ever rendered this form, so no assertion about a band has meant anything.\n\nServer-side counterpart: platform-backend#1093.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-ethic): the new test used it(), the file imports test()\n\nvitest ran it anyway; tsc is what caught it — the same gap this PR is about.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd13c31e6c69748dff5480beab824abf976ea693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/bd13c31e6c69748dff5480beab824abf976ea693"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6","verification":{"payload":"tree bd13c31e6c69748dff5480beab824abf976ea693\nparent 055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785677843 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785677843 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): the violation category, and a floor the form actually applies (#3375) (#1118)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): the violation category, and a floor the form actually applies (#3375)\n\nThe sanction form asked for a score, a type and a free-text \"escalation\nreason\" whose placeholder suggested typing \"kamu görevlisine rüşvet — cetvel\notomatik yükseltme listesi\". That was the whole of the automatic-escalation\nrule on this side: a hint, addressed to whoever was reading.\n\nThe category is now a field. Choosing one the scale escalates fixes the band\nat ÇOK AĞIR however the ten criteria totalled, and says so on the derived-band\nline rather than rejecting the handler on submit.\n\nTwo things the tests were hiding, both the same shape:\n\n- vi.mock empties exported constants, so AUTOMATIC_ESCALATIONS.has() would\n  have answered undefined and every assertion about the floor would have\n  passed for the wrong reason. Restored with getter spies.\n- bandForScore is auto-mocked too, and had been answering undefined all along:\n  the derived-band line read \"Puan 1–40 aralığında olmalı\" in every test that\n  ever rendered this form, so no assertion about a band has meant anything.\n\nServer-side counterpart: platform-backend#1093.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-ethic): the new test used it(), the file imports test()\n\nvitest ran it anyway; tsc is what caught it — the same gap this PR is about.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb0gTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbawQAKRhP35rDFl6V5R/9ltuMn71\nxccFmdibeSA19Bp7NyYUgdDSye8hfSAbQdNrSilhf8dbbkSOvHvDYEWbngMRYgU8\ncFRU804rY7AxQ/D7B9y/dmg/s+jW2nE3uufBwzp2tuSWCE68NFSKy3bH6fmuy+/B\nOrPV2JDCPQbQXqJR9mXCpAKjLS8aXkG/MPFkgstw+ocP4jxmCWGfVkViWqZnLQQ2\ngZCTZb7l5ZdyGiRcL2WsHIy1hbAs/VWvjkglSnUbmvLZakhSnkgNlQLy/A0YUBqX\nz91To7eZLpUrD3K4EMjhU5ugDEJhPX5tq1aKjggAbYS/axiWUXa+B/oZCDRCxK1U\ntgYgUXRiRfMHn32gxSrat1I47mlLnuOPmMl8/khmNVFCP/DB88SWkMfa+y1dkTtn\nrOGGy7mCC4WFT0y9JocbBnC7tfBF5ATFJjg3vrZ5ScSETgcI0HiuEzZ3eqcJKowU\n446zeeYTQxQgUVKesWzyMYiOEz+fAq/YO3p17aYSuWYo6mVoZy+4xteWryxhd9rZ\nL+SYVQxeCXzOez0VS2oZfmjXbRpgc8ntCb+KUdxD/QePXH1Sf9YhazOWy+3RgfNh\nNmyVC+1Y+tdTtxXcmX6K1prcDuxh/lTU/hcG1WmLjefXOH+VvVijxymYb0YswPgb\nIGDIa9UvNE/YMXIz8Ddf\n=WDZx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T13:37:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDQzMzY4ZDNlMWVjNzA1ZTA4NjRjZmJkZTYyY2M3ZTdlNmQ0NjRlZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12","sha":"055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12"}],"sha":"43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/43368d3e1ec705e0864cfbde62cc7e7e6d464ef6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:44:07Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:44:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): apply a sanction, move an appeal (#3375) (#1117)\n\nThe last two actions in the chain, closing the loop the panels opened.\n\nThe verification note is required, for the same reason a case cannot close\nwithout a finding: \"applied\" with nothing behind it is the state that makes a\nsanctions register worthless. The placeholder asks for how it was confirmed, not\nthat it was.\n\nBoth appeal outcomes sit side by side with equal weight. A screen that made\nupholding the easier click — a primary button against a link, or one hidden\nbehind a menu — would put a thumb on the scale of somebody''s appeal, and the\nhandler pressing it would never notice the nudge.\n\nApply is hidden once an appeal is overturned, matching the server, which refuses\nit. Offering a control the request will reject teaches the handler that this\nscreen guesses.\n\n68 tests pass; the manager typecheck is clean.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a1a16bfa7265261057d15e4940703e4f129756d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/1a1a16bfa7265261057d15e4940703e4f129756d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a1a16bfa7265261057d15e4940703e4f129756d\nparent d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785671047 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785671047 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): apply a sanction, move an appeal (#3375) (#1117)\n\nThe last two actions in the chain, closing the loop the panels opened.\n\nThe verification note is required, for the same reason a case cannot close\nwithout a finding: \"applied\" with nothing behind it is the state that makes a\nsanctions register worthless. The placeholder asks for how it was confirmed, not\nthat it was.\n\nBoth appeal outcomes sit side by side with equal weight. A screen that made\nupholding the easier click — a primary button against a link, or one hidden\nbehind a menu — would put a thumb on the scale of somebody''s appeal, and the\nhandler pressing it would never notice the nudge.\n\nApply is hidden once an appeal is overturned, matching the server, which refuses\nit. Offering a control the request will reject teaches the handler that this\nscreen guesses.\n\n68 tests pass; the manager typecheck is clean.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqby2HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATLsQAEMpsOhvfC9Mq6KClyVaQgwu\n8tdhPNkXeuEyW1BJ+tJA43AX0fqZCj0/zZECuqiLcUsvFlzWSUDlbHUmBkSSNKmZ\nHCnIgN8C+zt28JoRUTRnuEn4d1uHK+5JzIsnLQYu+/XE0GgOmfZYLB65EUGYBbwf\nUeJ+Gf7WCxmjUn2vl+qRpuGL9/EDTEHKILgVDLq7bJiVmU4CEx8GSWAA5QO3DN0m\nZrr0OuDu0VW8+mSbgq9H6Qq+Ux3o2/7EYHt6t1H73qtOaPw09on8NNMjsWCjY8AG\nPtl9O3gDHT+fSKpHOhIJ/392yaSbX2D254w5JX6LR0iv4sxV37eeHnMwn16INfq5\nriAJz+enFa0iqQIcL3SY9pkZKKh50USnm2Psoqve7l+LR11Zs2gu946bKsqE/ki4\nXVwPq5UyRrPTG3b0tnhLXRlzZcRafesWlycTibK5gZZHbV34qPHV0lvEzEKYU/tt\nSfVYPOlXm3BwTAjdWr/p7KwS6CPH1TAoXPSbb3ncfMZdfS+HoNot0EY87kcZxt7g\nb0LJcCF0mqfYcz77rJ+PTR9hw8ZQ7KUygp9A75KKexyTWvikrmsrxxNBN71DQ1xo\nLk50owMUXq8npdEEGVpPMEJUG8NmjsnCFsJZf4BNrTvnF2pwGsAACVydIrWRzdl4\nScqmejxgKW6NMbGrNPOo\n=OXkB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T11:44:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDA1NWMyNTk2NjNkYWI5OWQ2NGYyMTNkMDNhZDQ0NDE5NzI1MzFmMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423","sha":"d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423"}],"sha":"055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/055c259663dab99d64f213d03ad4441972531f12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:05:31Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:05:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): the write half — record a sanction, conclude a check (#3375) (#1116)\n\nThe panels showed the chain; these two forms let a handler move it.\n\nThe severity band is derived from the score and shown, not chosen. The scale\nreads the band off the ten-criterion total, and a handler picking both would\nreintroduce exactly what the scale exists to remove: two similar violations\nlanding in different bands because two people read the table differently. What a\nhandler may still do is escalate — the automatic list requires it for bribery,\nharassment, child labour and the rest — and that field is the reason, which is\nwhy it is the only way to reach ÇOK AĞIR from a low score.\n\nThe conclusion form asks about art. 19''s fifteen forms as named checkboxes rather\nthan offering a free-text box. The person being pushed out rarely has the word for\nwhat is happening, and the manager doing the pushing never volunteers it; asking\nabout each form turns one vague question into fifteen answerable ones.\n\nTwo guards are stated in the UI even though the server enforces both, because\nlearning a rule before typing four fields is different from learning it after:\nnaming an indicator while judging the risk NONE is refused, and a suspected or\nconfirmed finding cannot be saved without an action. Noticing is not protecting.\n\nThe sanction form appears only on a closed case, matching where the server accepts\none — offering it earlier would invite a decision the case has not yet justified.\n\n68 tests pass; the manager typecheck is clean.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8aa29d24ec5c43c4330f43fcf004ebec53e30621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/8aa29d24ec5c43c4330f43fcf004ebec53e30621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423","verification":{"payload":"tree 8aa29d24ec5c43c4330f43fcf004ebec53e30621\nparent 77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785668731 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785668731 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): the write half — record a sanction, conclude a check (#3375) (#1116)\n\nThe panels showed the chain; these two forms let a handler move it.\n\nThe severity band is derived from the score and shown, not chosen. The scale\nreads the band off the ten-criterion total, and a handler picking both would\nreintroduce exactly what the scale exists to remove: two similar violations\nlanding in different bands because two people read the table differently. What a\nhandler may still do is escalate — the automatic list requires it for bribery,\nharassment, child labour and the rest — and that field is the reason, which is\nwhy it is the only way to reach ÇOK AĞIR from a low score.\n\nThe conclusion form asks about art. 19''s fifteen forms as named checkboxes rather\nthan offering a free-text box. The person being pushed out rarely has the word for\nwhat is happening, and the manager doing the pushing never volunteers it; asking\nabout each form turns one vague question into fifteen answerable ones.\n\nTwo guards are stated in the UI even though the server enforces both, because\nlearning a rule before typing four fields is different from learning it after:\nnaming an indicator while judging the risk NONE is refused, and a suspected or\nconfirmed finding cannot be saved without an action. Noticing is not protecting.\n\nThe sanction form appears only on a closed case, matching where the server accepts\none — offering it earlier would invite a decision the case has not yet justified.\n\n68 tests pass; the manager typecheck is clean.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbyR7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwvMQAJ4uWyeQmLCBj0O/aH9YnqXD\nGnQ0RlQAnF/p0b4FO3d2LnVpgZduyBGKA035b4KaFmPYUHD55NmH3ROhNH2Wek3P\ndkarvIXt63O3HEBqsmeGjG2V+Ve8kmyL6SQeFqcvifN7LTZlHnZa1CTILyWbOIk5\nLv/g0p1lgAwqr3Mh8zJKy2q9K54rE8XT6mgICYYwKtCqhyxG3ZxIaV3OmhZfDxS4\naeCskI6eQe6Ookf+oSIk90RwKR1cgKnnPDDBaKy9NqYYahUeKeZYR5V7E/Eskoqj\nVItl89Q1pjjKacvSZ/SN+rOkdfU0RP/5YkHo5IVJ51FPCQn3QURHr/S0Zi6/Fo+v\nhK0yi44xbfKZQtVI5yIK5tGazfKDr9UlVebVwTk12tQciWD8nqpfbs0MAlx2sOzy\n4K0hbg31jM+B26HRGn5PSOJIacOFEB2NRG6ywL84OUMV3zv4YKo71LrIkwW0x63U\n5bIyndcHHDep4os4O2e6j4NUPatNjedc0BBew0jHtDvR32jYH7uxpoudWQeFyyPl\n55/h4Sgu2/TnRi5/bZXZjkhbDUWJqbdZS8OwqhBcEdRaz+533tkpCAp5e6IedKAa\n5PARpX1CH4vybvWQMkh0A9HtWmkiGe0LBMm8A6nvWRFXRfMsHhIwllad8z/yapyo\nNoqTodkka5EOtG/aw4hn\n=/3n2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T11:05:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKGQxNDliNWJkYTAyOWIyNjEyOGU5ZGRmOWI5M2I3NTUwNmIzZmY0MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03","sha":"77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03"}],"sha":"d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/d149b5bda029b26128e9ddf9b93b75506b3ff423"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:46:37Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:46:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): sanction and retaliation panels on the case detail (#3375) (#1115)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): sanction and retaliation panels on the case detail (#3375)\n\nTwo sections below the case history, using the client contract from #1114.\n\nBoth degrade the way the timeline does, and for the same reason: \"no sanction was\ndecided\" and \"the record could not be read\" are opposite conclusions, and a\nhandler acts on the first. So a failed load never leaves an empty list behind —\nit says, in an alert, that it failed and that this does not mean nothing happened.\n\nThe sanction row says decided-but-not-applied in words rather than leaving it as\nan absent date nobody scans for. That gap is the backlog the register exists to\nexpose, and it disappears if the reader has to notice a missing field.\n\nThe retaliation panel shows due and asked as separate facts. The distance between\nthem is the only honest measure of whether the programme is being run: a schedule\nfull of checks nobody has put to anyone looks, from a summary count, exactly like\none running on time. Overdue is called out with role=\"status\" so it reaches a\nscreen reader rather than only the sighted eye.\n\nThe empty states differ by case status, because on an open case the absence is\ncorrect: sanctions are recorded after closure, and the three checks are opened by\nthe server at closure. Saying \"none recorded\" on an open case would read as an\nomission rather than as the sequence working.\n\nTwo test-side notes worth keeping. vi.mock auto-mocks the whole module, so the\ntwo new list calls answer undefined until stubbed and the panels read .length on\nthe result — in production the API client validates the shape and throws, so\nundefined cannot reach state there; this is purely the auto-mock. And I wrote\n`detail?.status` for the selected case when the component calls it `selected`,\nwhich typechecks as an unresolved identifier only at render.\n\n68 tests pass across 7 files.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-ethic): the label maps never landed, and vitest could not see it (#3375)\n\nCI''s tsc caught four undefined identifiers the whole local suite was happy with:\n\n    App.tsx(1067,36): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''SANCTION_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1069,30): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''BAND_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1081,71): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''APPEAL_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1118,49): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''RISK_LABELS''\n\nThe maps were written against an anchor that does not exist — the component is\n`export default function App()`, not the name I reached for — so the insertion\nsilently did nothing and the panels referenced identifiers that were never\ndefined. 68 tests still passed, because vitest transpiles without typechecking:\na name that resolves to nothing at build time is invisible to it until the code\npath actually renders, and these render only for a closed case.\n\nAlso fixed a real portability fault in the new test: spreading a Set into\nMath.min fails the typecheck under the app''s iteration target even though vitest\nruns it fine. Array.from instead.\n\nLesson worth the two lines it costs: on this repo a green vitest run is not\nevidence the code compiles. The manager''s `validate` job runs tsc, and that is\nthe gate that tells the truth.\n\n68 tests pass; the identifiers now resolve.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c71435caca790925849cc5c97ea7085017369d2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/c71435caca790925849cc5c97ea7085017369d2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03","verification":{"payload":"tree c71435caca790925849cc5c97ea7085017369d2c\nparent e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785667597 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785667597 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): sanction and retaliation panels on the case detail (#3375) (#1115)\n\n* feat(mfe-ethic): sanction and retaliation panels on the case detail (#3375)\n\nTwo sections below the case history, using the client contract from #1114.\n\nBoth degrade the way the timeline does, and for the same reason: \"no sanction was\ndecided\" and \"the record could not be read\" are opposite conclusions, and a\nhandler acts on the first. So a failed load never leaves an empty list behind —\nit says, in an alert, that it failed and that this does not mean nothing happened.\n\nThe sanction row says decided-but-not-applied in words rather than leaving it as\nan absent date nobody scans for. That gap is the backlog the register exists to\nexpose, and it disappears if the reader has to notice a missing field.\n\nThe retaliation panel shows due and asked as separate facts. The distance between\nthem is the only honest measure of whether the programme is being run: a schedule\nfull of checks nobody has put to anyone looks, from a summary count, exactly like\none running on time. Overdue is called out with role=\"status\" so it reaches a\nscreen reader rather than only the sighted eye.\n\nThe empty states differ by case status, because on an open case the absence is\ncorrect: sanctions are recorded after closure, and the three checks are opened by\nthe server at closure. Saying \"none recorded\" on an open case would read as an\nomission rather than as the sequence working.\n\nTwo test-side notes worth keeping. vi.mock auto-mocks the whole module, so the\ntwo new list calls answer undefined until stubbed and the panels read .length on\nthe result — in production the API client validates the shape and throws, so\nundefined cannot reach state there; this is purely the auto-mock. And I wrote\n`detail?.status` for the selected case when the component calls it `selected`,\nwhich typechecks as an unresolved identifier only at render.\n\n68 tests pass across 7 files.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mfe-ethic): the label maps never landed, and vitest could not see it (#3375)\n\nCI''s tsc caught four undefined identifiers the whole local suite was happy with:\n\n    App.tsx(1067,36): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''SANCTION_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1069,30): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''BAND_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1081,71): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''APPEAL_LABELS''\n    App.tsx(1118,49): error TS2304: Cannot find name ''RISK_LABELS''\n\nThe maps were written against an anchor that does not exist — the component is\n`export default function App()`, not the name I reached for — so the insertion\nsilently did nothing and the panels referenced identifiers that were never\ndefined. 68 tests still passed, because vitest transpiles without typechecking:\na name that resolves to nothing at build time is invisible to it until the code\npath actually renders, and these render only for a closed case.\n\nAlso fixed a real portability fault in the new test: spreading a Set into\nMath.min fails the typecheck under the app''s iteration target even though vitest\nruns it fine. Array.from instead.\n\nLesson worth the two lines it costs: on this repo a green vitest run is not\nevidence the code compiles. The manager''s `validate` job runs tsc, and that is\nthe gate that tells the truth.\n\n68 tests pass; the identifiers now resolve.\n\nRefs #3375.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbyANCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbWEQACR5vgJrwxZ+FaRRRrHn8lRv\nd0e1ZsbIIVnxeRkDuZ+w+8//fM79RLUfLLRATO7bo4OyZetnQ3uNcuzwR6uW7aye\n5vbncTlaxq3XMr/2e+MFEGh6QNnantk4r4auWAdRYT5MTR0XRna6zzKSE3IfSbOV\nlYyMHuVURTDzkXPg/8ps6cF3aHEcIiWopTcO4a1EPewgg3Necim6SnBi+Bb99HAv\n1GiPLQoEopgwxJY1IwRFZdTRoFPLANZE0+vnSOy/Z0bEtHnz85kEpOTaWIhO1mlg\nDJH2BgcZUQPfF5Lk+dt3TJ4w8+KF+aFt9g0uhlkG6uE8l8JDwafKx/J+CPv51Q3y\nV8EzI337Zd8pZRL71ib5E4inCgab7ZjgAnTv19T8ZLm+RIdkwYso3qXzqBOZe05m\nT4YEiQOuAvtzFPrizZRnVeOlDXcfisuCUewCLiCztKpFk4pWr5LCzHjT7bj1fqVi\n1MLPR5HCqhhat/iO9GhgaxuRQJYBl0aoHSDR27NwClB1YtnDppPjp4viShXE3KIB\nzmmid73e4WEPNwGnK3RPhAvkdAad9rU67HH10uYwWuKBQcjnTnPpglpSKpyj5u2Y\n4eK57NVeOUT7Jd+2jpKvEagIrjvbEqmTwkzslQFBW75GgFTk7+EGOxoMYnmGrkPO\nR/OZ1jxyuj0nNxWvndER\n=BtnK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T10:46:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKDc3ZjYzZGJkOGU0N2Y3ZThlZTg0NWRlYWEzNGU2MjJiMDZjYjVkMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0","sha":"e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0"}],"sha":"77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/77f63dbd8e47f7e8ee845deaa34e622b06cb5d03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:09:26Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:09:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mfe-ethic): client contract for sanctions and retaliation checks (#3375) (#1114)\n\nSeven calls against the staff endpoints merged in #1089, plus the two vocabularies\nthe UI must not drift from — and tests that fail if it does.\n\nBoth vocabularies are written down elsewhere: the severity bands in Açık\nHolding''s İHLAL AĞIRLIK CETVELİ, the retaliation indicators in Directive\n2019/1937 art. 19. A UI that quietly disagrees with either shows a handler one\nthing and records another, and the divergence surfaces months later as a case\nwhose band nobody can explain.\n\nRETALIATION_INDICATORS is closed and carries a Turkish label per code. Closed\nbecause a handler who can type their own category will, and then \"how often does\nthis happen, and where\" becomes unanswerable across cases and years — the\nquestion the programme exists to answer. Labelled because a bare\nSCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE code reads as a system value rather than as a thing that\nhappened to a person.\n\nFour tests pin what would otherwise drift silently: the bands cover 1-40 with no\ngap and no overlap (a score in two bands would let the same violation be filed\neither way), every boundary maps as the scale says, the indicator list is all\nfifteen with a label each, and the codes match the server''s V22 CHECK exactly —\na code existing only here would be refused at conclude time, after the handler\nhad already written the observation.\n\n4 tests pass in the new file; 68 across the app.\n\nRefs #3375. Follows platform-backend#1089.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2f7e55ae1b35d941a1bd8bf7090e15b0844bde7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/a2f7e55ae1b35d941a1bd8bf7090e15b0844bde7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/e1a91a8da857a6408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0","verification":{"payload":"tree a2f7e55ae1b35d941a1bd8bf7090e15b0844bde7\nparent 2c4dc702594b2ff9766c4ec2c71ca1c0b35ae39b\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785665366 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785665366 +0300\n\nfeat(mfe-ethic): client contract for sanctions and retaliation checks (#3375) (#1114)\n\nSeven calls against the staff endpoints merged in #1089, plus the two vocabularies\nthe UI must not drift from — and tests that fail if it does.\n\nBoth vocabularies are written down elsewhere: the severity bands in Açık\nHolding''s İHLAL AĞIRLIK CETVELİ, the retaliation indicators in Directive\n2019/1937 art. 19. A UI that quietly disagrees with either shows a handler one\nthing and records another, and the divergence surfaces months later as a case\nwhose band nobody can explain.\n\nRETALIATION_INDICATORS is closed and carries a Turkish label per code. Closed\nbecause a handler who can type their own category will, and then \"how often does\nthis happen, and where\" becomes unanswerable across cases and years — the\nquestion the programme exists to answer. Labelled because a bare\nSCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE code reads as a system value rather than as a thing that\nhappened to a person.\n\nFour tests pin what would otherwise drift silently: the bands cover 1-40 with no\ngap and no overlap (a score in two bands would let the same violation be filed\neither way), every boundary maps as the scale says, the indicator list is all\nfifteen with a label each, and the codes match the server''s V22 CHECK exactly —\na code existing only here would be refused at conclude time, after the handler\nhad already written the observation.\n\n4 tests pass in the new file; 68 across the app.\n\nRefs #3375. Follows platform-backend#1089.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbxdWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN+0QAIym03BPqZFYU8Zb8cbuLqBa\n5lnevpoa/aQ+QLlRnrexz8yjOapbCbKYA9XLQ7KXCt7M+I3PJal0962okykYXGKZ\nM50adkTh8zCIBshQiTXaMzzek9oOICClx4vJxcXvubrgxnXn6mTiCSNeCnF8agK8\nC58m4uNxXNIrYOpW8sZc/TPgwRfYlui38ZLKI0r1uyumkzb3iq1MeyEeNyz/r4aA\nzpBUpZR2ylBuj9m+F6iG9de30v5JYQZGaVN6a2t+Rr878T12oAnypD06rQTwsb03\nkaYdbO5Fs5fDdxpi6+bJrJKRyIGZfDzno/oymPxoe7Y