408643947fb7ad7b98785ed6f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/2c4dc702594b2ff9766c4ec2c71ca1c0b35ae39b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:01:33Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:01:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(etik-speak): offer confidential and named reporting (#3370) (#1113)\n\nThe form showed three options and greyed two of them out with \"sonraki dilim\".\nNow it renders exactly the modes the organisation runs, read from\nGET /intake-options, and asks for an identity when one is needed.\n\nAbsent rather than disabled. A greyed-out option is still announced to a screen\nreader, so it tells the reporter that confidential reporting exists somewhere and\nis being withheld from them — which invites the wrong conclusion about why. If a\ntenant does not run a mode, the option is simply not there.\n\nThe list starts at anonymous-only and widens when the server answers, so the form\nis usable on first paint and never briefly offers a mode that will be refused.\nfetchIntakeOptions never rejects; on any failure it answers anonymous-only,\nmirroring the server''s own floor. No error banner for that case on purpose —\n\"reporting options could not be loaded\" would tell someone the channel is broken\nwhen they can still report.\n\nAnonymous sends no reporterIdentity key at all, not an empty object: the server\nrefuses an anonymous report that carries the field rather than ignoring it, so\nsending {} would break anonymous intake. Blank optional fields travel as\nundefined rather than \"\", so a later reader cannot mistake \"not given\" for \"given\nas empty\".\n\nThe old test pinned the disabled radio; it now pins absence, with a comment\nsaying what changed and where the enabled-path coverage lives. The three suites\nthat auto-mock the api module needed fetchIntakeOptions stubbed — vi.mock returns\nundefined for it otherwise, and every App render would have thrown.\n\nEvidence: 44 tests pass across 6 files; production build clean.\n\nRefs #3370. Pairs with platform-backend#1084.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d30e488eb4ed0889e81b4e426a3e4b056f8e7f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/8d30e488eb4ed0889e81b4e426a3e4b056f8e7f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/2c4dc702594b2ff9766c4ec2c71ca1c0b35ae39b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d30e488eb4ed0889e81b4e426a3e4b056f8e7f8\nparent 6f9ee66d8d3b7a8f4c1f4cc971b4a17edc854bd1\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785657693 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785657693 +0300\n\nfeat(etik-speak): offer confidential and named reporting (#3370) (#1113)\n\nThe form showed three options and greyed two of them out with \"sonraki dilim\".\nNow it renders exactly the modes the organisation runs, read from\nGET /intake-options, and asks for an identity when one is needed.\n\nAbsent rather than disabled. A greyed-out option is still announced to a screen\nreader, so it tells the reporter that confidential reporting exists somewhere and\nis being withheld from them — which invites the wrong conclusion about why. If a\ntenant does not run a mode, the option is simply not there.\n\nThe list starts at anonymous-only and widens when the server answers, so the form\nis usable on first paint and never briefly offers a mode that will be refused.\nfetchIntakeOptions never rejects; on any failure it answers anonymous-only,\nmirroring the server''s own floor. No error banner for that case on purpose —\n\"reporting options could not be loaded\" would tell someone the channel is broken\nwhen they can still report.\n\nAnonymous sends no reporterIdentity key at all, not an empty object: the server\nrefuses an anonymous report that carries the field rather than ignoring it, so\nsending {} would break anonymous intake. Blank optional fields travel as\nundefined rather than \"\", so a later reader cannot mistake \"not given\" for \"given\nas empty\".\n\nThe old test pinned the disabled radio; it now pins absence, with a comment\nsaying what changed and where the enabled-path coverage lives. The three suites\nthat auto-mock the api module needed fetchIntakeOptions stubbed — vi.mock returns\nundefined for it otherwise, and every App render would have thrown.\n\nEvidence: 44 tests pass across 6 files; production build clean.\n\nRefs #3370. Pairs with platform-backend#1084.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbvldCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhBEQAJO+cHZsSSyewgkTbkfDnj8z\n4CH01/qbseEUC54QDdqDVZwhi6uinykdwzSkKMk5E3VmZr0cUAmHLkjL+VeNyh76\nVMbS4ZJPzPl+4+7HiT6e6dy6DezSaWCuNXJgw3te2UikDovfLtttD0jUic8Pmkkm\nRvK9sBVBvOfia1IywJw6GQT3rssTbwMHyLBtbZMnfuiioNIka+S4+IpuZ3qj1X3o\ne2s6TSR0X0v8Mm0D6wAsjRbM+aDlkUPQ0R8PRfqrZCdAxd8fCfdiJ6ofSPmjTAzV\nSpVKTQ6Dkx4yMTG2r78kg6sOKhGd+phDKmeYbBPJhB+E/qjeqW3MLo9/fa9UZpgb