her_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/b4fa6d0eb9d0b93d02581c1381c8f3418a092cfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T09:58:23Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T09:58:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(users): the authenticator app joins the method boxes, and the boxes tell the truth (#1102)\n\nTwo changes to the same control, both about it saying what is actually the case.\n\n**The authenticator app is a checkbox now.** It was deliberately left out while\nthe privileged flow ran stock `auth-otp-form`, which never reads `mfaMethods`:\na box in front of it would have looked like a control and done nothing.\nplatform-backend#1048 puts a gate behind it, so the box governs something.\n\n**The boxes show what is offered, not the stored restriction.** The attribute is\na restriction and an absent one means \"none\" — so rendering it raw left every\nbox empty on an account where in fact every method was on offer. The display\nsaid the opposite of the truth, and the hint text underneath was doing the work\nthe control should have been doing. An unrestricted account now shows all three\nticked, and unticking one withdraws exactly that method.\n\nTicking the last missing box clears the attribute rather than storing all three.\nBoth read as unrestricted, but only one of them silently freezes the account\nagainst any method added later.\n\nThe note that remains is the single case where a ticked state and reality can\nstill differ, and it is a deliberate one: if no other method is usable for that\nuser, the authenticator app is offered even when unticked. A restriction is not\nallowed to close the last door.\n\n  UserDetailDrawer.mfa.spec        15 tests\n  user-management drawer suite  10 files, 67 tests, 0 failures\n\nRefs: gitops#3251, platform-backend#1048\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e57b85f96fdbe6a0672814d58f10116cddf8af2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/6e57b85f96fdbe6a0672814d58f10116cddf8af2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/b4fa6d0eb9d0b93d02581c1381c8f3418a092cfb","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e57b85f96fdbe6a0672814d58f10116cddf8af2\nparent a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785578303 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785578303 +0300\n\nfeat(users): the authenticator app joins the method boxes, and the boxes tell the truth (#1102)\n\nTwo changes to the same control, both about it saying what is actually the case.\n\n**The authenticator app is a checkbox now.** It was deliberately left out while\nthe privileged flow ran stock `auth-otp-form`, which never reads `mfaMethods`:\na box in front of it would have looked like a control and done nothing.\nplatform-backend#1048 puts a gate behind it, so the box governs something.\n\n**The boxes show what is offered, not the stored restriction.** The attribute is\na restriction and an absent one means \"none\" — so rendering it raw left every\nbox empty on an account where in fact every method was on offer. The display\nsaid the opposite of the truth, and the hint text underneath was doing the work\nthe control should have been doing. An unrestricted account now shows all three\nticked, and unticking one withdraws exactly that method.\n\nTicking the last missing box clears the attribute rather than storing all three.\nBoth read as unrestricted, but only one of them silently freezes the account\nagainst any method added later.\n\nThe note that remains is the single case where a ticked state and reality can\nstill differ, and it is a deliberate one: if no other method is usable for that\nuser, the authenticator app is offered even when unticked. A restriction is not\nallowed to close the last door.\n\n  UserDetailDrawer.mfa.spec        15 tests\n  user-management drawer suite  10 files, 67 tests, 0 failures\n\nRefs: gitops#3251, platform-backend#1048\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbcM/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKKcQAE5Ab4t4U908fCEPB6uBMzFI\n97M/Z7Yw/UI5XzXFqpTmgD58n+Dw0W34XX8InOe/BN2BGFSXA2GdRUVb6L+Plnwx\nzNQ2aTBN7Wu3ro+5gztffQVgVgcqmQyc/aOCDZQiUsabxwwhe4Y3a98M3Nm/yBMA\n5YrJALh9hhLLO3NtHX6P5OSPt4pIV3jPloBSbbsF253ubWTatG/C393M1fNvoeIZ\nUEzGS/VE9JACWx8DB2pXgwx+2H4mUQJibqAEMkbDFeAXas03rJDibghQvO2CUlcO\nMH2M4fcktCt2HAwwSU3fMBE9lp3B0ueLM987g0RvxXQ6D3iH4YZF5RJDJXi/h15v\nth7D7grEAIWjGz4Mi1Cs3eeot96g48AZkX3556SGjNuukMLfYVpJ0kmlMXJa4foo\n1OqkaoV3gnyU9dhMhQbymz0VQ34eeV6uldDWyGF4q7Nqj3c/rGpQ4ZmOWWIqsm6P\nLykJ9HogDVvynl5bXtKvh7cFCMdpqnBQhGCNlh8HRHI65DXwalwC3VQNtm+TkzaP\nwAry/G4nkPlYpDoL2oFXQ1k05RoPFsSfsH+RR0W3425Z0inNjtn9Ooc+Nk9gCCos\nPiLEtPrnyafu4TKjqW2ltO1EAM4GDqGN8NPeyRGDpjt7N0Ntl48O2l6l2HxWSPYm\nzN7ggm+JJ4GkFeUFAn5I\n=xFBi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T09:58:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/b4fa6d0eb9d0b93d02581c1381c8f3418a092cfb","node_id":"C_kwDOSLwOTNoAKGI0ZmE2ZDBlYjlkMGI5M2QwMjU4MWMxMzgxYzhmMzQxOGEwOTJjZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-web/commit/a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825","sha":"a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825"}],"sha":"b4fa6d0eb9d0b93d02581c1381c8f3418a092cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/b4fa6d0eb9d0b93d02581c1381c8f3418a092cfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/commits/a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T08:08:43Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T08:08:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(etik-public): lapsed-channel refusal gets its own view — mailbox stays one click away (#885) (#1100)\n\nBackend (platform-backend #1045) now refuses new intake with 403\nINTAKE_CHANNEL_INACTIVE when the org''s subscription lapsed beyond grace —\nand nothing else. This is the UI half of the owner decision (2026-08-01):\n\n- public-api request() now carries the machine-readable error code, so the\n  UI reacts to the code instead of matching Turkish message text\n- the specific refusal routes to a ChannelInactive view (not an alert line)\n  keeping the two promises the reporter needs: existing reports stay fully\n  reachable (takip/yanıt/ek açık), and external avenues are named — Directive\n  2019/1937 Art. 9(1)(g) obliges that information regardless of channel state\n- any other failure keeps the plain error line; the routing is pinned by a\n  second test so INTAKE_CHANNEL_INACTIVE stays the only view-changing code\n\nEvidence: vitest 34/34 (2 new: refusal view + mailbox reachability; non-lapse\nerrors unchanged). Live browser proof follows the backend image promotion —\nthe test cell still runs the pre-gate image, so the closed state cannot be\nexercised there yet (honest gap, tracked on #885).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"015cee2681490e088045ad6e2518cec648ed1060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/trees/015cee2681490e088045ad6e2518cec648ed1060"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-web/git/commits/a0e360c82d73dbff0a75d27673e289f3d171d825","verification":{"payload":"tree 015cee2681490e088045ad6e2518cec648ed1060\nparent 162872b10c622ee6d1ce459a643af54baf36a61f\nauthor halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1785571723 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785571723 +0300\n\nfeat(etik-public): lapsed-channel refusal gets its own view — mailbox stays one click away (#885) (#1100)\n\nBackend (platform-backend #1045) now refuses new intake with 403\nINTAKE_CHANNEL_INACTIVE when the org''s subscription lapsed beyond grace —\nand nothing else. This is the UI half of the owner decision (2026-08-01):\n\n- public-api request() now carries the machine-readable error code, so the\n  UI reacts to the code instead of matching Turkish message text\n- the specific refusal routes to a ChannelInactive view (not an alert line)\n  keeping the two promises the reporter needs: existing reports stay fully\n  reachable (takip/yanıt/ek açık), and external avenues are named — Directive\n  2019/1937 Art. 9(1)(g) obliges that information regardless of channel state\n- any other failure keeps the plain error line; the routing is pinned by a\n  second test so INTAKE_CHANNEL_INACTIVE stays the only view-changing code\n\nEvidence: vitest 34/34 (2 new: refusal view + mailbox reachability; non-lapse\nerrors unchanged). Live browser proof follows the backend image promotion —\nthe test cell still runs the pre-gate image, so the closed state cannot be\nexercised there yet (honest gap, tracked on #885).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbamLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQFgQAAwU3eHYv04xO2J3jxR0Kxoo\nu99n3TgwVTuK6OdaBcr0grLa0WHERohM4NI2CVhHF3LcOyHHQBAWScUHgwuJkzBA\n38oPn2GiFBGaIJ4Jymz4qB1GqGZBcY81Oz+mc3LkSyjr9DhN2r75+J8uVaeM8Ful\nf9qCV706QDVEix//+eJp9bfo5HbY4QuQuMHzmcv/XTnYXFxrKD1U5j0vMUgb64p7\nM565EC9KZFxR9fLh7E1X/Jh4fj2iRPoQdBMk1cvBGhtnFExtiCk+LGQzKM0zvabE\n9Y