2Z","email":"132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AR-base"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T10:01:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs+ci: add README, LICENSE, SECURITY.md, lint CI, and .env.example (#5)\n\nThere was no top-level README — visitors had to read DEPLOY-VERCEL.md\nto understand what the project is. The new README leads with what the\nproject does, what it''s built on, the security posture, and how to run\nor deploy it; DEPLOY-VERCEL.md stays as the long-form walkthrough.\n\nLICENSE (MIT) and SECURITY.md adopt the same shape Bastion uses, so\noperators have a clear reporting channel and downstream users know\nwhere they stand legally.\n\nThe lint workflow runs `node --check` on every JS file, validates\nvercel.json as parseable JSON, and greps the tree for committed\nAnthropic API keys — the same secret-scan gate that already protects\nBastion.\n\n.env.example documents every var the runtime expects, including the\nnew ALLOWED_ORIGIN added in the API-hardening PR.","tree":{"sha":"c2daf929955f37562b981d591c7c6245dd5fba58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/trees/c2daf929955f37562b981d591c7c6245dd5fba58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/commits/88425c6815450946068dd56fb95c02a4ae818159","verification":{"payload":"tree c2daf929955f37562b981d591c7c6245dd5fba58\nparent 3bb7983753c9205289dc29fa99dd4ab86ae79291\nauthor AR-base <132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com> 1782468102 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782468102 +0530\n\ndocs+ci: add README, LICENSE, SECURITY.md, lint CI, and .env.example (#5)\n\nThere was no top-level README — visitors had to read DEPLOY-VERCEL.md\nto understand what the project is. The new README leads with what the\nproject does, what it''s built on, the security posture, and how to run\nor deploy it; DEPLOY-VERCEL.md stays as the long-form walkthrough.\n\nLICENSE (MIT) and SECURITY.md adop