mments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T10:01:38Z","email":"132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AR-base"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T10:01:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"security: add baseline response headers via vercel.json (#4)\n\nvercel.json now sets HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options,\nReferrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, and a Content-Security-Policy\nwith default-src ''self'' and frame-ancestors ''none''.\n\nThe CSP keeps ''unsafe-inline'' in script-src because index.html relies\non inline onclick handlers (setLang, setRole, q, startApp, etc.).\nRemoving those is a separate refactor; the rest of the CSP still\ndefends meaningfully — connect-src ''self'' blocks data exfiltration,\nimg-src caps where avatars can come from, frame-ancestors blocks\nclickjacking.\n\nimg-src explicitly allows https://www.esaip.org for the bot avatar\nwhich is loaded from there.","tree":{"sha":"e3580de5299bafba72fb6d3fa2e917eaf816b39e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/trees/e3580de5299bafba72fb6d3fa2e917eaf816b39e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/commits/3bb7983753c9205289dc29fa99dd4ab86ae79291","verification":{"payload":"tree e3580de5299bafba72fb6d3fa2e917eaf816b39e\nparent 9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582\nauthor AR-base <132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com> 1782468098 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782468098 +0530\n\nsecurity: add baseline response headers via vercel.json (#4)\n\nvercel.json now sets HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options,\nReferrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, and a Content-Security-Policy\nwith default-src ''self'' and frame-ancestors ''none''.\n\nThe CSP keeps ''unsafe-inline'' in script-src because index.html relies\non inline onclick handlers (setLang, setRole, q, startApp, etc.).\nRemoving those is a separate refactor; the rest of the CSP still\ndefends meaningfully — connect-src ''self'' blocks data exfiltration,\nimg-src caps where avatars can come from, frame-ancestors blocks\nclickjacking.\n\nimg-src explicitly allows https://www.esaip.org for the bot avatar\nwhich is loaded from there.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPk4CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhWsQAArvkylBAGrYG058LTQkyizT\nICXtEPqHnOiV5EkcsMgagtLKU9xVbYoEuMJOj4Wz1sy3SiT1sjiP/BTdPhT1oSEx\nMEiDUTzityGMy2qP6DsOXdhNs2OSr94a7IB4M82+Nn6cIRHTlJjkqJVuTtKH/ubo\nVv2jk4YevG0IfXs9fhqklqvBTjUNJ7PohFo14jn3DXVVR1oT+uyiIhzpP//Pl9l2\n0pllposf6ow7Eepu+dJyq4QH8PjpKdmaOb9sIGp1qLoT6myHdEb1/lFsm7QSYIdD\nypu/XgjE+r5dEPqIQoBq8E/kGO6QdcF9eJBJuFm+3J1YgajRwE+bX621Y9wKZHWM\nPFqWamZc0UiVRRuYH1GfPCdvgprA87ZE+MRzFOEw7NUEvWaCs0VEVP1em+3UE/n/\nxQfr/ghJ5HAx3FbUlDGklSzTwst63V0GIPHH4jLbL1d/pFnYYqzzRSyvt8gu9N9d\nibNczQs4BAYonVfyysC6CeY3uaw5A69uwihr7mmysvfA3NmUGZLKjaoU8NhQnajk\n5tWfoz0Vw4YO0xcmqA6JeFClIucuqycNG4EqG7sUBysVZjbHFq+FmjOWOWgcwGHk\n4EM/mYeBFJBPFPeeQc5cwdWJ533eq+m368xRsqPHjZDP8H8TfTW7utv0ZdNXrw7j\niI7nTVVCWRtjFy13kcn8\n=XVIr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T10:01:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/commit/3bb7983753c9205289dc29fa99dd4ab86ae79291","node_id":"C_kwDOSMPYM9oAKDNiYjc5ODM3NTNjOTIwNTI4OWRjMjlmYTk5ZGQ0YWI4NmFlNzkyOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/commit/9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582","sha":"9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/commits/9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582"}],"sha":"3bb7983753c9205289dc29fa99dd4ab86ae79291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/commits/3bb7983753c9205289dc29fa99dd4ab86ae79291"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132471197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AR-base","id":132471197,"login":"AR-base","node_id":"U_kgDOB-VZnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AR-base","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/commits/9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T10:00:38Z","email":"132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AR-base"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T10:00:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"security: harden /api/chat — rate-limit before auth, CORS allowlist, size caps (#3)\n\nSeveral concerns on the API surface were merged into one pass:\n\n- Rate-limit now runs before the password check, and there''s a separate\n  smaller bucket (10/hour/IP) just for failed authentication. Previously,\n  an attacker brute-forcing /api/chat with the wrong password got 401s\n  for free without counting against any limit.\n\n- Password comparison now uses a SHA-256 digest compare so it runs in\n  constant time over a fixed-length value, closing the (mostly\n  theoretical, over the public internet) timing-attack surface.\n\n- CORS no longer reflects `*` to every origin. The function reads\n  ALLOWED_ORIGIN (optional, comma-separated allowlist) and only echoes\n  matching origins; legitimate same-origin browser traffic from the\n  frontend on the same Vercel domain needs no CORS header at all.\n\n- Message validation caps per-message text length and per-content-block\n  serialized size, so a single 100 MB JSON body can''t blow up the\n  function.\n\n- Upstream model errors are no longer forwarded verbatim — the function\n  returns a generic 502 so we don''t leak Anthropic rate-limit or\n  billing internals to the public.\n\n- A few standard response headers (X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy)\n  are added to every response for defense in depth.\n\nDEPLOY-VERCEL.md no longer suggests the literal string `esaip2026`\nas a password — anyone reading the deploy doc could guess it. The\ninstructions now point to generating a random secret with openssl /\nPowerShell and explain the new ALLOWED_ORIGIN var.","tree":{"sha":"23dd55e4d1a04f4578cefa987dd960bcd247f2f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/trees/23dd55e4d1a04f4578cefa987dd960bcd247f2f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AR-base/esaip-ai-assistant/git/commits/9250be7e6249485546ee3ea053e6d832ad694582","verification":{"payload":"tree 23dd55e4d1a04f4578cefa987dd960bcd247f2f7\nparent 83f0eb1cdb1d32b99a3904e86a8d8812a469b1c2\nauthor AR-base <132471197+AR-base@users.noreply.github.com> 1782468038 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782468038 +0530\n\nsecurity: harden /api/chat — rate-limit before auth, CORS allowlist, size caps (#3)\n\nSeveral concerns on the API surface were merged into one pass:\n\n- Rate-limit now runs before the password check, and there''s a separate\n  smaller bucket (10/hour/IP) just for failed authentication. Previously,\n  an attacker brute-forcing /api/chat with the wrong password got 401s\n  for free without counting against any limit.\n\n- Password comparison now uses a SHA-256 digest compare so it runs in\n  constant time over a fixed-length value, closing the (mostly\n  theoretical, over the public internet) timing-attack surface.\n\n- CORS no longer reflects `*` to every origin. The function reads\n  ALLOWED_ORIGIN (optional, comma-separated allowlist) and only echoes\n  matching origins; legitimate same-origin browser traffic from the\n  frontend on the same Vercel domain needs no CORS header at all.\n\n- Message validation caps per-message text length and per-content-block\n  serialized size, so a single 100 MB JSON body can''t blow up the\n  function.\n\n- Upstream model errors are no longer forwarded verbatim — the function\n  returns a generic 502 so we don''t leak Anthropic rate-limit or\n  billing internals to the public.\n\n- A few standard response headers (X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy)\n  are added to every response for defense in depth.\n\nDEPLOY-VERCEL.md no longer suggests the literal string `esaip2026`\nas a password — anyone reading the deploy doc could guess it. The\ninstructions now point to generating a random secret with openssl /\nPowerShell and explain the new ALLOWED_ORIGIN var.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPk3GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAerUQAHGjl2rP8ryFPDgEq+hnPMRa\nCsNZgR6MS4et1VWsODW/ZuRzdUrhUr1P+wL7gUbgdGCndFJrkdnKwCbEYWVj0