"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/commits/eb7c35e950b83f73d6fd61e89f7d4b377db2ad50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T14:33:46Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T14:33:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Operations Hub dashboard redesign + terminal emulation (#504)\n\n* feat: dashboard Operations Hub redesign + task UX improvements\n\nDashboard redesign (issue #501):\n- Briefing Bar: at-a-glance operational summary replacing decorative header\n- Activity Timeline: real-time mission log with time-ago, source labels, status badges\n- Fleet Status: per-runtime rows with SVG sparklines, session counts, cost tracking\n- Task Pipeline: horizontal flow visualization (Inbox → Done) with bottleneck highlighting\n- System Health: compact expandable bar with CPU, memory, disk, uptime\n- Quick Actions: state-aware contextual actions (errors, reviews, idle agents)\n\nTask improvements:\n- @mention auto-assignment: mentioning an agent in comments auto-assigns unassigned tasks\n- Comment count indicator on task cards (speech bubble icon + count)\n- Agent assignment dropdown in task detail modal\n- Redesigned task detail modal: header with status/priority badges, icon-only actions,\n  prominent assignment row, vertical metadata layout, GitHub pill-style links\n\n* feat: improve loading screen UX with step checklist and progress counter\n\n- Show completed steps with green checkmarks (not just active step)\n- Add step counter (e.g. \"5/9\") and percentage indicator\n- Thicker progress bar for better visibility\n- Completed steps fade to 40% opacity, active step pulses\n- Smoother visual sense of progress during boot sequence\n\n* fix: redesign task pipeline as stage pills instead of stretched bar\n\n- Replace spread-out label row + progress bar with compact stage pills\n- Each stage is a self-contained pill: dot + label + count\n- Active stages are color-coded, empty stages fade out\n- Running stage dot pulses to show activity\n- Chevron arrows between stages instead of text arrows\n- Empty state shown when no tasks exist\n- Bottleneck warning uses a warning icon\n\n* feat: add xterm.js terminal emulation for agent sessions\n\nServer-side PTY proxy:\n- pty-manager.ts: manages node-pty instances with session pool, idle cleanup, multi-client broadcast\n- pty-websocket.ts: WebSocket upgrade handler for /ws/pty with JSON protocol\n- /api/pty/attach: REST endpoint to check PTY support and get WebSocket path\n- mc-server.cjs: custom server wrapper intercepting WebSocket upgrades\n\nClient-side terminal:\n- terminal-view.tsx: xterm.js React wrapper with dark theme, reconnection,\n  mode indicator (RO/RW), connection state overlays\n- terminal-toolbar.tsx: session info bar with view mode toggle (terminal/transcript),\n  interactive mode confirmation, detach button\n\nDependencies: node-pty, @xterm/xterm, @xterm/addon-fit, @xterm/addon-web-links\n\n* feat: cmux-style sidebar, split-pane layout, attention detection, tmux auto-install\n\nSession sidebar redesign (Phase 3):\n- Working directory leaf shown per session card\n- Last user prompt preview with $ prefix\n- Simplified active/recent sections with counts\n- Model info on hover, color tag dots\n- Unified gateway + local into single active/recent groups\n\nSplit-pane layout (Phase 4):\n- 2-horizontal, 2-vertical, and 2x2 grid modes\n- Each pane gets its own terminal + toolbar\n- Layout switcher with visual icons\n- Pane detach (close) per pane\n\nAttention detection (Phase 5):\n- Heuristic scanner for PTY output patterns: [Y/n], errors, approval prompts\n- Debounced (5s) to prevent notification spam\n- clearAttention/hasAttention API for sidebar integration\n\ntmux auto-install:\n- GET /api/pty/setup — check tmux prerequisites, platform detection\n- POST /api/pty/setup — opt-in tmux installation (admin only)\n- Supports brew (macOS), apt/yum (Linux)\n\n* fix: loading screen shows real-time progress instead of all steps at once\n\n- Reduced fade-in delay from 2.4s to 0.8s so progress shows immediately\n- Show only the current active step label (not all completed steps)\n- Clean \"Ready\" checkmark when all steps complete\n- Removed the 9-line step checklist that showed everything at once\n- Progress bar still shows smooth fill from 0% to 100%\n\n* fix: Claude/Codex session avatars, chat loading state, footer to sidebar\n\n- Add claude-logo.png as imageSrc for claude-code sessions (was showing\n  generic \"C\" letter while Hermes/Codex showed brand logos)\n- Add loading indicator to conversation list (\"Loading sessions...\" with\n  pulsing dot) instead of showing \"No conversations yet\" on first render\n- Remove footer from main content area\n- Add \"Built with care by nyk\" attribution to sidebar (only when expanded)\n\n* feat: wire xterm.js terminal into session viewer + fix message padding\n\n- Add Terminal/Transcript toggle in session info bar for active\n  claude-code and codex-cli sessions\n- TerminalView renders when Terminal mode is selected, falls back to\n  transcript on PTY error\n- Fix tool result padding: consistent px-3 py-1.5 with ▸ prefix\n  matching tool use visual alignment\n\n* fix: terminal tab stays selected when session re-renders\n\nThe viewMode state was resetting to ''transcript'' on every parent\nre-render because the session object changes on each poll cycle.\nNow tracks session ID with a ref and only resets viewMode when\nthe user actually switches to a different session.\n\n* fix: terminal tab no longer flips back on re-render\n\nRoot cause: supportsPty depended on session.active which changes on\nevery poll cycle. When session.active briefly evaluates differently\nduring a re-render, the conditional rendering switched from Terminal\nto Transcript view even though viewMode state was still ''terminal''.\n\nFix: Renamed to isPtyCapableKind (based only on session kind, not\nactive state). The toggle is now stable — viewMode state controls\nwhich view renders, and only resets when switching to a new session.\nAlso added stable key={sessionId} to prevent component remounting.\n\n* feat: wire split-pane view, attention rings, and session controls\n\nSplit-pane integration:\n- \"Split\" button in session header opens the session in split view\n- Split pane bar with \"+ Add\" and \"Close all\" controls\n- SplitPaneLayout renders when panes are active, single view otherwise\n- Max 4 panes, deduplication by session ID\n- \"Switch to transcript\" from split pane navigates back to single view\n\nAttention notification rings:\n- sessionAttention state in store (Record<sessionId, ''waiting''|''error''>)\n- Blue ring animation on session avatar when attention detected\n- Error dot (red) replaces green active dot when error detected\n- Auto-clear attention when user selects the session\n\nStore additions:\n- splitPanes, addSplitPane, removeSplitPane, clearSplitPanes\n- sessionAttention, setSessionAttention\n\n* fix: boot loader no longer blocks on slow session/memory loading\n\nSessions (/api/sessions) scans hundreds of JSONL files and can take\nseveral seconds. Memory graph is similarly slow. Both were blocking\nthe boot sequence — the loader showed \"Loading active sessions\" for\nthe entire duration.\n\nFix: Mark sessions and memory steps as done immediately, let the\nactual data load in the background. The dashboard renders instantly\nand session list populates when data arrives.\n\nAlso reduced boot-complete delay from 400ms to 150ms.\n\n* fix: eliminate loader flash on boot completion\n\nThe loader had a 300ms opacity CSS transition that conflicted with\nthe 150ms setTimeout before setBootComplete(). The dashboard content\npopped in while the loader was mid-fade, causing a visual flash.\n\nFix:\n- Remove transition-opacity from loader (clean instant swap)\n- Remove setTimeout delay — setBootComplete fires synchronously\n  when all steps are done\n\n* fix: add PTY API routes to openapi.json for contract parity\n\nAdd /api/pty/attach (GET, POST) and /api/pty/setup (GET, POST)\nto the OpenAPI spec so the api:parity check passes in CI.\n\n* fix: validate runtime install actually succeeded before reporting success\n\nOpenClaw and Hermes installers use curl piped to bash, which can\nsilently fail (e.g., curl not found in Docker containers). The bash\nprocess itself exits 0 even if curl fails, causing false success.\n\nFix:\n- Add set -o pipefail to propagate curl failures\n- Verify binary exists after install (detectBinary/isHermesInstalled)\n- If command exits 0 but binary not found, report failure with\n  \"curl may not be installed\" hint\n\n* fix: add curl to Docker runtime image for agent runtime installers\n\nThe runtime stage (node:22-slim) did not include curl, causing\nOpenClaw and Hermes installer scripts to silently fail in Docker.\n\nAlso adds post-install binary verification and pipefail to\ncatch installer failures properly.\n\n* fix: add ca-certificates to Docker image for HTTPS downloads\n\n* fix: add ~/.local/bin to install PATH for uv-installed Python\n\nHermes installer uses uv to install Python, which places binaries\nin ~/.local/bin. This path wasn''t included in the install environment\nPATH, causing subsequent installer steps to fail finding Python.\n\n* fix: add python3 and git to Docker runtime for Hermes installer\n\nThe Hermes installer uses uv to download Python, but uv stores it\nin a managed directory not on PATH. Adding python3 directly to the\nDocker image avoids this issue. Git is also needed by some installers.\n\n* feat: polished loading state for runtime install cards\n\nReplace boring ''Installing...'' text with a full-card loading state:\n- Spinning ring with runtime initial in center\n- Shimmer gradient overlay across the card\n- Indeterminate progress bar at bottom edge\n- Card border glows primary color during install\n- Clean transition back to normal state on completion\n\n* feat: live install output + fix non-interactive Docker installs\n\nInstall card improvements:\n- Show last 6 lines of live install output during installation\n- Green-themed shimmer and progress bar\n- Spinner with runtime initial + name header\n\nDocker install fixes:\n- Set CI=1, NONINTERACTIVE=1, HERMES_NONINTERACTIVE=1 env vars\n- Pipe yes to handle interactive prompts (fixes /dev/tty error)\n- Both OpenClaw and Hermes installers now run non-interactively\n\n* fix: Hermes/OpenClaw install uses --skip-setup and live output\n\n- Hermes installer now passes --skip-setup flag (MC handles setup in\n  its own UI via the RuntimeSetupModal)\n- OpenClaw installer passes --non-interactive flag\n- Removed yes pipe workaround — the flags handle non-interactivity\n- Install card shows last 6 lines of live stdout/stderr in a dark\n  terminal box, updated every 2s during installation\n- Green-themed shimmer and indeterminate progress bar on install card\n- Fixes /dev/tty error in Docker containers\n\n* fix: detect hermes binary at Docker install paths\n\nisHermesInstalled() only checked system PATH for ''hermes'' and\n''hermes-agent''. In Docker, hermes installs to {dataDir}/.local/bin/\nand ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/ — neither on system PATH.\n\nNow checks these additional paths:\n- {dataDir}/.local/bin/hermes\n- ~/.local/bin/hermes\n- ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes\n\nSame fix applied to detectHermes() version check in agent-runtimes.ts.\n\n* fix: hermes detection checks dataDir paths for Docker (HOME=/nonexistent)\n\nIn Docker, os.homedir() returns /nonexistent since the nextjs user\nhas no real home directory. The installer uses dataDir (/app/.data)\nas HOME, so hermes ends up at /app/.data/.local/bin/hermes and\n/app/.data/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes.\n\nDetection now checks dataDir-based paths first, before homedir paths.\n\n* debug: add logging to hermes detection for Docker troubleshooting\n\n* feat: polished install loading for settings + runtime setup modal\n\nSettings panel runtime cards now match onboarding style:\n- Shimmer overlay + indeterminate progress bar during install\n- Spinning ring with runtime initial\n- Live output tail (last 6 lines) in dark terminal box\n- Configure button for OpenClaw/Hermes after install\n- RuntimeSetupModal for guided post-install setup\n\n* fix: clear hermes detection cache on runtime status API call\n\nAfter install succeeds, the UI polls GET /api/agent-runtimes which\nused a 30-second cached ''not installed'' result. Now clears the\nhermes detection cache before each detection so freshly installed\nruntimes are found immediately.\n\n* fix: hermes hook writes to dataDir in Docker (HOME=/nonexistent)\n\nHERMES_HOME was hardcoded to config.homeDir/.hermes which resolves\nto /nonexistent/.hermes in Docker. Now checks dataDir/.hermes first\n(where the installer actually puts Hermes), falling back to homeDir.\n\n* fix: hermes setup verify step doesn''t block on gateway + actionable provider config\n\n- Verify step now shows ''Done'' button directly (not blocked by gateway)\n- Gateway card shows ''Not started (optional)'' instead of just ''-''\n- Provider config section is more actionable: shows hermes model command\n  and multiple provider options (Nous Portal, Anthropic, OpenAI)\n- Gateway info is a soft note, not a blocking condition\n- Removed redundant ''done'' step — verify completes directly\n\n* feat: full Hermes setup wizard — provider config, identity, next steps\n\nReplaced the 2-step hook+verify flow with a 4-step guided wizard:\n1. Hook — install MC hook (unchanged)\n2. Provider — choose LLM provider (Anthropic/OpenAI/OpenRouter/Nous),\n   enter API key, saved to ~/.hermes/.env\n3. Identity — optional SOUL.md personality config\n4. Ready — summary + next steps (hermes cli, gateway setup)\n\nNew API actions:\n- POST /api/hermes { action: ''set-env'' } — write API key to .env\n- POST /api/hermes { action: ''set-soul'' } — write SOUL.md content\nOnly allows allowlisted env keys (ANTHROPIC/OPENAI/OPENROUTER/NOUS).\n\nEach step is skippable. Gateway is noted as optional, not blocking.\n\n* feat: add OAuth OpenAI option, gateway/channels step, Google AI provider\n\nHermes setup wizard now has 5 steps:\n1. Hook — install MC hook\n2. Provider — Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenAI OAuth, OpenRouter, Nous Portal, Google AI\n   - OAuth option shows hermes model command instead of API key input\n3. Identity — optional SOUL.md personality\n4. Gateway — set up messaging channels (Telegram/Discord/Slack/WhatsApp/Signal)\n   with step-by-step commands, non-blocking (skip for now)\n5. Ready — summary + next steps\n\nAlso added Google AI and XAI to API env key allowlist.\n\n* feat: copyable commands throughout Hermes setup wizard\n\nAll terminal commands in the setup wizard now have a ''Copy'' button\nthat copies the command to clipboard. Used in:\n- OpenAI OAuth step (hermes model openai, hermes setup)\n- Gateway step (hermes gateway setup, hermes gateway start)\n- Ready step (hermes, hermes setup, hermes gateway setup/start)\n\nCopyableCommand component shows $ prefix, command text, Copy button,\nand a description label.\n\n* feat: real-time streaming install output + faster polling\n\nBefore: runCommand collected all stdout/stderr and stored it only\nwhen the process exited. The UI showed ''Installing...'' with no\nprogress for the entire 60-90 second install.\n\nAfter: runCommand streams output chunks via onData callback directly\ninto job.output as they arrive. The UI polls every 1s (was 2s) and\nshows the last 6 lines of live installer output — you see each step\nas it happens (Downloading Python, Cloning repo, Installing deps, etc).\n\n* feat: runnable commands in Hermes setup — Run button executes server-side\n\nCopyableCommand now has an optional Run button that executes the\ncommand server-side via POST /api/hermes { action: ''run-command'' }.\n\nSecurity: only allows commands starting with ''hermes'', uses the\nvenv binary path, sets non-interactive env vars, 30s timeout.\n\nCommands with Run buttons:\n- hermes model openai (OAuth setup)\n- hermes setup (full interactive setup)\n- hermes gateway setup / start\n- hermes (start chatting)\n\nOutput streams into a dark terminal box below the command.\n\n* feat: polished security scan loading with animated category checklist\n\nReplaced the tiny ''Scanning...'' spinner with a full loading state:\n- Spinning ring with security icon in center\n- Title + subtitle explaining what''s happening\n- Each category (Credentials, Network, OpenClaw, Runtime, OS) shown\n  as a row with staggered fade-in animation\n- Indeterminate progress bar per category with staggered delays\n- Matches the visual style of the runtime install loading cards\n\n* fix: replace interactive commands with non-interactive hermes config set\n\nhermes model and hermes setup require a TTY and can''t run from the\nweb UI. Replaced with hermes config set commands that work headless:\n- hermes config set model.provider openai\n- hermes config set model.default gpt-4.1\n- hermes status, hermes doctor (for diagnostics)\n- hermes gateway start (non-interactive)\n\nOpenAI OAuth option now also shows an API key input as fallback.\nReady step shows practical non-interactive commands with note about\ninteractive commands needing the Chat panel terminal.\n\n* feat: dynamic provider/model selection in Hermes setup wizard\n\nProvider config commands now dynamically update based on selection:\n- Each provider card defines hermesProvider name and available models\n- hermes config set commands update to match selected provider\n- Model dropdown shows provider-specific models (e.g., claude-sonnet-4-6\n  for Anthropic, gpt-4.1 for OpenAI, gemini-2.5-pro for Google)\n- Clicking a provider card auto-selects its default model\n- API key input label updates to match provider name\n- Save works with or without key (Continue if no key entered)\n\n* feat: clickable model grid + custom model input in provider setup\n\nReplaced the dropdown with a grid of model buttons per provider:\n- Click a model to select it (highlighted with primary border)\n- Custom model text input below for models not in the list\n- Model grid updates when switching providers\n- selectedModel initializes to anthropic''s default (claude-sonnet-4-6)\n- Both ''Set provider'' and ''Set model'' have Run buttons\n- Custom model input takes precedence when filled\n\n* feat: clean up provider UI — merged OAuth into OpenAI, added xAI/Codex models\n\n- Merged ''OpenAI'' and ''OpenAI OAuth'' into single ''OpenAI'' card\n- Added xAI (Grok) provider\n- Added codex-mini-latest, gpt-4.1-nano to OpenAI models\n- Added deephermes, deepseek, llama-4 to OpenRouter models\n- Compact model pills (flex-wrap) instead of 2-col grid\n- Tighter spacing throughout the provider step\n- Custom model input below the model pills\n\n* fix: gateway commands for Docker — remove systemd-dependent start\n\nhermes gateway start requires systemd (not available in Docker).\nReplaced with:\n- hermes status / hermes doctor as runnable commands\n- Gateway commands shown as copy-paste reference with explanations\n  (gateway setup = interactive, gateway = foreground, gateway start = systemd)\n- Ready step shows status/doctor/version as runnable diagnostics\n\n* feat: inline provider/model config in onboarding + OpenClaw migration\n\nAfter Hermes installs in onboarding, the runtime card now shows:\n- Quick Setup section with provider pills (Anthropic/OpenAI/OpenRouter/\n  Google/Nous/xAI) and model pills per provider\n- API key input inline in the card\n- ''Apply Configuration'' button that sets provider, model, and API key\n- ''Migrate from OpenClaw'' option if OpenClaw is detected (runs\n  hermes claw migrate --preset user-data)\n- Setup modal still available via full wizard button\n\nAll config happens right in the card — no need to open a modal for\nbasic provider setup.\n\n* feat: add gpt-5.3-codex model + OpenAI OAuth hint\n\n- Added gpt-5.3-codex and gpt-4.1-nano to OpenAI model lists\n  (both onboarding inline config and setup modal)\n- Added OAuth hint under OpenAI API key field: ''Or use OAuth:\n  run hermes model in a terminal for browser login''\n\n* feat: dropdown selects for provider/model in quick setup\n\nReplaced pill buttons with compact dropdown selects — cleaner\nfor the small card space. Provider and model side by side.\n\n* feat: add OpenAI OAuth option in onboarding quick setup\n\n- Separate ''OpenAI (API Key)'' and ''OpenAI (OAuth)'' in provider dropdown\n- OAuth shows device code instructions instead of API key input\n- API key input hidden when OAuth selected\n\n* feat(onboarding): run OpenAI OAuth device flow from quick setup\n\n- add interactive /api/hermes run-oauth-model action using PTY\n\n- add Run button + output panel + clickable login URL in OpenAI OAuth setup\n\n- clarify Node version guard as >=22 (future versions allowed)\n\n* feat: finalize dashboard ops updates and docker runtime fixes\n\n* feat(onboarding): improve oauth log UX and device-code flow\n\n* fix(onboarding): auto-advance hermes model oauth prompt\n\n* fix(onboarding): widen runtimes modal and rebalance card layout\n\n* fix(onboarding): extend Hermes device-code auth timeout\n\n* fix(security): enforce auth and validation for PTY websocket upgrades","tree":{"sha":"c325095b9e454b3ece9c9f5d705b7212a59deeb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/git/trees/c325095b9e454b3ece9c9f5d705b7212a59deeb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/git/commits/eb7c35e950b83f73d6fd61e89f7d4b377db2ad50","verification":{"payload":"tree c325095b9e454b3ece9c9f5d705b7212a59deeb1\nparent 445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1774967626 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774967626 +0700\n\nfeat: Operations Hub dashboard redesign + terminal emulation (#504)\n\n* feat: dashboard Operations Hub redesign + task UX improvements\n\nDashboard redesign (issue #501):\n- Briefing Bar: at-a-glance operational summary replacing decorative header\n- Activity Timeline: real-time mission log with time-ago, source labels, status badges\n- Fleet Status: per-runtime rows with SVG sparklines, session counts, cost tracking\n- Task Pipeline: horizontal flow visualization (Inbox → Done) with bottleneck highlighting\n- System Health: compact expandable bar with CPU, memory, disk, uptime\n- Quick Actions: state-aware contextual actions (errors, reviews, idle agents)\n\nTask improvements:\n- @mention auto-assignment: mentioning an agent in comments auto-assigns unassigned tasks\n- Comment count indicator on task cards (speech bubble icon + count)\n- Agent assignment dropdown in task detail modal\n- Redesigned task detail modal: header with status/priority badges, icon-only actions,\n  prominent assignment row, vertical metadata layout, GitHub pill-style links\n\n* feat: improve loading screen UX with step checklist and progress counter\n\n- Show completed steps with green checkmarks (not just active step)\n- Add step counter (e.g. \"5/9\") and percentage indicator\n- Thicker progress bar for better visibility\n- Completed steps fade to 40% opacity, active step pulses\n- Smoother visual sense of progress during boot sequence\n\n* fix: redesign task pipeline as stage pills instead of stretched bar\n\n- Replace spread-out label row + progress bar with compact stage pills\n- Each stage is a self-contained pill: dot + label + count\n- Active stages are color-coded, empty stages fade out\n- Running stage dot pulses to show activity\n- Chevron arrows between stages instead of text arrows\n- Empty state shown when no tasks exist\n- Bottleneck warning uses a warning icon\n\n* feat: add xterm.js terminal emulation for agent sessions\n\nServer-side PTY proxy:\n- pty-manager.ts: manages node-pty instances with session pool, idle cleanup, multi-client broadcast\n- pty-websocket.ts: WebSocket upgrade handler for /ws/pty with JSON protocol\n- /api/pty/attach: REST endpoint to check PTY support and get WebSocket path\n- mc-server.cjs: custom server wrapper intercepting WebSocket upgrades\n\nClient-side terminal:\n- terminal-view.tsx: xterm.js React wrapper with dark theme, reconnection,\n  mode indicator (RO/RW), connection state overlays\n- terminal-toolbar.tsx: session info bar with view mode toggle (terminal/transcript),\n  interactive mode confirmation, detach button\n\nDependencies: node-pty, @xterm/xterm, @xterm/addon-fit, @xterm/addon-web-links\n\n* feat: cmux-style sidebar, split-pane layout, attention detection, tmux auto-install\n\nSession sidebar redesign (Phase 3):\n- Working directory leaf shown per session card\n- Last user prompt preview with $ prefix\n- Simplified active/recent sections with counts\n- Model info on hover, color tag dots\n- Unified gateway + local into single active/recent groups\n\nSplit-pane layout (Phase 4):\n- 2-horizontal, 2-vertical, and 2x2 grid modes\n- Each pane gets its own terminal + toolbar\n- Layout switcher with visual icons\n- Pane detach (close) per pane\n\nAttention detection (Phase 5):\n- Heuristic scanner for PTY output patterns: [Y/n], errors, approval prompts\n- Debounced (5s) to prevent notification spam\n- clearAttention/hasAttention API for sidebar integration\n\ntmux auto-install:\n- GET /api/pty/setup — check tmux prerequisites, platform detection\n- POST /api/pty/setup — opt-in tmux installation (admin only)\n- Supports brew (macOS), apt/yum (Linux)\n\n* fix: loading screen shows real-time progress instead of all steps at once\n\n- Reduced fade-in delay from 2.4s to 0.8s so progress shows immediately\n- Show only the current active step label (not all completed steps)\n- Clean \"Ready\" checkmark when all steps complete\n- Removed the 9-line step checklist that showed everything at once\n- Progress bar still shows smooth fill from 0% to 100%\n\n* fix: Claude/Codex session avatars, chat loading state, footer to sidebar\n\n- Add claude-logo.png as imageSrc for claude-code sessions (was showing\n  generic \"C\" letter while Hermes/Codex showed brand logos)\n- Add loading indicator to conversation list (\"Loading sessions...\" with\n  pulsing dot) instead of showing \"No conversations yet\" on first render\n- Remove footer from main content area\n- Add \"Built with care by nyk\" attribution to sidebar (only when expanded)\n\n* feat: wire xterm.js terminal into session viewer + fix message padding\n\n- Add Terminal/Transcript toggle in session info bar for active\n  claude-code and codex-cli sessions\n- TerminalView renders when Terminal mode is selected, falls back to\n  transcript on PTY error\n- Fix tool result padding: consistent px-3 py-1.5 with ▸ prefix\n  matching tool use visual alignment\n\n* fix: terminal tab stays selected when session re-renders\n\nThe viewMode state was resetting to ''transcript'' on every parent\nre-render because the session object changes on each poll cycle.\nNow tracks session ID with a ref and only resets viewMode when\nthe user actually switches to a different session.\n\n* fix: terminal tab no longer flips back on re-render\n\nRoot cause: supportsPty depended on session.active which changes on\nevery poll cycle. When session.active briefly evaluates differently\nduring a re-render, the conditional rendering switched from Terminal\nto Transcript view even though viewMode state was still ''terminal''.\n\nFix: Renamed to isPtyCapableKind (based only on session kind, not\nactive state). The toggle is now stable — viewMode state controls\nwhich view renders, and only resets when switching to a new session.\nAlso added stable key={sessionId} to prevent component remounting.\n\n* feat: wire split-pane view, attention rings, and session controls\n\nSplit-pane integration:\n- \"Split\" button in session header opens the session in split view\n- Split pane bar with \"+ Add\" and \"Close all\" controls\n- SplitPaneLayout renders when panes are active, single view otherwise\n- Max 4 panes, deduplication by session ID\n- \"Switch to transcript\" from split pane navigates back to single view\n\nAttention notification rings:\n- sessionAttention state in store (Record<sessionId, ''waiting''|''error''>)\n- Blue ring animation on session avatar when attention detected\n- Error dot (red) replaces green active dot when error detected\n- Auto-clear attention when user selects the session\n\nStore additions:\n- splitPanes, addSplitPane, removeSplitPane, clearSplitPanes\n- sessionAttention, setSessionAttention\n\n* fix: boot loader no longer blocks on slow session/memory loading\n\nSessions (/api/sessions) scans hundreds of JSONL files and can take\nseveral seconds. Memory graph is similarly slow. Both were blocking\nthe boot sequence — the loader showed \"Loading active sessions\" for\nthe entire duration.\n\nFix: Mark sessions and memory steps as done immediately, let the\nactual data load in the background. The dashboard renders instantly\nand session list populates when data arrives.\n\nAlso reduced boot-complete delay from 400ms to 150ms.\n\n* fix: eliminate loader flash on boot completion\n\nThe loader had a 300ms opacity CSS transition that conflicted with\nthe 150ms setTimeout before setBootComplete(). The dashboard content\npopped in while the loader was mid-fade, causing a visual flash.\n\nFix:\n- Remove transition-opacity from loader (clean instant swap)\n- Remove setTimeout delay — setBootComplete fires synchronously\n  when all steps are done\n\n* fix: add PTY API routes to openapi.json for contract parity\n\nAdd /api/pty/attach (GET, POST) and /api/pty/setup (GET, POST)\nto the OpenAPI spec so the api:parity check passes in CI.\n\n* fix: validate runtime install actually succeeded before reporting success\n\nOpenClaw and Hermes installers use curl piped to bash, which can\nsilently fail (e.g., curl not found in Docker containers). The bash\nprocess itself exits 0 even if curl fails, causing false success.\n\nFix:\n- Add set -o pipefail to propagate curl failures\n- Verify binary exists after install (detectBinary/isHermesInstalled)\n- If command exits 0 but binary not found, report failure with\n  \"curl may not be installed\" hint\n\n* fix: add curl to Docker runtime image for agent runtime installers\n\nThe runtime stage (node:22-slim) did not include curl, causing\nOpenClaw and Hermes installer scripts to silently fail in Docker.\n\nAlso adds post-install binary verification and pipefail to\ncatch installer failures properly.\n\n* fix: add ca-certificates to Docker image for HTTPS downloads\n\n* fix: add ~/.local/bin to install PATH for uv-installed Python\n\nHermes installer uses uv to install Python, which places binaries\nin ~/.local/bin. This path wasn''t included in the install environment\nPATH, causing subsequent installer steps to fail finding Python.\n\n* fix: add python3 and git to Docker runtime for Hermes installer\n\nThe Hermes installer uses uv to download Python, but uv stores it\nin a managed directory not on PATH. Adding python3 directly to the\nDocker image avoids this issue. Git is also needed by some installers.\n\n* feat: polished loading state for runtime install cards\n\nReplace boring ''Installing...'' text with a full-card loading state:\n- Spinning ring with runtime initial in center\n- Shimmer gradient overlay across the card\n- Indeterminate progress bar at bottom edge\n- Card border glows primary color during install\n- Clean transition back to normal state on completion\n\n* feat: live install output + fix non-interactive Docker installs\n\nInstall card improvements:\n- Show last 6 lines of live install output during installation\n- Green-themed shimmer and progress bar\n- Spinner with runtime initial + name header\n\nDocker install fixes:\n- Set CI=1, NONINTERACTIVE=1, HERMES_NONINTERACTIVE=1 env vars\n- Pipe yes to handle interactive prompts (fixes /dev/tty error)\n- Both OpenClaw and Hermes installers now run non-interactively\n\n* fix: Hermes/OpenClaw install uses --skip-setup and live output\n\n- Hermes installer now passes --skip-setup flag (MC handles setup in\n  its own UI via the RuntimeSetupModal)\n- OpenClaw installer passes --non-interactive flag\n- Removed yes pipe workaround — the flags handle non-interactivity\n- Install card shows last 6 lines of live stdout/stderr in a dark\n  terminal box, updated every 2s during installation\n- Green-themed shimmer and indeterminate progress bar on install card\n- Fixes /dev/tty error in Docker containers\n\n* fix: detect hermes binary at Docker install paths\n\nisHermesInstalled() only checked system PATH for ''hermes'' and\n''hermes-agent''. In Docker, hermes installs to {dataDir}/.local/bin/\nand ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/ — neither on system PATH.\n\nNow checks these additional paths:\n- {dataDir}/.local/bin/hermes\n- ~/.local/bin/hermes\n- ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes\n\nSame fix applied to detectHermes() version check in agent-runtimes.ts.\n\n* fix: hermes detection checks dataDir paths for Docker (HOME=/nonexistent)\n\nIn Docker, os.homedir() returns /nonexistent since the nextjs user\nhas no real home directory. The installer uses dataDir (/app/.data)\nas HOME, so hermes ends up at /app/.data/.local/bin/hermes and\n/app/.data/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes.\n\nDetection now checks dataDir-based paths first, before homedir paths.\n\n* debug: add logging to hermes detection for Docker troubleshooting\n\n* feat: polished install loading for settings + runtime setup modal\n\nSettings panel runtime cards now match onboarding style:\n- Shimmer overlay + indeterminate progress bar during install\n- Spinning ring with runtime initial\n- Live output tail (last 6 lines) in dark terminal box\n- Configure button for OpenClaw/Hermes after install\n- RuntimeSetupModal for guided post-install setup\n\n* fix: clear hermes detection cache on runtime status API call\n\nAfter install succeeds, the UI polls GET /api/agent-runtimes which\nused a 30-second cached ''not installed'' result. Now clears the\nhermes detection cache before each detection so freshly installed\nruntimes are found immediately.\n\n* fix: hermes hook writes to dataDir in Docker (HOME=/nonexistent)\n\nHERMES_HOME was hardcoded to config.homeDir/.hermes which resolves\nto /nonexistent/.hermes in Docker. Now checks dataDir/.hermes first\n(where the installer actually puts Hermes), falling back to homeDir.\n\n* fix: hermes setup verify step doesn''t block on gateway + actionable provider config\n\n- Verify step now shows ''Done'' button directly (not blocked by gateway)\n- Gateway card shows ''Not started (optional)'' instead of just ''-''\n- Provider config section is more actionable: shows hermes model command\n  and multiple provider options (Nous Portal, Anthropic, OpenAI)\n- Gateway info is a soft note, not a blocking condition\n- Removed redundant ''done'' step — verify completes directly\n\n* feat: full Hermes setup wizard — provider config, identity, next steps\n\nReplaced the 2-step hook+verify flow with a 4-step guided wizard:\n1. Hook — install MC hook (unchanged)\n2. Provider — choose LLM provider (Anthropic/OpenAI/OpenRouter/Nous),\n   enter API key, saved to ~/.hermes/.env\n3. Identity — optional SOUL.md personality config\n4. Ready — summary + next steps (hermes cli, gateway setup)\n\nNew API actions:\n- POST /api/hermes { action: ''set-env'' } — write API key to .env\n- POST /api/hermes { action: ''set-soul'' } — write SOUL.md content\nOnly allows allowlisted env keys (ANTHROPIC/OPENAI/OPENROUTER/NOUS).\n\nEach step is skippable. Gateway is noted as optional, not blocking.\n\n* feat: add OAuth OpenAI option, gateway/channels step, Google AI provider\n\nHermes setup wizard now has 5 steps:\n1. Hook — install MC hook\n2. Provider — Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenAI OAuth, OpenRouter, Nous Portal, Google AI\n   - OAuth option shows hermes model command instead of API key input\n3. Identity — optional SOUL.md personality\n4. Gateway — set up messaging channels (Telegram/Discord/Slack/WhatsApp/Signal)\n   with step-by-step commands, non-blocking (skip for now)\n5. Ready — summary + next steps\n\nAlso added Google AI and XAI to API env key allowlist.\n\n* feat: copyable commands throughout Hermes setup wizard\n\nAll terminal commands in the setup wizard now have a ''Copy'' button\nthat copies the command to clipboard. Used in:\n- OpenAI OAuth step (hermes model openai, hermes setup)\n- Gateway step (hermes gateway setup, hermes gateway start)\n- Ready step (hermes, hermes setup, hermes gateway setup/start)\n\nCopyableCommand component shows $ prefix, command text, Copy button,\nand a description label.\n\n* feat: real-time streaming install output + faster polling\n\nBefore: runCommand collected all stdout/stderr and stored it only\nwhen the process exited. The UI showed ''Installing...'' with no\nprogress for the entire 60-90 second install.\n\nAfter: runCommand streams output chunks via onData callback directly\ninto job.output as they arrive. The UI polls every 1s (was 2s) and\nshows the last 6 lines of live installer output — you see each step\nas it happens (Downloading Python, Cloning repo, Installing deps, etc).\n\n* feat: runnable commands in Hermes setup — Run button executes server-side\n\nCopyableCommand now has an optional Run button that executes the\ncommand server-side via POST /api/hermes { action: ''run-command'' }.\n\nSecurity: only allows commands starting with ''hermes'', uses the\nvenv binary path, sets non-interactive env vars, 30s timeout.\n\nCommands with Run buttons:\n- hermes model openai (OAuth setup)\n- hermes setup (full interactive setup)\n- hermes gateway setup / start\n- hermes (start chatting)\n\nOutput streams into a dark terminal box below the command.\n\n* feat: polished security scan loading with animated category checklist\n\nReplaced the tiny ''Scanning...'' spinner with a full loading state:\n- Spinning ring with security icon in center\n- Title + subtitle explaining what''s happening\n- Each category (Credentials, Network, OpenClaw, Runtime, OS) shown\n  as a row with staggered fade-in animation\n- Indeterminate progress bar per category with staggered delays\n- Matches the visual style of the runtime install loading cards\n\n* fix: replace interactive commands with non-interactive hermes config set\n\nhermes model and hermes setup require a TTY and can''t run from the\nweb UI. Replaced with hermes config set commands that work headless:\n- hermes config set model.provider openai\n- hermes config set model.default gpt-4.1\n- hermes status, hermes doctor (for diagnostics)\n- hermes gateway start (non-interactive)\n\nOpenAI OAuth option now also shows an API key input as fallback.\nReady step shows practical non-interactive commands with note about\ninteractive commands needing the Chat panel terminal.\n\n* feat: dynamic provider/model selection in Hermes setup wizard\n\nProvider config commands now dynamically update based on selection:\n- Each provider card defines hermesProvider name and available models\n- hermes config set commands update to match selected provider\n- Model dropdown shows provider-specific models (e.g., claude-sonnet-4-6\n  for Anthropic, gpt-4.1 for OpenAI, gemini-2.5-pro for Google)\n- Clicking a provider card auto-selects its default model\n- API key input label updates to match provider name\n- Save works with or without key (Continue if no key entered)\n\n* feat: clickable model grid + custom model input in provider setup\n\nReplaced the dropdown with a grid of model buttons per provider:\n- Click a model to select it (highlighted with primary border)\n- Custom model text input below for models not in the list\n- Model grid updates when switching providers\n- selectedModel initializes to anthropic''s default (claude-sonnet-4-6)\n- Both ''Set provider'' and ''Set model'' have Run buttons\n- Custom model input takes precedence when filled\n\n* feat: clean up provider UI — merged OAuth into OpenAI, added xAI/Codex models\n\n- Merged ''OpenAI'' and ''OpenAI OAuth'' into single ''OpenAI'' card\n- Added xAI (Grok) provider\n- Added codex-mini-latest, gpt-4.1-nano to OpenAI models\n- Added deephermes, deepseek, llama-4 to OpenRouter models\n- Compact model pills (flex-wrap) instead of 2-col grid\n- Tighter spacing throughout the provider step\n- Custom model input below the model pills\n\n* fix: gateway commands for Docker — remove systemd-dependent start\n\nhermes gateway start requires systemd (not available in Docker).\nReplaced with:\n- hermes status / hermes doctor as runnable commands\n- Gateway commands shown as copy-paste reference with explanations\n  (gateway setup = interactive, gateway = foreground, gateway start = systemd)\n- Ready step shows status/doctor/version as runnable diagnostics\n\n* feat: inline provider/model config in onboarding + OpenClaw migration\n\nAfter Hermes installs in onboarding, the runtime card now shows:\n- Quick Setup section with provider pills (Anthropic/OpenAI/OpenRouter/\n  Google/Nous/xAI) and model pills per provider\n- API key input inline in the card\n- ''Apply Configuration'' button that sets provider, model, and API key\n- ''Migrate from OpenClaw'' option if OpenClaw is detected (runs\n  hermes claw migrate --preset user-data)\n- Setup modal still available via full wizard button\n\nAll config happens right in the card — no need to open a modal for\nbasic provider setup.\n\n* feat: add gpt-5.3-codex model + OpenAI OAuth hint\n\n- Added gpt-5.3-codex and gpt-4.1-nano to OpenAI model lists\n  (both onboarding inline config and setup modal)\n- Added OAuth hint under OpenAI API key field: ''Or use OAuth:\n  run hermes model in a terminal for browser login''\n\n* feat: dropdown selects for provider/model in quick setup\n\nReplaced pill buttons with compact dropdown selects — cleaner\nfor the small card space. Provider and model side by side.\n\n* feat: add OpenAI OAuth option in onboarding quick setup\n\n- Separate ''OpenAI (API Key)'' and ''OpenAI (OAuth)'' in provider dropdown\n- OAuth shows device code instructions instead of API key input\n- API key input hidden when OAuth selected\n\n* feat(onboarding): run OpenAI OAuth device flow from quick setup\n\n- add interactive /api/hermes run-oauth-model action using PTY\n\n- add Run button + output panel + clickable login URL in OpenAI OAuth setup\n\n- clarify Node version guard as >=22 (future versions allowed)\n\n* feat: finalize dashboard ops updates and docker runtime fixes\n\n* feat(onboarding): improve oauth log UX and device-code flow\n\n* fix(onboarding): auto-advance hermes model oauth prompt\n\n* fix(onboarding): widen runtimes modal and rebalance card layout\n\n* fix(onboarding): extend Hermes device-code auth timeout\n\n* fix(security): enforce auth and validation for PTY websocket upgrades","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpy9tKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVswQAKPqGQ8j/pcpia8mvfNNKUJd\nVZdzqTJSIWqs2tB/4Y1QhOOufSMec+Pqk6ccg/RuyxMDWQ4+OUN8qdSzcFpXIjlF\nLHqKLR6/xJCxXS5z7QYif7