}],"sha":"69e89a97a1131049de336c1b14f344f7a25fe473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/commits/69e89a97a1131049de336c1b14f344f7a25fe473"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40316131?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/danielaustralia1","id":40316131,"login":"danielaustralia1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzE2MTMx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielaustralia1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/commits/465cd96107da24cfc9d841147ea1538e30b99bec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-19T15:40:55Z","email":"40316131+danielaustralia1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"danielaustralia1"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-19T15:40:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add system monitor panel (btop-style) (#455)\n\n* feat: add system monitor panel with live CPU, memory, disk, and GPU metrics\n\nNew btop-inspired monitoring page in the OBSERVE sidebar group.\nPolls /api/system-monitor every 2s and renders rolling Recharts area\ncharts for CPU/memory/GPU and progress bars for disk usage.\n\n* feat: add network I/O monitoring to system monitor panel\n\nAdd live network throughput (rx/tx bytes/sec) as a dual area chart.\nAPI returns cumulative byte counters per interface (stateless), frontend\ncomputes rates from deltas between 2s polls. Supports Linux (/proc/net/dev)\nand macOS (netstat -ib).\n\n* feat: add top processes list to system monitor\n\nShows top 8 processes by CPU usage in a compact table with CPU%, Mem%,\nand RSS columns. Color-codes high usage values. Uses ps on both Linux\nand macOS with fallback for platforms without --sort support.\n\n* fix: normalize process CPU% to 0-100 and filter out ps itself\n\nCPU% from ps is per-core (e.g. 200% on 4 cores), now divided by core\ncount to show total system percentage. Also filters out the ps command\nthat briefly appears while collecting process data.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dan <github@bookkept.com.au>","tree":{"sha":"1f69b27b27ec314296f7ed8cbc61e3a51834f7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/git/trees/1f69b27b27ec314296f7ed8cbc61e3a51834f7d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ElSpaniard97/hermes-mission-control/git/commits/465cd96107da24cfc9d841147ea1538e30b99bec","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f69b27b27ec314296f7ed8cbc61e3a51834f7d0\nparent 84319928661398dbecae10076a23be465e63c899\nauthor danielaustralia1 <40316131+danielaustralia1@users.noreply.github.com> 1773934855 +1100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773934855 +0700\n\nfeat: add system monitor panel (btop-style) (#455)\n\n* feat: add system monitor panel with live CPU, memory, disk, and GPU metrics\n\nNew btop-inspired monitoring page in the OBSERVE sidebar group.\nPolls /api/system-monitor every 2s and renders rolling Recharts area\ncharts for CPU/memory/GPU and progress bars for disk usage.\n\n* feat: add network I/O monitoring to system monitor panel\n\nAdd live network throughput (rx/tx bytes/sec) as a dual area chart.\nAPI returns cumulative byte counters per interface (stateless), frontend\ncomputes rates from deltas between 2s polls. Supports Linux (/proc/net/dev)\nand macOS (netstat -ib).\n\n* feat: add top processes list to system monitor\n\nShows top 8 processes by CPU usage in a compact table with CPU%, Mem%,\nand RSS columns. Color-codes high usage values. Uses ps on both Linux\nand macOS with fallback for platforms without --sort support.\n\n* fix: normalize process CPU% to 0-100 and filter out ps itself\n\nCPU% from ps is per-core (e.g. 200% on 4 cores), now divided by core\ncount to show total system percentage. Also filters out the ps command\nthat briefly appears while collecting process data.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dan <github@bookkept.com.au>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpvBkHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK9kQAJCiJfph1XqZU0R3JGn/wH3K\nP1xJPMvYI07u7cPKYpu8KcqD5YMxNGUZjJncmye40XM4GFZ+QMd3nkB+IkcUWuQ7\nhk7eGN/dlyiUOFu096t4SPUc1fCYNNJZVAhAjeaWk4krhOIUf19yx0liuVkQ1s07\nEz9/Cf1SQeuFgA/vyz+MzhC5gZlNJWabUNyw4H9x2DXU0NAz5f1SquEMKaK95p0g\nJWkI0rSMwFOuVYZwgeygH6HH3gsxXlMvLm8NyGCuiWZB7f/vRGh++lej60vzmX5G\nRMHc+xC9Ak93E6D+fVuoe4UFyPcJ/0E0WJKIHIq75Mp5ro4mS8Z4ECaVR4lFOgpA\nUMTUURxkA0R1I52VSmU8sIERzvgUtaOYNltTQFVit5PK/JFP+zXGD+ZdKVm4QzVC\ne3UtjziShPdqDp68QYPunP8qpia16CNhkKL5GJS8/7EZiPpwQ6xf+wjOLV75DkCM\nhcUwU4smeSBtR4hqbD6TsR//dLY/qbU+FesGDnvtlKcxuON7pQtW9mRJywF2SWKq\nc7ueb28VuudROpBbL1Hsw/56x4mPVpXivbK+tEdl2izWMYqC+0/2I1S1AI7lVkYV\ntQXF4x2ggP15CiDvn4W4BFoKWQX+tTaOG9Ipk/Akw1dJeXaTMr1XfG4tkN1ln16+\nLsk2yFm0nX2O/UmzqXz0\n=3z1h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-25T16:58:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-