ser_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LaurenceGuws/howl/commits/3d0896d161763221d1a5cda91880323f0f9ae531/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:44:34Z","email":"lggousie46@gmail.com","name":"Laurence"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:44:34Z","email":"lggousie46@gmail.com","name":"Laurence"},"message":"vt: honor row edges when printing beyond horizontal margins\n\nUse the existing directional right boundary for scalar/repeated writes and\ngrapheme lead lookup, and the anchor position for presentation widening.\nThis keeps semantic wide cells in one physical row after CUP beyond DECSLRM\nand preserves their reflow. Reject REP when its wide glyph cannot fit.\n\nProve ordinary Unicode, REP with combining state and VS16 at margin/physical\nedges with autowrap on/off, actual resize, outside-margin following text\nand one-column REP rejection.\n\nVT 681/681; root 197/197 steps and 888/888 tests. Frozen default10 benchmark,\nprotocol, audits, fmt and diff checks pass. Fresh Odin 207 tests / native\nbridge 15 tests; tui-zoo Rain, ASCII/Unicode cells and input canaries pass.\nThe wide case survives an observed 124x29 to 152x35 Odin/PTY resize.","tree":{"sha":"c91c045dc91a92ea84e44631ebb32718b325c4f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LaurenceGuws/howl/git/trees/c91c045dc91a92ea84e44631ebb32718b325c4f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LaurenceGuws/howl/git/commits/3d0896d161763221d1a5cda91880323f0f9ae531","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98704251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LaurenceGuws/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LaurenceGuws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LaurenceGuws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LaurenceGuws/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_