tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/9575d1fa8531fb6517fa7e4cc3bf3b70e67e367f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:34:03Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:34:03Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Merge feat/courses: course paths, AI generation, /review integration\n\nThree-phase course feature:\n- Phase 1 (15c776d): 13 hand-authored MDX manifests + viewer + progress\n- Phase 2 (341e949): AI-generated courses with strict slug validation\n- Phase 3 (9a24a01): note/exercise course steps auto-seed /review queue","tree":{"sha":"6351774294fa61a36ee1383f5afd88fc3b6cf554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/6351774294fa61a36ee1383f5afd88fc3b6cf554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/9575d1fa8531fb6517fa7e4cc3bf3b70e67e367f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/9575d1fa8531fb6517fa7e4cc3bf3b70e67e367f","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDk1NzVkMWZhODUzMWZiNjUxN2ZhN2U0Y2MzYmYzYjcwZTY3ZTM2N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","sha":"6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9","sha":"9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9"}],"sha":"9575d1fa8531fb6517fa7e4cc3bf3b70e67e367f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/9575d1fa8531fb6517fa7e4cc3bf3b70e67e367f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:33:47Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:33:47Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Phase 3: course step → /review queue auto-seeding\n\nWhen a user marks a course step done that''s a note or exercise,\nthe route auto-seeds a fresh ReviewItem in the SM-2 review queue\n(if not already present). Quiz and interview steps skip — the\nexisting ReviewItem schema only has note/exercise types.\n\nImportant guard: we only insert when the review item doesn''t\nyet exist. We never overwrite an in-progress review item''s\nschedule (interval/repetitions/efactor) — the user would lose\ntheir progress. The /review page''s existing bulk-seed-on-load\ncovers most known content; this Phase 3 path catches anything\nadded later (e.g. a new note from a future commit, or an\nAI-generated course pulling from content that wasn''t review-\nseeded yet).\n\nUI: when seeding actually happens (review_items doesn''t already\nhave the item), a green \"Added <kind> to /review queue · view\nqueue\" toast appears for 3 seconds with a link to /review.\n\nWire-up:\n- markStepDone(courseSlug, stepId, step?) now passes the step\n  to the API\n- /api/course-progress POST accepts optional step + checks kind\n- maybeSeedReview() looks up real title via getNote/getExercise\n  and inserts a fresh SM-2 item\n\nSmoke-tested: marking a note step posts back reviewSeeded:false\nbecause the bulk seed already included it. Behavior matches\nintent — non-disruptive for existing items, automatic for new\nones.\n\nThis closes the courses feature trio (Phase 1: manifests +\nviewer; Phase 2: AI generation; Phase 3: review integration).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6351774294fa61a36ee1383f5afd88fc3b6cf554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/6351774294fa61a36ee1383f5afd88fc3b6cf554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDlhMjRhMDE2OGVhMTM4ZWIxZDQ2MzBhNDFjYjhiZGU4MTg3Y2IxZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08","sha":"341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08"}],"sha":"9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/9a24a0168ea138eb1d4630a41cb8bde8187cb1e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:30:56Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:30:56Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Phase 2: AI-generated courses with validated slugs\n\nLocal-AI course assembly. User clicks \"Generate a course\" on\n/courses, supplies a topic + level + target hours; the local\nqwen2.5:14b model assembles a manifest by picking from real\nnotes/exercises and inventing quiz topics + interview tracks.\n\nValidation pipeline:\n1. Strict JSON parse (with fence-salvage)\n2. Schema check: every note/exercise slug must exist in the\n   real catalog; every interview track must be a real track;\n   sections > 0; steps > 0; required fields present\n3. If invalid, the loop sends the model its own bad output\n   plus the validation errors and asks for a fix. Up to 3\n   attempts before giving up.\n\nThis means the user NEVER sees broken links — if the model\ncan''t produce a valid manifest in 3 tries, generation errors\nout cleanly.\n\nStorage:\n- ai_courses MongoDB collection\n- API: POST /api/ai-courses (creates), GET (lists), GET/DELETE\n  per id\n- Viewer at /courses/ai/[id] with the same step-list UI as\n  hand-authored courses, plus a \"Generated from: <prompt>\"\n  attribution and a delete button\n- /courses index renders an AI section above the curated list\n  when any AI courses exist; \"Generate a course\" button is\n  always visible\n\nProgress tracking reuses the existing course_progress table —\nAI course steps are keyed by `ai:<id>:<sectionIdx>:<stepIdx>`\nso they don''t collide with hand-authored manifests.\n\nSmoke-test: generated \"Async JavaScript Mastery\" with 4 sections\nand 12 valid steps; all slugs verified against real content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86639dc9424d9813a3ddd4bb407b09c77f914a43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/86639dc9424d9813a3ddd4bb407b09c77f914a43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDM0MWU5NDlkZjk2YTAzMjIyNTUxZTNjODVlNDkwZmFkZGNjZGRjMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451","sha":"15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451"}],"sha":"341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/341e949df96a03222551e3c85e490faddccddc08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:25:57Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T18:25:57Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Phase 1: Courses feature — manifests, viewer, progress tracking\n\n11 hand-authored MDX course manifests under content/courses/\ncovering DSA, JavaScript, React, TypeScript, MongoDB, Postgres,\nDatabases, Microservices/MFE, Coding Standards, Node.js, HTML/CSS,\nState Management, and a Front-End Interview Boot Camp super-course.\n\nSchema: gray-matter frontmatter holds the structured course\n(title, level, estimatedHours, tags, sections[].steps[]). MDX\nbody is optional intro prose rendered above the lesson tree.\n\nStep types: note (links /notes/<slug>), exercise (/exercises/<slug>),\nquiz (/quiz?source=topic&topic=<x>), interview (/interview),\nexternal (URL).\n\nUI:\n- /courses — index with progress bars + \"continue where you left\n  off\" hero, level badges, course cards with tag chips\n- /courses/[slug] — viewer with section-grouped lesson tree,\n  per-step circle/check toggle, Open buttons, MDX intro\n\nPersistence: course_progress collection in MongoDB, keyed by\nstepId (`${courseSlug}:${sectionIdx}:${stepIdx}`). API route\nsupports GET (all or per-course), POST (upsert), DELETE.\nSmoke-tested end-to-end.\n\nArchitecture note: lib/courses.ts is client-safe (types + pure\nhelpers + fetch wrappers); lib/courses-server.ts is server-only\n(fs reading via gray-matter, marked with the server-only package).\nThis split keeps fs out of the client bundle.\n\nPhase 2 (AI-generated courses) and Phase 3 (review-queue\nintegration) follow on the same feat/courses branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5c4c10354089affb36204ca3e0744bd8fd38db43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/5c4c10354089affb36204ca3e0744bd8fd38db43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDE1Yzc3NmRhY2FhMGQ4YzRmMTI5MTc3MzIxYzgwZTUyNjkwNjE0NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","sha":"6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76"}],"sha":"15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/15c776dacaa0d8c4f129177321c80e5269061451"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:55:18Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:55:18Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add ''restart dev'' sequence for laptop-sleep recovery\n\nscripts/restart-dev.sh handles the after-sleep / after-lock case\nwhere Docker containers go stale, Next file watchers desync, and\nconnections to Ollama / mongod can be left half-open.\n\nModes:\n- (no arg) / all  — smart full restart: kills :3000, restarts\n  searxng container, defers to dev.sh for Mongo / Ollama / Next\n- status          — read-only status report of all services\n- next            — just kill :3000 and re-run npm run dev\n- searxng         — docker restart searxng + health check\n- mongo           — brew services restart or pkill+fork\n- ollama          — pkill + ollama serve in background\n\nWired up as:\n- npm run restart           (full)\n- npm run restart:status    (status only)\n- bash scripts/restart-dev.sh <service>  (per-service)\n\nAGENTS.md gets a new \"Trigger phrases (for agents)\" table at the\ntop so any AI session knows exactly what command to run when the\nuser says \"restart dev\". Pre-authorized — agents shouldn''t ask\npermission for this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0129c9783070d85cac7ae4107975bcb3f32a0783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/0129c9783070d85cac7ae4107975bcb3f32a0783"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDY1MTgzNzdiMGU0YTE2ZjdlOTMyNWNjODBmMGE4Mjc2YzI5M2ZkNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359","sha":"1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359"}],"sha":"6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/6518377b0e4a16f7e9325cc80f0a8276c293fd76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:45:08Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:45:08Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add 5 cheat-sheet notes (React, Redux/Zustand, Postgres, Node, SQL/NoSQL)\n\nInterview-prep oriented notes following the existing react-hooks\nstyle — opinionated, code-heavy, structured around the questions\ninterviewers actually ask. Each ends with a \"Likely interview\nquestions\" section.\n\n- react-cheat-sheet — JSX, rendering, forms, context, memo,\n  refs, server vs client components, Suspense, React 19 adds,\n  common pitfalls\n- redux-zustand-cheat-sheet — side-by-side, full APIs for both,\n  selector + subscription patterns, decision flow\n- postgres-cheat-sheet — schema, CRUD, joins, indexes, JSONB,\n  transactions, performance gotchas\n- nodejs-cheat-sheet — ESM/CJS, fs/http/fetch, streams, event\n  loop, async patterns, workers, crypto, CLI flags\n- databases-sql-vs-nosql — CAP, indexing, ACID, scaling moves,\n  decision flow\n\nTagged with \"cheat-sheet\" so they''re filterable, plus topic tags\nfor /tags/[tag] aggregation. Cross-linked via `related`\nfrontmatter to existing notes (react-hooks, node-server-side,\nmongodb).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"75ac091a7aa2ce60dc225ca49057556534081f41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/75ac091a7aa2ce60dc225ca49057556534081f41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDFhMGU5NmRiZWFlNDBlY2MzMjZmZTg2Y2M3MjI1OGIyNDBhNTMzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a","sha":"118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a"}],"sha":"1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/1a0e96dbeae40ecc326fe86cc72258b240a53359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:38:58Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:38:58Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Fix Hint panel: abort fetch on close so loading state clears\n\nClosing the Hint/Review/Explain panel mid-stream only set\nopen=false; the in-flight fetch kept running and setResponse /\nsetLoading kept mutating state. So:\n- Action buttons stayed disabled (loading never cleared until\n  the backend stream finished naturally).\n- Reopening the panel briefly flashed stale tokens.\n- Spawning a new request before the previous one finished\n  caused the older stream to keep appending tokens into the\n  newer one''s response state.\n\nFix: an AbortController in a ref is now signalled on close,\nwhen a new ask() starts (cancels the previous), and on\nunmount. The reader loop also short-circuits if the signal\nfires mid-stream. Aborted-state errors are suppressed so they\ndon''t surface to the user. The setLoading(null) in finally is\nguarded so a stale finally from an aborted request can''t clear\nthe loading state of a fresh in-flight one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"faa607bdc510e7dc05232fb6faf02b4a68e07fbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/faa607bdc510e7dc05232fb6faf02b4a68e07fbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDExOGY2YzU3MDUyM2M0M2ExNDIxYmU2OGM4NmQ0ODc0ODE1M2JkMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0","sha":"f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0"}],"sha":"118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/118f6c570523c43a1421be68c86d48748153bd2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:31:07Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:31:07Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Broaden web-search intent regex + harden anti-anchoring prompt\n\nLive-testing the web search pipeline surfaced two issues:\n\n1. Intent regex was too narrow. \"Look up the latest React 19 use()\n   hook docs\" didn''t match because /\\blook\\s+(it|this|that)\\s+up\\b/\n   required a pronoun. Also missed \"with sources\", \"on the web\",\n   \"latest <anything>\", and source name-drops like \"MDN\" alone.\n   Broadened — false positives are cheap (the model can decline\n   to call the tool); false negatives mean the user asked for\n   web search and didn''t get it.\n\n2. The model was actively rewriting \"React 19\" to \"React 18\"\n   in the search query because its training prior thought 18\n   was the latest, then ignoring fresh react.dev results that\n   confirmed React 19''s use() hook. Anti-anchoring fixes:\n   - Inject today''s date so the model knows time has passed\n     since training\n   - Explicit instruction to preserve user-supplied tokens\n     (especially version numbers / library / API names) in\n     the search query verbatim\n   - Strengthened \"trust the search results\" clause with named\n     hedge phrases the model is forbidden to use\n\nAfter fixes: model preserves \"React 19\" in its query, cites\nreact.dev/reference/react/use directly, drops the \"speculative\"\nlanguage. Still somewhat under-confident on snippet content\n(SearXNG returns ~150 char snippets, not full pages) — fixable\nlater with a results-page fetcher if needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdf981fd11adbe7d4f79ceab04229da9f10c6ac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/fdf981fd11adbe7d4f79ceab04229da9f10c6ac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKGY0MTRmMmY5OWUwY2Q2NGU4MGVjNDVkOTEyYWQ4M2E5YjMzMjllYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98","sha":"2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98"}],"sha":"f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/f414f2f99e0cd64e80ec45d912ad83a9b3329eb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:18:23Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T07:18:23Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Auto-start Docker + SearXNG in dev.sh (web search now zero-config)\n\ndev.sh now handles the full SearXNG lifecycle so users don''t have\nto run docker commands manually:\n- If docker not installed → warn + skip (web search disabled)\n- If docker daemon down → boot it (Docker Desktop on macOS,\n  systemctl on Linux) and wait up to 60s for it to come online\n- If searxng container exists and stopped → start it\n- If searxng container missing → docker run with the pre-baked\n  config volume; wait for /healthz\n\nEvery check degrades to a warning rather than killing the script,\nsince web search is opt-in. The rest of the app works fine\nwithout it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a7ce252ae5473c361f5276703729a36e04390cdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/a7ce252ae5473c361f5276703729a36e04390cdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDJmNTlhZDhkMTI3YmUzMDA2Yjg5MDliNjk2NTUxZDI4YjVjMThhOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c","sha":"b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c"}],"sha":"2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/2f59ad8d127be3006b8909b696551d28b5c18a98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T02:53:43Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T02:53:43Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add on-demand web search via local SearXNG (Ollama tool calling)\n\nFloating study assistant can now call a local SearXNG container\nfor live web results when the user explicitly asks. Triggering is\nintent-driven — a regex over the user''s last message detects\nphrases like \"search online\", \"look it up\", \"verify\", \"cite\nsources\", \"provide a reference\", \"latest <X>\", \"as of 2026\",\n\"is that still accurate\", \"MDN says\", etc. Only when matched do\nwe attach the web_search tool, keeping the streaming path fast\nfor normal Q&A.\n\nWhen triggered:\n- Route probes SearXNG via /healthz with a 1.5s timeout\n- If up: chatWithTools() runs the multi-turn tool loop non-\n  streamed; status messages (\"Searching the web for: X…\") are\n  streamed back as italic content chunks so the user sees\n  progress. Final answer includes markdown source links.\n- If down: existing streaming path runs with a single-line\n  inline notice telling the user search isn''t running.\n\nThe interview chatbot (/api/ai/interview) intentionally does NOT\nhave web search wired in — interviewers don''t browse mid-\nquestion, and giving the LLM tools there would break roleplay.\n\nSetup is documented in AGENTS.md as Step 5 (optional). One\ndocker run command mounts our pre-baked searxng/settings.yml\nwhich enables JSON output (off by default) and disables the\nlimiter for local-only use.\n\nEnv: SEARXNG_URL (default http://localhost:8888).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39c2aaa6d9842be906ee0e0515f7e6e27af6e969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/39c2aaa6d9842be906ee0e0515f7e6e27af6e969"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKGIxNDUxN2ZmMTY0Nzc5ZGRiZDkwYTIxMjgzN2ZjYmRhMjc5ZWUxOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec","sha":"0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec"}],"sha":"b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/b14517ff164779ddbd90a212837fcbda279ee18c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T02:21:48Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T02:21:48Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add /quiz with validated AI generation + Quiz me buttons\n\nNew /quiz drill-mode page that generates MCQ + predict-output\nquestions from a topic, a saved interview note, an MDX note, or\na coding exercise. Every question is validated before the user\nsees it:\n\n1. Strict JSON parse of the model''s output\n2. Schema validator (distinct options, correctIndex in range,\n   rationale per option, exactly 4 MCQ options, etc.)\n3. For predict-output: the snippet is actually executed in a\n   sandboxed vm.runInNewContext, and the real captured stdout is\n   compared to the AI''s claimed expectedOutput. Mismatches are\n   discarded — this catches the bulk of hallucinations.\n4. If too many fail, generator retries up to 3 times to top up\n   the batch.\n\nDrill UX: one question at a time, immediate per-question\nfeedback (MCQ shows per-option rationale, predict-output shows\nexpected vs typed), per-topic mastery breakdown on the summary\nscreen. Each attempt is saved to MongoDB (quiz_attempts) for\nfuture spaced-repetition integration.\n\nUniversal \"Quiz me\" entry-point button (components/QuizMeButton.tsx)\nwired into:\n- Coding exercise pages → quizzes from problem + concepts\n- MDX note pages → quizzes from note body + tags\n- Saved interview-note pages → quizzes from the AI study note\n- Interview session pages → quizzes from the saved note (button\n  appears after Save to Notes runs once)\n\nAlso installs @playwright/test as a dev dep — no tests yet.\nFuture plan: a tutorial page that uses Playwright headlessly to\ncapture annotated screenshots for documentation.\n\nEnv: OLLAMA_QUIZ_NUM_CTX (default 8192) for the generator.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"443521efd2a4704aa4ef15f911b4bc49df6f2507","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/443521efd2a4704aa4ef15f911b4bc49df6f2507"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDBkZjkyODc2NGNlZGQzMTY5MTAxMWI3NWM1NjgxMDJmYzY4MTBhZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83","sha":"38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83"}],"sha":"0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/0df928764cedd31691011b75c568102fc6810aec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T01:57:39Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T01:57:39Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add Save to Notes (AI-generated, 1:1 with session) + retroactive docs\n\nSave to Notes header button on the interview session page sends\nthe transcript to Ollama with a summarizer system prompt and\nstores the AI-generated study note in MongoDB. Schema:\n{ id, sessionId, title, track, context?, tags, content, createdAt }\nwith id === sessionId so a session has at most one note — re-saving\nupserts. Title and tags are parsed out of the AI''s markdown output\n(# heading + **Tags:** line).\n\nChat input is locked while the note is generating to avoid two\nconcurrent Ollama requests fighting for the model. Status banner\nshows \"Generating study note — chat paused (~30–60s)…\" and a\ngreen confirmation banner with a \"View note →\" link appears on\nsuccess.\n\nNotes surface on /notes in a new \"From your mock interviews\"\nsection and have their own viewer at /notes/saved/[id] (rendered\nwith react-markdown + Mermaid + tag links + delete).\n\nAlso retroactively documents this session''s prior commits in\nAGENTS.md: custom mock interview track, Web Speech voice\nfeatures, Mermaid diagrams, Claude-style chat controls, and the\nfloating-chat copy button. Added OLLAMA_NOTES_NUM_CTX env var.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9390693b4b89bd7b7243f3d75274093dd301cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/b9390693b4b89bd7b7243f3d75274093dd301cf1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKDM4YjU1MWYzMDU1NWY2ZDQ3MDk1MjQ4NDcwYTBiMWQ1M2QyNTBiODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d","sha":"ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d"}],"sha":"38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/38b551f30555f6d47095248470a0b1d53d250b83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T01:44:09Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T01:44:09Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add chat controls and cap answer textarea at max-h-64\n\nChat controls (Claude-style action toolbar below each bubble,\nhover-revealed):\n- Copy message as Markdown with check-icon confirmation\n- Regenerate response on the latest assistant turn (rolls back\n  the transcript and re-streams the last user message)\n- Export full transcript as a .md file with track / role context,\n  job description, and turn-by-turn blocks\n\nFloatingChat: copy button per message.\n\nAlso caps the interview answer textarea at max-h-64 with\noverflow-y-auto so long answers scroll inside the textarea instead\nof pushing the transcript off-screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e56c080819d026236b6b2d144839a544e6d2b1ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/trees/e56c080819d026236b6b2d144839a544e6d2b1ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/git/commits/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d","node_id":"C_kwDOSMlDG9oAKGVhNjI4ODdhYTRlNmMxNGYwYzQ0ZTBhZmE2N2E0NDdmMzgyMThkMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commit/70103abb6984b45a7488f0d79c3584ef4e382690","sha":"70103abb6984b45a7488f0d79c3584ef4e382690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/70103abb6984b45a7488f0d79c3584ef4e382690"}],"sha":"ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/ea62887aa4e6c14f0c44e0afa67a447f38218d0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3442038?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/balbonits","id":3442038,"login":"balbonits","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDIwMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/balbonits","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/balbonits/coding-interview-reviewer/commits/70103abb6984b45a7488f0d79c3584ef4e382690/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T00:51:57Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T00:51:57Z","email":"balbonits@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Dilig"},"message":"Add custom mock interview, Web Speech voice, and Mermaid diagrams\n\nCustom mock interview track lets the user paste a JD and have the\ninterviewer simulate a realistic round for that specific role —\ntemplated system prompt splices role/company/JD/notes into the\nexisting per-track interviewer rules.\n\nVoice features wire the Web Speech API into the interview session:\nmic button (SpeechRecognition) for dictating answers, per-message\nspeaker icons + auto-speak toggle (SpeechSynthesis) for hearing the\ninterviewer back. Feature-detected so unsupported browsers degrade.\n\nMermaid diagrams render inline from fenced ```mermaid blocks in\nboth the interview transcript and the floating study assistant.\nSystem prompts updated to permit (and for the assistant, encourage)\ndiagrams when a visual would clarify the explanation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tr