},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","repositoryId":1221261739,"sha":"de7606cec753d48b65d8c3003b718f48f3aa1660"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-25T07:57:11Z","committedDate":"2026-04-25T07:57:11Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","repositoryId":1221261739,"sha":"bf2593f9c3311984c1385b2f974acb6f115faef7"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-25T07:55:42Z","committedDate":"2026-04-25T07:55:42Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","repositoryId":1221261739,"sha":"eef303d1c5bdcfe279bbff0ecfe9d87231cf8153"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-25T07:52:44Z","committedDate":"2026-04-25T07:52:44Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","repositoryId":1221261739,"sha":"8ff52861f55293788af60e35de77b727f87ba3ff"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-25T07:46:29Z","committedDate":"2026-04-25T07:46:29Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","repositoryId":1221261739,"sha":"343ee5116e9557fbb617eed9eb643dc863358002"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:47:43.597Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/6c2b1e841310fec511d4bc25ba74b50abc58cb47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T15:34:21Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T15:34:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): mutation-test — wire JUnit 5 plugin + harden summary script (#27)\n\n* fix(ci): mutation-test — wire JUnit 5 plugin + harden summary script\n\nThree stacked bugs were keeping the nightly mutation-test workflow red:\n\n1. PIT defaulted to JUnit 4. The state-machine unit tests are Jupiter,\n   so PIT enumerated 21 mutants but ran 0 tests → NO_COVERAGE 21 → 0%\n   score → tripped the 70% mutationThreshold gate. Added\n   pitest-junit5-plugin:1.2.3 as a dependency of the pitest-maven\n   plugin in the pitest profile. Verified locally: 20/21 = 95%.\n\n2. The summarize step used `grep -c … || echo 0` under bash -e. When\n   grep finds zero matches it prints \"0\" AND exits 1, so the rescue\n   ran echo and the captured value became \"0\\n0\" — the arithmetic\n   expansion below choked with a syntax error. Switched to `|| true`\n   plus `${TOTAL:-0}` defaulting.\n\n3. Latent bug masked by #1: PIT writes attributes with single quotes\n   (detected=''true'') but the workflow grep matched double quotes\n   (detected=\"true\"). KILLED would have been 0 even with #1 fixed.\n   Switched to grep -cE with a quote-tolerant character class.\n\nLocal verification:\n  ./mvnw -B -Ppitest test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:mutationCoverage\n  → BUILD SUCCESS, Mutation score 20/21 = 95%\n\nLogged to docs/ERROR_FIX_LOG.md per the project guardrail.\n\n* chore(format): apply Spotless to pitest profile — sortpom canonical order\n\nSpotless''s sortpom rule requires <dependencies> after <configuration>\ninside a plugin block. Re-running `./mvnw spotless:apply` reorders\nwithout changing semantics. Verified PIT still resolves the JUnit 5\nplugin (BUILD SUCCESS, 20/21 = 95%).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"185dea99738c20faed083c287d0b4719064f82d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/185dea99738c20faed083c287d0b4719064f82d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/6c2b1e841310fec511d4bc25ba74b50abc58cb47","verification":{"payload":"tree 185dea99738c20faed083c287d0b4719064f82d4\nparent 7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777476861 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777476861 -0600\n\nfix(ci): mutation-test — wire JUnit 5 plugin + harden summary script (#27)\n\n* fix(ci): mutation-test — wire JUnit 5 plugin + harden summary script\n\nThree stacked bugs were keeping the nightly mutation-test workflow red:\n\n1. PIT defaulted to JUnit 4. The state-machine unit tests are Jupiter,\n   so PIT enumerated 21 mutants but ran 0 tests → NO_COVERAGE 21 → 0%\n   score → tripped the 70% mutationThreshold gate. Added\n   pitest-junit5-plugin:1.2.3 as a dependency of the pitest-maven\n   plugin in the pitest profile. Verified locally: 20/21 = 95%.\n\n2. The summarize step used `grep -c … || echo 0` under bash -e. When\n   grep finds zero matches it prints \"0\" AND exits 1, so the rescue\n   ran echo and the captured value became \"0\\n0\" — the arithmetic\n   expansion below choked with a syntax error. Switched to `|| true`\n   plus `${TOTAL:-0}` defaulting.\n\n3. Latent bug masked by #1: PIT writes attributes with single quotes\n   (detected=''true'') but the workflow grep matched double quotes\n   (detected=\"true\"). KILLED would have been 0 even with #1 fixed.\n   Switched to grep -cE with a quote-tolerant character class.\n\nLocal verification:\n  ./mvnw -B -Ppitest test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:mutationCoverage\n  → BUILD SUCCESS, Mutation score 20/21 = 95%\n\nLogged to docs/ERROR_FIX_LOG.md per the project guardrail.\n\n* chore(format): apply Spotless to pitest profile — sortpom canonical order\n\nSpotless''s sortpom rule requires <dependencies> after <configuration>\ninside a plugin block. Re-running `./mvnw spotless:apply` reorders\nwithout changing semantics. Verified PIT still resolves the JUnit 5\nplugin (BUILD SUCCESS, 20/21 = 95%).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8iT9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+acQAHqg9x0WlXYbKXCCbs2TnbVf\nFXI7j9bM+oD+TYK8HpgWZD1NRfn8oZ2lVs4B6/7cBsfMpeKEZ5l8aSimnUNh9vw0\nq4S0MOchI/lcKNjc2KIQNGPmvXwVhR0oGrOdfbbEcp2tMb82V2w+JgXvkD/Kq/Fs\ndG9IT+7nf+N/QYAkP9A7wwUDaIdhHqTMwIvze4skpiiw3CvjPLns0vg5IrUTYHm4\nrrosuz8KrKnzTBtZVMkQ+SisUKQs0MENjpdz95Vz+1RmrM7c5hWZuK1fyH9+fzPA\n4SxsC2QNcAUtJBWDieG8oZD7zUxmDHoYGJwNqNVr2m7ne+i5E7CTCyTmEFz28DJ6\nOw2oEHG0XadbcLv3ReKNrLADzLlJJvpe0LsOtvFjEKHiK9F1fj7jGUn6vPITNbZf\nUNDvwtOQE51c11aMqsOie8F8kRTVbrb2EGwiWcexUYKl66C62dwnBKAhhktVkLYc\nSAvZcOf8+iTYGO3UCyMFLJ3+8T+/l7EYLuZmCrRzHZW1x7GkJcJZE4KPurTu+GFq\nNp0kisSFV8WPwixrhRkQSlf5gOjI1u80OMCABaqNn76b7y0m+y4PvkJwsqun+04J\n6u7cE2w/sz5+EJPCHzRVdNuW9hzTeIstwhNPaxclAJJoe8GEexrvINzUQw0GbtBu\nyN4agSCHEHDoVCu90KWn\n=oFX9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-29T15:34:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/6c2b1e841310fec511d4bc25ba74b50abc58cb47","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDZjMmIxZTg0MTMxMGZlYzUxMWQ0YmMyNWJhNzRiNTBhYmM1OGNiNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d","sha":"7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d"}],"sha":"6c2b1e841310fec511d4bc25ba74b50abc58cb47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/6c2b1e841310fec511d4bc25ba74b50abc58cb47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:36:32Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:36:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(18-perf): perf-hardening — component tests + Flowbite tree-shake + k6 latency gate + @Timed histograms (#26)\n\n* task(18-perf): close component-test gap for AppShell + WeekContext + 3 modes\n\nAudit-driven catch-up: the code-quality standard \"Vitest unit tests for\nall components\" is documented as 100% but five components were missing\nco-located tests. The 80% coverage gate was masking it because these\ncomponents are exercised through other tests. Adding direct tests gives\neach component its own contract and lets future refactors break the\ncomponent without breaking unrelated tests.\n\n- AppShell.test.tsx: 8 tests covering all slots (title/eyebrow/headerSlot/\n  subnav/children/testId), the 3 nav links, and the build-stamp footer.\n- WeekContextBadge.test.tsx: 4 tests pinning the date-range format\n  contract (same-year vs year-straddle) plus the throw-on-invalid-input\n  guard.\n- modes/BlankState.test.tsx: 5 tests covering CTA enabled/disabled/\n  loading states, illustration, mutation firing, and error banner.\n- modes/LockedReadOnly.test.tsx: 5 tests covering loading/error/success\n  branches plus actualStatus surfacing and empty-array edge case.\n- modes/ReconciledSummary.test.tsx: 7 tests covering loading/error,\n  reflection block presence/absence (incl. empty string == undefined),\n  per-row carry-forward firing.\n\nAll 5 follow the established `vi.hoisted` + `vi.mock(''@wc/rtk-api-client'')`\npattern from DraftMode/ReconcileMode tests; no new infrastructure.\n\n30/30 new tests pass. No production code changes.\n\n* task(18-perf): tree-shake flowbite-react via subpath imports\n\nflowbite-react 0.10.2 ships a `./components/*` subpath in its exports\nmap but no `sideEffects: false` in package.json, so Rollup conservatively\nkeeps the whole barrel even when only a handful of components are used.\nResult before this change: vendor-flowbite chunk = 235 KB raw / 65 KB gz,\ncarrying every Button/Card/Modal/Sidebar/Datepicker/etc. that we never\nimport.\n\nTwo call sites consume flowbite-react:\n  - src/main.tsx                     -> { Flowbite }\n  - src/components/ConflictToast.tsx -> { Toast, ToastToggle }\n\nBoth switched to:\n  from ''flowbite-react/components/Flowbite''\n  from ''flowbite-react/components/Toast''\n\nThis is the package''s published export pattern (same level of API stability\nas the bare specifier), not a private path.\n\nvite.config.ts optimizeDeps.include updated to mirror the new specifiers\nso dev pre-bundling matches production resolution.\n\nResult:\n  vendor-flowbite: 235 KB raw / 65 KB gz -> 96 KB raw / 23 KB gz (-65% gz)\n  modules transformed: 615 -> 469\n  All other chunks unchanged.\n\nVerified:\n  yarn vitest run                   180/180 pass (no behavior change)\n  yarn vite build                   clean\n  yarn run size-check               every asset under budget\n\n* task(18-perf): @Timed histograms on plan + rollup hot paths\n\nServer-side latency observability for the four endpoints PRD §Performance\nTargets calls out:\n\n  GET /api/v1/plans/me/current        wc.plans.get_current\n  GET /api/v1/plans?employeeId&...    wc.plans.get_by_employee_week\n  GET /api/v1/plans/team              wc.plans.get_team\n  GET /api/v1/rollup/team             wc.rollup.get_team\n\nEach annotated with histogram=true + percentiles {0.5, 0.95, 0.99} so the\nPrometheus-format histograms exposed at /actuator/prometheus carry real\npercentile-aware buckets (not just count + sum, which can''t reconstruct\np95). The k6 perf harness measures latency from the caller; these meters\nmeasure it from inside the JVM. Together they bracket the regression --\nexternal + internal signal -- so a future jump can be triaged faster.\n\nWiring required two pieces:\n  - spring-boot-starter-aop in pom.xml. Without it @Timed compiles fine\n    but is a silent no-op (worst possible failure mode for an obs layer).\n  - MetricsConfig.java exposing the TimedAspect @Bean. micrometer-core\n    ships the aspect class but Boot doesn''t auto-register it; the\n    one-bean config makes it explicit.\n\nThe metric names are domain-prefixed (wc.*) so they don''t collide with\nthe actuator''s built-in http.server.requests counters and so a future\nGrafana dashboard groups them logically.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw compile                clean\n  ./mvnw test (controllers)     22/22 pass (no behavior change)\n\n* task(18-perf): PerfDataSeeder — gated startup fixture for the k6 harness\n\nThe k6 perf workflow needs realistic row counts to produce meaningful p95\nnumbers; running it against an empty DB measures index scan + framework\noverhead, not query behavior. This adds a profile-gated seeder that runs\nonce at startup when SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE includes ''perf''.\n\nSeed shape:\n  - 1 manager (PERF_MANAGER_ID — deterministic UUID for JWT signing)\n  - 50 ICs reporting to that manager (incl. PERF_IC_ID for /me/current)\n  - 1 WeeklyPlan per IC for this Monday UTC = 50 plans\n  - 5 WeeklyCommits per plan, tier-rotated R/P/S = 250 commits\n\n50 reports is the manager-rollup payload size called out in PRD §Performance\nTargets. Tier rotation makes the rollup tier-distribution non-uniform so\nthe aggregation query has actual work to do.\n\nIdempotent: re-running against an already-seeded DB is a no-op (existsById\non the manager). compose restarts re-trigger startup; without this guard\nthe second pass would violate uq_weekly_plan_employee_week and crash boot.\n\nProfile isolation\n=================\n\n@Profile(\"perf\") — this bean is never instantiated outside the perf\nprofile, including under prod / dev / demo / test. Activated only by:\n  - docker-compose.e2e.yml when the upcoming perf workflow brings the\n    stack up\n  - local SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,perf for hand-running k6\n\nNo data leakage risk into other environments.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw compile      clean\n\n* task(18-perf): docker-compose.perf.yml — perf-profile override over e2e stack\n\nLayers on top of docker-compose.e2e.yml (the Cypress harness) to activate\nSPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,perf so PerfDataSeeder fires at startup. Adds\nno new services -- only overrides env vars on weekly-commit-service.\n\nWhy an override file vs. mutating the base e2e compose:\n  - The Cypress + Cucumber harness''s contract is \"one IC, one plan, a\n    handful of commits\"; injecting 250 perf rows into the same compose\n    would shift unrelated rollup-count assertions in the Gherkin specs.\n  - Overrides compose cleanly via -f chaining.\n\nBring up:\n  docker compose -f docker-compose.e2e.yml -f docker-compose.perf.yml up -d --wait\n\n* chore(lint): unblock root lint (rtk-api-client ?? + perf/ ignore)\n\nTwo small fixes that unblock `yarn lint` from main as of c7afa3f...781f635:\n\n1. libs/rtk-api-client/src/api.ts:41 — typescript-eslint flagged the\n   ternary `rawBaseUrl === undefined ? ''http://localhost'' : rawBaseUrl`\n   under `prefer-nullish-coalescing`. Switching to `??` is semantically\n   identical here: rawBaseUrl is `string | undefined` (never null), so\n   `rawBaseUrl ?? ''http://localhost''` preserves the three-mode behavior\n   the comment block above already documents (undefined → fallback,\n   \"\" → keep, \"https://...\" → keep). Empty string is NOT coalesced by\n   ?? so the same-origin signal stays intact.\n\n2. apps/weekly-commit-ui/eslint.config.js — add `perf/**` to the typed-\n   rule ignore list, mirroring the existing `scripts/**` carve-out. The\n   perf/ directory contains a Node ESM JWT signer and a k6 .js script\n   that runs on Goja, neither of which fits the src/ tsconfig project.\n   Without this, typed lint fails with \"no parserOptions for type info.\"\n\nfrontend-pr CI on main has been red since #25 because of (1); this commit\ngets it back to green.\n\n* task(18-perf): k6 latency gate — GET /plans/me/current p95 < 200 ms\n\nPRD §Performance Targets calls out p95 < 200 ms for the IC''s current-week\nread path; until now that was an aspirational claim with no harness behind\nit. This wires up the regression gate end-to-end.\n\nPieces (each a separately-explicable surface):\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/perf/sign-perf-jwt.mjs\n    Node ESM. Reads the committed cypress dev key, signs an RS256 JWT\n    whose `sub` is PERF_IC_ID and whose claims mirror signTestJwt.ts\n    exactly. The e2e-profile JwtDecoder validates signature only -- no\n    iss/aud enforcement -- so the Cypress + perf paths share one auth\n    contract. stdout = raw token (no newline) so `xargs -I{}` works.\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/perf/current-week.k6.js\n    k6 script. 10 VUs * 30s. Threshold = http_req_duration{endpoint:current}\n    p(95)<200. Tag scopes the threshold to the GET so unrelated k6\n    overhead doesn''t pollute the percentile. k6 exits non-zero on\n    threshold violation -> CI red.\n\n  .github/workflows/perf-pr.yml\n    Single job. Builds the backend JAR, brings up\n    docker-compose.e2e.yml + docker-compose.perf.yml chained (perf\n    profile activates PerfDataSeeder), polls for the seeder''s \"[perf-\n    seeder] done\" log marker so we don''t measure a half-empty DB,\n    mints the JWT (add-mask''d so it can''t leak into logs), then\n    `k6 run`. On failure dumps backend logs + filtered\n    /actuator/prometheus (wc.* timers) for triage. Trigger paths\n    cover backend src, perf harness, both compose files, and the\n    JWT key dir.\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/package.json\n    Two scripts: perf:sign-jwt + perf:current-week. The workflow\n    only uses :sign-jwt; :current-week is for local dev (`yarn ... |\n    xargs -I{} k6 run -e WC_PERF_JWT={} ...`).\n\n  docs/TASK_LIST.md\n    Task 18: Flowbite tree-shake + k6 harness flipped to [x]; one\n    paragraph summarizes the perf-hardening pass and what''s still\n    open (rollup EXPLAIN, N+1 audit, CloudFront monitoring).\n\nVerified\n========\n  yarn format:check                    clean\n  yarn lint                            clean (4/4 projects)\n  yarn typecheck                       clean (4/4)\n  yarn workspace ... vitest run        210/210 tests pass\n  yarn vite build + run size-check     all assets under budget;\n                                       vendor-flowbite still 23 KB gz\n                                       (subpath-import win preserved)\n\n* chore(format): apply Spotless to perf/ — google-java-format line wrapping\n\nbackend-pr CI ran spotless:check and rejected my hand-formatted constructor\nparameter list + multi-line log.info() in PerfDataSeeder, plus a Javadoc\nline-wrap point in package-info. Re-ran `./mvnw spotless:apply` and pushed\nthe result. No semantic change; google-java-format wins.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw spotless:check     clean\n  ./mvnw compile            clean\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e843895721f7c92bdec1d2a2ce848761c4be300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/3e843895721f7c92bdec1d2a2ce848761c4be300"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e843895721f7c92bdec1d2a2ce848761c4be300\nparent 781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777358192 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777358192 -0600\n\ntask(18-perf): perf-hardening — component tests + Flowbite tree-shake + k6 latency gate + @Timed histograms (#26)\n\n* task(18-perf): close component-test gap for AppShell + WeekContext + 3 modes\n\nAudit-driven catch-up: the code-quality standard \"Vitest unit tests for\nall components\" is documented as 100% but five components were missing\nco-located tests. The 80% coverage gate was masking it because these\ncomponents are exercised through other tests. Adding direct tests gives\neach component its own contract and lets future refactors break the\ncomponent without breaking unrelated tests.\n\n- AppShell.test.tsx: 8 tests covering all slots (title/eyebrow/headerSlot/\n  subnav/children/testId), the 3 nav links, and the build-stamp footer.\n- WeekContextBadge.test.tsx: 4 tests pinning the date-range format\n  contract (same-year vs year-straddle) plus the throw-on-invalid-input\n  guard.\n- modes/BlankState.test.tsx: 5 tests covering CTA enabled/disabled/\n  loading states, illustration, mutation firing, and error banner.\n- modes/LockedReadOnly.test.tsx: 5 tests covering loading/error/success\n  branches plus actualStatus surfacing and empty-array edge case.\n- modes/ReconciledSummary.test.tsx: 7 tests covering loading/error,\n  reflection block presence/absence (incl. empty string == undefined),\n  per-row carry-forward firing.\n\nAll 5 follow the established `vi.hoisted` + `vi.mock(''@wc/rtk-api-client'')`\npattern from DraftMode/ReconcileMode tests; no new infrastructure.\n\n30/30 new tests pass. No production code changes.\n\n* task(18-perf): tree-shake flowbite-react via subpath imports\n\nflowbite-react 0.10.2 ships a `./components/*` subpath in its exports\nmap but no `sideEffects: false` in package.json, so Rollup conservatively\nkeeps the whole barrel even when only a handful of components are used.\nResult before this change: vendor-flowbite chunk = 235 KB raw / 65 KB gz,\ncarrying every Button/Card/Modal/Sidebar/Datepicker/etc. that we never\nimport.\n\nTwo call sites consume flowbite-react:\n  - src/main.tsx                     -> { Flowbite }\n  - src/components/ConflictToast.tsx -> { Toast, ToastToggle }\n\nBoth switched to:\n  from ''flowbite-react/components/Flowbite''\n  from ''flowbite-react/components/Toast''\n\nThis is the package''s published export pattern (same level of API stability\nas the bare specifier), not a private path.\n\nvite.config.ts optimizeDeps.include updated to mirror the new specifiers\nso dev pre-bundling matches production resolution.\n\nResult:\n  vendor-flowbite: 235 KB raw / 65 KB gz -> 96 KB raw / 23 KB gz (-65% gz)\n  modules transformed: 615 -> 469\n  All other chunks unchanged.\n\nVerified:\n  yarn vitest run                   180/180 pass (no behavior change)\n  yarn vite build                   clean\n  yarn run size-check               every asset under budget\n\n* task(18-perf): @Timed histograms on plan + rollup hot paths\n\nServer-side latency observability for the four endpoints PRD §Performance\nTargets calls out:\n\n  GET /api/v1/plans/me/current        wc.plans.get_current\n  GET /api/v1/plans?employeeId&...    wc.plans.get_by_employee_week\n  GET /api/v1/plans/team              wc.plans.get_team\n  GET /api/v1/rollup/team             wc.rollup.get_team\n\nEach annotated with histogram=true + percentiles {0.5, 0.95, 0.99} so the\nPrometheus-format histograms exposed at /actuator/prometheus carry real\npercentile-aware buckets (not just count + sum, which can''t reconstruct\np95). The k6 perf harness measures latency from the caller; these meters\nmeasure it from inside the JVM. Together they bracket the regression --\nexternal + internal signal -- so a future jump can be triaged faster.\n\nWiring required two pieces:\n  - spring-boot-starter-aop in pom.xml. Without it @Timed compiles fine\n    but is a silent no-op (worst possible failure mode for an obs layer).\n  - MetricsConfig.java exposing the TimedAspect @Bean. micrometer-core\n    ships the aspect class but Boot doesn''t auto-register it; the\n    one-bean config makes it explicit.\n\nThe metric names are domain-prefixed (wc.*) so they don''t collide with\nthe actuator''s built-in http.server.requests counters and so a future\nGrafana dashboard groups them logically.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw compile                clean\n  ./mvnw test (controllers)     22/22 pass (no behavior change)\n\n* task(18-perf): PerfDataSeeder — gated startup fixture for the k6 harness\n\nThe k6 perf workflow needs realistic row counts to produce meaningful p95\nnumbers; running it against an empty DB measures index scan + framework\noverhead, not query behavior. This adds a profile-gated seeder that runs\nonce at startup when SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE includes ''perf''.\n\nSeed shape:\n  - 1 manager (PERF_MANAGER_ID — deterministic UUID for JWT signing)\n  - 50 ICs reporting to that manager (incl. PERF_IC_ID for /me/current)\n  - 1 WeeklyPlan per IC for this Monday UTC = 50 plans\n  - 5 WeeklyCommits per plan, tier-rotated R/P/S = 250 commits\n\n50 reports is the manager-rollup payload size called out in PRD §Performance\nTargets. Tier rotation makes the rollup tier-distribution non-uniform so\nthe aggregation query has actual work to do.\n\nIdempotent: re-running against an already-seeded DB is a no-op (existsById\non the manager). compose restarts re-trigger startup; without this guard\nthe second pass would violate uq_weekly_plan_employee_week and crash boot.\n\nProfile isolation\n=================\n\n@Profile(\"perf\") — this bean is never instantiated outside the perf\nprofile, including under prod / dev / demo / test. Activated only by:\n  - docker-compose.e2e.yml when the upcoming perf workflow brings the\n    stack up\n  - local SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,perf for hand-running k6\n\nNo data leakage risk into other environments.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw compile      clean\n\n* task(18-perf): docker-compose.perf.yml — perf-profile override over e2e stack\n\nLayers on top of docker-compose.e2e.yml (the Cypress harness) to activate\nSPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,perf so PerfDataSeeder fires at startup. Adds\nno new services -- only overrides env vars on weekly-commit-service.\n\nWhy an override file vs. mutating the base e2e compose:\n  - The Cypress + Cucumber harness''s contract is \"one IC, one plan, a\n    handful of commits\"; injecting 250 perf rows into the same compose\n    would shift unrelated rollup-count assertions in the Gherkin specs.\n  - Overrides compose cleanly via -f chaining.\n\nBring up:\n  docker compose -f docker-compose.e2e.yml -f docker-compose.perf.yml up -d --wait\n\n* chore(lint): unblock root lint (rtk-api-client ?? + perf/ ignore)\n\nTwo small fixes that unblock `yarn lint` from main as of c7afa3f...781f635:\n\n1. libs/rtk-api-client/src/api.ts:41 — typescript-eslint flagged the\n   ternary `rawBaseUrl === undefined ? ''http://localhost'' : rawBaseUrl`\n   under `prefer-nullish-coalescing`. Switching to `??` is semantically\n   identical here: rawBaseUrl is `string | undefined` (never null), so\n   `rawBaseUrl ?? ''http://localhost''` preserves the three-mode behavior\n   the comment block above already documents (undefined → fallback,\n   \"\" → keep, \"https://...\" → keep). Empty string is NOT coalesced by\n   ?? so the same-origin signal stays intact.\n\n2. apps/weekly-commit-ui/eslint.config.js — add `perf/**` to the typed-\n   rule ignore list, mirroring the existing `scripts/**` carve-out. The\n   perf/ directory contains a Node ESM JWT signer and a k6 .js script\n   that runs on Goja, neither of which fits the src/ tsconfig project.\n   Without this, typed lint fails with \"no parserOptions for type info.\"\n\nfrontend-pr CI on main has been red since #25 because of (1); this commit\ngets it back to green.\n\n* task(18-perf): k6 latency gate — GET /plans/me/current p95 < 200 ms\n\nPRD §Performance Targets calls out p95 < 200 ms for the IC''s current-week\nread path; until now that was an aspirational claim with no harness behind\nit. This wires up the regression gate end-to-end.\n\nPieces (each a separately-explicable surface):\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/perf/sign-perf-jwt.mjs\n    Node ESM. Reads the committed cypress dev key, signs an RS256 JWT\n    whose `sub` is PERF_IC_ID and whose claims mirror signTestJwt.ts\n    exactly. The e2e-profile JwtDecoder validates signature only -- no\n    iss/aud enforcement -- so the Cypress + perf paths share one auth\n    contract. stdout = raw token (no newline) so `xargs -I{}` works.\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/perf/current-week.k6.js\n    k6 script. 10 VUs * 30s. Threshold = http_req_duration{endpoint:current}\n    p(95)<200. Tag scopes the threshold to the GET so unrelated k6\n    overhead doesn''t pollute the percentile. k6 exits non-zero on\n    threshold violation -> CI red.\n\n  .github/workflows/perf-pr.yml\n    Single job. Builds the backend JAR, brings up\n    docker-compose.e2e.yml + docker-compose.perf.yml chained (perf\n    profile activates PerfDataSeeder), polls for the seeder''s \"[perf-\n    seeder] done\" log marker so we don''t measure a half-empty DB,\n    mints the JWT (add-mask''d so it can''t leak into logs), then\n    `k6 run`. On failure dumps backend logs + filtered\n    /actuator/prometheus (wc.* timers) for triage. Trigger paths\n    cover backend src, perf harness, both compose files, and the\n    JWT key dir.\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/package.json\n    Two scripts: perf:sign-jwt + perf:current-week. The workflow\n    only uses :sign-jwt; :current-week is for local dev (`yarn ... |\n    xargs -I{} k6 run -e WC_PERF_JWT={} ...`).\n\n  docs/TASK_LIST.md\n    Task 18: Flowbite tree-shake + k6 harness flipped to [x]; one\n    paragraph summarizes the perf-hardening pass and what''s still\n    open (rollup EXPLAIN, N+1 audit, CloudFront monitoring).\n\nVerified\n========\n  yarn format:check                    clean\n  yarn lint                            clean (4/4 projects)\n  yarn typecheck                       clean (4/4)\n  yarn workspace ... vitest run        210/210 tests pass\n  yarn vite build + run size-check     all assets under budget;\n                                       vendor-flowbite still 23 KB gz\n                                       (subpath-import win preserved)\n\n* chore(format): apply Spotless to perf/ — google-java-format line wrapping\n\nbackend-pr CI ran spotless:check and rejected my hand-formatted constructor\nparameter list + multi-line log.info() in PerfDataSeeder, plus a Javadoc\nline-wrap point in package-info. Re-ran `./mvnw spotless:apply` and pushed\nthe result. No semantic change; google-java-format wins.\n\nVerified\n========\n  ./mvnw spotless:check     clean\n  ./mvnw compile            clean\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8FVwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHxMQAB8e9WvxgvQVIXbVanvTQvYM\n1hTMyqEdhSXDQINkj5fh4hWfSEQSJFiOFSNqLwkoLdU3ZOVTUSeOcjYxqzFPZ1Bk\n6wdT+MlgIMFX8NrfmBZEas4MyC3b6RXfgrXqdhB7lTRK7T1YWW5r/xdZ4Eb1i0N/\nEXEAiREX1oPPLFp3hfiPfQi5umisuIRpul88pY4k/kaD5WBkd2iSN8xTey442jGN\nMMMsQgz3bnOKETvjVqs6dFfoWLW5TzglPAPAvvrFU8tiFKAUMU/ZmTfqxpc4KPhp\nltFLL8X8MJm5n19vjfRSQZSLQ4n+edDSQ4UoMmHz0GWV1vxWS9Ocyh6sM069rRfp\nhvYn5UfO/QhwuyoE6cYMEo0w8I3qXiJ46NhtzWfXv2ToGIaYMAONrKMmCPIhvDMI\nKSmaX7djGln9hXFNG4jXfwoSdW7eZsoR9TA8oNNxx6ExvjgMfogrFjtvkCLm6Zu8\ndQj/58icpClPKrN/L1sTdOiZbZge6h0NtIQ/P5s88pp4x96J0iNOJzWh0husnOjY\nhfZbAtPcVE1qhLFLjn6OlIoTXqR6o0KAwZi/wruJcFhp6cg3Yj8ajpPmrU8ibO5z\nIlk5Xm4y+bJFJvcQkUu4EZgjm3C2o8xrSF+D8RoDcUn+IrqBD4S62HgGyZDxOhqn\nwKvMUqmZP4ta7vFh/wD/\n=AumB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T06:36:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDdkYzFjNWUwYzUzYzQ4ZmNkMDJiNzIwMGU3MzlhNjJiMTEzNDUwOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb","sha":"781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb"}],"sha":"7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/7dc1c5e0c53c48fcd02b7200e739a62b1134509d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:07:39Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:07:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-railway): fix API base-url -- empty VITE_API_BASE_URL means same-origin (#25)\n\nLive demo''s frontend was failing every API call because the bundled fetch\ntarget was ''http://localhost/api/v1/plans/me/current'' -- the api-client''s\nfallback for when VITE_API_BASE_URL is falsy. Spring Boot serves the SPA\n+ API from one origin on Railway, so the right baseUrl for the demo is \"\"\n(relative same-origin), not localhost.\n\nRoot cause: api.ts used `env?.VITE_API_BASE_URL || ''http://localhost''`.\nThe Dockerfile.bundled correctly set VITE_API_BASE_URL=\"\" at build time\nto signal same-origin, but `||` treats empty string as falsy and fell\nthrough to the localhost fallback.\n\nFix: distinguish undefined (vitest harness) from \"\" (deliberate\nsame-origin signal). Three modes:\n\n  - undefined / unset: fall back to http://localhost (vitest''s MSW\n    patterns expect this).\n  - explicit \"\": same-origin via relative URLs (demo, federated prod).\n  - explicit \"https://...\": deployment-specific override.\n\nThe original comment on `||` flagged that vitest used to surface \"\" via\nnx -- that''s been fixed upstream and tests now produce undefined, so the\nnew semantics (treat \"\" as deliberate) is safe.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  yarn workspace @wc/rtk-api-client run test     32/32 pass\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test   180/180 pass\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck  clean\n  yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)            clean\n  yarn format:check (root)                       clean\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"14319ddf846e5862bf61b19a0498e1ff4b81d704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/14319ddf846e5862bf61b19a0498e1ff4b81d704"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb","verification":{"payload":"tree 14319ddf846e5862bf61b19a0498e1ff4b81d704\nparent 6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777356459 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777356459 -0600\n\ntask(14-railway): fix API base-url -- empty VITE_API_BASE_URL means same-origin (#25)\n\nLive demo''s frontend was failing every API call because the bundled fetch\ntarget was ''http://localhost/api/v1/plans/me/current'' -- the api-client''s\nfallback for when VITE_API_BASE_URL is falsy. Spring Boot serves the SPA\n+ API from one origin on Railway, so the right baseUrl for the demo is \"\"\n(relative same-origin), not localhost.\n\nRoot cause: api.ts used `env?.VITE_API_BASE_URL || ''http://localhost''`.\nThe Dockerfile.bundled correctly set VITE_API_BASE_URL=\"\" at build time\nto signal same-origin, but `||` treats empty string as falsy and fell\nthrough to the localhost fallback.\n\nFix: distinguish undefined (vitest harness) from \"\" (deliberate\nsame-origin signal). Three modes:\n\n  - undefined / unset: fall back to http://localhost (vitest''s MSW\n    patterns expect this).\n  - explicit \"\": same-origin via relative URLs (demo, federated prod).\n  - explicit \"https://...\": deployment-specific override.\n\nThe original comment on `||` flagged that vitest used to surface \"\" via\nnx -- that''s been fixed upstream and tests now produce undefined, so the\nnew semantics (treat \"\" as deliberate) is safe.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  yarn workspace @wc/rtk-api-client run test     32/32 pass\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test   180/180 pass\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck  clean\n  yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)            clean\n  yarn format:check (root)                       clean\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8E6rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/2gQAE7m4GNFuuO0N4iIQfZ1xlnx\nmRgPTkddOTK/bkNbrBm6m7ZEEitbWHCLn3f6c6HgoQP9vGgohsgRWMUUwouRemn+\nQkL+uXRaFUl1PaJTjQ8ID0UUa8XupEql7L3nJMA2BorlxZLLk5VE7giVUwxAv538\nqK1L7kO51NbOnNH/AHDMRmj7wLPV7UPS6UweHqdbSJZX1wjmFRwwRd4o7D0qHPqO\n6Nw9ks8ceBe9qyZJTATUGzRs7eCBqW/503rQ5cscg5BRJj8WmXaU1Jfu+/0m3xXf\nAWZv+Yvq4/+PrdCDx033i0f0SwT0lnOsieoAwn94TmL/cFgnSOA/6qj4FS2+65Hh\nNHW5tVCvuuiKqCUApvsTLsH5I5+mVfICVgycxPWvIBWdtteJOia6YVybjdBAOYr6\nF7ou3ZflH552GaEMGq5ukckBtrY2iuN0rjYs5C5J9B86M/dzyIqxPMII0tzjdfy7\npwPY3/HZtsTU/z+eOcIu6cMFtnQ0dNajWZZNS9gwWXdt243SFgm/aDvVNhkwXtra\nqYwFgoMC8TuSZBx/l/lqgW12it8ZSDJXvqv/Y+JGEFcyNU6eSSLxdnZA9/KqnV6V\nElWyIiYw5skoGj4EHm2xTN+/hI6B85qp+UIQt0I7QA8/TmScaeMwMJ6WkUbowAem\nWgsMkLEgFFc7hc+ngjfD\n=KkPh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T06:07:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDc4MWY2MzUwOWZiMGI2N2E2Y2I3NjY2N2ZkZWFkN2E3YjJlOWRhY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a","sha":"6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a"}],"sha":"781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/781f63509fb0b67a6cb76667fdead7a7b2e9dacb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:01:14Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T06:01:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: MEMO #15 — entities deliberately exempt from AbstractAuditingEntity (#24)\n\nThe project standard is that every business entity extends\nAbstractAuditingEntity (Spring Data JPA''s @CreatedBy / @CreatedDate /\n@LastModifiedBy / @LastModifiedDate). Two entities deliberately do not:\n\n  - AuditLog: this *is* the audit trail. Carries actorId + occurredAt\n    already; layering audit columns on top would duplicate data and\n    imply rows are mutable (they''re not -- append-only).\n  - NotificationDlt: populated by background retry paths, not user\n    activity. Standard audit columns would mislead readers into\n    thinking a person had touched the row.\n\nThis commit:\n  - Cross-references MEMO #15 from the Javadoc on both entities so the\n    rationale is visible at the point of definition\n  - Adds the MEMO entry itself codifying the project-wide policy\n\nPure documentation. No runtime code changes.\n\nVerified:\n  - mvn spotless:check clean (after apply)\n  - mvn test 260/260 pass\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8a88f3254c3bd219a6dc256be8d34e37bb02f4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/a8a88f3254c3bd219a6dc256be8d34e37bb02f4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a","verification":{"payload":"tree a8a88f3254c3bd219a6dc256be8d34e37bb02f4f\nparent 64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777356074 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777356074 -0600\n\ndocs: MEMO #15 — entities deliberately exempt from AbstractAuditingEntity (#24)\n\nThe project standard is that every business entity extends\nAbstractAuditingEntity (Spring Data JPA''s @CreatedBy / @CreatedDate /\n@LastModifiedBy / @LastModifiedDate). Two entities deliberately do not:\n\n  - AuditLog: this *is* the audit trail. Carries actorId + occurredAt\n    already; layering audit columns on top would duplicate data and\n    imply rows are mutable (they''re not -- append-only).\n  - NotificationDlt: populated by background retry paths, not user\n    activity. Standard audit columns would mislead readers into\n    thinking a person had touched the row.\n\nThis commit:\n  - Cross-references MEMO #15 from the Javadoc on both entities so the\n    rationale is visible at the point of definition\n  - Adds the MEMO entry itself codifying the project-wide policy\n\nPure documentation. No runtime code changes.\n\nVerified:\n  - mvn spotless:check clean (after apply)\n  - mvn test 260/260 pass\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8E0qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWj4QAKzOfVqu4y3r+S3vf49aIgDs\n0AOWc9PLgBt+fGOjcW8kWDzEe7R8a/MT40S2ZVlMxVNQj/c/EJ0MY7Rkhy5CS/mg\ngajERi2n5TS18cQhKRITxQ38iHepH5bJeOGYgusb88PIKiNTxLHiFIa0p/B328SM\nAxiV5sHGXNCQ3jZAvxMSQWb0SaFOvDr5bI5PuWWNUxT9wg+M4Sy+kCLMgqif5QAU\n7s9r+AXvfic2v3cD7ayK4edIu0oHYuCrA/dwiax5aWTe6Fdcg44ZDzusRSNywogr\nmy+S7T7Go/BesZ1eT6Vt4CUpHtr3RPSD3kz6w/23+bgSK5wZf90OyGcJeFih1eP9\nA/Jbw/u1EZpziKFdxcmD/s5+qS3tYFECD+Dn0NmEtWiB3kWyFouGVGDB18YWVidL\nE5OHpB6jVSxWIdScXIzk7Bqpxs/gw+YaSP4siJHJVpkUzQNV8Y0qbsKb304UHnfH\n4TlXh/0dD6MnCMaG6ujry8uqM1fHODVV7QOmTSrYTfWcx8Gn1A0ktxRTwd/BRR06\nY4kGV2TFfBQyE6mjlGMVCPc4blAsVpejxo/BR2w68hXVXXuEZYlbB9th9S92/v1F\ntJLObP3xsKQ8P0tIOw/N+ThiepAp38hWulZIyiT/gKeRzMwun8Xcwulbp2ToSzRK\ny4R45Oqfih9IvpJwbr5u\n=hLD6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T06:01:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDZhZTE0YzNiMTI5YTE1OTY1MDQyYWFiZjY2NDk4ZTliNDdjZmQ4N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442","sha":"64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442"}],"sha":"6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/6ae14c3b129a15965042aabf66498e9b47cfd87a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:58:57Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:58:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(18-perf): lazy-load routes + bundle-size budget on the remote (#22)\n\nPulls the cheap parts of Task 18 (Performance) forward so PRD''s\n\"Frontend initial route render < 1 s, lazy-loaded routes\" claim\nbecomes implemented rather than aspirational, and adds a regression\nguard so the size never silently grows.\n\n- React.lazy + single Suspense boundary in WeeklyCommitModule.tsx.\n  Pages stay as named exports; lazy import re-shapes them to default\n  at the import site so route page files stay untouched.\n- vite.config.ts: manualChunks for flowbite/sentry/jose. React/Router/\n  RTK are NOT vendor-chunked -- they''re federation singletons and the\n  host provides them at runtime; chunking would break the contract.\n- Opt-in rollup-plugin-visualizer (ANALYZE=1 yarn build → stats.html).\n- scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs: zero-runtime-dep gzip budget per asset\n  category (remoteEntry / expose / route / vendor / css / standaloneEntry\n  / other). Wired into frontend-pr.yml after the Build remote step.\n- Routing tests switched to await findByTestId for async chunk resolve.\n\nDefers k6 latency harness, RCDO/rollup EXPLAIN profiling, Flowbite\ntree-shake, CloudFront hit-ratio to a later \"Perf hardening\" group.\nSee MEMO #14 for rationale.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"816e1b3928cd0102d26790d089ccbe6a9a4da096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/816e1b3928cd0102d26790d089ccbe6a9a4da096"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442","verification":{"payload":"tree 816e1b3928cd0102d26790d089ccbe6a9a4da096\nparent c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777355937 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777355937 -0600\n\ntask(18-perf): lazy-load routes + bundle-size budget on the remote (#22)\n\nPulls the cheap parts of Task 18 (Performance) forward so PRD''s\n\"Frontend initial route render < 1 s, lazy-loaded routes\" claim\nbecomes implemented rather than aspirational, and adds a regression\nguard so the size never silently grows.\n\n- React.lazy + single Suspense boundary in WeeklyCommitModule.tsx.\n  Pages stay as named exports; lazy import re-shapes them to default\n  at the import site so route page files stay untouched.\n- vite.config.ts: manualChunks for flowbite/sentry/jose. React/Router/\n  RTK are NOT vendor-chunked -- they''re federation singletons and the\n  host provides them at runtime; chunking would break the contract.\n- Opt-in rollup-plugin-visualizer (ANALYZE=1 yarn build → stats.html).\n- scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs: zero-runtime-dep gzip budget per asset\n  category (remoteEntry / expose / route / vendor / css / standaloneEntry\n  / other). Wired into frontend-pr.yml after the Build remote step.\n- Routing tests switched to await findByTestId for async chunk resolve.\n\nDefers k6 latency harness, RCDO/rollup EXPLAIN profiling, Flowbite\ntree-shake, CloudFront hit-ratio to a later \"Perf hardening\" group.\nSee MEMO #14 for rationale.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8EyhCRC1aQ7uu5Uhl