Commit/commit/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67","sha":"c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67"}],"sha":"64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/64b556417884710522d812b6b07dcebc81881442"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:54:26Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:54:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-railway): disable Module Federation in demo builds -- fixes blank-screen boot (#23)\n\nLive URL was returning a fully-loaded HTML + 200-OK static chunks but\nReact never rendered: <div id=\"root\"></div> stayed empty, no console\nerrors. Spent forensic effort inspecting served chunks, content-types,\nnetwork responses -- all clean. Root cause was structural.\n\nThe bundle is built with @originjs/vite-plugin-federation, which at\nruntime calls `await importShared(''react'')` etc. via the federation\nruntime registered in the vendor-sentry chunk. Federation expects a\nhost application to call init() on the share scope before any expose''d\ncomponent can resolve its shared deps. With no host (i.e., a standalone\nproduction build), the importShared promises never resolve -- they sit\npending forever.\n\nmain.tsx''s top-level await chain hits these promises immediately:\n  const { StrictMode } = await d(\"react\");\n  const { HashRouter, Routes, ... } = await d(\"react-router-dom\");\n\nWhen d() hangs, the module never finishes evaluating, the boot()\nfunction never runs, render() never fires. No exception is thrown\nbecause the promises are simply pending, not rejected. Hence \"no\nconsole errors + blank screen.\"\n\nvite dev papered over this with a dev-mode share-scope auto-init that\nruns before anything imports. Production builds skipped that workaround\nsilently. We never noticed because:\n  - All previous deploy attempts failed at build / start, before reaching\n    runtime\n  - Local `vite dev` always worked because of the dev-mode init\n  - docker-compose.demo.yml runs the same yarn build, so it would have\n    hit the same blank-screen issue if anyone had loaded the localhost\n    URL in a browser past the initial smoke check\n\nFix\n===\n\nMake federation conditional on VITE_DEMO_MODE !== ''true''. Demo\nbuilds (Railway, docker-compose.demo, future single-origin demo\nhosts) skip federation and produce a regular SPA. Regular builds\n(CI''s `yarn build`, future federated production deploys consumed\nby the PA host) keep emitting remoteEntry.js + __federation_shared_*\nexactly as before.\n\nSingle-line gate. The federation plugin''s exposes/shared/etc config\nis preserved verbatim under the conditional.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  VITE_DEMO_MODE=true yarn build:\n    - emits a regular SPA: dist/index.html + dist/assets/index-*.js\n      (~524 KB) + DemoLoginPicker / DemoModeBanner / devAuth as async\n      chunks\n    - NO remoteEntry.js, NO __federation_* chunks\n    - No top-level await in entry chunk\n\n  VITE_DEMO_MODE=\"\" yarn build (regular):\n    - emits remoteEntry.js + __federation_expose_WeeklyCommitModule.js\n      + __federation_shared_react.js etc., exactly as before\n    - PA host integration path preserved\n\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck     clean\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test          180/180 pass\n  yarn lint (root)                                      clean\n  yarn format:check (root)                              clean\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0bb8abde320646df82d72dd38b9688b1adce5a48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/0bb8abde320646df82d72dd38b9688b1adce5a48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bb8abde320646df82d72dd38b9688b1adce5a48\nparent 3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777355666 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777355666 -0600\n\ntask(14-railway): disable Module Federation in demo builds -- fixes blank-screen boot (#23)\n\nLive URL was returning a fully-loaded HTML + 200-OK static chunks but\nReact never rendered: <div id=\"root\"></div> stayed empty, no console\nerrors. Spent forensic effort inspecting served chunks, content-types,\nnetwork responses -- all clean. Root cause was structural.\n\nThe bundle is built with @originjs/vite-plugin-federation, which at\nruntime calls `await importShared(''react'')` etc. via the federation\nruntime registered in the vendor-sentry chunk. Federation expects a\nhost application to call init() on the share scope before any expose''d\ncomponent can resolve its shared deps. With no host (i.e., a standalone\nproduction build), the importShared promises never resolve -- they sit\npending forever.\n\nmain.tsx''s top-level await chain hits these promises immediately:\n  const { StrictMode } = await d(\"react\");\n  const { HashRouter, Routes, ... } = await d(\"react-router-dom\");\n\nWhen d() hangs, the module never finishes evaluating, the boot()\nfunction never runs, render() never fires. No exception is thrown\nbecause the promises are simply pending, not rejected. Hence \"no\nconsole errors + blank screen.\"\n\nvite dev papered over this with a dev-mode share-scope auto-init that\nruns before anything imports. Production builds skipped that workaround\nsilently. We never noticed because:\n  - All previous deploy attempts failed at build / start, before reaching\n    runtime\n  - Local `vite dev` always worked because of the dev-mode init\n  - docker-compose.demo.yml runs the same yarn build, so it would have\n    hit the same blank-screen issue if anyone had loaded the localhost\n    URL in a browser past the initial smoke check\n\nFix\n===\n\nMake federation conditional on VITE_DEMO_MODE !== ''true''. Demo\nbuilds (Railway, docker-compose.demo, future single-origin demo\nhosts) skip federation and produce a regular SPA. Regular builds\n(CI''s `yarn build`, future federated production deploys consumed\nby the PA host) keep emitting remoteEntry.js + __federation_shared_*\nexactly as before.\n\nSingle-line gate. The federation plugin''s exposes/shared/etc config\nis preserved verbatim under the conditional.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  VITE_DEMO_MODE=true yarn build:\n    - emits a regular SPA: dist/index.html + dist/assets/index-*.js\n      (~524 KB) + DemoLoginPicker / DemoModeBanner / devAuth as async\n      chunks\n    - NO remoteEntry.js, NO __federation_* chunks\n    - No top-level await in entry chunk\n\n  VITE_DEMO_MODE=\"\" yarn build (regular):\n    - emits remoteEntry.js + __federation_expose_WeeklyCommitModule.js\n      + __federation_shared_react.js etc., exactly as before\n    - PA host integration path preserved\n\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck     clean\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test          180/180 pass\n  yarn lint (root)                                      clean\n  yarn format:check (root)                              clean\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8EuSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsNUQACfmfkMzfLObmBtctSa9A/Z6\ng+ZbFlF42WfgXaZAvUewQTP4hYyPxZxP494VhZPGh3YZNDhrPZxXiDAwObFgX2vb\nLW6WnfYyQJo1+sdosWCfpyNDiHn1s+sdJO4mGOqzp+eHERsVkbjyI3gtPqpvl/GG\nUiqKNOk2UOwyPwe2tCUYX0rQ3Tu9ckaP+rhFxY7xMyy0J1OLVoGNvJ3acUKlkaGK\nlvz5s33YZxIaLg16KYJD90Q0Dvy2VxVWEuFjcpTpgSo0xq2HwPdFgvLWSRVFnLm/\nmsEgZhVBLoko3iv3yOr6NsDFkDUcxfL3GBY5la9ybkrX2kdi0Qqc75nXxEIYRjZj\nZXN7MaTp2XXSijefJJfxkGw5Oz5X2whmNjwMd2pe8KWXgtOeXs2bVcCm2po87e57\n4iIRH7O+lyTcvGju9YiZ4xYUCYR3Db8ZeA56+f72S6MzGldXO8Cxo4g/SGlNwm+c\neT9+E7FLhdhm1nc3CO9CK4GrbsICUGwUoidJZEGbuM8buhpWpNhbfejJtSTkgxlh\n4sBzk4N2G416h9tZCXcQRS7IOO8ksupz1MtcvOZOCq+jBOWIajv/+dOwiN+0MNR0\nnKSgoJa4oZx0Ztkz1siMP4VKjI7C/7Q1NaTD70TmIwAvY7mSrouC2QevDvk70Yrf\nTliCLVK+wspZ5G3MqzQF\n=3Dva\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T05:54:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGM3YWZhM2Y3MjI1ZDRlNWU2ODQxZDIxZGU5N2M1Yzg2NTBjNGNjNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317","sha":"3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317"}],"sha":"c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c7afa3f7225d4e5e6841d21de97c5c8650c4cc67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:14:17Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:14:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-railway): install curl in backend-build stage -- mvnw needs it on alpine (#21)\n\nAfter fixing the .yarn issue (PR #20), Railway''s Metal builder hit:\n\n  ./mvnw: line 46: curl: not found\n  exit code: 127\n\nThe Maven wrapper script (apps/weekly-commit-service/mvnw) downloads\nmaven-wrapper-3.3.2.jar from Maven Central on first run. Its first\npreference is curl, second is wget. Alpine ships neither by default;\nlocal Docker Desktop tolerated this because (it appears) the local\nmvnw download was already cached at a layer Railway invalidated.\n\nFix: `apk add --no-cache curl` early in the JDK stage. Standard\nsingle-line addition, no caveats.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"89a27e1f98a919cb19d3230e35430e73d1ff6713","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/89a27e1f98a919cb19d3230e35430e73d1ff6713"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317","verification":{"payload":"tree 89a27e1f98a919cb19d3230e35430e73d1ff6713\nparent 77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777353257 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777353257 -0600\n\ntask(14-railway): install curl in backend-build stage -- mvnw needs it on alpine (#21)\n\nAfter fixing the .yarn issue (PR #20), Railway''s Metal builder hit:\n\n  ./mvnw: line 46: curl: not found\n  exit code: 127\n\nThe Maven wrapper script (apps/weekly-commit-service/mvnw) downloads\nmaven-wrapper-3.3.2.jar from Maven Central on first run. Its first\npreference is curl, second is wget. Alpine ships neither by default;\nlocal Docker Desktop tolerated this because (it appears) the local\nmvnw download was already cached at a layer Railway invalidated.\n\nFix: `apk add --no-cache curl` early in the JDK stage. Standard\nsingle-line addition, no caveats.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8EIpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAimMQALCVVgz2KkJMuKusjlxwYA/U\nZTnUenrMJpubfxaSD+0jYZ1wW0M00mDZcLZfO2+t1Pd7hRiWLp4fshXlWLOC1CXX\npyWK6fqF/iT503L6GCw+oe0XqqtiC2Jn2GeBeEUGxyW5OoO+9Kna50xtbWRLdX5L\nL668nP14tkAHfyL8m4pv5zIWdiFUXN8/tqqstP2to40n5I60rYZ52Z2S7crgYIQF\nmbBsoI2DPnhaifUKYXZ9lPJua23sjQPmboFblNuaLQakO/LagCSv4EgYxIiVavri\ntg7FZKrsJWiRjlaSUB8IIcGdM9rKvhMxIm2AyLBkP3OuZFoI+ZLOUMcy8/vYIJzH\nC9WeK7ZJf3TpWpvjJOMAl4k2sb5ZGuQE4SZVIyTXapEtY7yUgtQCe1VyjlozZqFv\nSP5579yZBy+ZxMR/SH6sEGubx9tfUVrer8IxNl5SqLV0UoSMPL1y7/PgTQofDVrH\nhQCOaZEojjZSY0CFJ5Wb+56ePVzhZtw+HtMU8wjS41JsvK3VJW3FqsgI2n8MHF2m\noYe5B1G3F0S/B0nCzxYmZGf8Dm41quKYrZ/6myGXtlWQHAAHv4ncLb4oYBc7pBNc\n2QyNvEe1MdzPB4YMC8pIxQ0PRU95y4HpemqhH/5E6jCT696LxZa4du9tCcu9esCp\nWTDCZzqKRlVguFSgvIRJ\n=i7wT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T05:14:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDNhMTg5MGMwYzc4MTEzY2MyOGZiNWVlYzM3MjQxMWFmODJlNzgzMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6","sha":"77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6"}],"sha":"3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/3a1890c0c78113cc28fb5eec372411af82e78317"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:08:42Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T05:08:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-railway): drop COPY .yarn from Dockerfile.bundled -- Railway BuildKit fails on empty dir (#20)\n\nRailway''s first build of Dockerfile.bundled failed at:\n\n  COPY .yarn ./.yarn\n  -> failed to compute cache key: \"/.yarn\": not found\n\nRoot cause: this repo''s .yarn/ directory contains only .yarn/cache,\n.yarn/install-state.gz, and .yarn/unplugged -- all three are listed in\nthe repo-root .dockerignore, so the build context''s .yarn/ has zero\ncontents. BuildKit''s checksum step under Railway is stricter than\ndocker build under our local Docker Desktop and fails when the source\nof a COPY resolves to nothing.\n\nFix: drop the COPY .yarn line. With corepack-managed yarn 4.5.0\n(activated in the prior step) and `yarn install --immutable`, the\nlocal .yarn/ artifacts aren''t needed -- yarn resolves from the\nregistry using package.json + yarn.lock + .yarnrc.yml.\n\nTrade-off: marginally slower first install on a cold registry cache\n(~10-20s) since we lose the local .yarn/cache hint. Acceptable for\nthe demo deploy. Future optimization: add `.yarn/cache` to git\nvia `enableGlobalCache: false` in .yarnrc + commit the cache, but\nthat adds repo weight that isn''t worth it for a demo.\n\nThe same COPY pattern still appears in apps/weekly-commit-ui/Dockerfile\n(the AWS-era frontend image) and works there because our local Docker\nDesktop is more lenient. Leaving it -- if Railway becomes the only\ntarget, we''d revisit and remove there too.\n\nVerified locally:\n  docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled -t weekly-commit:bundled-test .\n  builds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe5ec710f6a3b2e9953f293f2540c90dd068d224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/fe5ec710f6a3b2e9953f293f2540c90dd068d224"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6","verification":{"payload":"tree fe5ec710f6a3b2e9953f293f2540c90dd068d224\nparent c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777352922 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777352922 -0600\n\ntask(14-railway): drop COPY .yarn from Dockerfile.bundled -- Railway BuildKit fails on empty dir (#20)\n\nRailway''s first build of Dockerfile.bundled failed at:\n\n  COPY .yarn ./.yarn\n  -> failed to compute cache key: \"/.yarn\": not found\n\nRoot cause: this repo''s .yarn/ directory contains only .yarn/cache,\n.yarn/install-state.gz, and .yarn/unplugged -- all three are listed in\nthe repo-root .dockerignore, so the build context''s .yarn/ has zero\ncontents. BuildKit''s checksum step under Railway is stricter than\ndocker build under our local Docker Desktop and fails when the source\nof a COPY resolves to nothing.\n\nFix: drop the COPY .yarn line. With corepack-managed yarn 4.5.0\n(activated in the prior step) and `yarn install --immutable`, the\nlocal .yarn/ artifacts aren''t needed -- yarn resolves from the\nregistry using package.json + yarn.lock + .yarnrc.yml.\n\nTrade-off: marginally slower first install on a cold registry cache\n(~10-20s) since we lose the local .yarn/cache hint. Acceptable for\nthe demo deploy. Future optimization: add `.yarn/cache` to git\nvia `enableGlobalCache: false` in .yarnrc + commit the cache, but\nthat adds repo weight that isn''t worth it for a demo.\n\nThe same COPY pattern still appears in apps/weekly-commit-ui/Dockerfile\n(the AWS-era frontend image) and works there because our local Docker\nDesktop is more lenient. Leaving it -- if Railway becomes the only\ntarget, we''d revisit and remove there too.\n\nVerified locally:\n  docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled -t weekly-commit:bundled-test .\n  builds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8EDaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANPsQAAHiUHw6tHvrUw4KfD80kgVL\nneZEX6ChGb5XhAWsCY/Q4BTcnIAZxWkTruMKH9j+usZ/6vIdQeUJKlfoCLUm0Y3q\n5Sj6880PLS0313DcVOBEElL5dPyElvNlVym4Zg9pt0Qtii5qOIPLpqZGWAle+lir\nTb6yJwF1NLFy5bAkZ9io64uaGQyXYF8Zce0pLhxbK8u4BJpkU+ggTW6tk78qjuXi\nJRElSRhfhKPgqJy00Z9KfyqRBMxfzbq7dCYwcm88JAR6Ez0VfrJfOMxsheCCB0o0\nuAFaYJr+2Y4Wj+3J7wkjdimu8c0unFge7l6jTBjIZcVXQcltK3n8uYne2OLScn0J\nCbImSaDFwQKxOGbX5aflK3v3QWK9+atAlCCSDXYLRg1gF3yQhrCMBR67k1dKnTq8\nc6OVbbYC5IiLBNT1CP483OMXNgTzvpTVPbd/wxoZD2aLkC0CeV1dgBNl8L5no+a5\nxVHtIFHQPJpVYPtK/FSDX0HXAX1kLPLTFt1aUUM9l1+Eye7bY03OV+w48a032aOm\n9SK+0ATZZp1eG1YddisdzyPcSP8Uz+NAh/q/2wXKsRTeK9XlgQjOB1eunletxyiI\nvhHSag63A7QTGyYETlXRA1SuLKp8ASB1f9i+tDPKr8O5rFy7fDo43IowkD9yJ/Hm\n+LsyFSM9lySeG8MLWUUf\n=s9It\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T05:08:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDc3ZWM0ZjJmZDUzMzJkYWIwMjc2ZDEyOGIxMDg2MmVmYjVlODExYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3","sha":"c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3"}],"sha":"77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/77ec4f2fd5332dab0276d128b10862efb5e811c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:51:05Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:51:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14): demo login picker + identity banner for the live demo URL (#19)\n\nA live demo URL with no real auth is fine, but \"edit ?devRole=IC into\nthe URL bar\" is a hostile entry point for stakeholders or recruiters.\nReplaces the silent MANAGER auto-default with an explicit identity-\npicker landing page, plus a thin always-visible banner once a role is\nchosen.\n\nMechanism\n=========\n\nmain.tsx now boots in three branches:\n\n  1. demoMode && no devRole param  -> render <DemoLoginPicker />\n                                       (skip devAuth, skip app routes)\n  2. demoMode && devRole param     -> install devAuth, render the app\n                                       with <DemoModeBanner /> on top\n  3. neither (real production)     -> install devAuth only if DEV;\n                                       render app; banner stays out\n\nDemo mode is gated on VITE_DEMO_MODE === ''true'', the same flag that\nkeeps devAuth in the production-built bundle (MEMO #12). The picker\nis dynamically imported so non-demo builds don''t pay the bundle cost.\n\nThe picker''s click handler sets `?devRole=<role>` on\nwindow.location.href and calls window.location.assign(...) -- a full\nreload, so devAuth''s boot-time URL parse picks up the new role.\nHashRouter routes live after `#`; the query param goes on the *real*\nlocation.search so devAuth''s `new URLSearchParams(window.location.\nsearch)` finds it.\n\nComponents\n==========\n\nsrc/dev/DemoLoginPicker.tsx\n  Centred card with four role buttons. Names match DemoDataSeeder:\n    - Ada Lovelace       (MANAGER)\n    - Ben Carter         (IC reporting to Ada)\n    - Frankie Hopper     (IC, no manager)\n    - Site Admin         (ADMIN)\n  Each card has the role''s title, name, and a one-line description of\n  what the viewer will see if they pick it. Bottom note clarifies the\n  demo data: \"1 manager · 3 ICs · 1 unassigned · current week + 1\n  prior reconciled week.\"\n\nsrc/dev/DemoModeBanner.tsx\n  Thin amber strip above the AppShell. Shows \"DEMO  Viewing as <name>\n  · <title>\" and a \"Switch identity\" link that drops the devRole\n  param and reloads (back to the picker). Banner is gated outside any\n  route so it survives navigation.\n\nExisting devAuth.ts is unchanged. The picker writes the same query\nparam devAuth already reads; this is a UX wrapper, not a re-impl.\n\nmain.tsx changes\n================\n\n  - parseDemoRole() helper replaces the inline `?devRole=` parsing\n    that used to live only inside devAuth.ts. main.tsx and devAuth.ts\n    now share the same role-resolution contract: URL param wins, then\n    VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE env, then null. Returning null is the new\n    \"show the picker\" signal.\n  - VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE env-var path preserved so Playwright + Cypress\n    (which preset role via env) skip the picker.\n  - Banner imports dynamically so the federated production build\n    (which never reaches main.tsx anyway) doesn''t accidentally pay\n    the bundle cost via tree-shaker confusion.\n\nTests\n=====\n\n  src/dev/DemoLoginPicker.test.tsx (5 tests)\n    - renders four role cards\n    - exposes each role with a name + title\n    - navigates to ?devRole=<role> on click (per role)\n    - preserves existing query params (utm_source etc.) when adding\n      devRole\n\n  src/dev/DemoModeBanner.test.tsx (3 tests)\n    - renders the active identity name + title\n    - rerenders correctly across IC / IC_NULL_MANAGER / ADMIN\n    - clears ?devRole= and reloads on Switch click; preserves the\n      hash route so the user lands back at the same page\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck  clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test       180/180 pass (was 172;\n                                                       +8 new)\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit  coverage 88.23/84.45/\n                                                       91.83/88.23 -- over 80%\n  - yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)                clean\n  - yarn format:check (root)                           clean\n\nWhat this doesn''t do\n====================\n\n  - No real authentication. Picker hands out any identity to anyone.\n    The banner explicitly says so.\n  - No password-reset / email-verification / MFA / any of that.\n    Not in scope for a demo.\n  - No backend changes. Backend still trusts JWTs signed with the\n    e2e-keys public key; identity is whatever the picker tells the\n    devAuth shim to mint.\n\nReal auth (Auth0, MEMO #12 + #13) remains the production target;\nthe picker turns OFF when VITE_DEMO_MODE is false.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0c94a5cff824c1f9d6a1f42bb3fec720b3f751a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/e0c94a5cff824c1f9d6a1f42bb3fec720b3f751a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3","verification":{"payload":"tree e0c94a5cff824c1f9d6a1f42bb3fec720b3f751a\nparent 19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777351865 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777351865 -0600\n\ntask(14): demo login picker + identity banner for the live demo URL (#19)\n\nA live demo URL with no real auth is fine, but \"edit ?devRole=IC into\nthe URL bar\" is a hostile entry point for stakeholders or recruiters.\nReplaces the silent MANAGER auto-default with an explicit identity-\npicker landing page, plus a thin always-visible banner once a role is\nchosen.\n\nMechanism\n=========\n\nmain.tsx now boots in three branches:\n\n  1. demoMode && no devRole param  -> render <DemoLoginPicker />\n                                       (skip devAuth, skip app routes)\n  2. demoMode && devRole param     -> install devAuth, render the app\n                                       with <DemoModeBanner /> on top\n  3. neither (real production)     -> install devAuth only if DEV;\n                                       render app; banner stays out\n\nDemo mode is gated on VITE_DEMO_MODE === ''true'', the same flag that\nkeeps devAuth in the production-built bundle (MEMO #12). The picker\nis dynamically imported so non-demo builds don''t pay the bundle cost.\n\nThe picker''s click handler sets `?devRole=<role>` on\nwindow.location.href and calls window.location.assign(...) -- a full\nreload, so devAuth''s boot-time URL parse picks up the new role.\nHashRouter routes live after `#`; the query param goes on the *real*\nlocation.search so devAuth''s `new URLSearchParams(window.location.\nsearch)` finds it.\n\nComponents\n==========\n\nsrc/dev/DemoLoginPicker.tsx\n  Centred card with four role buttons. Names match DemoDataSeeder:\n    - Ada Lovelace       (MANAGER)\n    - Ben Carter         (IC reporting to Ada)\n    - Frankie Hopper     (IC, no manager)\n    - Site Admin         (ADMIN)\n  Each card has the role''s title, name, and a one-line description of\n  what the viewer will see if they pick it. Bottom note clarifies the\n  demo data: \"1 manager · 3 ICs · 1 unassigned · current week + 1\n  prior reconciled week.\"\n\nsrc/dev/DemoModeBanner.tsx\n  Thin amber strip above the AppShell. Shows \"DEMO  Viewing as <name>\n  · <title>\" and a \"Switch identity\" link that drops the devRole\n  param and reloads (back to the picker). Banner is gated outside any\n  route so it survives navigation.\n\nExisting devAuth.ts is unchanged. The picker writes the same query\nparam devAuth already reads; this is a UX wrapper, not a re-impl.\n\nmain.tsx changes\n================\n\n  - parseDemoRole() helper replaces the inline `?devRole=` parsing\n    that used to live only inside devAuth.ts. main.tsx and devAuth.ts\n    now share the same role-resolution contract: URL param wins, then\n    VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE env, then null. Returning null is the new\n    \"show the picker\" signal.\n  - VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE env-var path preserved so Playwright + Cypress\n    (which preset role via env) skip the picker.\n  - Banner imports dynamically so the federated production build\n    (which never reaches main.tsx anyway) doesn''t accidentally pay\n    the bundle cost via tree-shaker confusion.\n\nTests\n=====\n\n  src/dev/DemoLoginPicker.test.tsx (5 tests)\n    - renders four role cards\n    - exposes each role with a name + title\n    - navigates to ?devRole=<role> on click (per role)\n    - preserves existing query params (utm_source etc.) when adding\n      devRole\n\n  src/dev/DemoModeBanner.test.tsx (3 tests)\n    - renders the active identity name + title\n    - rerenders correctly across IC / IC_NULL_MANAGER / ADMIN\n    - clears ?devRole= and reloads on Switch click; preserves the\n      hash route so the user lands back at the same page\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck  clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test       180/180 pass (was 172;\n                                                       +8 new)\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit  coverage 88.23/84.45/\n                                                       91.83/88.23 -- over 80%\n  - yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)                clean\n  - yarn format:check (root)                           clean\n\nWhat this doesn''t do\n====================\n\n  - No real authentication. Picker hands out any identity to anyone.\n    The banner explicitly says so.\n  - No password-reset / email-verification / MFA / any of that.\n    Not in scope for a demo.\n  - No backend changes. Backend still trusts JWTs signed with the\n    e2e-keys public key; identity is whatever the picker tells the\n    devAuth shim to mint.\n\nReal auth (Auth0, MEMO #12 + #13) remains the production target;\nthe picker turns OFF when VITE_DEMO_MODE is false.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8Dy5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEiAQAI1hbrF7VwTxUNiCBUj3VDK6\nf0zqc+kULOwb8zSS5Z9biyEhi1+8R0lxKxHmFhFLNNhuMoaLfz1K8lGcDfnwPqhg\nICnzz31cTa2XC46vf3nb+BtqP3r7ftUnb+/WimEtZHLNIVpNbKVxXZD7Z9OZ8EXM\nqs6byT2/yyNOoLgGW0Q02MV2646ML2S1+iQ5+G29ww5GYgVSdd9rxsLXhk1ws+eK\n7smXjRyLm+wdqqTp4RRSO5pkBL+4bfwS1M49wwOd/lLFPC8JB