/api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c5b9cf8ac43877948eaccfb5f5ea44a35dc3bbe3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:38:29Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:38:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-railway): single-service Railway deploy — $5-7/mo always-on demo (#18)\n\n* task(14-railway): single-service Railway deploy -- $5-7/mo always-on demo\n\nSwitches the active demo target from AWS to Railway under the $10/mo\nbudget. AWS Terraform stays in the repo (dormant) per MEMO #12; Railway\nbecomes the path that actually has a live URL. See MEMO #13 for the\ntrade-offs accepted.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\napps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled\n---------------------------------------------\n\nNew three-stage Dockerfile that bundles frontend + backend into one\nSpring Boot jar. Stage 1 builds the frontend (yarn + vite) with\nVITE_DEMO_MODE=true and VITE_API_BASE_URL=\"\" (same-origin). Stage 2\ncopies the resulting `dist/` into\napps/weekly-commit-service/src/main/resources/static/ before\nmvn package, so Spring''s default ResourceHandlerRegistry picks it\nup. Stage 3 is the JRE runtime image.\n\nHonors Railway''s $PORT injection: ENTRYPOINT maps PORT -> SERVER_PORT\nvia -Dserver.port=${PORT:-8080}.\n\nThe original apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile (used by AWS ECS +\ndocker-compose.demo.yml) is unchanged. Two Dockerfiles, one per\ndeployment target.\n\nSecurityConfig opens static-asset paths\n---------------------------------------\n\nAdds a permitAll() matcher for `/`, `/index.html`, `/favicon.ico`,\n`/assets/**`. The frontend bundle has to load before any JS runs and\nmints a JWT, so the static surface has to be open. The matcher is\ndeliberately specific (not `/*`) so future API routes added at the\nroot won''t accidentally fall under permitAll. On the AWS / dev paths\nwhere the frontend is hosted separately, these matchers don''t match\nany real request -- effectively a no-op there.\n\nrailway.toml\n------------\n\nTells Railway to use the bundled Dockerfile, with healthcheck path\n/actuator/health/readiness and ON_FAILURE restart. Everything else\n(Postgres add-on, env vars, GitHub link, domain) is dashboard-only\nper Railway''s current product surface; documented in\ninfra/railway/SETUP.md.\n\n.github/workflows/deploy-railway.yml\n------------------------------------\n\nTriggered on push to main. Pre-flights RAILWAY_TOKEN; if absent,\nemits a clear summary pointing at SETUP.md and exits cleanly. If\npresent, installs the Railway CLI, runs `railway up --service ... --ci`\nto trigger a build, then prints the live URL via `railway domain`.\n\ninfra/railway/SETUP.md\n----------------------\n\nThe dashboard walk-through that Railway''s CLI doesn''t cover: project\ncreation, Postgres add-on, env-var mapping (Railway''s PG* vars ->\nSpring''s SPRING_DATASOURCE_*), token generation, GH secrets wiring.\n~10 minutes of dashboard clicks once.\n\nMEMO #13 + TASK_LIST group 14\n-----------------------------\n\nRecords the deviation. The PRD''s MVP18 \"S3 + CloudFront + remoteEntry.js\"\ntarget is further from this single-origin Spring service than from the\nAWS path it replaced; the trade-off favoured \"URL is reliably online\nfor under $10/mo\" over \"matches PRD architecture more closely.\" AWS\ncode is preserved unchanged so the path back is git-revert-clean.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  - mvn spotless:check, spotbugs:check                   clean\n  - mvn test                                             260/260 pass\n  - mvn -Djacoco.check.halt=true verify -DskipUnitTests=true\n                                                         39 ITs pass + JaCoCo gate met\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck    clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test         172/172 pass\n  - yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)                  clean\n  - yarn format:check (root)                             clean\n  - docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled .   builds clean\n\nNot verified (cannot from agent context):\n  - Railway dashboard setup -- your hands; ~10 min once\n  - End-to-end smoke against the *.up.railway.app URL after first deploy\n\nApply path\n==========\n\n  1. Follow infra/railway/SETUP.md once (~10 min dashboard work)\n  2. gh secret set RAILWAY_TOKEN --body <project token>\n  3. gh variable set RAILWAY_SERVICE --body weekly-commit\n  4. Merge this PR. Next push to main triggers deploy-railway.yml,\n     which builds + deploys + prints the live URL.\n\n* task(14-railway): add top-level README\n\nThe repo had no top-level README -- a new contributor or anyone\nclicking through from GitHub had to grep the docs/ directory to figure\nout what the project is, how to run it, and where to deploy. Adding a\nsingle-page tour that points at the right docs.\n\nSections:\n\n  - Quick start for the docker-compose demo + per-component dev commands\n  - Architecture overview (stack table + pointer to TECH_STACK.md /\n    MEMO.md)\n  - Repository layout (annotated tree of apps/, libs/, infra/, docs/,\n    .github/workflows/)\n  - Deployment paths (Railway active, AWS dormant, PRD prod target\n    deferred) -- pointers to MEMO #12-#13 for the why\n  - Contributing -- pointer to CLAUDE.md for the guardrails, plus the\n    actual lint/test commands CI runs\n  - Status table summarising MVP coverage, test coverage, mutation\n    score target, and the live URL (pending Railway dashboard setup)\n\nNo .prettierignore rule violation -- *.md is already on the ignore list\nso root format:check stays clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"00ad4085c18717fa772c93f96509db7093eae9aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/00ad4085c18717fa772c93f96509db7093eae9aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 00ad4085c18717fa772c93f96509db7093eae9aa\nparent 0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777351109 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777351109 -0600\n\ntask(14-railway): single-service Railway deploy — $5-7/mo always-on demo (#18)\n\n* task(14-railway): single-service Railway deploy -- $5-7/mo always-on demo\n\nSwitches the active demo target from AWS to Railway under the $10/mo\nbudget. AWS Terraform stays in the repo (dormant) per MEMO #12; Railway\nbecomes the path that actually has a live URL. See MEMO #13 for the\ntrade-offs accepted.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\napps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled\n---------------------------------------------\n\nNew three-stage Dockerfile that bundles frontend + backend into one\nSpring Boot jar. Stage 1 builds the frontend (yarn + vite) with\nVITE_DEMO_MODE=true and VITE_API_BASE_URL=\"\" (same-origin). Stage 2\ncopies the resulting `dist/` into\napps/weekly-commit-service/src/main/resources/static/ before\nmvn package, so Spring''s default ResourceHandlerRegistry picks it\nup. Stage 3 is the JRE runtime image.\n\nHonors Railway''s $PORT injection: ENTRYPOINT maps PORT -> SERVER_PORT\nvia -Dserver.port=${PORT:-8080}.\n\nThe original apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile (used by AWS ECS +\ndocker-compose.demo.yml) is unchanged. Two Dockerfiles, one per\ndeployment target.\n\nSecurityConfig opens static-asset paths\n---------------------------------------\n\nAdds a permitAll() matcher for `/`, `/index.html`, `/favicon.ico`,\n`/assets/**`. The frontend bundle has to load before any JS runs and\nmints a JWT, so the static surface has to be open. The matcher is\ndeliberately specific (not `/*`) so future API routes added at the\nroot won''t accidentally fall under permitAll. On the AWS / dev paths\nwhere the frontend is hosted separately, these matchers don''t match\nany real request -- effectively a no-op there.\n\nrailway.toml\n------------\n\nTells Railway to use the bundled Dockerfile, with healthcheck path\n/actuator/health/readiness and ON_FAILURE restart. Everything else\n(Postgres add-on, env vars, GitHub link, domain) is dashboard-only\nper Railway''s current product surface; documented in\ninfra/railway/SETUP.md.\n\n.github/workflows/deploy-railway.yml\n------------------------------------\n\nTriggered on push to main. Pre-flights RAILWAY_TOKEN; if absent,\nemits a clear summary pointing at SETUP.md and exits cleanly. If\npresent, installs the Railway CLI, runs `railway up --service ... --ci`\nto trigger a build, then prints the live URL via `railway domain`.\n\ninfra/railway/SETUP.md\n----------------------\n\nThe dashboard walk-through that Railway''s CLI doesn''t cover: project\ncreation, Postgres add-on, env-var mapping (Railway''s PG* vars ->\nSpring''s SPRING_DATASOURCE_*), token generation, GH secrets wiring.\n~10 minutes of dashboard clicks once.\n\nMEMO #13 + TASK_LIST group 14\n-----------------------------\n\nRecords the deviation. The PRD''s MVP18 \"S3 + CloudFront + remoteEntry.js\"\ntarget is further from this single-origin Spring service than from the\nAWS path it replaced; the trade-off favoured \"URL is reliably online\nfor under $10/mo\" over \"matches PRD architecture more closely.\" AWS\ncode is preserved unchanged so the path back is git-revert-clean.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  - mvn spotless:check, spotbugs:check                   clean\n  - mvn test                                             260/260 pass\n  - mvn -Djacoco.check.halt=true verify -DskipUnitTests=true\n                                                         39 ITs pass + JaCoCo gate met\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck    clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test         172/172 pass\n  - yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects)                  clean\n  - yarn format:check (root)                             clean\n  - docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile.bundled .   builds clean\n\nNot verified (cannot from agent context):\n  - Railway dashboard setup -- your hands; ~10 min once\n  - End-to-end smoke against the *.up.railway.app URL after first deploy\n\nApply path\n==========\n\n  1. Follow infra/railway/SETUP.md once (~10 min dashboard work)\n  2. gh secret set RAILWAY_TOKEN --body <project token>\n  3. gh variable set RAILWAY_SERVICE --body weekly-commit\n  4. Merge this PR. Next push to main triggers deploy-railway.yml,\n     which builds + deploys + prints the live URL.\n\n* task(14-railway): add top-level README\n\nThe repo had no top-level README -- a new contributor or anyone\nclicking through from GitHub had to grep the docs/ directory to figure\nout what the project is, how to run it, and where to deploy. Adding a\nsingle-page tour that points at the right docs.\n\nSections:\n\n  - Quick start for the docker-compose demo + per-component dev commands\n  - Architecture overview (stack table + pointer to TECH_STACK.md /\n    MEMO.md)\n  - Repository layout (annotated tree of apps/, libs/, infra/, docs/,\n    .github/workflows/)\n  - Deployment paths (Railway active, AWS dormant, PRD prod target\n    deferred) -- pointers to MEMO #12-#13 for the why\n  - Contributing -- pointer to CLAUDE.md for the guardrails, plus the\n    actual lint/test commands CI runs\n  - Status table summarising MVP coverage, test coverage, mutation\n    score target, and the live URL (pending Railway dashboard setup)\n\nNo .prettierignore rule violation -- *.md is already on the ignore list\nso root format:check stays clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8DnGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmtYQAFk1qDLrw/TEEW4nbp+zxsQS\nnZ6RG1of6t2f98KgFEj3SjU7ha4L/yA2A6STOBcLu0UmpopliO/+F5F39W9u2zhj\nINx2Lf59mFw54TIkfORPneyOHS6ofr5K3qAJRJk4T2XMI+kHCFpmZyFr/0P72j3A\n6APjauq+oH3b24i91eVjwQ9VEdomebNLwJCSPT/mzN4IflKaLqsvoAV2ShDiSnT9\nuPrHotZJP8J7ZdnJ5SmObMLO0xP8zIOSV0U3+nVaH8vAWYIfkC45Pk1qUb/KfK21\nkR3eRTgKm8UjwDN5PD1wSZay4L+kP8pcMxuN5rwQndxvXQrrD3QJdJVNzDaTb/cd\nqiIxoZuHf/zb5POvgtcvTff1RUxFsDx5pTOp9GwLsFnYOa00uuJoV+eaQWqhtcxd\nixBsrOSOgd/gohsJAHwt5M733uQ3TqP/LoDsRrSdrSD3VZ2qWmazD4zppDL4Y9mF\n5GpTkQ56o9ld5o0sly6tlFJCByQtIsKKeXcbu6fJcz8xt/zu+anzGJNKWwzs2t2d\nmwgL5mxNAnF1HHbubrVmmpQ2DuGDue0H7U1SfvGRtEXRVjjEKZf9iIDsxW+V+9Ik\nFfLEOTKKNkElKkjjHLD9zuRP7LWpcFh/e5ulSmEpF5yz5TGrNwybr4bPIbmiDAKQ\nDfZJ5VX1sBtxM42SkQzF\n=giGY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T04:38:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDE5Y2Q3OTBmNjg2MTkyNTYzMzg1YTU0MDY3Mjg1ZGEzMWJmYmY4YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d","sha":"0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d"}],"sha":"19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/19cd790f686192563385a54067285da31bfbf8b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:15:26Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T04:15:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-cloud): deploy-demo guard rails — skip on docs + fail fast on missing creds (#17)\n\n* task(14-cloud): deploy-demo guard rails -- skip on docs, fail fast on missing creds\n\nTwo related fixes after the merge of #15 and #16 each triggered a\ndeploy-demo run that failed at \"Could not load credentials from any\nproviders\" -- no useful signal for an operator looking at the failure.\n\nFix 1: paths-ignore for doc-only changes\n========================================\n\nThe previous path filter included `infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**`,\nwhich catches the README and .gitignore inside that directory. A\ndoc-only PR shouldn''t trigger a deploy attempt.\n\nAdded paths-ignore covering:\n  - **/*.md           docs anywhere\n  - **/.gitignore     gitignores anywhere\n  - **/README         non-md README variants\n  - apps/.../cypress/, tests/, wiremock/, src/test/  test-only dirs\n\nFix 2: preflight job that fails fast with a clear message\n=========================================================\n\nBefore this commit, a missing AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN secret produced this\nerror in step 1 of the terraform job:\n\n  Error: Credentials could not be loaded, please check your action\n  inputs: Could not load credentials from any providers\n\nThat error is technically correct but doesn''t tell anyone what to do\nabout it -- the action doesn''t know the secret is missing vs. the role\nARN being malformed.\n\nThe new preflight job runs first, checks for AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN +\nTF_STATE_BUCKET + TF_LOCK_TABLE, and on miss emits ::error:: + writes\na markdown block to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY explaining the bootstrap path:\n\n  ./infra/terraform/apply.sh\n\nPlus the dependency wiring: terraform needs preflight, and the rest of\nthe jobs transitively depend through terraform -> preflight, so the\nwhole pipeline shorts cleanly when bootstrap hasn''t run yet.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - python3 -c yaml.safe_load: parses clean\n  - yarn format:check (root, prettier): clean\n  - YAML structure: preflight is the only new job; existing job\n    dependencies preserved (build-backend / build-frontend / smoke\n    all transitively depend on preflight via terraform)\n\nAfter this lands the next push that matches the path filter and has\nthe secrets configured will work; pushes that match but lack secrets\nwill fail in <30 seconds with a clear summary instead of cryptic\nerrors. Doc-only pushes won''t trigger the workflow at all.\n\n* task(14-cloud): fix workflow parse error -- paths + paths-ignore mutually exclusive\n\nGitHub Actions rejects workflows with both `paths` and `paths-ignore`\non the same event filter. PyYAML and other generic YAML parsers accept\nthe combination (it''s syntactically valid YAML), so my pre-push parse\ncheck returned green and the failure only surfaced when GitHub tried\nto instantiate the workflow.\n\nSymptom on the previous push:\n  conclusion: failure\n  jobs: []\n  log: log not found\n  workflow name reported as \".github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml\" (the\n  file path) rather than the resolved name \"deploy-demo\" -- GitHub''s\n  signal that it never got past the YAML-load step.\n\nFix: drop paths-ignore, replace the broad `paths` globs with narrower\nones that already exclude docs + test dirs. Specific changes:\n\n  - Drop:    apps/weekly-commit-service/**\n    Add:     apps/weekly-commit-service/src/main/**, pom.xml, Dockerfile\n\n  - Drop:    apps/weekly-commit-ui/**\n    Add:     apps/weekly-commit-ui/src/**, Dockerfile, nginx-demo.conf,\n             package.json, vite.config.ts, tailwind.config.ts\n\n  - Drop:    libs/**\n    Add:     libs/**/src/**, libs/**/package.json\n\n  - Drop:    infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**\n    Add:     infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**.tf\n\nThis excludes README, .gitignore, src/test/, cypress/, tests/,\nwiremock/ from triggering the workflow without needing paths-ignore.\n\nTrade-off documented inline: someone editing just the bootstrap/\ndirectory won''t trigger a redeploy (correct -- bootstrap doesn''t\ntouch the running stack). Someone editing only the demo-deploy\nREADME still won''t because the path filter requires *.tf in that dir.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  python3 -c yaml.safe_load: parses (false positive on the previous\n                              attempt; flagging here so I don''t repeat)\n  yarn format:check: clean\n\nThis is a forward fix on top of the previous commit, not an amend.\nHistory stays clear about the bug and its fix.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e380ca9976093d49a64067bf34e5686765ec80d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/4e380ca9976093d49a64067bf34e5686765ec80d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e380ca9976093d49a64067bf34e5686765ec80d\nparent d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777349726 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777349726 -0600\n\ntask(14-cloud): deploy-demo guard rails — skip on docs + fail fast on missing creds (#17)\n\n* task(14-cloud): deploy-demo guard rails -- skip on docs, fail fast on missing creds\n\nTwo related fixes after the merge of #15 and #16 each triggered a\ndeploy-demo run that failed at \"Could not load credentials from any\nproviders\" -- no useful signal for an operator looking at the failure.\n\nFix 1: paths-ignore for doc-only changes\n========================================\n\nThe previous path filter included `infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**`,\nwhich catches the README and .gitignore inside that directory. A\ndoc-only PR shouldn''t trigger a deploy attempt.\n\nAdded paths-ignore covering:\n  - **/*.md           docs anywhere\n  - **/.gitignore     gitignores anywhere\n  - **/README         non-md README variants\n  - apps/.../cypress/, tests/, wiremock/, src/test/  test-only dirs\n\nFix 2: preflight job that fails fast with a clear message\n=========================================================\n\nBefore this commit, a missing AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN secret produced this\nerror in step 1 of the terraform job:\n\n  Error: Credentials could not be loaded, please check your action\n  inputs: Could not load credentials from any providers\n\nThat error is technically correct but doesn''t tell anyone what to do\nabout it -- the action doesn''t know the secret is missing vs. the role\nARN being malformed.\n\nThe new preflight job runs first, checks for AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN +\nTF_STATE_BUCKET + TF_LOCK_TABLE, and on miss emits ::error:: + writes\na markdown block to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY explaining the bootstrap path:\n\n  ./infra/terraform/apply.sh\n\nPlus the dependency wiring: terraform needs preflight, and the rest of\nthe jobs transitively depend through terraform -> preflight, so the\nwhole pipeline shorts cleanly when bootstrap hasn''t run yet.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - python3 -c yaml.safe_load: parses clean\n  - yarn format:check (root, prettier): clean\n  - YAML structure: preflight is the only new job; existing job\n    dependencies preserved (build-backend / build-frontend / smoke\n    all transitively depend on preflight via terraform)\n\nAfter this lands the next push that matches the path filter and has\nthe secrets configured will work; pushes that match but lack secrets\nwill fail in <30 seconds with a clear summary instead of cryptic\nerrors. Doc-only pushes won''t trigger the workflow at all.\n\n* task(14-cloud): fix workflow parse error -- paths + paths-ignore mutually exclusive\n\nGitHub Actions rejects workflows with both `paths` and `paths-ignore`\non the same event filter. PyYAML and other generic YAML parsers accept\nthe combination (it''s syntactically valid YAML), so my pre-push parse\ncheck returned green and the failure only surfaced when GitHub tried\nto instantiate the workflow.\n\nSymptom on the previous push:\n  conclusion: failure\n  jobs: []\n  log: log not found\n  workflow name reported as \".github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml\" (the\n  file path) rather than the resolved name \"deploy-demo\" -- GitHub''s\n  signal that it never got past the YAML-load step.\n\nFix: drop paths-ignore, replace the broad `paths` globs with narrower\nones that already exclude docs + test dirs. Specific changes:\n\n  - Drop:    apps/weekly-commit-service/**\n    Add:     apps/weekly-commit-service/src/main/**, pom.xml, Dockerfile\n\n  - Drop:    apps/weekly-commit-ui/**\n    Add:     apps/weekly-commit-ui/src/**, Dockerfile, nginx-demo.conf,\n             package.json, vite.config.ts, tailwind.config.ts\n\n  - Drop:    libs/**\n    Add:     libs/**/src/**, libs/**/package.json\n\n  - Drop:    infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**\n    Add:     infra/terraform/demo-deploy/**.tf\n\nThis excludes README, .gitignore, src/test/, cypress/, tests/,\nwiremock/ from triggering the workflow without needing paths-ignore.\n\nTrade-off documented inline: someone editing just the bootstrap/\ndirectory won''t trigger a redeploy (correct -- bootstrap doesn''t\ntouch the running stack). Someone editing only the demo-deploy\nREADME still won''t because the path filter requires *.tf in that dir.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  python3 -c yaml.safe_load: parses (false positive on the previous\n                              attempt; flagging here so I don''t repeat)\n  yarn format:check: clean\n\nThis is a forward fix on top of the previous commit, not an amend.\nHistory stays clear about the bug and its fix.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8DReCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPZcQAAQtvEnsuCEiaT9pO1VKF17R\nAX2rJrm3SSq3VSSqd3oyhS7q+Kkz7U83fcViFwtf8ZSB+eDbFGxxziZJp0jBy3Go\n6M239HUbWHezLLvlnvmHR4QIAqr8JOiPOgUpb1+vEYbMZrggRoKLwp+Zatp7QXi/\nIwtmaV50QFObZdpszKebiboZ1AQNTCEATrb9IhUXJnLj7UF2SAXMNiFNbbk4C87G\n1kPzbMDljcKN7GK7eva6sHUiMvtw7PkpQjvjVJuK03TpV1SgQxEoFsluwR2N7M/g\nf/UJrh9ZEuZ8L2RtCXcbA1xVYW+vlxhsVVq4smtbCTalEn9bqtqkU6NLobX4IAOO\ngCJwrOsh3U3eHc5fOVdq7y51TJi7uRGOwVQTuzbO5ac04rjCjVD3j8DT8FhMocy6\nIS/HSu5FvCgY2ZEXhLW6UQB1erDwB5qaTfRT4USSC4u8MW5fcA8rb3J2is0Vxwwk\nBR9T9C+ii7QfYk/uVMHuqehXYCjs18XG9xUxLFE0fz1jAE3WmU+wCu4oQrF+5pEA\nLb9BPLXZPfIRSIvqfIPVY4u9+THL27PWTG3cFv95tqxNmuOR0ZwoUCKk657/6RHG\n7X5wnzezCON2Rz0QkHxEcdhwfGqpIoX8cA4Ep6zNyq2Qdur6AKscrB8hZwJ1QGcN\nSKyqLDqy+6qKmAyGd6+Y\n=zwQf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T04:15:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDBmYTZmMDYyMTBkNzhjMmFjNjg1ZWY5YWM4MjhiMDdlZGFlZTFiNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e","sha":"d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e"}],"sha":"0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0fa6f06210d78c2ac685ef9ac828b07edaee1b4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:16:51Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T03:16:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-cloud): add infra/terraform/apply.sh -- one-shot AWS deploy (#16)\n\nSingle-command path from \"merged Terraform\" to \"AWS infrastructure\nprovisioned.\" Replaces the six-command manual sequence in the README\nwith a guided script that runs bootstrap -> wires GitHub repo\nsecrets/vars -> applies demo-deploy with a placeholder image.\n\nWhat the script does\n====================\n\n  1. Pre-flight: confirms aws / terraform / gh / jq are installed and\n     prints versions. Confirms aws sts get-caller-identity returns an\n     identity (clear error if not, with three suggested fixes:\n     `aws configure`, `aws sso login`, your org''s auth tool). Confirms\n     gh auth status. Resolves the GitHub repo via `gh repo view`.\n\n  2. Confirmation prompt: prints the AWS account, region, repo, and\n     what the script will create + cost estimate, then asks y/N.\n     Aborts cleanly on N or Ctrl+C.\n\n  3. Bootstrap apply: terraform init + apply in the bootstrap/ stack,\n     captures the four outputs (state bucket, lock table, GHA role\n     ARN, account id).\n\n  4. GitHub repo secrets/vars: sets AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN as a secret;\n     TF_STATE_BUCKET, TF_LOCK_TABLE, AWS_REGION as variables.\n\n  5. demo-deploy apply: terraform init with the bootstrap-output backend\n     config, then apply with image_tag=placeholder. Captures the live\n     CloudFront URL + ECR repo URL + S3 bucket name.\n\n  6. Final report: prints the next step (gh workflow run deploy-demo)\n     plus the four demo identity URLs (devRole query params).\n\nWhat the script does NOT do\n===========================\n\n  - Take or transmit AWS credentials. The script never reads\n    ~/.aws/credentials or any environment variable that might contain\n    a credential. It calls aws sts get-caller-identity and uses the\n    shell''s existing auth state. If the shell isn''t authenticated,\n    the script aborts with a clear error -- no silent failure.\n\n  - Push images. The deploy-demo.yml workflow does that on the next\n    main push (or via gh workflow run deploy-demo.yml --ref main).\n    The script''s final output points the user there.\n\nPortability notes\n=================\n\n  - bash 3.2 compatible (macOS default). Avoided ${var,,} -- used\n    `tr ''[:upper:]'' ''[:lower:]''` instead.\n  - set -euo pipefail at top; clean failure on any command error.\n  - Works from any cwd (resolves SCRIPT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE).\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - bash -n syntax check passes\n  - Pre-flight checks all four CLIs by name, not by behavior, so the\n    script doesn''t try to actually authenticate before it knows the\n    shell is set up.\n  - yarn format:check (root, prettier) clean\n  - terraform fmt -check / validate unchanged from previous commits\n\nThe script remains user-invoked. The agent does not have AWS\ncredentials and cannot run it. This script is the cleanest possible\nhand-off from \"code merged\" to \"infrastructure provisioned\" --\ndocumented as the recommended path in both the demo-deploy README\nand docs/runbook.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0913fee221888d5e97def5c282cb8b0da2a24122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/0913fee221888d5e97def5c282cb8b0da2a24122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0913fee221888d5e97def5c282cb8b0da2a24122\nparent 18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777346211 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777346211 -0600\n\ntask(14-cloud): add infra/terraform/apply.sh -- one-shot AWS deploy (#16)\n\nSingle-command path from \"merged Terraform\" to \"AWS infrastructure\nprovisioned.\" Replaces the six-command manual sequence in the README\nwith a guided script that runs bootstrap -> wires GitHub repo\nsecrets/vars -> applies demo-deploy with a placeholder image.\n\nWhat the script does\n====================\n\n  1. Pre-flight: confirms aws / terraform / gh / jq are installed and\n     prints versions. Confirms aws sts get-caller-identity returns an\n     identity (clear error if not, with three suggested fixes:\n     `aws configure`, `aws sso login`, your org''s auth tool). Confirms\n     gh auth status. Resolves the GitHub repo via `gh repo view`.\n\n  2. Confirmation prompt: prints the AWS account, region, repo, and\n     what the script will create + cost estimate, then asks y/N.\n     Aborts cleanly on N or Ctrl+C.\n\n  3. Bootstrap apply: terraform init + apply in the bootstrap/ stack,\n     captures the four outputs (state bucket, lock table, GHA role\n     ARN, account id).\n\n  4. GitHub repo secrets/vars: sets AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN as a secret;\n     TF_STATE_BUCKET, TF_LOCK_TABLE, AWS_REGION as variables.\n\n  5. demo-deploy apply: terraform init with the bootstrap-output backend\n     config, then apply with image_tag=placeholder. Captures the live\n     CloudFront URL + ECR repo URL + S3 bucket name.\n\n  6. Final report: prints the next step (gh workflow run deploy-demo)\n     plus the four demo identity URLs (devRole query params).\n\nWhat the script does NOT do\n===========================\n\n  - Take or transmit AWS credentials. The script never reads\n    ~/.aws/credentials or any environment variable that might contain\n    a credential. It calls aws sts get-caller-identity and uses the\n    shell''s existing auth state. If the shell isn''t authenticated,\n    the script aborts with a clear error -- no silent failure.\n\n  - Push images. The deploy-demo.yml workflow does that on the next\n    main push (or via gh workflow run deploy-demo.yml --ref main).\n    The script''s final output points the user there.\n\nPortability notes\n=================\n\n  - bash 3.2 compatible (macOS default). Avoided ${var,,} -- used\n    `tr ''[:upper:]'' ''[:lower:]''` instead.\n  - set -euo pipefail at top; clean failure on any command error.\n  - Works from any cwd (resolves SCRIPT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE).\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - bash -n syntax check passes\n  - Pre-flight checks all four CLIs by name, not by behavior, so the\n    script doesn''t try to actually authenticate before it knows the\n    shell is set up.\n  - yarn format:check (root, prettier) clean\n  - terraform fmt -check / validate unchanged from previous commits\n\nThe script remains user-invoked. The agent does not have AWS\ncredentials and cannot run it. This script is the cleanest possible\nhand-off from \"code merged\" to \"infrastructure provisioned\" --\ndocumented as the recommended path in both the demo-deploy README\nand docs/runbook.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8CajCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhWoQAIccZ0chTjEbTeUSUXLA7JHZ\nLlHEtDfYznXGSvHNyGg97iFaaAf6tVLwqQFBdB62fYg5G09ec+k1XO0lPl1RUTjO\n7kSZLz0vo/DDJlmUbeLZfYebWiOtZbAT4mV3KB4lyop1yfc56eVeOhm6v7WTcISk\nsvCM9DyO7nXHwJPdlMaUKWuMxEQM2lOqyZ+vGgd9G/jqM6uGHtwoJlUdylGGRusk\nwSMf6RHcTHzzBSworHpexFezPTRzbqnUryZK9POhrpnpDFuRpjanW0KwQXpmKbcQ\nLLdbf17JVoIz/WWQak+reDjqwLRPVTfrJAvq9DaebLG3w0+NdwL93PCS7NBIKcs7\nKAP2TIhB9MfB+2CDQNZJ84ev+LOA5BZzU6rkePboybknJOfqOKU4fKFs8ocvPIxD\nbvs1Px5Dhl3RlmaRedQ09fuIJ9/Eev7tdUxQyEzC/CP0gElYRkOE3HeERyp7BBrZ\nkNMsMFqx3ioz3d7rjDN0mHKYae2qv5eUmMZW8ji69zDUqMLPeoaD3wN/LrLBJcai\nuWzaVJFLz22EQWoNGnxZX2xkXUm19A/20SmhSxfkLMZBBoiZxOK9k8FsdLFI11Sv\nRLH9pesRQY+d8sjyuaV+ZOVWnWvQbQAELwtXd10HiLbNSKYwnThR47KraoDIngWW\nrZn9aDtbrYCB6ZEcaKr0\n=V+LY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T03:16:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGQ3MzMxYjhkNGYxODVhOTIwYzk4Y2VhNDFjMmJmMjRjNDc2NmI3MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33","sha":"18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33"}],"sha":"d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d7331b8d4f185a920c98cea41c2bf24c4766b72e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:12:41Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T02:12:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14-cloud): AWS cloud lift — Terraform + GHA deploy → live CloudFront URL (#15)\n\n* task(14-cloud): bootstrap module -- TF state bucket + DynamoDB lock + GitHub OIDC\n\nThe demo-deploy stack assumes its remote state bucket already exists.\nChicken-and-egg: a single root module can''t apply with a backend that\nreferences a bucket the same module is creating. Splitting bootstrap\ninto its own root module (with local state) breaks the cycle and keeps\nthe apply order linear: bootstrap once, demo-deploy any number of times.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n  - aws_s3_bucket \"tf_state\": versioned, AES256-encrypted, public-access-\n    blocked, 90-day non-current-version lifecycle. Bucket name includes\n    the AWS account id so two accounts can each own their own state\n    bucket without collision.\n\n  - aws_dynamodb_table \"tf_lock\": PAY_PER_REQUEST billing, single LockID\n    string hash key per the Terraform S3-backend lock contract. Empty\n    most of the time; transient rows during apply.\n\n  - aws_iam_openid_connect_provider \"github\" + aws_iam_role\n    \"github_actions_deploy\": trust policy gates assumption to the\n    configured `github_repository` (default seeincodes/WeeklyCommit) on\n    main branch + pull-request refs only. Permissions are deliberately\n    broad (\"ec2:*\", \"ecs:*\", etc.) for the demo; a follow-up commit can\n    scope down to specific resource ARNs once the demo-deploy stack has\n    applied at least once and ARNs are stable.\n\n  - .gitignore: keeps terraform.tfstate / .terraform/ out of the repo.\n    Bootstrap state is small, applied once, and the human running it\n    owns the file. If lost, re-import.\n\n  - README.md: apply procedure + the four outputs that need to be\n    pasted into demo-deploy/backend.tf and the GitHub repo secrets.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - terraform init -backend=false  (clean)\n  - terraform validate              (Success! The configuration is valid.)\n  - terraform fmt -check            (clean)\n\nApply runs from the user''s AWS-credentialed shell -- agent has no\ncredentials. Once applied, the next branch commits build the\ndemo-deploy stack on top.\n\n* task(14-cloud): demo-deploy Terraform stack -- VPC + ECR + RDS + ECS + ALB + S3 + CloudFront\n\nBuilds on the bootstrap module from the previous commit. State backend\nreferences the bootstrap-created bucket via -backend-config flags from CI\n(or hand-edit for local apply). All resources tagged for traceability.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n- versions.tf / variables.tf / locals.tf -- provider config + tunable\n  knobs + computed names. Defaults: us-east-1, demo environment, latest\n  image tag, smallest valid Fargate sizing (256 cpu / 512 mem).\n\n- backend.tf -- S3 backend with placeholder bucket + dynamodb_table\n  fields. CI passes them via `terraform init -backend-config=...`.\n\n- vpc.tf -- public-only VPC (no NAT). Two subnets across AZs as ALB +\n  RDS subnet group both require >=2 AZs. Three security groups:\n    alb         : 80 from world\n    ecs_task    : 8080 from alb sg only\n    rds         : 5432 from ecs_task sg only\n\n- ecr.tf -- backend image repo, AES256 encryption, scan-on-push, last-10\n  lifecycle rule.\n\n- rds.tf -- Postgres 16.4 db.t4g.micro single-AZ, gp3 20GB, encrypted\n  storage, 7d backups. Master password is `random_password` -> Secrets\n  Manager -> ECS task definition (never plaintext in TF state user-side).\n  parameter group sets log_min_duration_statement=1000ms.\n\n- iam.tf -- task_execution role with AWS-managed\n  AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy + inline secrets-read for the RDS\n  password ARN. Empty `task` role for the application; demo backend\n  makes no AWS API calls.\n\n- alb.tf -- ALB + target group + HTTP-only listener. Health check at\n  /actuator/health/readiness, 30s deregistration delay.\n\n- ecs.tf -- Fargate cluster with container insights enabled. Task\n  definition wires SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,demo, JDBC URL composed\n  from RDS endpoint, secrets-from-Secrets-Manager pattern for the DB\n  password. Service has lifecycle.ignore_changes on task_definition +\n  desired_count so the deploy workflow''s `aws ecs update-service` calls\n  don''t fight Terraform on subsequent applies.\n\n  IMPORTANT first-apply note in file: ECR is empty until the deploy\n  workflow runs, so the service will fail to start its first task\n  until at least one image is pushed. Deploy workflow handles this.\n\n- s3.tf + cloudfront.tf -- S3 bucket locked down to public-access-block;\n  CloudFront OAC fronts it. CloudFront distribution has two origins\n  (S3 default, ALB for /api/* + /actuator/*) and uses managed cache\n  policies (CachingOptimized for static, CachingDisabled for API).\n  custom_error_response sends 403/404 to /index.html for SPA fallback.\n  Default *.cloudfront.net cert; no domain set up.\n\n- cloudwatch.tf -- two alarms: rds-cpu-high (CPU >80% for 10m) and\n  ecs-running-low (running task count <1 for 5m).\n\n- outputs.tf -- cloudfront_url is the live URL once the deploy\n  workflow has shipped at least one bundle. Other outputs are wiring\n  for the deploy workflow.\n\n- .gitignore -- keeps .terraform/ + .terraform.lock.hcl out of repo.\n  Lock file commit is environment-specific; opt in later.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  terraform init -backend=false  : OK\n  terraform validate             : OK\n  terraform fmt -recursive       : clean (auto-formatted 3 files)\n\nNot verified (cannot from agent context):\n  terraform plan / apply against your AWS account. The user runs\n  the bootstrap apply once, then either runs the demo-deploy apply\n  manually or merges the next commit (the GHA deploy workflow) and\n  pushes. First apply has known chicken-and-egg with ECR (no image\n  yet); workflow handles it.\n\n* task(14-cloud): deploy-demo workflow + apply runbook + cloud README\n\nWires the GitHub Actions push-to-main → live URL pipeline on top of the\nTerraform stacks from the previous two commits.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n.github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml\n---------------------------------\n\nFour jobs, sequential dependency chain:\n\n  1. terraform: configure AWS via OIDC, init with -backend-config from\n     repo vars (TF_STATE_BUCKET, TF_LOCK_TABLE, AWS_REGION), plan with\n     image_tag=$GITHUB_SHA, apply, capture outputs for downstream jobs.\n     `if: skip_terraform != ''true''` so workflow_dispatch can refresh the\n     deploy without re-running terraform.\n\n  2. build-backend: docker build, ECR login + push, force-new-deployment\n     on the ECS service, wait services-stable (10-min budget).\n\n  3. build-frontend: yarn install, vite build with VITE_API_BASE_URL\n     pointing at the CloudFront URL + VITE_DEMO_MODE=true, sync to S3\n     with two passes (immutable cache for /assets/, no-cache for\n     /index.html), invalidate /index.html on CloudFront.\n\n  4. smoke: poll the live URL for up to 5 minutes; on first 200 print\n     it to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY. Bounded retry catches CloudFront\n     edge-propagation lag without hanging the workflow.\n\nSecurity: every interpolation in `run:` steps goes through env: blocks\nper GitHub''s workflow-injection guidance, even though the only sources\nare secrets/vars/inputs/github.sha/needs.outputs (none of which are\nuser-controllable). Belt + suspenders so no one needs to audit later.\n\nConcurrency group \"deploy-demo\" + cancel-in-progress: false: only one\ndeploy at a time, queue rather than abort. Critical for ECS rolling\ndeploys + CloudFront invalidations which don''t tolerate parallel runs.\n\ninfra/terraform/demo-deploy/README.md\n-------------------------------------\n\nReplaces the earlier placeholder with the full apply procedure: bootstrap\norder, repo secret/var setup, the chicken-and-egg first-apply (placeholder\nimage OR -target ECR-only first), cost breakdown (~$43/mo), destroy\nprocedure, deviations from PRD production target.\n\ndocs/runbook.md\n---------------\n\nReplaces the \"AWS demo deploy (deferred)\" section with the actual apply\nrecipe + recovery paths for stuck deploys (image pull failure, health\ncheck failing, subnet routing) and stale CloudFront content. Gives the\non-call enough to debug without re-reading every TF file.\n\ndocs/TASK_LIST.md\n-----------------\n\nGroup 14 cloud-lift sub-block: 4 of 6 items checked off (TF code +\nworkflow + runbook + README). Two remain unchecked because they require\nthe AWS-credentialed apply which the agent can''t run:\n  - First terraform apply\n  - Validate full IC + Manager flow against the live URL\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - terraform init + validate + fmt clean on both bootstrap and\n    demo-deploy stacks\n  - yarn format:check, yarn lint (fresh, --skip-nx-cache), all clean\n  - Workflow YAML hasn''t been parsed by actionlint (not installed\n    locally); GitHub''s parser will catch any syntax error on first run\n\nApply path\n==========\n\nThe user runs:\n\n  cd infra/terraform/bootstrap && terraform init && terraform apply\n  gh secret set AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN --body \"$(terraform output -raw github_actions_role_arn)\"\n  gh variable set TF_STATE_BUCKET --body \"$(terraform output -raw tf_state_bucket)\"\n  gh variable set TF_LOCK_TABLE --body \"$(terraform output -raw tf_lock_table)\"\n  gh variable set AWS_REGION --body \"us-east-1\"\n  cd ../demo-deploy\n  terraform init -backend-config=...\n  terraform apply -var \"image_tag=placeholder\"\n\nThen merge this PR. The next push to main triggers deploy-demo.yml,\nwhich builds the real image, deploys it, and prints the live URL.\n\n* task(14-cloud): add terraform-pr workflow -- validate + fmt on infra changes\n\nWithout this, the cloud-lift PR has zero required checks because the\nexisting PR workflows (frontend-pr, backend-pr, e2e-pr) all have path\nfilters scoped to apps/** and libs/** -- the infra/terraform/ changes\nfall outside.\n\nThe terraform-pr workflow runs on PRs that touch infra/terraform/** or\nthis workflow file itself. Matrix-runs against both stacks (bootstrap\nand demo-deploy) so an HCL bug in either fails the PR check.\n\nSteps:\n  - terraform fmt -check -recursive: formatting consistency\n  - terraform init -backend=false: skips the S3-backend-config that\n    demo-deploy normally needs from CI vars; validate is a static\n    check and doesn''t need a real state backend\n  - terraform validate: type + reference + provider checks\n\nfail-fast: false so a bug in bootstrap doesn''t mask a separate bug in\ndemo-deploy.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"18315572cc9875043856d5b44784af79b3de9e3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/18315572cc9875043856d5b44784af79b3de9e3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33","verification":{"payload":"tree 18315572cc9875043856d5b44784af79b3de9e3b\nparent abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777342361 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777342361 -0600\n\ntask(14-cloud): AWS cloud lift — Terraform + GHA deploy → live CloudFront URL (#15)\n\n* task(14-cloud): bootstrap module -- TF state bucket + DynamoDB lock + GitHub OIDC\n\nThe demo-deploy stack assumes its remote state bucket already exists.\nChicken-and-egg: a single root module can''t apply with a backend that\nreferences a bucket the same module is creating. Splitting bootstrap\ninto its own root module (with local state) breaks the cycle and keeps\nthe apply order linear: bootstrap once, demo-deploy any number of times.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n  - aws_s3_bucket \"tf_state\": versioned, AES256-encrypted, public-access-\n    blocked, 90-day non-current-version lifecycle. Bucket name includes\n    the AWS account id so two accounts can each own their own state\n    bucket without collision.\n\n  - aws_dynamodb_table \"tf_lock\": PAY_PER_REQUEST billing, single LockID\n    string hash key per the Terraform S3-backend lock contract. Empty\n    most of the time; transient rows during apply.\n\n  - aws_iam_openid_connect_provider \"github\" + aws_iam_role\n    \"github_actions_deploy\": trust policy gates assumption to the\n    configured `github_repository` (default seeincodes/WeeklyCommit) on\n    main branch + pull-request refs only. Permissions are deliberately\n    broad (\"ec2:*\", \"ecs:*\", etc.) for the demo; a follow-up commit can\n    scope down to specific resource ARNs once the demo-deploy stack has\n    applied at least once and ARNs are stable.\n\n  - .gitignore: keeps terraform.tfstate / .terraform/ out of the repo.\n    Bootstrap state is small, applied once, and the human running it\n    owns the file. If lost, re-import.\n\n  - README.md: apply procedure + the four outputs that need to be\n    pasted into demo-deploy/backend.tf and the GitHub repo secrets.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - terraform init -backend=false  (clean)\n  - terraform validate              (Success! The configuration is valid.)\n  - terraform fmt -check            (clean)\n\nApply runs from the user''s AWS-credentialed shell -- agent has no\ncredentials. Once applied, the next branch commits build the\ndemo-deploy stack on top.\n\n* task(14-cloud): demo-deploy Terraform stack -- VPC + ECR + RDS + ECS + ALB + S3 + CloudFront\n\nBuilds on the bootstrap module from the previous commit. State backend\nreferences the bootstrap-created bucket via -backend-config flags from CI\n(or hand-edit for local apply). All resources tagged for traceability.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n- versions.tf / variables.tf / locals.tf -- provider config + tunable\n  knobs + computed names. Defaults: us-east-1, demo environment, latest\n  image tag, smallest valid Fargate sizing (256 cpu / 512 mem).\n\n- backend.tf -- S3 backend with placeholder bucket + dynamodb_table\n  fields. CI passes them via `terraform init -backend-config=...`.\n\n- vpc.tf -- public-only VPC (no NAT). Two subnets across AZs as ALB +\n  RDS subnet group both require >=2 AZs. Three security groups:\n    alb         : 80 from world\n    ecs_task    : 8080 from alb sg only\n    rds         : 5432 from ecs_task sg only\n\n- ecr.tf -- backend image repo, AES256 encryption, scan-on-push, last-10\n  lifecycle rule.\n\n- rds.tf -- Postgres 16.4 db.t4g.micro single-AZ, gp3 20GB, encrypted\n  storage, 7d backups. Master password is `random_password` -> Secrets\n  Manager -> ECS task definition (never plaintext in TF state user-side).\n  parameter group sets log_min_duration_statement=1000ms.\n\n- iam.tf -- task_execution role with AWS-managed\n  AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy + inline secrets-read for the RDS\n  password ARN. Empty `task` role for the application; demo backend\n  makes no AWS API calls.\n\n- alb.tf -- ALB + target group + HTTP-only listener. Health check at\n  /actuator/health/readiness, 30s deregistration delay.\n\n- ecs.tf -- Fargate cluster with container insights enabled. Task\n  definition wires SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e,demo, JDBC URL composed\n  from RDS endpoint, secrets-from-Secrets-Manager pattern for the DB\n  password. Service has lifecycle.ignore_changes on task_definition +\n  desired_count so the deploy workflow''s `aws ecs update-service` calls\n  don''t fight Terraform on subsequent applies.\n\n  IMPORTANT first-apply note in file: ECR is empty until the deploy\n  workflow runs, so the service will fail to start its first task\n  until at least one image is pushed. Deploy workflow handles this.\n\n- s3.tf + cloudfront.tf -- S3 bucket locked down to public-access-block;\n  CloudFront OAC fronts it. CloudFront distribution has two origins\n  (S3 default, ALB for /api/* + /actuator/*) and uses managed cache\n  policies (CachingOptimized for static, CachingDisabled for API).\n  custom_error_response sends 403/404 to /index.html for SPA fallback.\n  Default *.cloudfront.net cert; no domain set up.\n\n- cloudwatch.tf -- two alarms: rds-cpu-high (CPU >80% for 10m) and\n  ecs-running-low (running task count <1 for 5m).\n\n- outputs.tf -- cloudfront_url is the live URL once the deploy\n  workflow has shipped at least one bundle. Other outputs are wiring\n  for the deploy workflow.\n\n- .gitignore -- keeps .terraform/ + .terraform.lock.hcl out of repo.\n  Lock file commit is environment-specific; opt in later.\n\nVerified locally\n================\n\n  terraform init -backend=false  : OK\n  terraform validate             : OK\n  terraform fmt -recursive       : clean (auto-formatted 3 files)\n\nNot verified (cannot from agent context):\n  terraform plan / apply against your AWS account. The user runs\n  the bootstrap apply once, then either runs the demo-deploy apply\n  manually or merges the next commit (the GHA deploy workflow) and\n  pushes. First apply has known chicken-and-egg with ECR (no image\n  yet); workflow handles it.\n\n* task(14-cloud): deploy-demo workflow + apply runbook + cloud README\n\nWires the GitHub Actions push-to-main → live URL pipeline on top of the\nTerraform stacks from the previous two commits.\n\nWhat''s here\n===========\n\n.github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml\n---------------------------------\n\nFour jobs, sequential dependency chain:\n\n  1. terraform: configure AWS via OIDC, init with -backend-config from\n     repo vars (TF_STATE_BUCKET, TF_LOCK_TABLE, AWS_REGION), plan with\n     image_tag=$GITHUB_SHA, apply, capture outputs for downstream jobs.\n     `if: skip_terraform != ''true''` so workflow_dispatch can refresh the\n     deploy without re-running terraform.\n\n  2. build-backend: docker build, ECR login + push, force-new-deployment\n     on the ECS service, wait services-stable (10-min budget).\n\n  3. build-frontend: yarn install, vite build with VITE_API_BASE_URL\n     pointing at the CloudFront URL + VITE_DEMO_MODE=true, sync to S3\n     with two passes (immutable cache for /assets/, no-cache for\n     /index.html), invalidate /index.html on CloudFront.\n\n  4. smoke: poll the live URL for up to 5 minutes; on first 200 print\n     it to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY. Bounded retry catches CloudFront\n     edge-propagation lag without hanging the workflow.\n\nSecurity: every interpolation in `run:` steps goes through env: blocks\nper GitHub''s workflow-injection guidance, even though the only sources\nare secrets/vars/inputs/github.sha/needs.outputs (none of which are\nuser-controllable). Belt + suspenders so no one needs to audit later.\n\nConcurrency group \"deploy-demo\" + cancel-in-progress: false: only one\ndeploy at a time, queue rather than abort. Critical for ECS rolling\ndeploys + CloudFront invalidations which don''t tolerate parallel runs.\n\ninfra/terraform/demo-deploy/README.md\n-------------------------------------\n\nReplaces the earlier placeholder with the full apply procedure: bootstrap\norder, repo secret/var setup, the chicken-and-egg first-apply (placeholder\nimage OR -target ECR-only first), cost breakdown (~$43/mo), destroy\nprocedure, deviations from PRD production target.\n\ndocs/runbook.md\n---------------\n\nReplaces the \"AWS demo deploy (deferred)\" section with the actual apply\nrecipe + recovery paths for stuck deploys (image pull failure, health\ncheck failing, subnet routing) and stale CloudFront content. Gives the\non-call enough to debug without re-reading every TF file.\n\ndocs/TASK_LIST.md\n-----------------\n\nGroup 14 cloud-lift sub-block: 4 of 6 items checked off (TF code +\nworkflow + runbook + README). Two remain unchecked because they require\nthe AWS-credentialed apply which the agent can''t run:\n  - First terraform apply\n  - Validate full IC + Manager flow against the live URL\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - terraform init + validate + fmt clean on both bootstrap and\n    demo-deploy stacks\n  - yarn format:check, yarn lint (fresh, --skip-nx-cache), all clean\n  - Workflow YAML hasn''t been parsed by actionlint (not installed\n    locally); GitHub''s parser will catch any syntax error on first run\n\nApply path\n==========\n\nThe user runs:\n\n  cd infra/terraform/bootstrap && terraform init && terraform apply\n  gh secret set AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN --body \"$(terraform output -raw github_actions_role_arn)\"\n  gh variable set TF_STATE_BUCKET --body \"$(terraform output -raw tf_state_bucket)\"\n  gh variable set TF_LOCK_TABLE --body \"$(terraform output -raw tf_lock_table)\"\n  gh variable set AWS_REGION --body \"us-east-1\"\n  cd ../demo-deploy\n  terraform init -backend-config=...\n  terraform apply -var \"image_tag=placeholder\"\n\nThen merge this PR. The next push to main triggers deploy-demo.yml,\nwhich builds the real image, deploys it, and prints the live URL.\n\n* task(14-cloud): add terraform-pr workflow -- validate + fmt on infra changes\n\nWithout this, the cloud-lift PR has zero required checks because the\nexisting PR workflows (frontend-pr, backend-pr, e2e-pr) all have path\nfilters scoped to apps/** and libs/** -- the infra/terraform/ changes\nfall outside.\n\nThe terraform-pr workflow runs on PRs that touch infra/terraform/** or\nthis workflow file itself. Matrix-runs against both stacks (bootstrap\nand demo-deploy) so an HCL bug in either fails the PR check.\n\nSteps:\n  - terraform fmt -check -recursive: formatting consistency\n  - terraform init -backend=false: skips the S3-backend-config that\n    demo-deploy normally needs from CI vars; validate is a static\n    check and doesn''t need a real state backend\n  - terraform validate: type + reference + provider checks\n\nfail-fast: false so a bug in bootstrap doesn''t mask a separate bug in\ndemo-deploy.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8BeZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA9YQAFOk1/1bAN+i+ED4IugnB3u/\nbxu9uMXoXHOQ2U4hUG7l8E4aPZf0SxfKH/7d/fg9W8bA8OaUOGKHoa6mrkfGrY9o\nTjEytOhpVwhz6Y1YObEL9FE4vXKq9nYAAnRDqyuSNtCJndHeUM1R5QAHM/W5i9rk\nlITGd8S3gCOUnxY/Dk+MVzPzoxBa/JEJEqz997vOFgKnIbQFr/OSdYfBRD5P0Oum\nGfmqcKYLRUjT3xJc8bgUqrG0M25aLa8yCuUjZIRbPn5SQWrWLXZJpbXbD/yizQPP\nNqyvZbXvh2WbaVUiPkUllFuAA/s/Xlj/s11XO1r+jmR9edbP0JqD6qnaZ+rCZuaG\nFI5Sh2BIiP9+Pa9ueRnpRDGsS5G20zI6Wflrtu2YIEpUK1usHIq1SMFD/zqb6BYj\n+/R5CHoMiM1/O9pu5YyPZu4UgYRg8r2JUef1Xr96BzW1R+fcQQ9sBdvwukZdKxtF\n+qyQ5KI1jFEqA63eL8muRuVGNh/9qqRh9Efj6ovhFEfXm64B0wK6tS4C9vEPv/fQ\n+UknQi4vsUgizorPjz2BRRWS/uWAA+pzjC1UAU88L4csFvezaffOQD2cwuOuxPf2\nutnaUKPuwEL0xqLh5oRiheUJd3zwjWUFzjX/refxxv4tQ8RSGAZinDT24tX0i7WY\nCn49uHC/I5dWFGQgoOo/\n=4W+j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T02:12:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDE4YTliOTY0OWM2OTVmNGE0MDk0MTIyOWMyNjM4NjJhZjU5YTZmMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5","sha":"abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5"}],"sha":"18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/18a9b9649c695f4a40941229c263862af59a6f33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T01:13:24Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T01:13:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(14): demo deploy stack — docker-compose Postgres+backend+frontend (#14)\n\n* task(14): demo deploy stack -- docker-compose Postgres+backend+frontend\n\nDelivers the α-local scope of group 14: a one-command demo stack that runs\nthe full Weekly Commit product on localhost via docker-compose. The AWS\ncloud lift (EKS / RDS Multi-AZ / CloudFront / ArgoCD per the PRD) is\ndeliberately deferred to a follow-up branch -- see MEMO #11 for the\ndeployment-split rationale and infra/terraform/demo-deploy/README.md for\nthe planned cloud-lift scope.\n\nWhy ship local before cloud\n===========================\n\nThe first `terraform apply` for the AWS lift requires AWS credentials\nonly the user has, and the apply ↔ debug ↔ apply loop is incompatible\nwith single-conversation execution. Validating the application stack\nend-to-end on docker-compose first means the cloud apply only debugs\n*infrastructure* issues, not application behaviour.\n\nWhat landed\n===========\n\nBackend (Spring Boot, e2e + demo profiles)\n------------------------------------------\n\n  - Dockerfile: multi-stage with the layered-jar pattern. Stage 1 builds\n    via the Maven wrapper; Stage 2 extracts the spring-boot-loader layers\n    onto a JRE-21 alpine runtime as a non-root `spring` user. Layer order\n    means iterative rebuilds where only application code changes reuse\n    the dependency layer (~85% of jar weight).\n\n  - .dockerignore at the service module + repo root: excludes target/,\n    node_modules/, yarn caches, the local .m2, docs/, infra/. Repo-root\n    ignore is the one that matters for the multi-stage build context\n    (which is invoked from repo root with `-f apps/.../Dockerfile .`).\n\n  - application-demo.yml: layers on top of the existing e2e profile.\n    Disables scheduled jobs (so background timers don''t mutate seeded\n    plans during a demo), points RCDO base-url at http://localhost:8080\n    so the WebClient hits StubRcdoController on a self-loopback, and\n    keeps notification-svc on the existing LoggingNotificationSender\n    (@Profile(\"!prod\") catches `demo`).\n\n  - StubRcdoController: in-process @RestController serving 5 hardcoded\n    Supporting Outcomes at /rcdo/supporting-outcomes. Mirrors the\n    existing wiremock seed file''s data shape so the picker dropdown\n    looks identical in demo mode and standalone-dev mode. Profile-gated\n    to \"demo\"; production deploys never instantiate it.\n\n  - DemoSecurityConfig: a profile-gated SecurityFilterChain at\n    HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE that opens /rcdo/** to unauthenticated requests.\n    Necessary because RcdoClient calls into the loopback path with a\n    service-token bearer header (not a JWT) and the default chain would\n    reject it.\n\n  - DemoDataSeeder: idempotent ApplicationRunner that on first boot\n    writes 1 manager (Ada Lovelace, UUID matches the canonical\n    cypress/devAuth MANAGER user), 3 ICs reporting to her (Ben/Cleo/Dax;\n    Ben matches the cypress IC user, Cleo + Dax are demo-only), 1\n    unassigned IC (Frankie, matches the cypress IC_NULL_MANAGER user),\n    plus current-week DRAFT plans and a prior-week RECONCILED week with\n    realistic completion outcomes (Cleo unreviewed for 72h triggers the\n    UNREVIEWED_72H flag; Dax has a MISSED commit). Detects already-\n    seeded state via the manager UUID check; subsequent boots skip.\n\nFrontend (Vite + React + nginx)\n-------------------------------\n\n  - main.tsx: introduces VITE_DEMO_MODE flag. The existing devAuth shim\n    was previously gated only on import.meta.env.DEV, so production\n    `vite build` tree-shook it out -- correct for the federated\n    production path, fatal for a static-bundle demo. New gate is\n    `DEV || VITE_DEMO_MODE === ''true''` so the demo-deploy production\n    build keeps the shim and signs JWTs in-browser against the e2e-\n    profile backend. Both flags collapse to compile-time constants;\n    the conditional branch is dead-code-eliminated when both are false.\n\n  - Dockerfile: yarn install via Corepack-pinned 4.5.0 with --immutable,\n    `vite build` with VITE_DEMO_MODE=true and configurable\n    VITE_API_BASE_URL build-arg, then nginx 1.27-alpine serving the\n    `dist/` output. SPA fallback to /index.html, 1y immutable cache on\n    /assets/ (content-hashed bundles), no-cache on remoteEntry.js so\n    the manifest gets picked up immediately on redeploy.\n\n  - nginx-demo.conf: SPA fallback config with the cache rules above\n    plus a /healthz target for compose''s healthcheck block.\n\nStack glue\n----------\n\n  - docker-compose.demo.yml at repo root: postgres:16.4-alpine +\n    backend (built from apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile) +\n    frontend (built from apps/weekly-commit-ui/Dockerfile). depends_on\n    + healthcheck wait gates ensure the backend doesn''t try to migrate\n    against a not-ready postgres, and the frontend doesn''t try to\n    serve before the backend''s actuator readiness probe goes UP.\n\n  - Single localhost URL at http://localhost:5173. Postgres and backend\n    expose ports for easier debugging; the user only needs to hit the\n    frontend port.\n\nDocs\n----\n\n  - docs/runbook.md: covers the local demo path end-to-end including\n    common-issue table, plus state-machine recovery, DLT replay,\n    scheduled-job re-run, remote rollback, legal escalation. Closes\n    out the long-open task list item \"Runbook in docs/runbook.md\".\n\n  - docs/MEMO.md decision #12: documents the deployment-split rationale,\n    explicit deviations from the PRD''s production architecture (EKS →\n    ECS Fargate, Multi-AZ → single-AZ, real Auth0 → e2e JWT decoder,\n    federated remote → standalone SPA bundle), and what the cloud-lift\n    follow-up branch will need to land.\n\n  - docs/TASK_LIST.md group 14: split into three sub-blocks --\n    \"α-local demo (this branch)\", \"Cloud lift (deferred -- needs your\n    AWS account)\", \"Production target (deferred -- needs Auth0 tenant)\".\n    Each item is checkboxed individually.\n\n  - infra/terraform/demo-deploy/README.md: empty placeholder dir with\n    a README detailing the planned ~$48/mo AWS posture, file layout,\n    GHA deploy workflow shape, and recommended commit sequencing for\n    the cloud lift.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - mvn test: 260/260 pass (no new tests added; existing tests still\n    green with the new demo-package code on the classpath)\n  - mvn compile clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test: 172/172 pass\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run lint clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run format:check clean\n  - VITE_DEMO_MODE=true VITE_API_BASE_URL=... yarn build clean;\n    confirmed devAuth-CNUH4np5.js (21.93 KB) appears in dist/assets/\n    only when the flag is set\n  - docker compose -f docker-compose.demo.yml config validates\n  - docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile clean\n  - docker build -f apps/weekly-commit-ui/Dockerfile clean (with the\n    demo build-args)\n\nKnown caveats\n=============\n\n  - Full `docker compose up` smoke partially blocked by port 8080\n    being held by Docker Desktop''s daemon during the verify run.\n    Compose''s healthcheck path was exercised to the point of \"postgres\n    healthy, backend trying to bind 8080\". The runbook documents this\n    as a prerequisite (ports 5173 / 8080 / 5432 must be free).\n  - Demo deploy bundles the cypress test private key into the public\n    static bundle so the in-browser devAuth shim can sign JWTs. Anyone\n    with the demo URL can mint a JWT for any seeded user. Acceptable\n    for a demo, NOT for a production deploy. MEMO #11 records this.\n  - Cloud lift (Terraform + GHA deploy + first apply) intentionally\n    NOT in this branch; tracked in TASK_LIST group 14 and the README\n    in infra/terraform/demo-deploy/.\n\n* task(14): fix CI prettier -- root format:check covers tailwind.config.ts + compose yml\n\nFrontend-pr CI failed on root `yarn format:check` against two files my\nlocal verification missed:\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/tailwind.config.ts  (pre-existing drift; predates\n                                              this branch -- the redesign\n                                              landed against a workspace-\n                                              scoped format:check that\n                                              skipped the tailwind config)\n  docker-compose.demo.yml                   (added in 0fdb5e3)\n\nLocal trap: `yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run format:check` only\nchecks `src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}` per its package.json script. CI runs the\nROOT `yarn format:check` which globs `**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,json,md,yml,yaml}`\n-- catches workspace-config files (tailwind.config.ts) and repo-root yaml\n(docker-compose.demo.yml).\n\nLesson: default to `yarn format:check` from the repo root (not the\nper-workspace one) when changes touch any non-src file. Same pattern as\nthe workspace-vs-root `yarn lint` trap from feedback_workspace_lint_scope.\n\nVerified locally:\n  - yarn format:check (root):  all matched files clean\n  - yarn lint (root, all 4 nx projects): clean\n  - mvn spotless:check (backend): clean\n\nThis fix also unbroke main: main''s frontend-pr CI has been red since the\npush of 76336e8..ff558ee (the redesign merge) because tailwind.config.ts\nwas already prettier-dirty. Squash-merging this PR formats the file in\nthe squashed commit and brings main back to green.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"7379178fc3c966b565dd6a9667c3bf3aed96d9cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/7379178fc3c966b565dd6a9667c3bf3aed96d9cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7379178