uction\n    build keeps the shim and signs JWTs in-browser against the e2e-\n    profile backend. Both flags collapse to compile-time constants;\n    the conditional branch is dead-code-eliminated when both are false.\n\n  - Dockerfile: yarn install via Corepack-pinned 4.5.0 with --immutable,\n    `vite build` with VITE_DEMO_MODE=true and configurable\n    VITE_API_BASE_URL build-arg, then nginx 1.27-alpine serving the\n    `dist/` output. SPA fallback to /index.html, 1y immutable cache on\n    /assets/ (content-hashed bundles), no-cache on remoteEntry.js so\n    the manifest gets picked up immediately on redeploy.\n\n  - nginx-demo.conf: SPA fallback config with the cache rules above\n    plus a /healthz target for compose''s healthcheck block.\n\nStack glue\n----------\n\n  - docker-compose.demo.yml at repo root: postgres:16.4-alpine +\n    backend (built from apps/weekly-commit-service/Dockerfile) +\n    frontend (built from apps/weekly-commit-ui/Dockerfile). depends_on\n    + healthcheck wait gates ensure the backend doesn''t try to migrate\n    against a not-ready postgres, and the frontend doesn''t try to\n    serve before the backend''s actuator readiness probe goes UP.\n\n  - Single localhost URL at http://localhost:5173. Postgres and backend\n    expose ports for easier debugging; the user only needs to hit the\n    frontend port.\n\nDocs\n----\n\n  - docs/runbook.md: covers the local demo path end-to-end including\n    common-issue table, plus state-machine recovery, DLT replay,\n    scheduled-job re-run, remote rollback, legal escalation. Closes\n    out the long-open task list item \"Runbook in docs/runbook.md\".\n\n  - docs/MEMO.md decision #12: documents the deployment-split rationale,\n    explicit deviations from the PRD''s production architecture (EKS →\n    ECS Fargate, Multi-AZ → single-AZ, real Auth0 → e2e JWT decoder,\n    federated remote → standalone SPA bundle), and what the cloud-lift\n    follow-up branch will need to land.\n\n  - docs/TASK