09cc3c5a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c"}],"sha":"abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/abcf0619357471d1d321d9d0a5a3cfb7c1aca6f5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:33:55Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): record group-19 scope expansion (MEMO #11) + restructure TASK_LIST entry\n\nThe 5-item group-19 polish list (\"ConflictToast copy, empty-state\nillustrations, carry-streak transition, 480+ char warning, flag\ntooltips\") expanded mid-stream into a full visual-design pass across IC\n+ Manager surfaces. Documenting the why + the what so future-me can\ntrace why ~700 LOC of tailwind / DOM-shape work landed under a heading\nthat originally scoped 5 small polish items.\n\nMEMO.md gains decision #11 explaining the trigger (\"functionally\ncomplete but visually generic\"), what changed (tokens, shell, chess\nspine, DraftMode, team rollup, mode panes), what was deliberately not\nchanged (original line-by-line copy / micro-interactions), and the\ntech-stack guardrails that held throughout (Tailwind + Flowbite only,\nno new deps, every test contract preserved, 172/172 vitest pass).\n\nTASK_LIST.md group 19 was rewritten:\n\n  - \"Visual redesign\" sub-block lists the 12 items checked off on the\n    `task/19-ui-redesign` branch.\n  - \"Original group-19 polish items (still TODO)\" block keeps the 5\n    original items unchecked + adds two new ones surfaced during the\n    redesign: the HistoryPage real list (placeholder shell is in place;\n    data layer is group 11), and a no-direct-reports illustration on\n    /team paralleling BlankState.\n\nGroup title also expanded from \"UX polish\" to \"UX polish + visual\nredesign\" so the heading no longer understates the scope.\n\nNo code change in this commit -- docs only.","tree":{"sha":"1c704fce89b3171abe4cc6de04ac876529a50a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/1c704fce89b3171abe4cc6de04ac876529a50a77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGZmNTU4ZWVjZDg4ZGM3MWU4ZWIyZTcxOTA3MGNlNTA5Y2MzYzVhMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6","sha":"1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6"}],"sha":"ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ff558eecd88dc71e8eb2e719070ce509cc3c5a0c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:32:17Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): empty-state illustration + token pass on remaining mode panes\n\nBrings the rest of the IC + Manager surfaces in line with the redesign\nthat landed in earlier commits on this branch (foundation tokens, app\nshell, chess spine, DraftMode, team rollup + member cards).\n\nBlankState\n==========\n\nWas a single line + a flat blue rectangle button. Now renders as a\ncentred empty-state card with an illustrative tier-glyph cluster (Rock,\nPebble, Sand glyphs in their tier colours, deliberately overlapping so\nthey read as one emblem rather than three icons), a title + supporting\ncopy that frames the next action, and a primary brand CTA with leading\nsparkle and trailing arrow glyphs. Soft fade-in on mount via the new\n`fade-in-up` animation, gated on motion-safe so prefers-reduced-motion\nusers skip it.\n\nThis is the IC''s first impression of the product on a fresh week --\npreviously the most lackluster surface in the codebase. Now it reads as\na deliberate first step.\n\nLockedReadOnly + ReconciledSummary\n==================================\n\nState badge promoted to its own header card so it sits at the same\nvisual weight as DraftMode''s header (the mode-pane headers were\ninconsistent before). Each commit row gets the leading tier glyph\ntreatment from the chess-spine redesign (tinted square + tier ink) so\nthe row reads its tier visually before the title.\n\nReconciledSummary''s reflection block moves from a flat gray box with\nplain text to a slate-50 card with eyebrow label + body-weight content,\nmatching the pattern used in IcDrawer''s reflection panel.\n\nReconcileMode\n=============\n\nState badge + Submit-CTA pair gets the same header-card framing as\nDraftMode. Submit button repaletted from raw `bg-emerald-600` to the\n`bg-ok` semantic token + check-circle glyph + `bg-ok-ink` hover ramp,\nso the success-action button reads consistently with the rest of the\nproduct. Loading + error fallbacks use the same `text-slate-500`\n(loading) and `border-danger/30 bg-danger-soft` (error) treatment as\nDraftMode for cross-pane consistency.\n\nIcDrawer\n========\n\nBackdrop gains a subtle blur (`bg-slate-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm`) so\nthe underlying rollup softens behind the dialog rather than disappearing\ninto a flat black overlay. The drawer panel slides in from the right\nvia the existing `slide-in-right` animation (gated on motion-safe).\n\nHeader band restructured: an eyebrow (\"Team member\") sits above the\nemployee name in display weight, the close button moves from the\nshouting `✕` character to the inline-icon `<CloseIcon />` with a\nfocus ring so keyboard users get a clear focus target.\n\nBody sections wrap in white cards with the soft-sm shadow, matching the\nteam-rollup card treatment so the drawer reads as the same product, not\na different surface. Reflection panel uses the same left-accent +\nitalic body treatment as the member card preview. Commit rows gain the\nleading tier-glyph chip.\n\nTests preserved\n===============\n\nEvery drawer / reconcile / reconciled / locked test contract held:\n  - week-editor-blank, blank-state-error, week-editor-reconcile,\n    reconcile-loading, reconcile-error, reconcile-submit-error,\n    week-editor-reconciled, reconciled-loading, reconciled-error,\n    reconciled-reflection, week-editor-locked-readonly,\n    locked-readonly-loading, locked-readonly-error, ic-drawer-backdrop,\n    ic-drawer-loading, ic-drawer-no-plan, ic-drawer-no-reflection,\n    ic-drawer-reflection: all preserved\n  - row testids (locked-row-{id}, reconciled-row-{id}, plus their\n    -status variants): preserved\n  - getByRole(''button'', { name: /create plan|submit reconciliation|close/i }):\n    accessible names unchanged (the new icon buttons keep aria-label=\"Close\"\n    and the submit button text stays \"Submit reconciliation\")\n  - getByRole(''dialog''): preserved on IcDrawer\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - 172/172 vitest pass\n  - typecheck, lint, prettier all clean\n  - root `yarn lint` (across all 4 nx projects, including @wc/rtk-api-client\n    which CI runs but the per-workspace lint skips) clean","tree":{"sha":"96d4287b2a09b22d262e2cf297dec2fe91e27418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/96d4287b2a09b22d262e2cf297dec2fe91e27418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDFiYmM4MDRkOTNhOTMyYjFjNWY4NmJmODNkMTcyZDNmY2ZmMDBlYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e","sha":"403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e"}],"sha":"1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1bbc804d93a932b1c5f86bf83d172d3fcff00ec6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:27:43Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): redesign team rollup stats + member cards into a real dashboard\n\nThe manager''s /team page used to be: a 2x2 stats grid showing\n\"Alignment / Completion / Unreviewed / Stuck\" all in identical 18px-bold\non a flat white card, then below that a list of single-column rounded-\nborder boxes labelled \"Ada Lovelace / reconciled / Top Rock: …\".\nFunctionally complete, visually inert. The whole reason a manager opens\nthis page is to triage the rows that need attention -- the previous\ntreatment forced reading every row to find them.\n\nHeadline stats (TeamRollup)\n===========================\n\nAlignment + Completion now render as big metric cards: a 30px tracking-\ntight numeral, a thin progress meter underneath, and a one-line context\nhint (\"Strong: nearly every plan has a Top Rock\", \"Many commits\nunfinished\"). The progress meter lets the eye decide on track / off\ntrack before the percentage parses. Aria progressbar role is wired so\nscreen readers get the same signal.\n\nUnreviewed + Stuck-commit counts are CountCards with one-glance status:\nneutral when zero, full warn / danger palette when nonzero. The previous\ntreatment painted both numbers identically regardless of whether the\nteam had problems; the new treatment goes quiet on a clean week.\n\nTier shape strip\n================\n\nThe flat 3-column tier readout is now a dashboard component: a\nhorizontal stacked progress bar showing the Rock / Pebble / Sand mix at\nglance, with per-tier labels + counts beneath. A team with no Rocks\nreads visually as \"all sand and pebbles\" before anyone reads the\nnumbers. This is exactly the at-altitude signal a manager scanning the\nrollup wants.\n\nMember cards (MemberCard)\n=========================\n\nVisual model rebuilt around a leading severity rail: stuck commits paint\na rose rail, unreviewed plans paint an amber rail, clean plans paint a\nquiet slate rail. A manager''s eye snaps down the column and lands on\nthe rows where action is needed without reading any text.\n\nOther improvements:\n  - Tier-shape went from \"R 2 P 4 S 1\" plain text to three tinted chips\n    using the new tier tokens. A row with mostly Rocks is unmistakable\n    from a row with no Rocks.\n  - Top-Rock line uses an uppercase label-eyebrow + body-weight title;\n    \"no Top Rock\" promoted from a thin orange strip to a tinted warn\n    pill with the flag glyph (matches the chess-spine treatment).\n  - Reflection preview gains a 2px slate accent border on the left so\n    quoted text is visually quoted without smart-quote characters\n    (which would have collided with the `…` truncation assertion in\n    MemberCard.test.tsx).\n  - Flags render as colour-coded pills: stuck = danger-soft, unreviewed\n    = warn-soft, NO_TOP_ROCK = warn-soft, others = slate. The flag\n    glyph is in every chip so it reads as a flag at a glance.\n  - Trailing chevron + group-hover lift cue the \"drill in\" affordance\n    without forcing a \"view details\" link.\n  - Members list moves from single-column to a 1-col / 2-col responsive\n    grid so a manager with 50 reports can see ~10 cards per fold\n    instead of ~3.\n\nTests preserved\n===============\n\nEvery contract held:\n  - team-rollup-stats / team-rollup-tiers / team-rollup-empty testids\n    stay; stats strip still contains the percent + count text the tests\n    grep for; tier strip still contains the tier counts.\n  - member-card / member-card-state / member-card-top-rock /\n    member-card-no-top-rock / member-card-tiers / member-card-reflection\n    / flag-{FLAG} testids: all preserved.\n  - getByRole(''button'', { name: <member name> }): still resolves\n    (aria-label is the member''s name on the outer card).\n  - Reflection truncation assertion `endsWith(''…'')`: preserved by\n    keeping the truncation visible at the testid level (no decorative\n    wrapper characters around the textContent).\n  - Sort order (flagged-first then alphabetical): unchanged.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - 172/172 vitest pass\n  - typecheck, lint, prettier all clean","tree":{"sha":"d8223ff8cb387d76dc3efc67e37eee74f6d81b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/d8223ff8cb387d76dc3efc67e37eee74f6d81b5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDQwM2Y3MTRkMTliMzE2NWY1ZjQxY2FhNzgwNWEyNDk4ODc3OTI0M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9","sha":"0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9"}],"sha":"403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/403f714d19b3165f5f41caa7805a24988779243e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:24:23Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): redesign DraftMode + CommitCreateForm + StateBadge; remove Edit no-op\n\nDraftMode was the surface that triggered the \"lackluster\" complaint\nloudest -- a flat StateBadge, a flat blue Lock button, an \"Edit\" button\nthat pretended to work but only re-saved the unchanged title, and a row\nlist that was just `commit.title` + two underlined links. This commit\nrebuilds the pane to read as a real planning tool.\n\nWhat changed visually\n=====================\n\nStateBadge: pastel-100/800 mini-pill -> larger pill with a colour-coded\nleading dot, ring-1 ring-inset, semantic palette (brand/warn/ok/slate).\nNow reads at a glance from peripheral vision: indigo dot = drafting,\namber dot = locked, emerald dot = reconciled. Hint text bumped to body\nweight slate-600 so the next-action sentence carries.\n\nDraftMode shell: introduced a header band that pairs StateBadge with the\nLock-Week CTA on its own card -- the previous layout had the badge\nhanging off a flex row above the form with no surface separation. Lock\nbutton gained a lock glyph + brand-soft hover ramp + soft shadow so it\nreads as primary, not as a yellow-amber afterthought.\n\nDraftMode rows: the placeholder \"Edit\" button was REMOVED. It was wired\nto call updateCommit(commit.id, { title: commit.title }) -- a no-op that\nexisted solely to prove the hook was wired. Clicking it produced no\nvisible change, no toast, no error, nothing. That''s a UX bug, not a\npolish item: the button was lying about what it does. Real inline-edit\nlands as its own feature; deferring cleanly beats shipping a dishonest\naffordance. The Delete button stays, repalleted to a quieter slate-500\ndefault with a danger-soft hover so destructive actions read as\ndestructive only when intent is clear.\n\nDraftMode rows also gained a leading tier glyph in the tier''s colour\nchip, so a row reads its tier visually before the title text resolves.\n\nCommitCreateForm: full repalette to the new tokens (slate-200 borders,\nbrand focus ring), tier select moved into a 2-column grid with\nestimated-hours, and a section-titled wrapping (`Add a commit` with the\nsparkle eyebrow icon, `Your week` for the spine). Submit button gains a\nplus glyph and the brand-hover ramp.\n\nTests preserved\n===============\n\nEvery accessible-name and testid contract survived:\n\n  - draft-loading / draft-error / week-editor-draft / draft-mutation-error\n    testids: present\n  - draft-row-{id} testid: present (now wraps the redesigned row)\n  - state-badge testid + data-state attribute + state-badge-hint testid:\n    present, hint copy unchanged\n  - getByRole(''button'', { name: /lock week/i }) and /locking/i: present;\n    Lock button accessible name is \"Lock Week\" (the icon is aria-hidden,\n    the text is the accessible name)\n  - getByRole(''button'', { name: /delete/i }) on DraftRow: present; aria-\n    label is \"Delete <title>\" so the regex /delete/i still matches\n  - getByLabelText(/title/i), /estimated hours/i, /tier/i in\n    CommitCreateForm: present (Field component wraps each input in a\n    native <label> for binding)\n  - commit-create-form-selected-outcome testid: present (now styled as a\n    brand-soft pill instead of plain text)\n  - The placeholder Edit button removal does NOT break tests -- no test\n    asserted on its presence (it was a known no-op). The\n    `useUpdateCommitMutation` mock in DraftMode.test.tsx is now unused\n    but harmless; cleaning the test up is scope creep for this commit.\n\nBehavioural caveat\n==================\n\nI considered guarding \"lock empty week\" (disable the button when there\nare zero commits) since it''s almost never what an IC wants. It would\nbreak the existing \"transitions DRAFT -> LOCKED on Lock Week click\"\ntest, which exercises the empty-list path. Reverting -- this is a\nvisual/UX redesign, not a behavioural change. If we want the empty-week\nguard, it gets its own commit + a test update.\n\nVerified\n========\n\n  - 172/172 vitest pass (all DraftMode, CommitCreateForm, and StateBadge\n    suites green)\n  - typecheck, lint, prettier all clean","tree":{"sha":"231445afe33c0c0f897806dff15681adc90a2685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/231445afe33c0c0f897806dff15681adc90a2685"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDBlNDNiZDE0MDFlYmU4ODRlMjcyMTAxZDhhZDg5NTNlZThlMzIxYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39","sha":"098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39"}],"sha":"0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/0e43bd1401ebe884e272101d8ad8953ee8e321b9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:20:24Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): redesign chess-tier spine with tier-distinct accent and glyphs\n\nBefore: three near-identical bordered boxes stacked vertically, the only\nvisual difference between Rock / Pebble / Sand being border weight (2px,\n1px, 1px gray). The chess metaphor was labelled but not visualised --\nnothing on the page told a glancing reader that Rock matters more than\nSand. The whole tiering system was carrying its meaning in text.\n\nAfter: each tier renders as a card with a tier-coloured leading rail,\nthe tier glyph in a tinted square next to the heading, a soft surface\ntint behind the heading row, and a count chip showing how many commits\nsit in that tier. Rock reads as warm-amber (heaviest), Pebble as sky\n(mid), Sand as stone (lightest). The visual progression mirrors the\nconceptual progression so a manager scanning the page sees the tier\nshape before reading any text.\n\nOther improvements:\n  - \"No Top Rock\" banner promoted from a thin orange-bordered strip to\n    a proper status banner with the flag glyph + bold lead-in. It''s the\n    single most important nudge the page can show an IC; it now reads\n    that way.\n  - Per-tier empty state moved from a plain italic gray line to a\n    dashed-border placeholder so it reads as \"this slot is open\" rather\n    than \"this section is broken.\" Removes one source of the\n    \"lackluster\" complaint -- the empty rocks section was previously\n    indistinguishable from a layout bug.\n  - Tier sections gained `shadow-soft-sm` from the new token system so\n    they sit slightly above the page surface instead of looking pasted\n    onto the gray background.\n\nContract preserved end-to-end:\n  - <section role=\"group\" aria-label=\"...\">: still per-tier\n  - heading text matches /rock|pebble|sand/i: kept (h2 with tier label)\n  - chess-tier-empty-{ROCK,PEBBLE,SAND} testids: kept verbatim\n  - chess-tier-no-top-rock testid + role=status: kept\n  - <ul><li> commit rows: kept (ChessTier.test asserts via getAllByRole\n    listitem)\n  - chess-tier-spine outer testid: kept\n  - renderCommit(commit, isTopRock) signature: unchanged\n\nPulls TIER_META + TIERS_ORDERED from the new icons/tierMeta.ts module so\nthe tier visual descriptors live in one place. Future surfaces (member\ncard tier chips, drawer commit rows) reuse these tokens.\n\nVerified:\n  - 8/8 ChessTier.test.tsx pass\n  - 172/172 full vitest pass\n  - typecheck, lint, prettier all clean","tree":{"sha":"ea850920a0a2f0decd40e0e0bcf1fe4f187d6463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/ea850920a0a2f0decd40e0e0bcf1fe4f187d6463"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDA5OGMxZDg5YWNkOTdiMTNiYmQ5ZjYwNjNhZThiNDlmN2ViNjliMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466","sha":"1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466"}],"sha":"098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/098c1d89acd97b13bbd9f6063ae8b49f7eb69b39"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:16:46Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): unified AppShell with product header, nav, and footer build stamp\n\nReplaces the per-route \"div.p-6.bg-gray-50.min-h-screen > flowbite Card\"\npattern with a single shared shell so CurrentWeek, History, Team, and\nTeamMember all inherit the same product chrome. The four routes were each\nfloating an isolated card on a slab of gray; now they share a header band\n(product mark + primary nav + page eyebrow + title + headerSlot), a\ncontent area on slate-50, and a thin footer where the build stamp now\nlives.\n\nWhy this and not \"just style the cards more\":\n\n  - The product reads as one tool now. Before, each route looked like an\n    unrelated form sitting on a gray sheet -- there was no nav, no shared\n    identity, no way to tell from the page that History and Team were\n    the same product. The header bar with active-route highlighting fixes\n    that without touching the route''s internal layout.\n  - The build stamp was rendered visibly inside CurrentWeekPage''s body\n    (`<p>Build: <sha></p>` under the heading). It belongs in a footer.\n    Sentry release tracking still uses `__WC_GIT_SHA__` from main.tsx; this\n    only relocates where the human-visible string sits. The smoke-test\n    selector `getByTestId(''version'')` still resolves it, and the Playwright\n    \"contains text /Build:/\" regex passes (kept the colon on purpose).\n  - Smoke compatibility: the heading regex `getByRole(''heading'', { name:\n    /weekly commit/i })` looks inside `current-week-page`. AppShell wraps\n    the whole route in the test-id, so the page-title <h1> (\"Weekly Commit\"\n    on /current) sits inside the scope and the smoke test still resolves.\n\nWeekContextBadge is a small new component for the header right-slot:\n\"Week of Apr 27 – May 3\", calendar-icon prefixed, pill shape. Both Current\nand Team pages render it so the user always knows which week they''re\nlooking at without scanning the body.\n\nRoutes affected:\n  CurrentWeekPage  : eyebrow \"This week\",       title \"Weekly Commit\",\n                     headerSlot WeekContextBadge\n  HistoryPage      : eyebrow \"Past weeks\",      title \"History\"\n  TeamPage         : eyebrow \"Manager view\",    title \"Team rollup\",\n                     headerSlot WeekContextBadge\n  TeamMemberPage   : eyebrow \"Team detail\",     title \"Team member\"\n\nNo DOM testid removed; new testids added: app-shell-footer,\nweek-context-badge.\n\nVerified:\n  - 172/172 vitest pass (incl. WeeklyCommitModule.test.tsx route resolution)\n  - typecheck, lint, prettier all clean\n  - dev-server boot attempt blocked by an already-running 4184 (the user''s\n    own server). No regression to investigate; the static checks cover the\n    code path.","tree":{"sha":"2d765757e98fc088fd9649f28a75af04ddd60ece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/2d765757e98fc088fd9649f28a75af04ddd60ece"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDE1NzhmN2NlYjkxYzZiYTE5NWJhZDg0NGIyZjBlOWIxMGYyZTQ0NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e","sha":"95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e"}],"sha":"1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/1578f7ceb91c6ba195bad844b2f0e9b10f2e4466"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:04:12Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:18:18Z","email":"seeinplay@gmail.com","name":"Xian Zheng"},"message":"task(19): UI redesign foundation -- semantic tokens + inline icon set\n\nEstablishes the visual-design baseline for the option-B UX redesign agreed\nwith the user. No surfaces consume this yet; subsequent commits in this\nbranch wire it into CurrentWeekPage, DraftMode, ChessTier, the team\nrollup, MemberCard, the IcDrawer, and empty states.\n\ntailwind.config.ts adds three layers under theme.extend:\n\n  - Semantic colour tokens for the chess-tier palette (rock/pebble/sand,\n    each exposing bg/border/ink) and the action/status palette (brand,\n    warn, danger, ok, each exposing DEFAULT/soft/ink). Choosing\n    product-specific names over generic ones (rock vs primary) reduces\n    collision risk with whatever the host preset already defines once\n    the federated build resolves the host''s tailwind.config layer.\n  - A 4-step type scale (display, title, body, meta) so call sites stop\n    composing typography from 8 different `text-*` utilities. Body sits at\n    15px to give the dense IC + manager surfaces a more comfortable read\n    than the current 14px default.\n  - Three soft elevation shadows. The product is dense and tabular -- a\n    heavy drop shadow fights the layout. The defaults are intentionally\n    subtle.\n\nsrc/components/icons/index.tsx is the inline SVG icon set. Authored as\nplain components rather than pulling in lucide-react / @heroicons because:\n\n  - CLAUDE.md tech-stack lock disallows new top-level frontend deps\n    without justification, and these are 5-15 line shapes that don''t\n    warrant a library.\n  - Bundle weight: a third-party set would add ~10-30 KB to the\n    federated remote; the whole inline set is < 3 KB minified. This\n    sidesteps task 18.3''s bundle-size question entirely for icons.\n  - Predictability: SVGs render identically across host themes with no\n    runtime dynamic load, eliminating a class of host/remote dep skew.\n\nIncludes the three chess-piece glyphs (Rock as a faceted boulder, Pebble\nas a rounded stone, Sand as a tilted mound of grains) plus the action\nicons the redesign needs (calendar, lock, check, flag, arrow, chevron,\nclose, plus, pencil, trash, sparkle).\n\nsrc/components/icons/tierMeta.ts packages the per-tier visual descriptor\nthat ChessTier and friends consume (Icon, label, surface, border, ink,\nchip colours, rail). Lives in a separate file from the icon components\nso react-refresh''s only-export-components rule stays happy in dev HMR\n(mixing component exports with a constant export breaks fast refresh).\n\nVerified:\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run typecheck      clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run lint           clean\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test           172/172 pass\n  - yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run format:check   clean\n\nNo DOM changes, no test changes, no consumer changes -- this commit only\nadds files and tokens. Risk of regression is zero.","tree":{"sha":"6c21ddb378330c007e2079056b6fb6990b387792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/6c21ddb378330c007e2079056b6fb6990b387792"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDk1YzMyNjFjMzIzNTY5MjhmNjkzZjBiOGE0MjIxYWZiNDNiNTM0OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c","sha":"8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c"}],"sha":"95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/95c3261c32356928f693f0b8a4221afb43b5349e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:39:17Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:39:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(prd): tick MVP1-23 checkboxes with code-path references (#10)\n\nThe PRD''s MVP1-24 checklist had been left unchecked even as the work\nlanded across groups 1-13b. Brings the audit trail in sync with the\nshipped code: each ticked item now points at the controller or\ncomponent where the requirement is satisfied (or, for the few partial\nones, calls out the remaining piece -- legal sign-off on MVP17, S3\nserving on MVP18, CloudWatch alarm on MVP14, all gated on group 14\ninfra).\n\nMVP24 (host-side kill switch) intentionally left unchecked: it''s a\ncross-remote contract owned by the PA host. The contract is\ndocumented in cypress/e2e/kill-switch.feature with @pending tags\nthat flip on once the host harness exists. Tracked in TASK_LIST\ngroups 14 + 23.\n\nNo code changes; doc-only PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fff7c6e75f05bc9acd9a292067d1693e05d758d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/fff7c6e75f05bc9acd9a292067d1693e05d758d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c","verification":{"payload":"tree fff7c6e75f05bc9acd9a292067d1693e05d758d9\nparent 76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777329557 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777329557 -0600\n\ndocs(prd): tick MVP1-23 checkboxes with code-path references (#10)\n\nThe PRD''s MVP1-24 checklist had been left unchecked even as the work\nlanded across groups 1-13b. Brings the audit trail in sync with the\nshipped code: each ticked item now points at the controller or\ncomponent where the requirement is satisfied (or, for the few partial\nones, calls out the remaining piece -- legal sign-off on MVP17, S3\nserving on MVP18, CloudWatch alarm on MVP14, all gated on group 14\ninfra).\n\nMVP24 (host-side kill switch) intentionally left unchecked: it''s a\ncross-remote contract owned by the PA host. The contract is\ndocumented in cypress/e2e/kill-switch.feature with @pending tags\nthat flip on once the host harness exists. Tracked in TASK_LIST\ngroups 14 + 23.\n\nNo code changes; doc-only PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7+WVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8NYQAK4UdAQLy8TmFaH5iMiDbSEX\nu2XQzbOnUkNNvCbclXN/XxENCaWpYOc9WZWfXyg/p0esTCtrSMlI3Oq5Qvh36ZWo\nteiho3nEzmP8mZbzU6JcXan4tyFkXxUPsWgFXH4FDgV047TGsx2fIy2+Uh84kYs3\nZt2/9vHRsCS52y0Fmnt0ZfInhH/QEMI3T8ibszw2144x9xytqV3YD6ecel7Gf6XL\nuOpRztPcQkPijqJPmIGIvjjCfhAnGeZpGffo6SpV+90tp/xE9LoBSfhIZBBND9ed\nOdQIHyxvse+iYD