s/WeeklyCommit/commits/8a33913359cdf2e0a0a16c90c33ec1e4af0c026c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T18:15:22Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T18:15:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(19-3): perf — skip refetch round-trip on createCurrentForMe + pre-bundle heavy deps (#13)\n\n* task(19-3): perf -- skip refetch round-trip on createCurrentForMe + pre-bundle heavy deps\n\nReported: ''Create plan'' click -> DraftMode visible takes 3+ seconds.\nBackend timing curl-side is single-digit ms total for the full chain\n(POST /plans + GET /plans/me/current + GET /commits + GET /rcdo).\nThe latency is on the frontend side. Two fixes, both safe + reversible.\n\nFix 1 -- onQueryStarted populates getCurrentForMe cache directly\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nPrevious chain after the user clicked Create plan:\n  POST /plans -> tag invalidation refetches getCurrentForMe ->\n  GET /plans/me/current -> rerender -> DraftMode mounts ->\n  GET /commits\n\nThe middle GET is redundant: the POST response already contains the\nnew plan row. RTK Query''s onQueryStarted lets us write that row into\nthe getCurrentForMe cache directly via api.util.upsertQueryData, so\nthe re-fetch round-trip evaporates and the page transitions one network\nround-trip earlier. invalidatesTags is preserved so any other cache\nlistening on Plan / Rollup tags still refetches as expected.\n\nFix 2 -- Vite optimizeDeps pre-bundles DraftMode''s deps\n-------------------------------------------------------\nOn first ''Create plan'' click, DraftMode + CommitCreateForm + the\nRCDOPickerContainer chain pull in flowbite-react, react-redux,\n@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react, and jose for the first time in the dev\nsession. Vite''s on-demand optimizeDeps can take seconds on cold first-\nencounter. Listing these in optimizeDeps.include means Vite warm-bundles\nthem at server start, so the click pays only network + render time.\nProduction builds ignore optimizeDeps.\n\nVerified: 172/172 vitest, typecheck + lint + prettier clean. End-user\nverification (browser-side timing on the BlankState -> DraftMode click)\npending.\n\nIf 3+ seconds persists after this lands, fall back to actually measuring\nin the browser Network tab to find the real culprit -- this is an\neducated guess at the most likely cause, not a measured fix.\n\n* task(19-3): fix CI lint -- void the dispatched upsertQueryData thunk\n\nWorkspace-wide lint caught no-floating-promises on the upsertQueryData\ndispatch in onQueryStarted. Local verification used the UI-scoped\n''yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui lint'' which doesn''t reach the\nrtk-api-client lib''s lint config; CI runs all four nx projects.\n\nLesson: ''yarn lint'' (workspace root) is the correct local verification\nwhen changes touch libs/, not the per-workspace one. Updated mental\nnotes; nothing else to change here.\n\nThe thunk''s returned Promise is intentionally fire-and-forget -- the\nupsert is synchronous in practice and any failure is irrelevant to\nuser-visible flow because tag invalidation still triggers a refetch\nas a fallback. void marks the intent explicitly.\n\n172/172 vitest force-fresh; lint + format clean across all 4 projects.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"873ed71003c77f6bbac220153f0f47ab74448607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/873ed71003c77f6bbac220153f0f47ab74448607"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e","verification":{"payload":"tree 873ed71003c77f6bbac220153f0f47ab74448607\nparent 39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777313722 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777313722 -0600\n\ntask(19-3): perf — skip refetch round-trip on createCurrentForMe + pre-bundle heavy deps (#13)\n\n* task(19-3): perf -- skip refetch round-trip on createCurrentForMe + pre-bundle heavy deps\n\nReported: ''Create plan'' click -> DraftMode visible takes 3+ seconds.\nBackend timing curl-side is single-digit ms total for the full chain\n(POST /plans + GET /plans/me/current + GET /commits + GET /rcdo).\nThe latency is on the frontend side. Two fixes, both safe + reversible.\n\nFix 1 -- onQueryStarted populates getCurrentForMe cache directly\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nPrevious chain after the user clicked Create plan:\n  POST /plans -> tag invalidation refetches getCurrentForMe ->\n  GET /plans/me/current -> rerender -> DraftMode mounts ->\n  GET /commits\n\nThe middle GET is redundant: the POST response already contains the\nnew plan row. RTK Query''s onQueryStarted lets us write that row into\nthe getCurrentForMe cache directly via api.util.upsertQueryData, so\nthe re-fetch round-trip evaporates and the page transitions one network\nround-trip earlier. invalidatesTags is preserved so any other cache\nlistening on Plan / Rollup tags still refetches as expected.\n\nFix 2 -- Vite optimizeDeps pre-bundles DraftMode''s deps\n-------------------------------------------------------\nOn first ''Create plan'' click, DraftMode + CommitCreateForm + the\nRCDOPickerContainer chain pull in flowbite-react, react-redux,\n@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react, and jose for the first time in the dev\nsession. Vite''s on-demand optimizeDeps can take seconds on cold first-\nencounter. Listing these in optimizeDeps.include means Vite warm-bundles\nthem at server start, so the click pays only network + render time.\nProduction builds ignore optimizeDeps.\n\nVerified: 172/172 vitest, typecheck + lint + prettier clean. End-user\nverification (browser-side timing on the BlankState -> DraftMode click)\npending.\n\nIf 3+ seconds persists after this lands, fall back to actually measuring\nin the browser Network tab to find the real culprit -- this is an\neducated guess at the most likely cause, not a measured fix.\n\n* task(19-3): fix CI lint -- void the dispatched upsertQueryData thunk\n\nWorkspace-wide lint caught no-floating-promises on the upsertQueryData\ndispatch in onQueryStarted. Local verification used the UI-scoped\n''yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui lint'' which doesn''t reach the\nrtk-api-client lib''s lint config; CI runs all four nx projects.\n\nLesson: ''yarn lint'' (workspace root) is the correct local verification\nwhen changes touch libs/, not the per-workspace one. Updated mental\nnotes; nothing else to change here.\n\nThe thunk''s returned Promise is intentionally fire-and-forget -- the\nupsert is synchronous in practice and any failure is irrelevant to\nuser-visible flow because tag invalidation still triggers a refetch\nas a fallback. void marks the intent explicitly.\n\n172/172 vitest force-fresh; lint + format clean across all 4 projects.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp76e6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdeoQADIJv4Y0a9ySyeDKieZBghH2\nZc9NYRdPppZDqja1RN3XrjUloNZR20eiPeo9ItwSc1dEtpUcze13821hJK/vMytS\nCUc+xqZ62B9UxQnX94pDJ7lKnT3XUh7RaKtoLZGdnOWkBU1Utn/iMwCgYWat2BZF\nINk0YKMlXbUzcq609Bp6tvBC93T1wp+Er/h8xuMOXdOUbKNgpPO8C2pUYLLRpx2E\nBZ9lfUrV1n0EXRrElpH53C8WjiQl9cMGp8w783wTghOeeWGFbnUoIb/ZDYejJAgr\nSzuGQX3XwJoVOOL5aTaEm4KQYvutZ3ddMK/cZHIWR5Y8JRCrAnTRL46sGRRkSY/2\nU330dDIL+Yk8lnv1++KELKJqPvLsBIcF82m7408wRFeTPvUl6emwSnQ1oEx8dx3o\noJsx44DcOltcVaCopSnXF7rRbfVkpS45ixXxnprK/NvKCBS+1kwmc5cgn9kv17nM\nhUF7vl3xziKNhEuQoj5DGGmTVXttXyHRMKTfiM5IdJ3v7iVadVuhToFbUiqWj6wn\n/XeEVC9EwBtf1KYyoxLqvIkoSr79+eGr9NlPmijqr5AOZsDiEMUtrU/2Ly0jx+ut\nzYt7k/5U12gBGOyMumNxSTa583WdrgNsdq5SwJAnVNecOY1MGhN0d8F0LHKLAYSE\n5ICimvE9QLUicOo5DmDH\n=ARJj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T18:15:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDc2MzM2ZTgyMGVjMTBmOWJlZTY5YzFhYmZlNzY3OGNkNzJhYWQzMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb","sha":"39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb"}],"sha":"76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/76336e820ec10f9bee69c1abfe7678cd72aad31e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T18:00:39Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T18:00:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(19-1): mount <ConflictToast /> for the 409 retry path (#11)\n\nThe conflictToastSlice in @wc/rtk-api-client has been firing on every\n409 since group 10, but no UI component subscribed to it -- the user\nsaw their action take a beat longer (because conflictRetry''s automatic\nre-fetch+retry happened) but had no idea why.\n\nAdds:\n- src/components/ConflictToast.tsx -- Flowbite Toast subscribing to the\n  slice. Per-code copy (CONFLICT_OPTIMISTIC_LOCK -> ''Another tab updated\n  this plan. We just pulled the latest and retried.''); fallback for\n  unknown codes. Auto-dismisses after 5s; honors prefers-reduced-motion\n  via Tailwind''s motion-safe: variant on the slide-in keyframe.\n- Mounted once at WeeklyCommitModule -- inside the Provider so it can\n  read the slice, outside <Routes> so it persists across navigation.\n- tailwind.config.ts: keyframes + animation tokens for slide-in-right\n  (this PR) and stuck-pulse (queued for Tier-2 follow-up). Documented as\n  remote-owned UX-moment animations distinct from host-design-system\n  spacing/color tokens.\n- src/components/ConflictToast.test.tsx -- 7 cases: hidden-by-default,\n  optimistic-lock copy, fallback copy on unknown code, auto-dismiss\n  timer, no-dismiss when autoDismissMs=0, manual close button is\n  rendered + accessible, role/aria-live attributes for AT.\n\n172/172 vitest passing; typecheck + lint + prettier clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"63d3b4e22e02289c59080e41edcfcf48e94131bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/63d3b4e22e02289c59080e41edcfcf48e94131bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/39a80a112e4311ba241a8be1c344dc95f94ff3eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 63d3b4e22e02289c59080e41edcfcf48e94131bf\nparent b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777312839 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777312839 -0600\n\ntask(19-1): mount <ConflictToast /> for the 409 retry path (#11)\n\nThe conflictToastSlice in @wc/rtk-api-client has been firing on every\n409 since group 10, but no UI component subscribed to it -- the user\nsaw their action take a beat longer (because conflictRetry''s automatic\nre-fetch+retry happened) but had no idea why.\n\nAdds:\n- src/components/ConflictToast.tsx -- Flowbite Toast subscribing to the\n  slice. Per-code copy (CONFLICT_OPTIMISTIC_LOCK -> ''Another tab updated\n  this plan. We just pulled the latest and retried.''); fallback for\n  unknown codes. Auto-dismisses after 5s; honors prefers-reduced-motion\n  via Tailwind''s motion-safe: variant on the slide-in keyframe.\n- Mounted once at WeeklyCommitModule -- inside the Provider so it can\n  read the slice, outside <Routes> so it persists across navigation.\n- tailwind.config.ts: keyframes + animation tokens for slide-in-right\n  (this PR) and stuck-pulse (queued for Tier-2 follow-up). Documented as\n  remote-owned UX-moment animations distinct from host-design-system\n  spacing/color tokens.\n- src/components/ConflictToast.test.tsx -- 7 cases: hidden-by-default,\n  optimistic-lock copy, fallback copy on unknown code, auto-dismiss\n  timer, no-dismiss when autoDismissMs=0, manual close button is\n  rendered + accessible, role/aria-live attributes for AT.\n\n172/172 vitest passing; typecheck + lint + prettier clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp76RHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAreUQAII422LMKcRUWCj5Yr9KqQ/L\n6n9r/d6R7bm0k4xdkyUMTVGXz36YW2+49rXdDGHsueTYF/bFnrUHui3dXgjdTv9F\notMZpkj3yBfnwc49AAiAkZ+jwfJSYMZhqkBdyuOW97wPGuEFLxipabyF8UwZ45zs\nxpSLtqdwfkD5NdJwfrXhD7FtTmU3jqVS9SJUOAesS+JLPRTVi8xZe/KapzDW8nnf\nbj19NWH+quaxq2BDnEWOOxHrrETANjvp9/1ZInXEj5ct6bw3WU0zffvKzgqhsiX4\nut5cRilQ6RVPZZ7MV6vXHNzG8z1Ji1hedslupRO4YjCTx0UhTe0aXrXOMKF+bsga\nQHsTPfFemBCR+MfXVmAf18BCHa4Nxp9ooMlaAhTnJQP+NUvEztQ/+2fMex0EXj55\n6KkKhgYwQE+0UKAADi5ZATuJ5XHV4RPu2X5OY+knEbB3j6jRfV0miE+3IMA5F5ws\nGbJbIqOq4+pXMWf/WhUbu1ltM6EjOenLIr7uwcVVwFPh7V