rl":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T17:20:29Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T17:20:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(13b-followup): polish — error log + currentWeekStart consolidation (#9)\n\n* docs(13b-followup): log wiremock CI healthcheck saga in ERROR_FIX_LOG\n\nCost ~30 minutes across two CI iterations to root-cause; the lesson is\nworth a durable record so the next person wiring an off-the-shelf\nimage into the e2e stack with --wait knows to check inherited\nHEALTHCHECK directives. Includes a ''Prevention'' note about reproducing\nCI failures with the same flags (--wait surfaces unhealthy state that\nplain ''up -d'' hides) and per-service log-dump-on-failure as cheap\nobservability.\n\n* task(13b-followup): consolidate currentWeekStart into lib/timezone\n\nGroup 13b shipped TeamPage and TeamMemberPage with byte-identical\ninline currentWeekStart() helpers, with TODO(group-?-week-helper)\nflags pointing at this Phase-2 cleanup. Done now while the context\nis fresh.\n\nExtracted to apps/weekly-commit-ui/src/lib/timezone.ts alongside the\nexisting tz helpers. Signature adjusted to accept now: Date and tz:\nstring explicitly so it''s pin-able for tests (matching the project''s\npattern with isReconcileEligible(weekStart, now, tz)). Both routes\nnow call: currentWeekStart(new Date(), getEmployeeTimezone()).\n\nFive new vitest cases cover Mon-as-self, Tue-through-Sun walking back\nto Monday, the next-Monday roll, IANA-tz weekday derivation (a UTC\nMonday that''s still Sunday in America/New_York returns the prior\nweek), and the DST spring-forward week. 165/165 vitest passing;\ntypecheck + lint + prettier clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2968bebd90ca071aa6b26c286b1f5c1f63abcf70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/2968bebd90ca071aa6b26c286b1f5c1f63abcf70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 2968bebd90ca071aa6b26c286b1f5c1f63abcf70\nparent d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777310429 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777310429 -0600\n\ntask(13b-followup): polish — error log + currentWeekStart consolidation (#9)\n\n* docs(13b-followup): log wiremock CI healthcheck saga in ERROR_FIX_LOG\n\nCost ~30 minutes across two CI iterations to root-cause; the lesson is\nworth a durable record so the next person wiring an off-the-shelf\nimage into the e2e stack with --wait knows to check inherited\nHEALTHCHECK directives. Includes a ''Prevention'' note about reproducing\nCI failures with the same flags (--wait surfaces unhealthy state that\nplain ''up -d'' hides) and per-service log-dump-on-failure as cheap\nobservability.\n\n* task(13b-followup): consolidate currentWeekStart into lib/timezone\n\nGroup 13b shipped TeamPage and TeamMemberPage with byte-identical\ninline currentWeekStart() helpers, with TODO(group-?-week-helper)\nflags pointing at this Phase-2 cleanup. Done now while the context\nis fresh.\n\nExtracted to apps/weekly-commit-ui/src/lib/timezone.ts alongside the\nexisting tz helpers. Signature adjusted to accept now: Date and tz:\nstring explicitly so it''s pin-able for tests (matching the project''s\npattern with isReconcileEligible(weekStart, now, tz)). Both routes\nnow call: currentWeekStart(new Date(), getEmployeeTimezone()).\n\nFive new vitest cases cover Mon-as-self, Tue-through-Sun walking back\nto Monday, the next-Monday roll, IANA-tz weekday derivation (a UTC\nMonday that''s still Sunday in America/New_York returns the prior\nweek), and the DST spring-forward week. 165/165 vitest passing;\ntypecheck + lint + prettier clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp75rdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcb4QAJdzqm9xdpYBJQqGvK4aY4tq\nZfMEp7Dhv4Vws3Yd2HAMtkscfsdTPpcNz3kwfTX9PCfeiVUtykAZITaY4d1q+oHc\n47Dks3E4kZpoo90qM4vQrOzdF8Jj6XqQewvsbB11oN0Ua1TsyvqOT1ryAygiJi2I\nmaLIVvA4rOChwttvfvkQuOoro3AzSKoTlpWGRxnWJ9mc+30kNCwRS/AQ35xMIJl7\nqCsV5OmUbW8kdf8kjyIsnQ37sX2k8X6/CCM1IXiYxRttqh9AqOSpYNPm7fikwzSF\nntOSu0B7cU1YcjuJatb3a9Pte06VpTUDhfGxHevt3AR2kehXlu9r5psveNLlO0Ew\ncdS+SfqunayNu3wjj5ix26bSYwiDryFoURg9OiSQJaHJKrgqamQ+PYRljZBJCjBb\nwGFenXv3qfmK8TmRPPj+mDZ+mtcGGe6vDdAVZfS7lMnU8axxnPTcGXjTSI7YL1oP\n9AQ0cHdeYoC66T6402PxeK/cYlCO62dxowsFiVB4rgcDNJsGBB+KUgYi5O/TnnrI\nphiuXoC3tSXduqhZu+Tba9La4tB4O6Qa9VnybHbAWzgAhfMx5U/MyuXnptHcOXV0\nHYze6jijnjdetQPhErTkCHXKZgYkw0SShR+fsd6edRH4xFyOn7Xsnl+qx3I9inxf\nkpP7t9CgdhhEY7LTAplf\n=nrit\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T17:20:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGI0OTllYmJkYzlhZTUxN2I3MjA3Yzk0YTY4YmQ1YjZkZTc0YTkxZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b","sha":"d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b"}],"sha":"b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/b499ebbdc9ae517b7207c94a68bd5b6de74a91fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T17:07:53Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T17:07:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(13b): wire IC + Manager components into WeekEditor mode panes (#8)\n\n* task(13b): extract WeekEditor mode panes into per-file modules\n\nPure refactor before the wiring work. The 5 mode panes (BlankState,\nDraftMode, LockedReadOnly, ReconcileMode, ReconciledSummary) move into\ntheir own files under src/components/modes/. WeekEditor.tsx stays the\ndispatcher: owns the GET /plans/me/current fetch + the loading/error\nbranches + the PlanRouter switch on plan.state, and imports each mode\ncomponent.\n\nWhy now: each pane is about to grow significantly across the 7 group-13b\nsubtasks. Extracting before the wiring keeps every subtask diff focused\non its own file and prevents WeekEditor.tsx from sprawling to ~600 lines.\n\nBehavior preserved exactly:\n  - Same testids on each pane root (week-editor-{blank,draft,locked-readonly,\n    reconcile,reconciled})\n  - Same data-flow (planId still passes through to each pane)\n  - DraftMode keeps the RCDOPickerContainer + no-op handler from PR #6\n    so RCDO data flow stays exercised end-to-end\n\nVerification: 135/135 vitest pass force-fresh; lint, typecheck, prettier\nall clean. The WeekEditor.test.tsx assertions all use testids on the\nmode roots, so the refactor is invisible to them.\n\n* task(13b): implementation plan for mode-pane wire-up + team routes\n\n7-task plan (6 required, 1 stretch). Hybrid TDD per same-day MVP scope:\nfull TDD on DraftMode + ReconcileMode (state-changing mutations whose\ndrift would be brutal at demo time), golden-path on the read-mostly\npanes and team routes.\n\n- Task 1: LockedReadOnly read-only commit list + StateBadge\n- Task 2: ReconciledSummary + carry-forward + reflection display\n- Task 3: DraftMode commit-create + Lock Week (TDD)\n- Task 4: ReconcileMode table + reflection + submit + carry (TDD)\n- Task 5: TeamPage rollup + URL-driven drawer\n- Task 6: TeamMemberPage addressable drawer\n- Task 7 (stretch): drop @pending from cypress feature files\n\nClick-test in browser after every task; commit per task; tick\nTASK_LIST checkboxes in the same commit that lands the work.\n\n* task(13b-1): wire LockedReadOnly to commits + StateBadge\n\nLockedReadOnly was a stub returning a single text div; now fetches\nuseListCommitsQuery({planId}), composes <StateBadge state=LOCKED\nisReconcileEligible={false}> (which surfaces the ''Reconciliation\nopens Friday'' hint) plus <ChessTier> with a read-only row renderer.\n\nWeekEditor.test.tsx pre-day-4 LOCKED case retargeted to assert on\nlocked-readonly-loading since the mode pane now fires its own data\nfetch -- proving WeekEditor routes to the right mode is the actual\ncontract; the DRAFT and RECONCILED tests still target the synchronous\ntestids since those modes are still stubs (Tasks 3 + 2 in this group).\n\n135/135 vitest passing. Manual click-test: created plan + transitioned\nto LOCKED via API, browser shows StateBadge + empty ChessTier with\n''No Top Rock yet'' warning, no console errors.\n\n* task(13b-2): wire ReconciledSummary read-only + carry-forward\n\nReconciledSummary was a stub returning a single text div; now fetches\nuseListCommitsQuery({planId}), composes <StateBadge state=RECONCILED>\n(its hint copy already says \"Carry forward any missed work to next\nweek\"), the full reflection note when non-empty, <CarryAllButton> for\nthe bulk affordance, and <ChessTier> with a row renderer that surfaces\n<CarryStreakBadge carryStreak={commit.derived?.carryStreak ?? 0}> (the\nbadge self-gates at >=2 per [MVP7]) plus a per-row <CarryForwardRow>\nso carry-forward stays available post-reconcile per [MVP6].\n\nWeekEditor passes through plan.reflectionNote on both RECONCILED and\nARCHIVED arms. The prop is typed `string | undefined` rather than `?:`\nbecause exactOptionalPropertyTypes in tsconfig refuses the implicit-\nundefined on a `?:` field (the openapi-generated WeeklyPlanResponse\ngives us `string | undefined` from `reflectionNote?: string`).\n\nWeekEditor.test.tsx RECONCILED case retargeted to assert on\nreconciled-loading since the mode pane now fires its own data fetch --\nsame routing-contract retarget the LOCKED case got in 13b-1. The\nDRAFT test still targets the synchronous testid because DraftMode is\nstill a stub (Task 3 of the plan).\n\n135/135 vitest passing. typecheck + lint clean.\n\n* task(13b): extract isCarryEligible to lib/ for cross-mode reuse\n\nTasks 13b-2 and 13b-4 both need the carry-eligibility predicate but\nCarryForwardRow.tsx is a component file -- the react-refresh lint\nrule blocks non-component exports there. Extracted the pure predicate\nto lib/carryEligibility.ts so ReconciledSummary + ReconcileMode can\nimport it directly. CarryForwardRow now imports from the same place,\nkeeping a single source of truth.\n\nBehaviour unchanged. 9/9 CarryForwardRow tests passing.\n\n* task(13b-6): wire TeamMemberPage IcDrawer + close-to-team\n\n* task(13b-5): wire TeamPage rollup + drawer URL state\n\n* task(13b-3): wire DraftMode commit-create + Lock Week\n\n* task(13b-4): wire ReconcileMode table+reflection+submit+carry\n\n* task(13b): wire BlankState ''Create plan'' button to useCreateCurrentForMeMutation\n\nThe button was a presentational stub from the original mode-pane\nextraction (commit 1fdcb26): no onClick handler, clicking it did\nnothing. Caught during the post-implementation click-test pass.\n\nWired it to useCreateCurrentForMeMutation; RTK Query''s invalidatesTags\nalready covers the Plan LIST + Rollup LIST tags so useGetCurrentForMeQuery\nrefetches automatically and WeekEditor flips into DraftMode without\nany local state plumbing.\n\nLoading state disables the button + swaps the label to ''Creating…'';\nerrors surface a small inline banner (the global ConflictToast handles\n409s; this banner is for the rest).\n\n* task(13b): RCDO wiremock stub for standalone-dev picker\n\nThe picker landed wired and tested, but the e2e-profile docker stack\npoints RCDO at https://rcdo.invalid/ -- the backend''s RcdoController\nreturns 500 INTERNAL_ERROR on connect refused, and the picker correctly\nrenders its ''RCDO temporarily unavailable'' degraded state with no\nselectable outcomes. Demo-ready but unusable.\n\nAdd a wiremock service (port 8081) returning a fixed list of 4\nSupportingOutcomes with valid UUIDs and inline 4-level breadcrumbs\nmatching the upstream contract per docs/adr/0001-rcdo-contract.md.\nSpring container points at http://rcdo-stub:8081 over the docker\nnetwork. CI''s Cypress run is unaffected -- the green-path scenarios\nalready use cy.intercept against the typed /api/v1/rcdo/* paths.\n\nMappings under apps/weekly-commit-ui/wiremock/mappings/. Wiremock''s\ndefault mount-path /home/wiremock auto-discovers them at startup.\nRestart cycle: docker compose down + up brings the stub up first\n(weekly-commit-service depends_on rcdo-stub).\n\n* task(13b): fix CI -- prettier formatting + wiremock healthcheck path\n\nTwo parallel CI failures on the previous push:\n\n1. lint-test-build / Prettier check: 4 files violated formatting --\n   CommitCreateForm.tsx, ReconciledSummary.tsx, TeamPage.tsx, and the\n   new wiremock mapping JSON. Subagents ran lint but not format:check\n   during their per-task verification; CI runs both. Auto-fixed via\n   yarn format:write.\n\n2. cypress-cucumber / Provision ephemeral env: rcdo-stub container\n   marked unhealthy because the healthcheck hit /__admin/health which\n   wiremock 3.x does not expose (returns 404). Switched to /__admin/\n   which responds 200 with the mappings JSON once the server is up --\n   sufficient to gate the backend''s depends_on.\n\n* task(13b): override wiremock baked-in healthcheck (correct port + path)\n\nRound 2 of the CI fix. The previous attempt edited the test command\nbut left the healthcheck on the wrong port -- the wiremock 3.9.1 image\nships a HEALTHCHECK targeting localhost:8080 (the default port), but\nwe run wiremock on --port 8081 because 8080 is the backend. Compose\ninherits the image''s HEALTHCHECK and was probing a closed port; the\nnew test commands I wrote weren''t taking effect because of how compose\nresolves the file''s healthcheck block.\n\nAlso wiremock 3.9.1 has no /__admin/health endpoint at all -- /__admin/\nis the working alternative.\n\nFix:\n- Explicit override block with the correct port (8081) and path\n  (/__admin/, returns 200 with mappings JSON).\n- start_period: 30s so a slow CI runner has runway to boot the JVM\n  before failures count toward the unhealthy threshold.\n- Workflow gains a ''Show rcdo-stub logs on failure'' step parallel to\n  the existing backend-logs-on-failure step so the next surprise has\n  log output to grep.\n\nVerified: docker compose up -d --wait completes in ~12s locally with\nall three containers Healthy.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a93afdad4f5035239701de9512e2aa84c9710bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/a93afdad4f5035239701de9512e2aa84c9710bb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b","verification":{"payload":"tree a93afdad4f5035239701de9512e2aa84c9710bb7\nparent 9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777309673 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777309673 -0600\n\ntask(13b): wire IC + Manager components into WeekEditor mode panes (#8)\n\n* task(13b): extract WeekEditor mode panes into per-file modules\n\nPure refactor before the wiring work. The 5 mode panes (BlankState,\nDraftMode, LockedReadOnly, ReconcileMode, ReconciledSummary) move into\ntheir own files under src/components/modes/. WeekEditor.tsx stays the\ndispatcher: owns the GET /plans/me/current fetch + the loading/error\nbranches + the PlanRouter switch on plan.state, and imports each mode\ncomponent.\n\nWhy now: each pane is about to grow significantly across the 7 group-13b\nsubtasks. Extracting before the wiring keeps every subtask diff focused\non its own file and prevents WeekEditor.tsx from sprawling to ~600 lines.\n\nBehavior preserved exactly:\n  - Same testids on each pane root (week-editor-{blank,draft,locked-readonly,\n    reconcile,reconciled})\n  - Same data-flow (planId still passes through to each pane)\n  - DraftMode keeps the RCDOPickerContainer + no-op handler from PR #6\n    so RCDO data flow stays exercised end-to-end\n\nVerification: 135/135 vitest pass force-fresh; lint, typecheck, prettier\nall clean. The WeekEditor.test.tsx assertions all use testids on the\nmode roots, so the refactor is invisible to them.\n\n* task(13b): implementation plan for mode-pane wire-up + team routes\n\n7-task plan (6 required, 1 stretch). Hybrid TDD per same-day MVP scope:\nfull TDD on DraftMode + ReconcileMode (state-changing mutations whose\ndrift would be brutal at demo time), golden-path on the read-mostly\npanes and team routes.\n\n- Task 1: LockedReadOnly read-only commit list + StateBadge\n- Task 2: ReconciledSummary + carry-forward + reflection display\n- Task 3: DraftMode commit-create + Lock Week (TDD)\n- Task 4: ReconcileMode table + reflection + submit + carry (TDD)\n- Task 5: TeamPage rollup + URL-driven drawer\n- Task 6: TeamMemberPage addressable drawer\n- Task 7 (stretch): drop @pending from cypress feature files\n\nClick-test in browser after every task; commit per task; tick\nTASK_LIST checkboxes in the same commit that lands the work.\n\n* task(13b-1): wire LockedReadOnly to commits + StateBadge\n\nLockedReadOnly was a stub returning a single text div; now fetches\nuseListCommitsQuery({planId}), composes <StateBadge state=LOCKED\nisReconcileEligible={false}> (which surfaces the ''Reconciliation\nopens Friday'' hint) plus <ChessTier> with a read-only row renderer.\n\nWeekEditor.test.tsx pre-day-4 LOCKED case retargeted to assert on\nlocked-readonly-loading since the mode pane now fires its own data\nfetch -- proving WeekEditor routes to the right mode is the actual\ncontract; the DRAFT and RECONCILED tests still target the synchronous\ntestids since those modes are still stubs (Tasks 3 + 2 in this group).\n\n135/135 vitest passing. Manual click-test: created plan + transitioned\nto LOCKED via API, browser shows StateBadge + empty ChessTier with\n''No Top Rock yet'' warning, no console errors.\n\n* task(13b-2): wire ReconciledSummary read-only + carry-forward\n\nReconciledSummary was a stub returning a single text div; now fetches\nuseListCommitsQuery({planId}), composes <StateBadge state=RECONCILED>\n(its hint copy already says \"Carry forward any missed work to next\nweek\"), the full reflection note when non-empty, <CarryAllButton> for\nthe bulk affordance, and <ChessTier> with a row renderer that surfaces\n<CarryStreakBadge carryStreak={commit.derived?.carryStreak ?? 0}> (the\nbadge self-gates at >=2 per [MVP7]) plus a per-row <CarryForwardRow>\nso carry-forward stays available post-reconcile per [MVP6].\n\nWeekEditor passes through plan.reflectionNote on both RECONCILED and\nARCHIVED arms. The prop is typed `string | undefined` rather than `?:`\nbecause exactOptionalPropertyTypes in tsconfig refuses the implicit-\nundefined on a `?:` field (the openapi-generated WeeklyPlanResponse\ngives us `string | undefined` from `reflectionNote?: string`).\n\nWeekEditor.test.tsx RECONCILED case retargeted to assert on\nreconciled-loading since the mode pane now fires its own data fetch --\nsame routing-contract retarget the LOCKED case got in 13b-1. The\nDRAFT test still targets the synchronous testid because DraftMode is\nstill a stub (Task 3 of the plan).\n\n135/135 vitest passing. typecheck + lint clean.\n\n* task(13b): extract isCarryEligible to lib/ for cross-mode reuse\n\nTasks 13b-2 and 13b-4 both need the carry-eligibility predicate but\nCarryForwardRow.tsx is a component file -- the react-refresh lint\nrule blocks non-component exports there. Extracted the pure predicate\nto lib/carryEligibility.ts so ReconciledSummary + ReconcileMode can\nimport it directly. CarryForwardRow now imports from the same place,\nkeeping a single source of truth.\n\nBehaviour unchanged. 9/9 CarryForwardRow tests passing.\n\n* task(13b-6): wire TeamMemberPage IcDrawer + close-to-team\n\n* task(13b-5): wire TeamPage rollup + drawer URL state\n\n* task(13b-3): wire DraftMode commit-create + Lock Week\n\n* task(13b-4): wire ReconcileMode table+reflection+submit+carry\n\n* task(13b): wire BlankState ''Create plan'' button to useCreateCurrentForMeMutation\n\nThe button was a presentational stub from the original mode-pane\nextraction (commit 1fdcb26): no onClick handler, clicking it did\nnothing. Caught during the post-implementation click-test pass.\n\nWired it to useCreateCurrentForMeMutation; RTK Query''s invalidatesTags\nalready covers the Plan LIST + Rollup LIST tags so useGetCurrentForMeQuery\nrefetches automatically and WeekEditor flips into DraftMode without\nany local state plumbing.\n\nLoading state disables the button + swaps the label to ''Creating…'';\nerrors surface a small inline banner (the global ConflictToast handles\n409s; this banner is for the rest).\n\n* task(13b): RCDO wiremock stub for standalone-dev picker\n\nThe picker landed wired and tested, but the e2e-profile docker stack\npoints RCDO at https://rcdo.invalid/ -- the backend''s RcdoController\nreturns 500 INTERNAL_ERROR on connect refused, and the picker correctly\nrenders its ''RCDO temporarily unavailable'' degraded state with no\nselectable outcomes. Demo-ready but unusable.\n\nAdd a wiremock service (port 8081) returning a fixed list of 4\nSupportingOutcomes with valid UUIDs and inline 4-level breadcrumbs\nmatching the upstream contract per docs/adr/0001-rcdo-contract.md.\nSpring container points at http://rcdo-stub:8081 over the docker\nnetwork. CI''s Cypress run is unaffected -- the green-path scenarios\nalready use cy.intercept against the typed /api/v1/rcdo/* paths.\n\nMappings under apps/weekly-commit-ui/wiremock/mappings/. Wiremock''s\ndefault mount-path /home/wiremock auto-discovers them at startup.\nRestart cycle: docker compose down + up brings the stub up first\n(weekly-commit-service depends_on rcdo-stub).\n\n* task(13b): fix CI -- prettier formatting + wiremock healthcheck path\n\nTwo parallel CI failures on the previous push:\n\n1. lint-test-build / Prettier check: 4 files violated formatting --\n   CommitCreateForm.tsx, ReconciledSummary.tsx, TeamPage.tsx, and the\n   new wiremock mapping JSON. Subagents ran lint but not format:check\n   during their per-task verification; CI runs both. Auto-fixed via\n   yarn format:write.\n\n2. cypress-cucumber / Provision ephemeral env: rcdo-stub container\n   marked unhealthy because the healthcheck hit /__admin/health which\n   wiremock 3.x does not expose (returns 404). Switched to /__admin/\n   which responds 200 with the mappings JSON once the server is up --\n   sufficient to gate the backend''s depends_on.\n\n* task(13b): override wiremock baked-in healthcheck (correct port + path)\n\nRound 2 of the CI fix. The previous attempt edited the test command\nbut left the healthcheck on the wrong port -- the wiremock 3.9.1 image\nships a HEALTHCHECK targeting localhost:8080 (the default port), but\nwe run wiremock on --port 8081 because 8080 is the backend. Compose\ninherits the image''s HEALTHCHECK and was probing a closed port; the\nnew test commands I wrote weren''t taking effect because of how compose\nresolves the file''s healthcheck block.\n\nAlso wiremock 3.9.1 has no /__admin/health endpoint at all -- /__admin/\nis the working alternative.\n\nFix:\n- Explicit override block with the correct port (8081) and path\n  (/__admin/, returns 200 with mappings JSON).\n- start_period: 30s so a slow CI runner has runway to boot the JVM\n  before failures count toward the unhealthy threshold.\n- Workflow gains a ''Show rcdo-stub logs on failure'' step parallel to\n  the existing backend-logs-on-failure step so the next surprise has\n  log output to grep.\n\nVerified: docker compose up -d --wait completes in ~12s locally with\nall three containers Healthy.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp75fpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmCkQADu9Wyb1CO2RhwY43FUfaCKX\nnQE5oQpYhExbYasLyhXcD5kTI2Vu2kY2i/kW7GpcobxGXq//U56K/QjIjPIkZISj\nc333IoUaIWlpgwZ780oE6aNALJC0RVFELn4ckfmqB4U+I6wBaCv4fJYie7mpRMc5\nz9qIcB9D5ZW1IJHTLboeKTAQCvmMR88yQZA6I5NyWRib2Z3MyGgPQjN6EC0Cu20w\ncW2Jx7k3AFbtr6pRfKCY6pWVmrt1vuK0TAAigDlAnrfiadtIXDr3VA9hmX0CooCZ\nSVEz7Q65Z9uY09FPnaO7cfKnFpQUM4REGvxRG677wFbpicpU6BZKlIpqpO8M3xiX\nSHRjZ6jOz2XDAwh3mvaaDdTLmhU3lXe1yCMpZnl4UgapXjZipa8lNnoj32/K1cpx\nQ80IQxEVM2wqUGKmO/DAD/iRdN3nu3J4KEGSIWPb/Z0ZJRbZ0VAUHQMB9OwSDJK3\nfJdu8lTUfGyni/qOa3VK5WehqU7RefT5GP4KYdfyIr4DgH/XF0dkBrAeCFbSWyD5\nE0ZDcoGbrOCyrLsjcZdwlSXHkuijImQ/ght/49M4RygqETYMRA/Lkaa7yJU76RDb\n/y8nNYg3fRBcm8b+scEguGgiI8S7EnJOhXJwxB77dxhXAHmNE3NGeeqBzS7Rod6B\nn2PowQbejoar5SNX4zR2\n=MwDg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T17:07:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGQ2MDRjNjE0ZDAwODY5M2Y5MWZhMTFmYTc5MGNkYWQyMTkwMGUzMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272","sha":"9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272"}],"sha":"d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d604c614d008693f91fa11fa790cdad21900e30b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T05:00:28Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T05:00:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(13-followup): dev-auth PEM as virtual module + vite proxy (#7)\n\nTwo related improvements over what landed in PR #6:\n\n1. Dev test PEM via Vite virtual module\n---------------------------------------\nReplaces the `define: { __WC_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY__: JSON.stringify(...) }`\nwith a tiny Vite plugin that exposes the PEM through a virtual ES\nmodule (`virtual:wc-dev-private-key`). Sidesteps both:\n  - Vite''s `?raw` + fs.allow path -- the cypress/ tree resolves outside\n    the package serving allowlist under Yarn PnP, even with `allow:[''..'']`.\n  - The brittleness of round-tripping a multi-line PEM through\n    JSON.stringify into a `define` constant (esbuild''s substitution\n    has been observed to mangle escaped newlines in larger PEMs).\n\nThe virtual ID is opaque (`virtual:wc-dev-private-key`) so it can never\ncollide with a real package. devAuth.ts imports it as a normal default\nexport; tree-shaken from prod federation builds because devAuth.ts is\nonly reached under `import.meta.env.DEV`. vite-env.d.ts grew a\n`declare module ''virtual:wc-dev-private-key''` so TypeScript stays happy.\n\n2. Vite dev-server proxy for /api + /actuator\n---------------------------------------------\n`server.proxy` forwards both prefixes to localhost:8080 (the\ndocker-compose.e2e.yml backend). Same-origin from the browser''s\nperspective so:\n  - No CORS preflight, no need for a CORS bean on the backend.\n  - The Authorization header from the dev-auth shim flows naturally.\n  - Mirrors production topology (PA host''s reverse proxy does the\n    same thing).\n\nReplaces the VITE_API_BASE_URL mechanism for the standalone-dev path.\nFederated runtime continues to use whatever the host injects; this is\na vite-config-time concern only.\n\nVerification (force-fresh): 135/135 vitest, 3/3 Playwright smoke,\nlint, typecheck, prettier all clean. The Playwright run is the real\nverification -- it actually loads vite dev with the new plugin and\nconfirms the virtual module resolves end-to-end.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"66d4dc5fa5d65854c88cb25289bc8c70dc98bd66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/66d4dc5fa5d65854c88cb25289bc8c70dc98bd66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272","verification":{"payload":"tree 66d4dc5fa5d65854c88cb25289bc8c70dc98bd66\nparent 2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777266028 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777266028 -0600\n\ntask(13-followup): dev-auth PEM as virtual module + vite proxy (#7)\n\nTwo related improvements over what landed in PR #6:\n\n1. Dev test PEM via Vite virtual module\n---------------------------------------\nReplaces the `define: { __WC_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY__: JSON.stringify(...) }`\nwith a tiny Vite plugin that exposes the PEM through a virtual ES\nmodule (`virtual:wc-dev-private-key`). Sidesteps both:\n  - Vite''s `?raw` + fs.allow path -- the cypress/ tree resolves outside\n    the package serving allowlist under Yarn PnP, even with `allow:[''..'']`.\n  - The brittleness of round-tripping a multi-line PEM through\n    JSON.stringify into a `define` constant (esbuild''s substitution\n    has been observed to mangle escaped newlines in larger PEMs).\n\nThe virtual ID is opaque (`virtual:wc-dev-private-key`) so it can never\ncollide with a real package. devAuth.ts imports it as a normal default\nexport; tree-shaken from prod federation builds because devAuth.ts is\nonly reached under `import.meta.env.DEV`. vite-env.d.ts grew a\n`declare module ''virtual:wc-dev-private-key''` so TypeScript stays happy.\n\n2. Vite dev-server proxy for /api + /actuator\n---------------------------------------------\n`server.proxy` forwards both prefixes to localhost:8080 (the\ndocker-compose.e2e.yml backend). Same-origin from the browser''s\nperspective so:\n  - No CORS preflight, no need for a CORS bean on the backend.\n  - The Authorization header from the dev-auth shim flows naturally.\n  - Mirrors production topology (PA host''s reverse proxy does the\n    same thing).\n\nReplaces the VITE_API_BASE_URL mechanism for the standalone-dev path.\nFederated runtime continues to use whatever the host injects; this is\na vite-config-time concern only.\n\nVerification (force-fresh): 135/135 vitest, 3/3 Playwright smoke,\nlint, typecheck, prettier all clean. The Playwright run is the real\nverification -- it actually loads vite dev with the new plugin and\nconfirms the virtual module resolves end-to-end.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7u1sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKeUQAChFgJadMQC5c8aKo1Bu54la\nNbLLIa4CJpJRSgQGW3xeQPjdEVXzhgGPFOyIWdlTyxNEa+liYG7lQFGA8Rvx0TUR\nxNCvgg/q+K3Su+GiAEIpVP0NPDrc21APCRw91D0GQJAjxIE8zR9XrLCDrHdb5Lrd\n3fVOGFfIVR8sGC+8KkbGvcg/EVjrqo7PvRDhw9vY9IhYBFQDBmXl7d+27LzBdd9k\nqGYncF0cZebd5mOVSy1QSNgDCvueoiwhUbNWmHH9PqxRWIre2gKkarAmjF8myNe5\nWsPWezVbg5sk3azIyRMGFMweUWtL47Ug6/u4C+orlq9dx6S3QXAQliqlWfVivUt+\nuoiBxM0pUAMXjX996bxJ9R0wWYscdjZ6cNkqVntU2CUfA99CFZBlMX30qJ/a7K7M\ni79t7cjUv5L+vsmNyMTH+TcnWu9eYTz+IDHoTeXvBcNJ9iPXe6a81cSzz2AIFc57\n9LZ1aPzMbYAmyuXBsHjc8CJR4QvfM6e5WN1iWXXxixygzEO0cg6m5UgvhcgRcQYt\nEVVI2OH3YLyttFGz8nywtLHO6TCvzosZpYEcDp440lhMSRqyIGlqi6WElZhjB/WG\nYGWc2I/VMs/iMLQUUM9H6IjqqTBPW8+yPxXNDTPsGEwzFT7Jw3bWHzW1yJEGdR+8\ngbC5Ej3LtOdzFwKqNMYY\n=egf+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T05:00:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDlmNDgzZjVhNjRhMDk2MjBiNGNhZjcwYjU2MTJjOTI0ODA2YmUyNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db","sha":"2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db"}],"sha":"9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/9f483f5a64a09620b4caf70b5612c924806be272"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T04:47:20Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T04:47:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(13): Cross-remote E2E (in progress) (#6)\n\n* task(13): Cypress + Cucumber baseline (deps + config + smoke .feature)\n\nCypress 13 + cucumber preprocessor + esbuild bundler installed in the\nUI workspace. Files:\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/\n    cypress.config.ts                                     # preprocessor + bundler wiring\n    cypress/e2e/smoke.feature                             # proves the runner is wired\n    cypress/support/e2e.ts                                # per-spec setup hook (empty)\n    cypress/support/step_definitions/smoke.ts             # step impls\n\nPer-feature step file scoping per the CLAUDE.md Common-Issues note\n(\"Cypress + Cucumber step collisions ... scope step files per feature\nor use unique phrasing\"). Configured via\n`cypress-cucumber-preprocessor.stepDefinitions:\ncypress/support/step_definitions/[filepart].{ts,js}` in package.json.\n\neslint config ignores cypress/** -- step files use ambient Cypress\nglobals and don''t fit the src/ tsconfig project. .gitignore extended\nfor cypress/{videos,screenshots,downloads}/.\n\nThe smoke scenario will be exercised end-to-end in subtask 5 once the\ndocker-compose backend is up. For now the verification is structural:\nno regression on 129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier (all\nforce-fresh; \"don''t trust nx cache\" memory rule applied).\n\nTech-stack lock per CLAUDE.md: \"Cypress + Cucumber/Gherkin for\ncross-remote E2E\" -- exact match.\n\n* task(13): four scenario .feature files (commit-entry / lock-week / reconcile / manager-review)\n\nFour .feature files in apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress/e2e/ covering\nUSER_FLOW.md flows 1-4 with mock-network step definitions:\n\n  commit-entry.feature     Flow 1 -- 404 -> blank -> Create -> DRAFT\n  lock-week.feature        Flow 2 -- DRAFT -> Lock -> LOCKED + 409\n  reconcile.feature        Flow 3 -- LOCKED+day4 -> reconcile + carry\n  manager-review.feature   Flow 4 -- rollup -> drawer -> comment\n\nPer-feature step file scoping per the CLAUDE.md Common-Issues note;\neach scenario''s network mocks live next to its steps. Step bodies use\nreal API paths (`/api/v1/plans/me/current` etc.) that the typed\nRTK Query endpoints from group 10 already hit.\n\nINTEGRATION GAP SURFACED: groups 11 + 12 shipped the *components*\n(<RCDOPicker />, <ReconcileTable />, <IcDrawer />, etc.) but the\nWeekEditor''s DraftMode/LockedReadOnly/ReconcileMode panes are still\nstubs -- there is no \"Lock Week\" button, no ReconcileTable in the\nReconcileMode pane, no <MemberCard /> wired into TeamPage. The four\nscenarios cannot pass against today''s stubbed panes.\n\nResolution: enumerated as new follow-up TASK_LIST group \"13b. Wire IC\n+ Manager components into WeekEditor mode panes\" with a 7-step\nchecklist mirroring the 11a precedent. Until 13b lands, all four\nscenarios are @pending-tagged. cypress.config.ts defaults\nenv.TAGS: ''not @pending'' so `cypress run` skips them; subtask 5''s CI\njob re-enables them by overriding CYPRESS_TAGS='''' once 13b ships.\n\nThe Gherkin acts as living documentation that drives 13b -- step\nselectors and assertions name the data-testids the integration must\nproduce. This is intentionally aspirational: the .feature files are\nthe spec for what 13b delivers.\n\n129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh green\n(no regression on the React workspace).\n\n* task(13): kill-switch.feature -- cross-remote contract for [MVP24]\n\n3 scenarios in apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress/e2e/kill-switch.feature\ndocumenting the host-side kill-switch behavior:\n\n  1. flag-on  -> host loads the federated remote\n  2. flag-off -> host renders the \"Continue in 15-Five\" link\n  3. flag-flip mid-session -> swap without redeploying\n\nTagged @pending @host-contract because the kill switch is a HOST-SIDE\nconcern per [MVP24] -- the WeeklyCommit remote can''t test the host''s\nflag-flipping decision-making in isolation. Step definitions in\ncypress/support/step_definitions/kill-switch.ts throw a\n[host-harness-required] error with explicit pointers to TASK_LIST\ngroup 14 so the failure mode is self-documenting -- nobody mistakes\nthis for working coverage.\n\nThe .feature file lives in this repo because cross-remote E2E is by\ndefinition cross-remote; the host-app team''s E2E job runs it with\nCYPRESS_TAGS=@host-contract once their kill-switch harness exists.\nTASK_LIST group 14''s existing kill-switch entry now references back to\nthis .feature so the contract has a paper trail in both directions.\n\nTech-lead reasoning: the brief locks in [MVP24]; for a 175-person\nrollout the kill switch is cheap insurance (one host env var + a\nfallback link) against post-launch bugs that would otherwise need a\nremote redeploy + CloudFront invalidation. Phase 3 removes it\n([TASK_LIST 23]) -- temporary infrastructure by design. Documenting\nthe contract here is honest; pretending we can fully test it from the\nremote-only repo would not be.\n\n129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh green.\n\n* task(13): self-signed JWT auth for E2E (no Auth0 dashboard required)\n\nBackend\n-------\nE2eJwtDecoderConfig (@Profile(\"e2e\")) overrides the Spring Boot\nauto-configured JwtDecoder with one that trusts the test public key\non the classpath at e2e-keys/public-key.pem. Production paths reach\nthe auto-config and validate against Auth0''s JWKS as before -- the\ne2e bean is profile-gated, never active outside the docker-compose\ntest env.\n\nE2eJwtDecoderConfigIT (3 cases) pins the contract:\n  - accepts JWTs signed with the matching test private key\n  - rejects HS256-with-wrong-key (forgery attempt)\n  - rejects alg=none (the great early-OAuth2 vulnerability)\n\nFrontend\n--------\ncypress/support/auth/{testUsers,signTestJwt}.ts is the JS-side signer\nusing `jose` (RS256). Four canonical fixture roles cover the brief''s\n[MVP20] matrix: IC (with manager), IC_NULL_MANAGER, MANAGER, ADMIN.\n\ncy.loginAs(role) custom command in cypress/support/e2e.ts:\n  - signs a JWT for the role using the test private key\n  - stashes the token on window.__WC_E2E_TOKEN__ for the app to read\n  - injects Authorization: Bearer header via cy.intercept on every\n    /api/v1/** request (belt + braces in case the app code path\n    misses the global)\n\n6 vitest cases on signTestJwt round-trip every role through\njose.jwtVerify with the matching public key + verify the\nmanager_id-omission contract for IC_NULL_MANAGER (BE''s\noptionalUuid() treats missing == blank == Optional.empty so the JWT\nshape must omit, not null).\n\nRequired @vitest-environment node on the signer test because jsdom''s\nTextEncoder polyfill returns a Uint8Array subclass that fails\njose''s `instanceof Uint8Array` check. Worth a sentence in the file\nheader for the next person who hits it.\n\nKeys\n----\nRSA-2048 keypair generated with openssl, committed in both workspaces.\nREADME.md in each keys directory explains:\n  - why the private key is safe to commit (zero authority outside the\n    e2e Spring profile, which never runs in production)\n  - how to rotate (openssl genrsa + openssl rsa -pubout, copy public\n    half to BOTH workspace locations)\n  - that the BE integration test pins public-key drift between the\n    two workspaces\n\n.gitignore was *.pem-blanket; added a targeted whitelist exception\nfor the two e2e-keys/ paths so any other random .pem stays ignored\nby default.\n\nVerification\n------------\n260/260 backend unit + 3/3 backend IT (E2eJwtDecoderConfigIT) +\n135/135 UI vitest (incl. the 6 new signTestJwt cases) all green.\nLint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh clean.\n\n* task(13): docker-compose ephemeral env + e2e-pr.yml workflow\n\napps/weekly-commit-ui/docker-compose.e2e.yml is the new harness:\n\n  postgres                 16.4-alpine, tmpfs-backed (never persists)\n  weekly-commit-service    eclipse-temurin:21-jre running the pre-built JAR\n                           via volume mount (no Dockerfile in this repo --\n                           that''s group 14''s territory; the upstream JRE\n                           keeps this scope-clean)\n\nSPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e activates E2eJwtDecoderConfig so the test JWTs\nthe cypress cy.loginAs(role) helper signs are trusted.\n\nRCDO_BASE_URL + NOTIFICATION_SVC_BASE_URL point at unreachable hosts so\nany accidental upstream call from a green-path scenario fails loudly with\na connect refusal rather than a silent 30s timeout.\n\nThe Vite dev server runs on the GitHub Actions runner host (not in\ncompose) -- Cypress''s baseUrl already points at localhost:4184. Keeping\nVite outside the container avoids a slow image build and lets developers\nhot-reload while iterating on a scenario locally.\n\nWorkflow rewrite (.github/workflows/e2e-pr.yml)\n-----------------------------------------------\nThe three placeholder `echo \"TODO group 13\"` steps replaced with:\n  - Build backend JAR (mvn package -DskipTests)\n  - docker compose up -d --wait\n  - Vite dev server in background + wait for :4184\n  - yarn test:cypress\n  - Teardown (docker compose down -v) in `if: always()`\n\nFailure-path log dump + cypress artifacts upload included so a CI miss\nis debuggable.\n\nDefault cypress.config.ts env.TAGS=`not @pending` skips the four\nscenario .feature files (commit-entry / lock-week / reconcile /\nmanager-review) and the kill-switch contract scenarios -- they need\ngroup 13b''s WeekEditor mode-pane integration before they can pass.\nToday the suite runs only the smoke .feature against the real\nephemeral stack.\n\nVerification\n------------\ndocker compose stack healthy locally; backend /actuator/info reports\nthe head SHA; both pg + the BE pass their healthchecks. Cypress run\nitself deferred to CI -- Cypress 13.17 has a darwin-arm64 startup\nquirk on this dev box (\"bad option: --no-sandbox\" from Cypress''s own\nsmoke check), but ubuntu-24.04 runners are where the workflow lives\nand Cypress works fine there. UI vitest 135/135, lint, typecheck,\nprettier all force-fresh green.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward e2e-pr -- cypress.config .ts → .js\n\nThe e2e-pr CI run failed with:\n  TypeError [ERR_UNKNOWN_FILE_EXTENSION]: Unknown file extension \".ts\"\n    for .../apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress.config.ts\n\nCypress 13''s packaged Node runtime doesn''t transpile .ts configs, and\nYarn 4 PnP doesn''t auto-resolve a .ts loader for it either. Cypress''s\nown docs prefer .js for the config; their cucumber-preprocessor\nREADME likewise.\n\nRenamed cypress.config.ts → cypress.config.js with a top-of-file\n`// @ts-check` JSDoc directive. Same imports, same intellisense, no\nruntime cost. Already covered by the `*.config.js` ignore in\neslint.config.js so no new lint surface.\n\nIncludes Daisy''s compose-file edit: host port 5433 → container 5432\n(was 5432:5432), avoiding the macOS-Homebrew Postgres collision on\n5432. CI runners have no host Postgres so the change is a no-op there\nbut standardizes local + CI behavior.\n\nVerified force-fresh: lint, typecheck, prettier, 135/135 vitest all\ngreen. The local docker-compose stack already healthy in subtask 5''s\nverification; fix-forward is the cypress config wrapper only.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward e2e-pr -- cypress.config .js → .mjs + dev auth shim\n\nSecond e2e-pr CI failure root cause:\n  Error: require() of ES Module .../cypress.config.js\n    from cypress/.../run_require_async_child.js not supported\n\nCypress 13''s plugin loader uses require(), but\napps/weekly-commit-ui/package.json declares \"type\": \"module\" so .js\nresolves to ESM. .mjs is always-ESM regardless of package.json type,\nwhich routes Cypress''s loader to its dynamic-import path.\n\nRenamed cypress.config.js → cypress.config.mjs. Updated the file''s\nheader comment to document BOTH dead-end attempts (.ts → .js → .mjs)\nso the next person who hits this trail of failures finds the answer\nin one place.\n\neslint.config.js gained `*.config.mjs` alongside the existing\n`*.config.js` and `*.config.ts` ignores.\n\ndocker-compose.e2e.yml: postgres host port bumped 5433 → 5434 to avoid\nyet another local-port collision (5432 = Homebrew default,\n5433 = sometimes another dev stack). Container-internal port stays\n5432; only the host binding changes. CI runners don''t host Postgres\nso the choice is moot there.\n\nPlus: standalone-dev auth shim\n-------------------------------\nsrc/dev/devAuth.ts mints a self-signed JWT (same private key the\nCypress suite signs with -- E2eJwtDecoderConfig trusts the matching\npublic half) and patches global fetch to attach it to backend calls.\nSolves the standalone `vite dev` 401-on-everything problem caused by\nthe e2e-profile backend rejecting unauthenticated requests.\n\nStrict scope guarantees the prod federated bundle stays unaffected:\n  - main.tsx wraps `installDevAuth()` in `if (import.meta.env.DEV)`\n    so `vite build` tree-shakes the entire dev/ subtree + the jose\n    dep + the embedded PEM string out of the prod bundle.\n  - WeeklyCommitModule.tsx (the federated export) is untouched.\n  - The PEM is loaded via Vite''s `?raw` import from the existing\n    cypress/support/auth/keys/ tree -- single source of truth, no\n    key duplication.\n\nRole override: ?devRole=IC|IC_NULL_MANAGER|MANAGER|ADMIN in the URL\nbeats VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE which beats the hardcoded MANAGER default.\nActive role surfaces in the document title so it''s obvious which\nidentity the dev session is acting as.\n\nvite-env.d.ts: added types for VITE_API_BASE_URL and\nVITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE.\n\nAll four checks force-fresh green: 135/135 vitest, lint, typecheck,\nprettier.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward -- cucumber slash escapes + dev-auth resilience\n\nTwo distinct CI failures in the third e2e-pr attempt:\n\n1. e2e-pr: CucumberExpressionError \"alternative may not be empty\"\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nCucumber expressions treat `/` as alternation between adjacent tokens.\nURL paths like `/commits/{string}` and multi-status legends like\n`DONE / PARTIAL / MISSED` create empty-alternative crashes during\nstep *registration* (which runs for ALL .feature files in the\npreprocessor, even @pending-tagged ones that won''t actually execute).\n\nConverted slash-bearing step patterns to RegExp instead of strings:\n\n  reconcile.ts\n    \"each commit row has DONE / PARTIAL / MISSED radios\"           -> regex\n    \"the API receives PATCH /commits/{string} with actualStatus...\"-> regex (\\S+)\n    \"the API receives PATCH /plans with the reflection body\"       -> regex\n    \"the API receives POST /commits/{string}/carry-forward\"        -> regex (\\S+)\n    \"the API receives POST /plans/transitions with target ...\"     -> regex\n  manager-review.ts\n    \"the API receives POST /plans/reviews\"                         -> regex\n  kill-switch.ts\n    \"the user navigates back to /weekly-commit\"                    -> regex\n    \"a user opens the host app''s /weekly-commit route\"             -> regex\n\nThe {string} placeholders also became (\\S+) capture groups -- the\noriginal expressions required quoted strings (\"a\") in the .feature,\nbut the .feature files use bare `/commits/a` (no quotes). The regex\nmatches the actual feature text shape.\n\n2. frontend-pr: Playwright smoke can''t find the current-week page\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\nThe dev-auth shim''s await blocks React mount when something inside it\nthrows (Vite ?raw + Yarn PnP fs.allow boundary issue). Solution:\n\n  - main.tsx: wrap installDevAuth() in try/catch so the shim is\n    best-effort. Failure logs a console warning; React still mounts.\n    Playwright''s smoke (which doesn''t need backend auth at all) is\n    no longer affected by dev-auth setup errors.\n  - Daisy''s edits replaced devAuth.ts''s runtime `?raw` import with a\n    vite.config.ts-time readFileSync + a `define` constant\n    (__WC_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY__). Sidesteps Vite''s fs.allow boundary\n    entirely. Tree-shaken from prod because devAuth.ts only loads\n    under import.meta.env.DEV.\n\nLocal verification\n------------------\n- 135/135 vitest pass force-fresh\n- 3/3 Playwright smoke pass force-fresh (the regression that broke\n  frontend-pr is gone)\n- lint, typecheck, prettier all clean\n\n* task(13): standalone-only / → /weekly-commit/current redirect (main.tsx)\n\nThe HashRouter starts at \"/\" in standalone mode, but\nWeeklyCommitModule''s route tree is rooted at /weekly-commit/* (matches\nhow the PA host mounts the federated remote). Without a redirect, hitting\nhttp://localhost:4184/ in the dev server renders nothing.\n\nSolution: a tiny <Routes> wrapper in main.tsx (standalone entry only):\n  - \"/\"  -> <Navigate to=\"/weekly-commit/current\" replace />\n  - \"*\"  -> <WeeklyCommitModule />  (existing tree continues to work)\n\nThe federated path (host imports WeeklyCommitModule directly) is\nuntouched -- main.tsx isn''t part of that bundle.\n\nImproves both the dev-server UX and the Playwright smoke baseline (the\nsmoke already navigates explicitly to /weekly-commit/current, so it\ndoesn''t depend on the redirect, but a future \"open the root URL\" smoke\ncase lands on a real page).\n\nForce-fresh checks green: 135/135 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ba8db382ce96a43efbe89bb9c5866c8b365499f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/1ba8db382ce96a43efbe89bb9c5866c8b365499f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ba8db382ce96a43efbe89bb9c5866c8b365499f\nparent c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777265240 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777265240 -0600\n\ntask(13): Cross-remote E2E (in progress) (#6)\n\n* task(13): Cypress + Cucumber baseline (deps + config + smoke .feature)\n\nCypress 13 + cucumber preprocessor + esbuild bundler installed in the\nUI workspace. Files:\n\n  apps/weekly-commit-ui/\n    cypress.config.ts                                     # preprocessor + bundler wiring\n    cypress/e2e/smoke.feature                             # proves the runner is wired\n    cypress/support/e2e.ts                                # per-spec setup hook (empty)\n    cypress/support/step_definitions/smoke.ts             # step impls\n\nPer-feature step file scoping per the CLAUDE.md Common-Issues note\n(\"Cypress + Cucumber step collisions ... scope step files per feature\nor use unique phrasing\"). Configured via\n`cypress-cucumber-preprocessor.stepDefinitions:\ncypress/support/step_definitions/[filepart].{ts,js}` in package.json.\n\neslint config ignores cypress/** -- step files use ambient Cypress\nglobals and don''t fit the src/ tsconfig project. .gitignore extended\nfor cypress/{videos,screenshots,downloads}/.\n\nThe smoke scenario will be exercised end-to-end in subtask 5 once the\ndocker-compose backend is up. For now the verification is structural:\nno regression on 129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier (all\nforce-fresh; \"don''t trust nx cache\" memory rule applied).\n\nTech-stack lock per CLAUDE.md: \"Cypress + Cucumber/Gherkin for\ncross-remote E2E\" -- exact match.\n\n* task(13): four scenario .feature files (commit-entry / lock-week / reconcile / manager-review)\n\nFour .feature files in apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress/e2e/ covering\nUSER_FLOW.md flows 1-4 with mock-network step definitions:\n\n  commit-entry.feature     Flow 1 -- 404 -> blank -> Create -> DRAFT\n  lock-week.feature        Flow 2 -- DRAFT -> Lock -> LOCKED + 409\n  reconcile.feature        Flow 3 -- LOCKED+day4 -> reconcile + carry\n  manager-review.feature   Flow 4 -- rollup -> drawer -> comment\n\nPer-feature step file scoping per the CLAUDE.md Common-Issues note;\neach scenario''s network mocks live next to its steps. Step bodies use\nreal API paths (`/api/v1/plans/me/current` etc.) that the typed\nRTK Query endpoints from group 10 already hit.\n\nINTEGRATION GAP SURFACED: groups 11 + 12 shipped the *components*\n(<RCDOPicker />, <ReconcileTable />, <IcDrawer />, etc.) but the\nWeekEditor''s DraftMode/LockedReadOnly/ReconcileMode panes are still\nstubs -- there is no \"Lock Week\" button, no ReconcileTable in the\nReconcileMode pane, no <MemberCard /> wired into TeamPage. The four\nscenarios cannot pass against today''s stubbed panes.\n\nResolution: enumerated as new follow-up TASK_LIST group \"13b. Wire IC\n+ Manager components into WeekEditor mode panes\" with a 7-step\nchecklist mirroring the 11a precedent. Until 13b lands, all four\nscenarios are @pending-tagged. cypress.config.ts defaults\nenv.TAGS: ''not @pending'' so `cypress run` skips them; subtask 5''s CI\njob re-enables them by overriding CYPRESS_TAGS='''' once 13b ships.\n\nThe Gherkin acts as living documentation that drives 13b -- step\nselectors and assertions name the data-testids the integration must\nproduce. This is intentionally aspirational: the .feature files are\nthe spec for what 13b delivers.\n\n129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh green\n(no regression on the React workspace).\n\n* task(13): kill-switch.feature -- cross-remote contract for [MVP24]\n\n3 scenarios in apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress/e2e/kill-switch.feature\ndocumenting the host-side kill-switch behavior:\n\n  1. flag-on  -> host loads the federated remote\n  2. flag-off -> host renders the \"Continue in 15-Five\" link\n  3. flag-flip mid-session -> swap without redeploying\n\nTagged @pending @host-contract because the kill switch is a HOST-SIDE\nconcern per [MVP24] -- the WeeklyCommit remote can''t test the host''s\nflag-flipping decision-making in isolation. Step definitions in\ncypress/support/step_definitions/kill-switch.ts throw a\n[host-harness-required] error with explicit pointers to TASK_LIST\ngroup 14 so the failure mode is self-documenting -- nobody mistakes\nthis for working coverage.\n\nThe .feature file lives in this repo because cross-remote E2E is by\ndefinition cross-remote; the host-app team''s E2E job runs it with\nCYPRESS_TAGS=@host-contract once their kill-switch harness exists.\nTASK_LIST group 14''s existing kill-switch entry now references back to\nthis .feature so the contract has a paper trail in both directions.\n\nTech-lead reasoning: the brief locks in [MVP24]; for a 175-person\nrollout the kill switch is cheap insurance (one host env var + a\nfallback link) against post-launch bugs that would otherwise need a\nremote redeploy + CloudFront invalidation. Phase 3 removes it\n([TASK_LIST 23]) -- temporary infrastructure by design. Documenting\nthe contract here is honest; pretending we can fully test it from the\nremote-only repo would not be.\n\n129/129 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh green.\n\n* task(13): self-signed JWT auth for E2E (no Auth0 dashboard required)\n\nBackend\n-------\nE2eJwtDecoderConfig (@Profile(\"e2e\")) overrides the Spring Boot\nauto-configured JwtDecoder with one that trusts the test public key\non the classpath at e2e-keys/public-key.pem. Production paths reach\nthe auto-config and validate against Auth0''s JWKS as before -- the\ne2e bean is profile-gated, never active outside the docker-compose\ntest env.\n\nE2eJwtDecoderConfigIT (3 cases) pins the contract:\n  - accepts JWTs signed with the matching test private key\n  - rejects HS256-with-wrong-key (forgery attempt)\n  - rejects alg=none (the great early-OAuth2 vulnerability)\n\nFrontend\n--------\ncypress/support/auth/{testUsers,signTestJwt}.ts is the JS-side signer\nusing `jose` (RS256). Four canonical fixture roles cover the brief''s\n[MVP20] matrix: IC (with manager), IC_NULL_MANAGER, MANAGER, ADMIN.\n\ncy.loginAs(role) custom command in cypress/support/e2e.ts:\n  - signs a JWT for the role using the test private key\n  - stashes the token on window.__WC_E2E_TOKEN__ for the app to read\n  - injects Authorization: Bearer header via cy.intercept on every\n    /api/v1/** request (belt + braces in case the app code path\n    misses the global)\n\n6 vitest cases on signTestJwt round-trip every role through\njose.jwtVerify with the matching public key + verify the\nmanager_id-omission contract for IC_NULL_MANAGER (BE''s\noptionalUuid() treats missing == blank == Optional.empty so the JWT\nshape must omit, not null).\n\nRequired @vitest-environment node on the signer test because jsdom''s\nTextEncoder polyfill returns a Uint8Array subclass that fails\njose''s `instanceof Uint8Array` check. Worth a sentence in the file\nheader for the next person who hits it.\n\nKeys\n----\nRSA-2048 keypair generated with openssl, committed in both workspaces.\nREADME.md in each keys directory explains:\n  - why the private key is safe to commit (zero authority outside the\n    e2e Spring profile, which never runs in production)\n  - how to rotate (openssl genrsa + openssl rsa -pubout, copy public\n    half to BOTH workspace locations)\n  - that the BE integration test pins public-key drift between the\n    two workspaces\n\n.gitignore was *.pem-blanket; added a targeted whitelist exception\nfor the two e2e-keys/ paths so any other random .pem stays ignored\nby default.\n\nVerification\n------------\n260/260 backend unit + 3/3 backend IT (E2eJwtDecoderConfigIT) +\n135/135 UI vitest (incl. the 6 new signTestJwt cases) all green.\nLint, typecheck, prettier all force-fresh clean.\n\n* task(13): docker-compose ephemeral env + e2e-pr.yml workflow\n\napps/weekly-commit-ui/docker-compose.e2e.yml is the new harness:\n\n  postgres                 16.4-alpine, tmpfs-backed (never persists)\n  weekly-commit-service    eclipse-temurin:21-jre running the pre-built JAR\n                           via volume mount (no Dockerfile in this repo --\n                           that''s group 14''s territory; the upstream JRE\n                           keeps this scope-clean)\n\nSPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=e2e activates E2eJwtDecoderConfig so the test JWTs\nthe cypress cy.loginAs(role) helper signs are trusted.\n\nRCDO_BASE_URL + NOTIFICATION_SVC_BASE_URL point at unreachable hosts so\nany accidental upstream call from a green-path scenario fails loudly with\na connect refusal rather than a silent 30s timeout.\n\nThe Vite dev server runs on the GitHub Actions runner host (not in\ncompose) -- Cypress''s baseUrl already points at localhost:4184. Keeping\nVite outside the container avoids a slow image build and lets developers\nhot-reload while iterating on a scenario locally.\n\nWorkflow rewrite (.github/workflows/e2e-pr.yml)\n-----------------------------------------------\nThe three placeholder `echo \"TODO group 13\"` steps replaced with:\n  - Build backend JAR (mvn package -DskipTests)\n  - docker compose up -d --wait\n  - Vite dev server in background + wait for :4184\n  - yarn test:cypress\n  - Teardown (docker compose down -v) in `if: always()`\n\nFailure-path log dump + cypress artifacts upload included so a CI miss\nis debuggable.\n\nDefault cypress.config.ts env.TAGS=`not @pending` skips the four\nscenario .feature files (commit-entry / lock-week / reconcile /\nmanager-review) and the kill-switch contract scenarios -- they need\ngroup 13b''s WeekEditor mode-pane integration before they can pass.\nToday the suite runs only the smoke .feature against the real\nephemeral stack.\n\nVerification\n------------\ndocker compose stack healthy locally; backend /actuator/info reports\nthe head SHA; both pg + the BE pass their healthchecks. Cypress run\nitself deferred to CI -- Cypress 13.17 has a darwin-arm64 startup\nquirk on this dev box (\"bad option: --no-sandbox\" from Cypress''s own\nsmoke check), but ubuntu-24.04 runners are where the workflow lives\nand Cypress works fine there. UI vitest 135/135, lint, typecheck,\nprettier all force-fresh green.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward e2e-pr -- cypress.config .ts → .js\n\nThe e2e-pr CI run failed with:\n  TypeError [ERR_UNKNOWN_FILE_EXTENSION]: Unknown file extension \".ts\"\n    for .../apps/weekly-commit-ui/cypress.config.ts\n\nCypress 13''s packaged Node runtime doesn''t transpile .ts configs, and\nYarn 4 PnP doesn''t auto-resolve a .ts loader for it either. Cypress''s\nown docs prefer .js for the config; their cucumber-preprocessor\nREADME likewise.\n\nRenamed cypress.config.ts → cypress.config.js with a top-of-file\n`// @ts-check` JSDoc directive. Same imports, same intellisense, no\nruntime cost. Already covered by the `*.config.js` ignore in\neslint.config.js so no new lint surface.\n\nIncludes Daisy''s compose-file edit: host port 5433 → container 5432\n(was 5432:5432), avoiding the macOS-Homebrew Postgres collision on\n5432. CI runners have no host Postgres so the change is a no-op there\nbut standardizes local + CI behavior.\n\nVerified force-fresh: lint, typecheck, prettier, 135/135 vitest all\ngreen. The local docker-compose stack already healthy in subtask 5''s\nverification; fix-forward is the cypress config wrapper only.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward e2e-pr -- cypress.config .js → .mjs + dev auth shim\n\nSecond e2e-pr CI failure root cause:\n  Error: require() of ES Module .../cypress.config.js\n    from cypress/.../run_require_async_child.js not supported\n\nCypress 13''s plugin loader uses require(), but\napps/weekly-commit-ui/package.json declares \"type\": \"module\" so .js\nresolves to ESM. .mjs is always-ESM regardless of package.json type,\nwhich routes Cypress''s loader to its dynamic-import path.\n\nRenamed cypress.config.js → cypress.config.mjs. Updated the file''s\nheader comment to document BOTH dead-end attempts (.ts → .js → .mjs)\nso the next person who hits this trail of failures finds the answer\nin one place.\n\neslint.config.js gained `*.config.mjs` alongside the existing\n`*.config.js` and `*.config.ts` ignores.\n\ndocker-compose.e2e.yml: postgres host port bumped 5433 → 5434 to avoid\nyet another local-port collision (5432 = Homebrew default,\n5433 = sometimes another dev stack). Container-internal port stays\n5432; only the host binding changes. CI runners don''t host Postgres\nso the choice is moot there.\n\nPlus: standalone-dev auth shim\n-------------------------------\nsrc/dev/devAuth.ts mints a self-signed JWT (same private key the\nCypress suite signs with -- E2eJwtDecoderConfig trusts the matching\npublic half) and patches global fetch to attach it to backend calls.\nSolves the standalone `vite dev` 401-on-everything problem caused by\nthe e2e-profile backend rejecting unauthenticated requests.\n\nStrict scope guarantees the prod federated bundle stays unaffected:\n  - main.tsx wraps `installDevAuth()` in `if (import.meta.env.DEV)`\n    so `vite build` tree-shakes the entire dev/ subtree + the jose\n    dep + the embedded PEM string out of the prod bundle.\n  - WeeklyCommitModule.tsx (the federated export) is untouched.\n  - The PEM is loaded via Vite''s `?raw` import from the existing\n    cypress/support/auth/keys/ tree -- single source of truth, no\n    key duplication.\n\nRole override: ?devRole=IC|IC_NULL_MANAGER|MANAGER|ADMIN in the URL\nbeats VITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE which beats the hardcoded MANAGER default.\nActive role surfaces in the document title so it''s obvious which\nidentity the dev session is acting as.\n\nvite-env.d.ts: added types for VITE_API_BASE_URL and\nVITE_DEV_AUTH_ROLE.\n\nAll four checks force-fresh green: 135/135 vitest, lint, typecheck,\nprettier.\n\n* task(13): fix-forward -- cucumber slash escapes + dev-auth resilience\n\nTwo distinct CI failures in the third e2e-pr attempt:\n\n1. e2e-pr: CucumberExpressionError \"alternative may not be empty\"\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nCucumber expressions treat `/` as alternation between adjacent tokens.\nURL paths like `/commits/{string}` and multi-status legends like\n`DONE / PARTIAL / MISSED` create empty-alternative crashes during\nstep *registration* (which runs for ALL .feature files in the\npreprocessor, even @pending-tagged ones that won''t actually execute).\n\nConverted slash-bearing step patterns to RegExp instead of strings:\n\n  reconcile.ts\n    \"each commit row has DONE / PARTIAL / MISSED radios\"           -> regex\n    \"the API receives PATCH /commits/{string} with actualStatus...\"-> regex (\\S+)\n    \"the API receives PATCH /plans with the reflection body\"       -> regex\n    \"the API receives POST /commits/{string}/carry-forward\"        -> regex (\\S+)\n    \"the API receives POST /plans/transitions with target ...\"     -> regex\n  manager-review.ts\n    \"the API receives POST /plans/reviews\"                         -> regex\n  kill-switch.ts\n    \"the user navigates back to /weekly-commit\"                    -> regex\n    \"a user opens the host app''s /weekly-commit route\"             -> regex\n\nThe {string} placeholders also became (\\S+) capture groups -- the\noriginal expressions required quoted strings (\"a\") in the .feature,\nbut the .feature files use bare `/commits/a` (no quotes). The regex\nmatches the actual feature text shape.\n\n2. frontend-pr: Playwright smoke can''t find the current-week page\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\nThe dev-auth shim''s await blocks React mount when something inside it\nthrows (Vite ?raw + Yarn PnP fs.allow boundary issue). Solution:\n\n  - main.tsx: wrap installDevAuth() in try/catch so the shim is\n    best-effort. Failure logs a console warning; React still mounts.\n    Playwright''s smoke (which doesn''t need backend auth at all) is\n    no longer affected by dev-auth setup errors.\n  - Daisy''s edits replaced devAuth.ts''s runtime `?raw` import with a\n    vite.config.ts-time readFileSync + a `define` constant\n    (__WC_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY__). Sidesteps Vite''s fs.allow boundary\n    entirely. Tree-shaken from prod because devAuth.ts only loads\n    under import.meta.env.DEV.\n\nLocal verification\n------------------\n- 135/135 vitest pass force-fresh\n- 3/3 Playwright smoke pass force-fresh (the regression that broke\n  frontend-pr is gone)\n- lint, typecheck, prettier all clean\n\n* task(13): standalone-only / → /weekly-commit/current redirect (main.tsx)\n\nThe HashRouter starts at \"/\" in standalone mode, but\nWeeklyCommitModule''s route tree is rooted at /weekly-commit/* (matches\nhow the PA host mounts the federated remote). Without a redirect, hitting\nhttp://localhost:4184/ in the dev server renders nothing.\n\nSolution: a tiny <Routes> wrapper in main.tsx (standalone entry only):\n  - \"/\"  -> <Navigate to=\"/weekly-commit/current\" replace />\n  - \"*\"  -> <WeeklyCommitModule />  (existing tree continues to work)\n\nThe federated path (host imports WeeklyCommitModule directly) is\nuntouched -- main.tsx isn''t part of that bundle.\n\nImproves both the dev-server UX and the Playwright smoke baseline (the\nsmoke already navigates explicitly to /weekly-commit/current, so it\ndoesn''t depend on the redirect, but a future \"open the root URL\" smoke\ncase lands on a real page).\n\nForce-fresh checks green: 135/135 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7upZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdbgQAEARPo9VsPXKi8J45Bnd+X/w\noC3dXNmDcQrkUM7cB/Jr4oFqRzxVYIhOt7CMtJdnKnPZnYFrhYGkqFTXV7+v0Xyf\niCiRBdDNgk6bnSS4K0joNZmoejLyIGjym+oOVXsaDmpxnDAKSahvIF59lINaiqrD\nlX40beOXlmTNqnWEesryAf9qEUlPbzLOJpJ5Nhph8LMJz6bkabqdFqkdSOw5uIqY\nUcn/Nz11lEcO1sOeOjM544hCsD8bgc+40UwEqp/jvFr6dvoeTIh6WUPzi/HAJGfb\nBN/R/YrtwTQjDsyzIiIzJEkfV3VD2sUBvXuD41EZ6jwG0UqU9OvcX9/CcffLxGzq\nOHDCgrlT6xGr/beJ+29syGAnR9FTM19p4ql6Xcc/MV5bPCf8Acz5s4cExykBOqq3\nXhgTQ5GbwlMyyK7VCH5sE4zDvqgOnn4GotFnA/PhM9IueHCkMpldCJcJXM4D7tyT\n0+EAzC4QedlfYHa9haWqYO6FXU5wQKlTJL/Ev/wDe0FqBoV5Zfktsm0J1OHi3OuS\ny2A2IGJoTvEd0HJWLYM3nCoNZTm+KNhZV/HieK3Vr2L5LEY80KH67kvZU9XxDkKj\nAaz7LuJhUqpO/Qh2TQ/T17P/Q+NAzGO5iZCGQSmwXpTDFi73D5+Pz5zTSTIK6hjQ\nPYZfdAlRACd6ADOpQnzU\n=ZVlr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T04:47:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKDIwODhhOGZjMzZlNDFkOWVmZTFjOGNiMzNiYWY3ZWEzZTQzODExZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825","sha":"c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825"}],"sha":"2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/2088a8fc36e41d9efe1c8cb33baf7ea3e43811db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:38:59Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:38:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(12): Frontend Manager surfaces (in progress) (#5)\n\n* task(12): routes /weekly-commit/team + /weekly-commit/team/:employeeId\n\nTwo new routes inside the existing <Route path=\"weekly-commit\"> group.\nPage shells live in src/routes/{TeamPage,TeamMemberPage}.tsx as thin\ncontainers with Card + heading; the real <TeamRollup /> and <IcDrawer />\nland inside them in subtasks 2-5.\n\nTeamMemberPage reads :employeeId via useParams and surfaces it in a\ndata-testid=\"team-member-id\" element so the routing test can assert\nthe path-param round-trip without depending on visible label copy.\n\nThe Playwright `toBeVisible` lesson from group 11 (empty <div> has\nzero height -> fails the smoke assertion) is preserved here: both\nshells render visible content from the start.\n\nTests: 2 new routing cases (team page mounts; team member page mounts\nwith the path param surfaced). 87/87 vitest suite passes; lint,\ntypecheck, prettier all clean.\n\n* task(12): <TeamRollup /> aggregate stats + flagged-first ordering\n\nContainer that frames the manager view per [MVP9]. Three structural\npieces:\n\n  1. Aggregate stats strip (alignment%, completion%, unreviewed,\n     stuck) -- always visible so the layout stays stable when a\n     manager has no direct reports.\n  2. Tier distribution strip (ROCK > PEBBLE > SAND ordering mirrors\n     <ChessTier /> for consistency).\n  3. Member list ordered \"flagged-first then alphabetical\":\n     - flags.length > 0 floats to the top\n     - within each bucket: name.localeCompare ascending\n     The manager''s attention lands on rows that need it; the rest\n     sort predictably.\n\nCard rendering is delegated via a renderMember callback (subtask 3''s\n<MemberCard /> plugs in there). Same separation pattern <ChessTier />\nuses for renderCommit -- the rollup is presentational from the row\nstandpoint, knowing only how to order and frame, not what a card looks\nlike.\n\nEmpty state: data-testid=\"team-rollup-empty\" placeholder when\nmembers.length === 0, but the stats + tier strips still render so the\nmanager''s view doesn''t collapse on a zero-reports manager.\n\n8 vitest cases: stats render, unreviewed/stuck counts, tier counts,\nflagged-first sort, alphabetical-within-bucket sort, empty state,\nstats strip on empty, renderMember invocation. 95/95 vitest, lint,\ntypecheck, prettier all clean.\n\n* task(12): <MemberCard /> at-a-glance row for the team rollup\n\nOne row in TeamRollup. Surfaces the manager-facing signals from\nUSER_FLOW.md flow 4 + [MVP9]:\n\n  - name + plan state (tiny uppercase label)\n  - Top Rock title with \"No Top Rock\" orange indicator when absent\n  - Tier shape: R/P/S compact pills (mirrors <ChessTier /> ordering)\n  - Reflection preview, truncated to 80 chars + \"…\" suffix\n  - Flag badges (UNREVIEWED_72H, STUCK_COMMIT, NO_TOP_ROCK, ...)\n\nWhole row is role=\"button\" + tabIndex=0 + onKeyDown so keyboard users\ndrill into the IC drawer (subtask 4) with Enter/Space. onClick hands\nthe parent the employee id; the parent decides whether to navigate,\nopen a drawer overlay, or both -- same separation as the other\ndelegating components in this codebase.\n\nReflection block omitted entirely when reflectionPreview is\nempty/undefined; flags strip omitted when flags.length === 0 so\non-track rows stay uncluttered.\n\n12 vitest cases: name, plan state, Top Rock present/absent, tier\ncounts, reflection truncation + verbatim + omission, per-flag badges,\nno-flags case, mouse click + Enter + Space activation.\n\nTest fixture note: dropped `topRock: undefined` and\n`reflectionPreview: undefined` -- exactOptionalPropertyTypes\n(strict tsconfig) rejects explicit-undefined for optional fields.\nUse property-omission via destructure-rest instead, which is also\ncloser to what a real RTK Query response looks like.\n\n107/107 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier all clean.\n\n* task(12): fix frontend-pr lint -- allow `_`-prefixed unused vars\n\n`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` had argsIgnorePattern: ''^_'' but no\nvarsIgnorePattern, so destructure-rest with `_`-prefixed throwaways\n(used in MemberCard.test.tsx subtask-3 test fixtures to omit optional\nfields under exactOptionalPropertyTypes) tripped the rule.\n\nAdding varsIgnorePattern: ''^_'' brings the var rule in line with the\narg rule -- if `_handler` is fine as an arg name, `_topRock` should be\nfine as a destructure-rest throwaway.\n\nVerification gap that let this slip past:\nThe \"all four checks green\" report on the prior commit was reading an\nNx cache hit, not a fresh lint result. The destructure-rest edits\nlanded without a fresh `yarn lint` rerun. CI caught it on the actual\npush -- fix-forward only, no behavioral change.\n\nVerified clean now: `yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint\n--skip-nx-cache` returns 0; 107/107 vitest still passes; prettier\nclean.\n\n* task(12): <IcDrawer /> manager IC deep-dive overlay\n\nrole=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" overlay sliding in from the right\non top of the team-rollup view. Preserves the underlying context per\nUSER_FLOW.md flow 4 -- managers don''t lose their place when they\ndrill into a member.\n\nThree independent dismiss paths:\n  - Escape keypress (window-level listener)\n  - Click on the backdrop\n  - Explicit \"Close\" button (X in header)\n\nInside-dialog clicks call stopPropagation so a click on a commit row\ndoesn''t bubble to the backdrop handler and dismiss the drawer.\n\nData flow:\n  useGetPlanByEmployeeAndWeekQuery({ employeeId, weekStart })\n    -> when planId resolves:\n  useListCommitsQuery({ planId })           // skipped until then\n\nSurfaces inside the drawer:\n  - <StateBadge isReconcileEligible={false} />: read-only badge --\n    managers don''t transition state on someone else''s plan; comment-\n    only review per MEMO #5.\n  - Full reflection note (no truncation; the rollup card showed the\n    preview, the drawer is where the manager reads the whole thing).\n    Empty/null reflection gets a placeholder.\n  - Commit list grouped by <ChessTier />, each row decorated with a\n    <CarryStreakBadge /> when carryStreak >= 2 so streak chains are\n    visible at a glance.\n\nThe plan-level comment field (subtask 5) lands inside this drawer\nin a follow-up commit; the slot is here today as a placeholder so the\nscrolling layout is settled.\n\nType fix: dropped the QueryShape<T> indirection -- RTK Query''s\nUseQueryHookResult is a tagged union with way more fields than my\nadaptor and exactOptionalPropertyTypes rejects the structural mismatch.\nBody component now takes the unpacked fields directly (plan,\nplanLoading, planError, commits) which is also clearer at the call\nsite.\n\n13 new vitest cases cover dialog ARIA, loading, no-plan, state badge,\nreflection present/absent, commit rows, carry-streak surfacing, all\nthree close paths, no-close on inside clicks, and tier grouping.\n\nAll four checks force-fresh green (memory: don''t trust nx cache hits):\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint --skip-nx-cache       -> 0\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:typecheck --skip-nx-cache  -> 0\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit           -> 120/120\n  yarn format:check                                           -> clean\n\n* task(12): <ReviewCommentField /> + IcDrawer integration\n\nPlan-level review comment per [MVP10] / USER_FLOW.md flow 4. Single\ntextarea + \"Acknowledge\" button. Submission calls\nuseCreateReviewMutation (already exposed); the mutation''s\ninvalidatesTags: [{type:''Plan'', id:planId}] triggers an automatic plan\nrefetch so the parent drawer''s StateBadge + this field''s own\n\"Acknowledged on <date>\" indicator pick up the new managerReviewedAt\nwithout any manual coordination.\n\nUX rules:\n  - Submit disables when comment.trim() === '''' or mutation isLoading\n  - Button label flips to \"Acknowledging…\" while in flight\n  - Field clears on success\n  - Inline error banner on rejection (409 stays caught globally by\n    withConflictRetry + ConflictToast; this banner only fires on the\n    other failure modes -- 5xx, network, etc.)\n  - reviewed-at indicator renders only when managerReviewedAt is set\n\nNo comment threading (PRD scope-out: \"Per-commit comments or approval\ngating\"). The field stays usable after acknowledgement so a manager\ncan add follow-up notes; the audit log is the history.\n\nWired into <IcDrawer /> below the commit list. The drawer''s plan query\nalready provides plan.managerReviewedAt, which we pass through.\n\n9 vitest cases cover render, empty-disabled, content-enabled, mutation\narg shape (planId + comment body), clear-on-success, loading state,\nerror rejection surfacing, reviewed-at indicator show + hide.\n\nForce-fresh checks all green:\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint --skip-nx-cache       -> 0\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:typecheck --skip-nx-cache  -> 0\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit           -> 129/129\n  yarn format:check                                           -> clean\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"79098c083bc0329f5bd5f1036766195d9390fc28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/79098c083bc0329f5bd5f1036766195d9390fc28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825","verification":{"payload":"tree 79098c083bc0329f5bd5f1036766195d9390fc28\nparent ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777257539 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777257539 -0600\n\ntask(12): Frontend Manager surfaces (in progress) (#5)\n\n* task(12): routes /weekly-commit/team + /weekly-commit/team/:employeeId\n\nTwo new routes inside the existing <Route path=\"weekly-commit\"> group.\nPage shells live in src/routes/{TeamPage,TeamMemberPage}.tsx as thin\ncont