 line with the\narg rule -- if `_handler` is fine as an arg name, `_topRock` should be\nfine as a destructure-rest throwaway.\n\nVerification gap that let this slip past:\nThe \"all four checks green\" report on the prior commit was reading an\nNx cache hit, not a fresh lint result. The destructure-rest edits\nlanded without a fresh `yarn lint` rerun. CI caught it on the actual\npush -- fix-forward only, no behavioral change.\n\nVerified clean now: `yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint\n--skip-nx-cache` returns 0; 107/107 vitest still passes; prettier\nclean.\n\n* task(12): <IcDrawer /> manager IC deep-dive overlay\n\nrole=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" overlay sliding in from the right\non top of the team-rollup view. Preserves the underlying context per\nUSER_FLOW.md flow 4 -- managers don''t lose their place when they\ndrill into a member.\n\nThree independent dismiss paths:\n  - Escape keypress (window-level listener)\n  - Click on the backdrop\n  - Explicit \"Close\" button (X in header)\n\nInside-dialog clicks call stopPropagation so a click on a commit row\ndoesn''t bubble to the backdrop handler and dismiss the drawer.\n\nData flow:\n  useGetPlanByEmployeeAndWeekQuery({ employeeId, weekStart })\n    -> when planId resolves:\n  useListCommitsQuery({ planId })           // skipped until then\n\nSurfaces inside the drawer:\n  - <StateBadge isReconcileEligible={false} />: read-only badge --\n    managers don''t transition state on someone else''s plan; comment-\n    only review per MEMO #5.\n  - Full reflection note (no truncation; the rollup card showed the\n    preview, the drawer is where the manager reads the whole thing).\n    Empty/null reflection gets a placeholder.\n  - Commit list grouped by <ChessTier />, each row decorated with a\n    <CarryStreakBadge /> when carryStreak >= 2 so streak chains are\n    visible at a glance.\n\nThe plan-level comment field (subtask 5) lands inside this drawer\nin a follow-up commit; the slot is here today as a placeholder so the\nscrolling layout is settled.\n\nType fix: dropped the QueryShape<T> indirection -- RTK Query''s\nUseQueryHookResult is a tagged union with way more fields than my\nadaptor and exactOptionalPropertyTypes rejects the structural mismatch.\nBody component now takes the unpacked fields directly (plan,\nplanLoading, planError, commits) which is also clearer at the call\nsite.\n\n13 new vitest cases cover dialog ARIA, loading, no-plan, state badge,\nreflection present/absent, commit rows, carry-streak surfacing, all\nthree close paths, no-close on inside clicks, and tier grouping.\n\nAll four checks force-fresh green (memory: don''t trust nx cache hits):\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint --skip-nx-cache       -> 0\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:typecheck --skip-nx-cache  -> 0\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit           -> 120/120\n  yarn format:check                                           -> clean\n\n* task(12): <ReviewCommentField /> + IcDrawer integration\n\nPlan-level review comment per [MVP10] / USER_FLOW.md flow 4. Single\ntextarea + \"Acknowledge\" button. Submission calls\nuseCreateReviewMutation (already exposed); the mutation''s\ninvalidatesTags: [{type:''Plan'', id:planId}] triggers an automatic plan\nrefetch so the parent drawer''s StateBadge + this field''s own\n\"Acknowledged on <date>\" indicator pick up the new managerReviewedAt\nwithout any manual coordination.\n\nUX rules:\n  - Submit disables when comment.trim() === '''' or mutation isLoading\n  - Button label flips to \"Acknowledging…\" while in flight\n  - Field clears on success\n  - Inline error banner on rejection (409 stays caught globally by\n    withConflictRetry + ConflictToast; this banner only fires on the\n    other failure modes -- 5xx, network, etc.)\n  - reviewed-at indicator renders only when managerReviewedAt is set\n\nNo comment threading (PRD scope-out: \"Per-commit comments or approval\ngating\"). The field stays usable after acknowledgement so a manager\ncan add follow-up notes; the audit log is the history.\n\nWired into <IcDrawer /> below the commit list. The drawer''s plan query\nalready provides plan.managerReviewedAt, which we pass through.\n\n9 vitest cases cover render, empty-disabled, content-enabled, mutation\narg shape (planId + comment body), clear-on-success, loading state,\nerror rejection surfacing, reviewed-at indicator show + hide.\n\nForce-fresh checks all green:\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:lint --skip-nx-cache       -> 0\n  yarn nx run @wc/weekly-commit-ui:typecheck --skip-nx-cache  -> 0\n  yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:unit           -> 129/129\n  yarn format:check                                           -> clean\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7sxDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQbEQAEcwXeHU/FINVxSTne2RWTg2\n1zbsat/ALcIfBPY+kKdat9t8rqXfA+lhikFXV4mQm/x6QRUoELgE/laeTFArdKpH\nnr/AEMlBQ/SONQ7LoZOfCZ/YRwvJ1Fv1+s5N/eu2B0S558nG4fGkzr8KosE6nxoB\n81ZS2d3grOWjdFpMT9C7m7hzIWZvjQkM05shqX3svvbXSeDO7mL+cRpcSVV0aimp\nugwTncm7XVP9u4lNB9x5W5dColu7/CQFShwcswHOfimsBT6uUPhEpLAVDLfz0t55\nzuKzI41zI9ykzBtzeI2RJJLLQ5DbjVmcizOm3rVZVSiPy0HGfIdEWWxgsEjbU+DF\ntN36GEvmIIKl582/oXEq9ewbG3LzIvU0qbH1KcMchTmVgbnemcJ1nsXVeIbWTuvr\nmRQM6TRIHsViijm/tOlJcgbfzudJJa35C8cVJZifIBlbRZuJakVfbDBYAP6xh24Q\neroUyNJuD78H8mfY1tdCn/f5iQSkIdsbo6JJVGp9FwCTErGVJEtpzHLO54kfEPu1\nphvO6FILEn1QNt9dgl9Dqlv080aTEcy9YyySOb9VirFm2LZng7fJgsh10N87JK56\nosiYqqEF/qLRghKlBlmo3wQNegrQfnldS+QuXoWj6/taD9xfgZSKo4W80W0HPp7Q\nIj+rt21ikajXhEPTWP3T\n=HE8d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T02:39:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGMyZGM0MTQ4MjY4ODVhZmFjZmE1MTAzOGI1YWQ1ZTAwNDQ1ZjU4MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0","sha":"ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0"}],"sha":"c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/c2dc414826885afacfa51038b5ad5e00445f5825"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:06:14Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:06:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(11a): RCDO pass-through endpoints + picker integration (#4)\n\n* task(11a): RCDO pass-through controller (list + getById) + DTO\n\nThree subtasks landed together because they share the same minimal\nchange set:\n\n- RcdoController exposes GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes (list,\n  scoped to JWT org_id) and GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n  (single, unscoped because Supporting Outcome ids are globally unique\n  and the picker may need to hydrate an outcome from a previous-org\n  assignment).\n- SupportingOutcomeResponse mirrors the picker contract in\n  libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts -- record + nested Breadcrumb + Level\n  records. Static `from(SupportingOutcomeView)` lifts the integration\n  view into the UI shape so the upstream contract stays isolated from\n  the API contract.\n- The list endpoint derives orgId from the JWT (AuthenticatedPrincipal\n  .organizationId()) instead of accepting it as a query param -- an IC\n  cannot cross-org query, period. The follow-up TASK_LIST entry was\n  amended to reflect this.\n\nSide effect: GlobalExceptionHandler gained a WebClientResponseException\n-> 502 BAD_GATEWAY handler. Reaches here only after Resilience4j\nretries are exhausted on a non-2xx upstream response. Shared across\nall WebClient integrations going forward (notification-svc inherits\nthis for free), not RCDO-specific.\n\n8 controller tests cover: list 200 + envelope shape + breadcrumb\nlevels, list passes JWT org_id (not user-supplied), list 401 without\nJWT, list empty array on empty upstream, getById 200 + envelope,\ngetById 404 on Optional.empty, getById 401 without JWT, getById 502\non upstream 5xx. Full backend suite stays green: 260/260.\n\nThe follow-up entry''s two method-name guesses (listSupportingOutcomes,\ngetById) didn''t match the actual RcdoClient API\n(findActiveSupportingOutcomes, findSupportingOutcome) -- corrected in\nTASK_LIST inline rather than renaming the working RcdoClient.\n\n* task(11a): regenerate OpenAPI spec + TS types for /rcdo endpoints\n\nspringdoc auto-discovered the new @RestController mappings; running\nthe gen-openapi profile (./mvnw verify -Pgen-openapi -DskipUTs=true\n-DskipUnitTests=true) regenerated libs/contracts/openapi.yaml with\nboth paths plus the new schemas:\n\n  /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes\n  /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n  ApiEnvelopeListSupportingOutcomeResponse\n  ApiEnvelopeSupportingOutcomeResponse\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse$Breadcrumb\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse$Level\n\nyarn workspace @wc/contracts generate:ts then regenerated\nlibs/contracts/generated/types.d.ts; verify:ts confirms no drift.\nOpenApiSpecGenerationIT will catch any future code/spec divergence in\nCI just like Spotless catches formatting drift.\n\n* task(11a): RTK Query endpoints for the RCDO pass-through\n\nTwo new endpoints in libs/rtk-api-client/src/api.ts:\n\n  getSupportingOutcomes    GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes\n  getSupportingOutcomeById GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n\nBoth register providesTags for the existing ''RCDO'' tag (which until\nthis commit was declared but unused -- group 10''s task list noted\n\"first endpoint lands in group 11 with <RCDOPicker />\"; landing here\ninstead because the picker now goes through the BE pass-through).\nPer-endpoint `keepUnusedDataFor: 600` overrides the api-level 60s\ndefault to match MEMO #6''s 10-minute RCDO client cache -- the\nhierarchy doesn''t change minute-to-minute upstream and the picker is\ntypically opened once per planning session.\n\nHooks re-exported from the lib''s public surface\n(useGetSupportingOutcomesQuery + useGetSupportingOutcomeByIdQuery) so\nthe UI swap in subtask 6 can pull them in via @wc/rtk-api-client like\nevery other hook.\n\n3 new vitest cases via MSW:\n  - list 200 + breadcrumb shape\n  - single-outcome 200 + id roundtrip\n  - 404 propagation as result.error\n\nCut a fourth test that probed RTK''s internal endpointDefinitions to\nassert keepUnusedDataFor=600 -- tautological / brittle. The config\nsits visibly in api.ts; framework-guarantee territory per CLAUDE.md.\n\nAll checks green: 32/32 vitest in @wc/rtk-api-client, lint, typecheck,\nprettier across the workspace.\n\n* task(11a): RcdoControllerContractIT — full upstream → UI round-trip\n\nFull Spring boot IT with WireMock simulating the upstream RCDO\nservice. Pins both ends of the pass-through:\n\n  Input shape  (mirrors docs/spikes/rcdo-sample-responses.json)\n  -> RcdoClient WebClient deserialization\n  -> SupportingOutcomeView (integration-layer)\n  -> SupportingOutcomeResponse.from(view) mapping\n  -> Jackson serialization\n  Output shape (matches libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts)\n\nCatches failure modes the unit RcdoControllerTest cannot:\n\n- Jackson drift between SupportingOutcomeView and\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse (the unit test mocks the client and never\n  round-trips real JSON through Jackson)\n- Wire-level mapping bugs in RcdoClient (URL paths, query params)\n- Resilience4j wiring on the new endpoints\n\n3 IT cases: list translation + breadcrumb shape, getById translation,\n404 propagation when upstream returns 404.\n\nSuffix `IT` runs under Failsafe in mvn verify alongside the other\nSpring boot integration tests. Test pattern (manual WireMockServer\nlifecycle + DynamicPropertySource) mirrors RcdoClientResilienceIT.\n\nStatic-import collision note: WireMock.get and MockMvcRequestBuilders\n.get share the same simple name. Static-imported only the latter; the\nWireMock variants use `WireMock.get` qualified to avoid the compile\nerror (previous attempt resolved `get` to MappingBuilder, blowing up\nthe MockMvc call site).\n\nmvn verify: 3/3 RcdoControllerContractIT pass; full backend suite\nholds; coverage gate met; spotless + spotbugs clean.\n\n* task(11a): wire RCDOPicker into DraftMode via RTK Query (TODO removal)\n\nRCDOPickerContainer is the new data-fetching wrapper. Calls\nuseGetSupportingOutcomesQuery and feeds the result into the\npresentational <RCDOPicker />. Three render branches:\n\n  loading  -> spinner placeholder (picker not yet mounted)\n  error    -> picker with isStale={true}\n  success  -> picker populated, no banner\n\nThe error branch surfaces RTK Query''s \"last-known data on data field\nduring a failed refetch\" -- the IC can still pick from cache during an\nupstream outage, with the yellow banner explaining the data may be\nstale. First-load failure shows an empty picker + banner; degraded but\nnot broken, per MEMO Known Failure Modes.\n\nDraftMode in WeekEditor now mounts the container. The picker''s onSelect\nis a no-op for now -- commit creation lands in a separate subtask\nlater; the integration here proves data flows end-to-end without\ncommitting the picker to a particular write path.\n\nBoth TODO(group-11-rcdo-integration) markers (rcdo.ts + RCDOPicker.tsx)\nare now resolved and removed; the comments now describe the wired\nend-to-end path instead of pointing at unfinished work.\n\n4 new container vitest cases: loading, success, error, error-with-\ncached-fallback. Total UI suite 85/85 across 13 files. Lint, typecheck,\nprettier all clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ffbf329f4f067dd5fabdb61077957599a79bbde5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/ffbf329f4f067dd5fabdb61077957599a79bbde5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0","verification":{"payload":"tree ffbf329f4f067dd5fabdb61077957599a79bbde5\nparent d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777255574 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777255574 -0600\n\ntask(11a): RCDO pass-through endpoints + picker integration (#4)\n\n* task(11a): RCDO pass-through controller (list + getById) + DTO\n\nThree subtasks landed together because they share the same minimal\nchange set:\n\n- RcdoController exposes GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes (list,\n  scoped to JWT org_id) and GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n  (single, unscoped because Supporting Outcome ids are globally unique\n  and the picker may need to hydrate an outcome from a previous-org\n  assignment).\n- SupportingOutcomeResponse mirrors the picker contract in\n  libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts -- record + nested Breadcrumb + Level\n  records. Static `from(SupportingOutcomeView)` lifts the integration\n  view into the UI shape so the upstream contract stays isolated from\n  the API contract.\n- The list endpoint derives orgId from the JWT (AuthenticatedPrincipal\n  .organizationId()) instead of accepting it as a query param -- an IC\n  cannot cross-org query, period. The follow-up TASK_LIST entry was\n  amended to reflect this.\n\nSide effect: GlobalExceptionHandler gained a WebClientResponseException\n-> 502 BAD_GATEWAY handler. Reaches here only after Resilience4j\nretries are exhausted on a non-2xx upstream response. Shared across\nall WebClient integrations going forward (notification-svc inherits\nthis for free), not RCDO-specific.\n\n8 controller tests cover: list 200 + envelope shape + breadcrumb\nlevels, list passes JWT org_id (not user-supplied), list 401 without\nJWT, list empty array on empty upstream, getById 200 + envelope,\ngetById 404 on Optional.empty, getById 401 without JWT, getById 502\non upstream 5xx. Full backend suite stays green: 260/260.\n\nThe follow-up entry''s two method-name guesses (listSupportingOutcomes,\ngetById) didn''t match the actual RcdoClient API\n(findActiveSupportingOutcomes, findSupportingOutcome) -- corrected in\nTASK_LIST inline rather than renaming the working RcdoClient.\n\n* task(11a): regenerate OpenAPI spec + TS types for /rcdo endpoints\n\nspringdoc auto-discovered the new @RestController mappings; running\nthe gen-openapi profile (./mvnw verify -Pgen-openapi -DskipUTs=true\n-DskipUnitTests=true) regenerated libs/contracts/openapi.yaml with\nboth paths plus the new schemas:\n\n  /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes\n  /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n  ApiEnvelopeListSupportingOutcomeResponse\n  ApiEnvelopeSupportingOutcomeResponse\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse$Breadcrumb\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse$Level\n\nyarn workspace @wc/contracts generate:ts then regenerated\nlibs/contracts/generated/types.d.ts; verify:ts confirms no drift.\nOpenApiSpecGenerationIT will catch any future code/spec divergence in\nCI just like Spotless catches formatting drift.\n\n* task(11a): RTK Query endpoints for the RCDO pass-through\n\nTwo new endpoints in libs/rtk-api-client/src/api.ts:\n\n  getSupportingOutcomes    GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes\n  getSupportingOutcomeById GET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes/{id}\n\nBoth register providesTags for the existing ''RCDO'' tag (which until\nthis commit was declared but unused -- group 10''s task list noted\n\"first endpoint lands in group 11 with <RCDOPicker />\"; landing here\ninstead because the picker now goes through the BE pass-through).\nPer-endpoint `keepUnusedDataFor: 600` overrides the api-level 60s\ndefault to match MEMO #6''s 10-minute RCDO client cache -- the\nhierarchy doesn''t change minute-to-minute upstream and the picker is\ntypically opened once per planning session.\n\nHooks re-exported from the lib''s public surface\n(useGetSupportingOutcomesQuery + useGetSupportingOutcomeByIdQuery) so\nthe UI swap in subtask 6 can pull them in via @wc/rtk-api-client like\nevery other hook.\n\n3 new vitest cases via MSW:\n  - list 200 + breadcrumb shape\n  - single-outcome 200 + id roundtrip\n  - 404 propagation as result.error\n\nCut a fourth test that probed RTK''s internal endpointDefinitions to\nassert keepUnusedDataFor=600 -- tautological / brittle. The config\nsits visibly in api.ts; framework-guarantee territory per CLAUDE.md.\n\nAll checks green: 32/32 vitest in @wc/rtk-api-client, lint, typecheck,\nprettier across the workspace.\n\n* task(11a): RcdoControllerContractIT — full upstream → UI round-trip\n\nFull Spring boot IT with WireMock simulating the upstream RCDO\nservice. Pins both ends of the pass-through:\n\n  Input shape  (mirrors docs/spikes/rcdo-sample-responses.json)\n  -> RcdoClient WebClient deserialization\n  -> SupportingOutcomeView (integration-layer)\n  -> SupportingOutcomeResponse.from(view) mapping\n  -> Jackson serialization\n  Output shape (matches libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts)\n\nCatches failure modes the unit RcdoControllerTest cannot:\n\n- Jackson drift between SupportingOutcomeView and\n  SupportingOutcomeResponse (the unit test mocks the client and never\n  round-trips real JSON through Jackson)\n- Wire-level mapping bugs in RcdoClient (URL paths, query params)\n- Resilience4j wiring on the new endpoints\n\n3 IT cases: list translation + breadcrumb shape, getById translation,\n404 propagation when upstream returns 404.\n\nSuffix `IT` runs under Failsafe in mvn verify alongside the other\nSpring boot integration tests. Test pattern (manual WireMockServer\nlifecycle + DynamicPropertySource) mirrors RcdoClientResilienceIT.\n\nStatic-import collision note: WireMock.get and MockMvcRequestBuilders\n.get share the same simple name. Static-imported only the latter; the\nWireMock variants use `WireMock.get` qualified to avoid the compile\nerror (previous attempt resolved `get` to MappingBuilder, blowing up\nthe MockMvc call site).\n\nmvn verify: 3/3 RcdoControllerContractIT pass; full backend suite\nholds; coverage gate met; spotless + spotbugs clean.\n\n* task(11a): wire RCDOPicker into DraftMode via RTK Query (TODO removal)\n\nRCDOPickerContainer is the new data-fetching wrapper. Calls\nuseGetSupportingOutcomesQuery and feeds the result into the\npresentational <RCDOPicker />. Three render branches:\n\n  loading  -> spinner placeholder (picker not yet mounted)\n  error    -> picker with isStale={true}\n  success  -> picker populated, no banner\n\nThe error branch surfaces RTK Query''s \"last-known data on data field\nduring a failed refetch\" -- the IC can still pick from cache during an\nupstream outage, with the yellow banner explaining the data may be\nstale. First-load failure shows an empty picker + banner; degraded but\nnot broken, per MEMO Known Failure Modes.\n\nDraftMode in WeekEditor now mounts the container. The picker''s onSelect\nis a no-op for now -- commit creation lands in a separate subtask\nlater; the integration here proves data flows end-to-end without\ncommitting the picker to a particular write path.\n\nBoth TODO(group-11-rcdo-integration) markers (rcdo.ts + RCDOPicker.tsx)\nare now resolved and removed; the comments now describe the wired\nend-to-end path instead of pointing at unfinished work.\n\n4 new container vitest cases: loading, success, error, error-with-\ncached-fallback. Total UI suite 85/85 across 13 files. Lint, typecheck,\nprettier all clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7sSWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7eMQAF7IXOMQVQp1eHklzRTd3l85\nvbHn2AioNGAE/BGyifbvOIZ55YkEwk+WMY6phQ+x/xmqGQAwGZ/mzrN/XL4tfTEu\n2aVMc1CjNe/fgiNkhAmAZduT9X87oRmciUuXxRhfkxGS0OyzZ3ACQVAJRA/Ns/dd\nuJ71eT+l9Ubi6ooBMAefVu5FUrlD91hKcwKm7aRXs2wMw7WEenY0WK/CzTTWvra4\nnl2b/9r2m0jsinlbhZJP3HqAxJFbHJFTt7ds4bxkURnI90qIg0HzigenefqH+6JU\nQgQvfmFIGrCyT7tF9Y4/ZCnA3SWSy0IVvkoi9S3zma+Gjx3gL2NsbPIZf3hyn7r2\n/ZLk5/thbIacA68TMlpa1wIWlhgny1Tx6gB1W6cO3CCzeBMPEJfwuQ6LjRH1pije\nHyfP51eU6Oe+HKlP4N2d2bA07qSu21GoUYyAnYLYMRB/n0g4Mho5hwj/52N7k8Rz\nCX3BlItq56DJApY2ZIfhD5NqnY2dHK+AhPnbM/hLwTjqEH9vaxHzB4QUs6k0TcZJ\nKUKwEJXaD25hAMlHPCOJDQP4emRW9sfsmj/gOrsX0UxAvmy1Ggk0q1XagZaHoJZI\ny8M1Rf8N9HBAogu8JvsxQTn0n8ae2gHfRsjNkr4cpbTHzXqcrmmNwGRM3r99xEaE\nrAw3eirPVqrM5xKx/UFS\n=1cOh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T02:06:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0","node_id":"C_kwDOSMr5q9oAKGNhMGM2MzE4ZDIzNDIzMTU5ZGI5YjFhMDUwMjkxNjk1NjYxNDM0YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commit/d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2","sha":"d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2"}],"sha":"ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/ca0c6318d23423159db9b1a050291695661434c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100040464?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seeincodes","id":100040464,"login":"seeincodes","node_id":"U_kgDOBfZ_EA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seeincodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/commits/d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T00:20:32Z","email":"100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Xian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T00:20:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"task(11): Frontend IC surfaces (in progress) (#3)\n\n* task(11): routes /weekly-commit/current + /weekly-commit/history\n\nReact Router v6 nested route (`<Route path=\"weekly-commit\">`) with an\n`index` element that <Navigate replace> redirects to `current`. Page\nshells live in src/routes/ as thin containers; the state-aware\n<WeekEditor /> lands inside CurrentWeekPage in subtask 2.\n\nThe version-stamp markup that lived in the WeeklyCommitModule placeholder\nmoved into CurrentWeekPage so the Playwright smoke (and any operator\nsanity-check on a deployed bundle) keeps a stable target.\n\nTests:\n- 3 new Vitest cases on routing (current, history, redirect)\n- Playwright smoke updated to the new path shape (3 scenarios incl.\n  history mount)\n- eslint.config.js gained a `coverage/` ignore -- vitest v8''s lcov-report\n  was tripping recommendedTypeChecked rules because lcov files are\n  outside any tsconfig project.\n\nAll checks pass locally: 14/14 vitest, typecheck, prettier --check,\neslint --max-warnings=0.\n\n* task(11): <WeekEditor /> state-aware container\n\nOwns the GET /plans/me/current fetch and routes to one of five modes per\nUSER_FLOW.md flows 1-3 / MEMO #5:\n\n  - BlankState           404 / no plan exists for current week\n  - DraftMode            state=DRAFT, commit CRUD lands in subtasks 3-4\n  - LockedReadOnly       LOCKED + now < weekStart + 4d\n  - ReconcileMode        LOCKED + now >= weekStart + 4d\n  - ReconciledSummary    RECONCILED (and ARCHIVED falls through here for\n                         the off-path /current-page rendering)\n\nMode children are stubs with data-testid markers; subtasks 3-9 plug in\nRCDOPicker, ChessTier, ReconcileTable, ReflectionField, CarryForwardRow,\nCarryStreakBadge, StateBadge in place. Loading + non-404 error paths\neach get a generic placeholder so the full state matrix is observable\nfrom tests today.\n\nThe reconcile-eligibility check is inline UTC math\n`weekStart + 4 * 24h` with a TODO(subtask-10) marker; the IANA-aware\nhelper from the TZ-handling subtask replaces it without changing the\ncall site (now: Date is already injected as a prop). Pinning the clock\nvia prop also makes the test matrix deterministic without touching\nglobal Date.\n\n7 new vitest cases cover loading, blank, DRAFT, LOCKED-pre-day-4,\nLOCKED-reconcile, RECONCILED, and non-404 error. The mock targets\nuseGetCurrentForMeQuery only; the real api slice + middleware are wired\ninto the test store so middleware drift would surface.\n\nCurrentWeekPage now renders <WeekEditor now={new Date()} /> inside the\nexisting card heading + version stamp; the Playwright smoke remains on\ndata-testid=\"current-week-page\".\n\nAll checks green: 21/21 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): fix Playwright smoke -- HistoryPage needs visible content\n\nEmpty <div data-testid=\"history-page\" /> failed Playwright''s\n`toBeVisible()` because the assertion requires non-zero dimensions and\nan empty div has zero. Added the same minimal Card+heading scaffolding\nCurrentWeekPage uses so the route is observable in the smoke layer\nwithout committing to a real history-list design (that ships later in\ngroup 11).\n\nVerified locally: yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:playwright\n-> 3/3 pass; vitest 21/21; lint + prettier clean.\n\nFix-forward for the failing frontend-pr run on PR #3.\n\n* task(11): <RCDOPicker /> typeahead with 4-level breadcrumb\n\nPresentational typeahead per ADR-0001''s stubbed contract. Local\ncase-insensitive substring filter against an `outcomes` prop -- the data\nhook stays in the parent so the picker is trivially unit-testable. ARIA\ncombobox + listbox + option semantics give keyboard parity (Enter/Space\nselects). Breadcrumb rendered inline as\n\"Rally Cry > Defining Objective > Core Outcome > Supporting Outcome\"\nmatching the convention already in RollupResponse.java + USER_FLOW.md.\n\n`isStale` prop renders the cached-data banner described in MEMO Known\nFailure Modes -- the picker remains usable when the upstream RCDO is\nout, with a yellow warning that what they see may be stale.\n\nRCDO types live in libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts and are re-exported\nfrom the lib''s public surface. The future RTK Query endpoint that\nbacks the real wire-up slots in alongside without a type churn -- the\nshape on disk today is the shape the BE pass-through will conform to.\n\n7 vitest cases cover input + filter + breadcrumb + selection + empty +\nbanner show/hide. Selection assertions go through role=option instead\nof by-text because the supporting-outcome label appears twice per row\n(title + breadcrumb leaf).\n\nINTEGRATION DEFERRED: a backend pass-through endpoint\nGET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes (wrapping the existing RcdoClient)\nis the missing piece -- documented as new TASK_LIST group \"11a.\" with\nits own subtask checklist. The picker''s parent will swap the stub source\nfor the RTK hook once 11a lands; TODO(group-11-rcdo-integration)\nmarkers in this commit point at that handoff.\n\nAll checks green: 28/28 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ChessTier /> vertical spine container\n\nThree role=\"group\" sections in ROCK > PEBBLE > SAND order with\ndescending visual weight (border thickness + padding) so the chess\nmetaphor reads at a glance. Within a tier commits sort by displayOrder\nascending so future drag-reorder maps naturally and the Top Rock falls\nout as commits[0] in the ROCK bucket.\n\nTop Rock is computed here once (lowest displayOrder ROCK; undefined if\nno ROCK commits exist) and propagated to the parent via the\nrenderCommit(commit, isTopRock) callback. The container is purely\npresentational -- it doesn''t know what a commit row looks like in DRAFT\nvs RECONCILE mode -- so the parent owns the row UI and this component\nowns the structural rules. Top Rock is ROCK-only per MEMO #7.\n\n\"No Top Rock\" surfaces as a chess-tier-no-top-rock status banner when\nthe ROCK tier is empty -- managers care about this specifically per\nPRD [MVP8] (it appears in the rollup as a flag). Per-tier empty\nplaceholders fill PEBBLE/SAND when those tiers are empty so the spine\nalways shows the full structure.\n\n8 vitest cases cover: section order, commit-to-tier grouping,\ndisplayOrder ordering, Top Rock identification, Top Rock ROCK-only\nconstraint, per-tier empty placeholders, no-Top-Rock banner show/hide.\n\nAll checks green: 36/36 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ReconcileTable /> keyboard-first reconciliation\n\nOne row per commit; per row a radiogroup of DONE/PARTIAL/MISSED + a\ntextarea for actualNote. These are the only fields the IC can edit in\nreconcile mode per PRD [MVP5]; the table enforces that by simply not\nexposing inputs for anything else (commit title is read-only text).\n\nKeyboard-first: ArrowUp/ArrowDown on a status radio jumps between rows\npreserving the column. Reviewing \"did I do my Rocks?\" is one keystroke\nper row instead of three Tabs each. Within a row, native radiogroup\narrow nav handles intra-row column movement.\n\nradioRefs are a per-instance useRef<Record<key, HTMLInputElement|null>>\nkeyed by `${commitId}:${status}`. Simpler than a context provider for\none self-contained component, and the lookup is O(1).\n\nPer-row onUpdate(commitId, patch) callback gives the parent a clean\npatch shape to translate into PATCH /commits/{id} -- the table doesn''t\nknow about the API or batching, just emits each delta. Parent decides\non debounce / optimistic update.\n\n7 vitest cases: row count + headers, three radios per row, currently\nchecked status reflection, status-change patch, note-change patch,\nArrowUp/ArrowDown row nav, empty placeholder.\n\nAll checks green: 43/43 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ReflectionField /> 500-char cap + counter\n\nControlled textarea with maxLength={500} (browser-enforced per [MVP5])\nand a live \"<used>/500\" counter beneath. Counter flips to a\ndata-warning=\"true\" orange style at >= 480 chars to surface the wall\nbefore the user hits it.\n\nThe 480 threshold matches Phase 2''s \"480+ char warning color\" polish\nsubtask -- so this commit lands the styling hook ready. Polish work\nlater (animations, tooltips) can layer on the existing data-warning\nattribute without retesting the threshold logic.\n\n6 vitest cases: textarea + label render, onChange propagation, counter\ntext format, maxLength attribute, warning style at 480, no warning at\n479.\n\nAll checks green: 49/49 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <CarryForwardRow /> + <CarryAllButton />\n\nOne file, two sibling exports. Per-row affordance and bulk action share\nthe same `isCarryEligible` predicate so the rule lives in exactly one\nplace: actualStatus in {MISSED, PARTIAL} AND carriedForwardToId == null.\n\nCarryForwardRow returns null for ineligible rows (DONE / PENDING) and\nswaps to a \"Already carried to next week\" indicator when the commit was\nalready carried -- this guarantees a row can''t double-carry from the\nUI even if the parent''s optimistic-update sequencing is wonky.\n\nCarryAllButton computes the eligible-ids list once on render. Disabled\nwhen empty so the IC sees the button greyed out (rather than missing)\nwhen they reconciled everything DONE -- preserves the affordance map.\nThe callback hands the parent the explicit id list, not a \"do all\"\nsignal, so the parent translates into N independent\nPOST /commits/{id}/carry-forward calls without re-deriving the set.\n\n9 vitest cases cover per-status visibility (MISSED/PARTIAL/DONE/PENDING),\nonCarry callback shape, already-carried indicator, the bulk filter, and\nthe empty-disabled state.\n\nAll checks green: 58/58 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): <CarryStreakBadge /> streak indicator\n\nPure render component reading `WeeklyCommitResponse.derived.carryStreak`\n(server-derived, walk of carriedForwardFromId, capped at 52 per\n[MVP7]). Three render paths:\n\n  streak < 2  -> null (first-time commits don''t get a decoration)\n  streak == 2 -> neutral grey \"2x\" pill\n  streak >= 3 -> red \"stuck\" pill\n\n`data-stuck=\"true|false\"` is the test handle and the Phase-2 polish\nhook -- the ≥2→≥3 transition animation in the polish task layers on\nthis attribute without changing the threshold logic.\n\naria-label \"Carried forward N weeks in a row\" so screen readers get\nthe meaning, not just the \"Nx\" abbreviation.\n\n6 vitest cases verify: streak < 2 collapses to empty DOM, 2x neutral,\n3x stuck, 5x still-stuck, and the aria-label string. The TDD red-green\ncycle was verified with a temporary impl-aside-and-restore so I\nactually saw the red, not just claimed it.\n\nAll checks green: 64/64 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): <StateBadge /> + next-action hint\n\nPure render. (state, isReconcileEligible) -> (badge color, one-line\nhint) where the hints come straight from USER_FLOW.md flows 1-3:\n\n  DRAFT       -> \"Lock the week when you''re done planning.\"\n  LOCKED <d4  -> \"Reconciliation opens Friday.\"\n  LOCKED >=d4 -> \"Reconcile each commit and submit reconciliation.\"\n  RECONCILED  -> \"Carry forward any missed work to next week.\"\n  ARCHIVED    -> no hint (terminal state, nothing to do)\n\nisReconcileEligible is passed in rather than recomputed here -- both\nthe WeekEditor and this badge would otherwise duplicate the\n\"weekStart + 4 days\" math, which subtask 10''s TZ helper is going to\nunify. Keeping the badge purely presentational means subtask 10\nreplaces the predicate in exactly one place (the WeekEditor) and the\nprop just flows through.\n\ndata-state attribute hooks per-state styling and gives tests a stable\nselector that doesn''t depend on the visible label string.\n\n6 vitest cases cover all 5 hint branches + data-state across all 4\nstates.\n\nAll checks green: 70/70 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): IANA-aware timezone helpers + WeekEditor swap\n\napps/weekly-commit-ui/src/lib/timezone.ts is the new home for any UI\ndate math that touches employee-local time:\n\n  getEmployeeTimezone(override?)\n     Resolves IANA TZ. Override wins; v1 fallback is the browser''s\n     `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone`. JWT `timezone`\n     claim wiring lands with the auth integration task (TODO inline).\n\n  isReconcileEligible(weekStart, now, tz)\n     IANA-aware version of the inline UTC math the WeekEditor carried\n     with a TODO(subtask-10) flag. weekStart is YYYY-MM-DD; the\n     threshold is \"weekStart + 4 days, 00:00 local\" converted to UTC.\n\n  formatInstant(instant, opts, tz)\n     Pass-through to Intl.DateTimeFormat for display.\n\nThe midnight-in-tz-as-UTC bridge uses formatToParts to read the IANA\noffset at the candidate instant (the standard recipe). One\nformatToParts call resolves DST correctly because IANA offsets only\nchange at boundary moments and a 1-day-wide guess never straddles one.\n\nWeekEditor: dropped the inline UTC predicate and now calls\nisReconcileEligible with the resolved TZ. New `tz?: string` prop lets\ntests pin the TZ deterministically; default is the browser''s resolved\nTZ. Updated the LOCKED-eligible test to pass tz=\"UTC\" so the\n2026-05-01T00:00Z boundary still maps cleanly regardless of where the\ntest runner clock thinks it is.\n\n11 timezone vitest cases: thresholds before/at/after in\nAmerica/New_York + UTC, DST spring-forward (Mar 8 2026) + fall-back\n(Nov 1 2026) boundary weeks, formatInstant string + Date inputs,\ngetEmployeeTimezone override + browser fallback.\n\nAll checks green: 81/81 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"18c811bbf695df28d4b589284b65139d5017fc49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/trees/18c811bbf695df28d4b589284b65139d5017fc49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seeincodes/WeeklyCommit/git/commits/d9863879d093565fabb17292c3f509904a8720d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 18c811bbf695df28d4b589284b65139d5017fc49\nparent 90180a72b5289d1d39f6170451f8920101b5d7be\nauthor Xian <100040464+seeincodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1777249232 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777249232 -0600\n\ntask(11): Frontend IC surfaces (in progress) (#3)\n\n* task(11): routes /weekly-commit/current + /weekly-commit/history\n\nReact Router v6 nested route (`<Route path=\"weekly-commit\">`) with an\n`index` element that <Navigate replace> redirects to `current`. Page\nshells live in src/routes/ as thin containers; the state-aware\n<WeekEditor /> lands inside CurrentWeekPage in subtask 2.\n\nThe version-stamp markup that lived in the WeeklyCommitModule placeholder\nmoved into CurrentWeekPage so the Playwright smoke (and any operator\nsanity-check on a deployed bundle) keeps a stable target.\n\nTests:\n- 3 new Vitest cases on routing (current, history, redirect)\n- Playwright smoke updated to the new path shape (3 scenarios incl.\n  history mount)\n- eslint.config.js gained a `coverage/` ignore -- vitest v8''s lcov-report\n  was tripping recommendedTypeChecked rules because lcov files are\n  outside any tsconfig project.\n\nAll checks pass locally: 14/14 vitest, typecheck, prettier --check,\neslint --max-warnings=0.\n\n* task(11): <WeekEditor /> state-aware container\n\nOwns the GET /plans/me/current fetch and routes to one of five modes per\nUSER_FLOW.md flows 1-3 / MEMO #5:\n\n  - BlankState           404 / no plan exists for current week\n  - DraftMode            state=DRAFT, commit CRUD lands in subtasks 3-4\n  - LockedReadOnly       LOCKED + now < weekStart + 4d\n  - ReconcileMode        LOCKED + now >= weekStart + 4d\n  - ReconciledSummary    RECONCILED (and ARCHIVED falls through here for\n                         the off-path /current-page rendering)\n\nMode children are stubs with data-testid markers; subtasks 3-9 plug in\nRCDOPicker, ChessTier, ReconcileTable, ReflectionField, CarryForwardRow,\nCarryStreakBadge, StateBadge in place. Loading + non-404 error paths\neach get a generic placeholder so the full state matrix is observable\nfrom tests today.\n\nThe reconcile-eligibility check is inline UTC math\n`weekStart + 4 * 24h` with a TODO(subtask-10) marker; the IANA-aware\nhelper from the TZ-handling subtask replaces it without changing the\ncall site (now: Date is already injected as a prop). Pinning the clock\nvia prop also makes the test matrix deterministic without touching\nglobal Date.\n\n7 new vitest cases cover loading, blank, DRAFT, LOCKED-pre-day-4,\nLOCKED-reconcile, RECONCILED, and non-404 error. The mock targets\nuseGetCurrentForMeQuery only; the real api slice + middleware are wired\ninto the test store so middleware drift would surface.\n\nCurrentWeekPage now renders <WeekEditor now={new Date()} /> inside the\nexisting card heading + version stamp; the Playwright smoke remains on\ndata-testid=\"current-week-page\".\n\nAll checks green: 21/21 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): fix Playwright smoke -- HistoryPage needs visible content\n\nEmpty <div data-testid=\"history-page\" /> failed Playwright''s\n`toBeVisible()` because the assertion requires non-zero dimensions and\nan empty div has zero. Added the same minimal Card+heading scaffolding\nCurrentWeekPage uses so the route is observable in the smoke layer\nwithout committing to a real history-list design (that ships later in\ngroup 11).\n\nVerified locally: yarn workspace @wc/weekly-commit-ui run test:playwright\n-> 3/3 pass; vitest 21/21; lint + prettier clean.\n\nFix-forward for the failing frontend-pr run on PR #3.\n\n* task(11): <RCDOPicker /> typeahead with 4-level breadcrumb\n\nPresentational typeahead per ADR-0001''s stubbed contract. Local\ncase-insensitive substring filter against an `outcomes` prop -- the data\nhook stays in the parent so the picker is trivially unit-testable. ARIA\ncombobox + listbox + option semantics give keyboard parity (Enter/Space\nselects). Breadcrumb rendered inline as\n\"Rally Cry > Defining Objective > Core Outcome > Supporting Outcome\"\nmatching the convention already in RollupResponse.java + USER_FLOW.md.\n\n`isStale` prop renders the cached-data banner described in MEMO Known\nFailure Modes -- the picker remains usable when the upstream RCDO is\nout, with a yellow warning that what they see may be stale.\n\nRCDO types live in libs/rtk-api-client/src/rcdo.ts and are re-exported\nfrom the lib''s public surface. The future RTK Query endpoint that\nbacks the real wire-up slots in alongside without a type churn -- the\nshape on disk today is the shape the BE pass-through will conform to.\n\n7 vitest cases cover input + filter + breadcrumb + selection + empty +\nbanner show/hide. Selection assertions go through role=option instead\nof by-text because the supporting-outcome label appears twice per row\n(title + breadcrumb leaf).\n\nINTEGRATION DEFERRED: a backend pass-through endpoint\nGET /api/v1/rcdo/supporting-outcomes (wrapping the existing RcdoClient)\nis the missing piece -- documented as new TASK_LIST group \"11a.\" with\nits own subtask checklist. The picker''s parent will swap the stub source\nfor the RTK hook once 11a lands; TODO(group-11-rcdo-integration)\nmarkers in this commit point at that handoff.\n\nAll checks green: 28/28 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ChessTier /> vertical spine container\n\nThree role=\"group\" sections in ROCK > PEBBLE > SAND order with\ndescending visual weight (border thickness + padding) so the chess\nmetaphor reads at a glance. Within a tier commits sort by displayOrder\nascending so future drag-reorder maps naturally and the Top Rock falls\nout as commits[0] in the ROCK bucket.\n\nTop Rock is computed here once (lowest displayOrder ROCK; undefined if\nno ROCK commits exist) and propagated to the parent via the\nrenderCommit(commit, isTopRock) callback. The container is purely\npresentational -- it doesn''t know what a commit row looks like in DRAFT\nvs RECONCILE mode -- so the parent owns the row UI and this component\nowns the structural rules. Top Rock is ROCK-only per MEMO #7.\n\n\"No Top Rock\" surfaces as a chess-tier-no-top-rock status banner when\nthe ROCK tier is empty -- managers care about this specifically per\nPRD [MVP8] (it appears in the rollup as a flag). Per-tier empty\nplaceholders fill PEBBLE/SAND when those tiers are empty so the spine\nalways shows the full structure.\n\n8 vitest cases cover: section order, commit-to-tier grouping,\ndisplayOrder ordering, Top Rock identification, Top Rock ROCK-only\nconstraint, per-tier empty placeholders, no-Top-Rock banner show/hide.\n\nAll checks green: 36/36 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ReconcileTable /> keyboard-first reconciliation\n\nOne row per commit; per row a radiogroup of DONE/PARTIAL/MISSED + a\ntextarea for actualNote. These are the only fields the IC can edit in\nreconcile mode per PRD [MVP5]; the table enforces that by simply not\nexposing inputs for anything else (commit title is read-only text).\n\nKeyboard-first: ArrowUp/ArrowDown on a status radio jumps between rows\npreserving the column. Reviewing \"did I do my Rocks?\" is one keystroke\nper row instead of three Tabs each. Within a row, native radiogroup\narrow nav handles intra-row column movement.\n\nradioRefs are a per-instance useRef<Record<key, HTMLInputElement|null>>\nkeyed by `${commitId}:${status}`. Simpler than a context provider for\none self-contained component, and the lookup is O(1).\n\nPer-row onUpdate(commitId, patch) callback gives the parent a clean\npatch shape to translate into PATCH /commits/{id} -- the table doesn''t\nknow about the API or batching, just emits each delta. Parent decides\non debounce / optimistic update.\n\n7 vitest cases: row count + headers, three radios per row, currently\nchecked status reflection, status-change patch, note-change patch,\nArrowUp/ArrowDown row nav, empty placeholder.\n\nAll checks green: 43/43 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <ReflectionField /> 500-char cap + counter\n\nControlled textarea with maxLength={500} (browser-enforced per [MVP5])\nand a live \"<used>/500\" counter beneath. Counter flips to a\ndata-warning=\"true\" orange style at >= 480 chars to surface the wall\nbefore the user hits it.\n\nThe 480 threshold matches Phase 2''s \"480+ char warning color\" polish\nsubtask -- so this commit lands the styling hook ready. Polish work\nlater (animations, tooltips) can layer on the existing data-warning\nattribute without retesting the threshold logic.\n\n6 vitest cases: textarea + label render, onChange propagation, counter\ntext format, maxLength attribute, warning style at 480, no warning at\n479.\n\nAll checks green: 49/49 vitest, lint --max-warnings=0, typecheck,\nprettier --check.\n\n* task(11): <CarryForwardRow /> + <CarryAllButton />\n\nOne file, two sibling exports. Per-row affordance and bulk action share\nthe same `isCarryEligible` predicate so the rule lives in exactly one\nplace: actualStatus in {MISSED, PARTIAL} AND carriedForwardToId == null.\n\nCarryForwardRow returns null for ineligible rows (DONE / PENDING) and\nswaps to a \"Already carried to next week\" indicator when the commit was\nalready carried -- this guarantees a row can''t double-carry from the\nUI even if the parent''s optimistic-update sequencing is wonky.\n\nCarryAllButton computes the eligible-ids list once on render. Disabled\nwhen empty so the IC sees the button greyed out (rather than missing)\nwhen they reconciled everything DONE -- preserves the affordance map.\nThe callback hands the parent the explicit id list, not a \"do all\"\nsignal, so the parent translates into N independent\nPOST /commits/{id}/carry-forward calls without re-deriving the set.\n\n9 vitest cases cover per-status visibility (MISSED/PARTIAL/DONE/PENDING),\nonCarry callback shape, already-carried indicator, the bulk filter, and\nthe empty-disabled state.\n\nAll checks green: 58/58 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): <CarryStreakBadge /> streak indicator\n\nPure render component reading `WeeklyCommitResponse.derived.carryStreak`\n(server-derived, walk of carriedForwardFromId, capped at 52 per\n[MVP7]). Three render paths:\n\n  streak < 2  -> null (first-time commits don''t get a decoration)\n  streak == 2 -> neutral grey \"2x\" pill\n  streak >= 3 -> red \"stuck\" pill\n\n`data-stuck=\"true|false\"` is the test handle and the Phase-2 polish\nhook -- the ≥2→≥3 transition animation in the polish task layers on\nthis attribute without changing the threshold logic.\n\naria-label \"Carried forward N weeks in a row\" so screen readers get\nthe meaning, not just the \"Nx\" abbreviation.\n\n6 vitest cases verify: streak < 2 collapses to empty DOM, 2x neutral,\n3x stuck, 5x still-stuck, and the aria-label string. The TDD red-green\ncycle was verified with a temporary impl-aside-and-restore so I\nactually saw the red, not just claimed it.\n\nAll checks green: 64/64 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): <StateBadge /> + next-action hint\n\nPure render. (state, isReconcileEligible) -> (badge color, one-line\nhint) where the hints come straight from USER_FLOW.md flows 1-3:\n\n  DRAFT       -> \"Lock the week when you''re done planning.\"\n  LOCKED <d4  -> \"Reconciliation opens Friday.\"\n  LOCKED >=d4 -> \"Reconcile each commit and submit reconciliation.\"\n  RECONCILED  -> \"Carry forward any missed work to next week.\"\n  ARCHIVED    -> no hint (terminal state, nothing to do)\n\nisReconcileEligible is passed in rather than recomputed here -- both\nthe WeekEditor and this badge would otherwise duplicate the\n\"weekStart + 4 days\" math, which subtask 10''s TZ helper is going to\nunify. Keeping the badge purely presentational means subtask 10\nreplaces the predicate in exactly one place (the WeekEditor) and the\nprop just flows through.\n\ndata-state attribute hooks per-state styling and gives tests a stable\nselector that doesn''t depend on the visible label string.\n\n6 vitest cases cover all 5 hint branches + data-state across all 4\nstates.\n\nAll checks green: 70/70 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n* task(11): IANA-aware timezone helpers + WeekEditor swap\n\napps/weekly-commit-ui/src/lib/timezone.ts is the new home for any UI\ndate math that touches employee-local time:\n\n  getEmployeeTimezone(override?)\n     Resolves IANA TZ. Override wins; v1 fallback is the browser''s\n     `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone`. JWT `timezone`\n     claim wiring lands with the auth integration task (TODO inline).\n\n  isReconcileEligible(weekStart, now, tz)\n     IANA-aware version of the inline UTC math the WeekEditor carried\n     with a TODO(subtask-10) flag. weekStart is YYYY-MM-DD; the\n     threshold is \"weekStart + 4 days, 00:00 local\" converted to UTC.\n\n  formatInstant(instant, opts, tz)\n     Pass-through to Intl.DateTimeFormat for display.\n\nThe midnight-in-tz-as-UTC bridge uses formatToParts to read the IANA\noffset at the candidate instant (the standard recipe). One\nformatToParts call resolves DST correctly because IANA offsets only\nchange at boundary moments and a 1-day-wide guess never straddles one.\n\nWeekEditor: dropped the inline UTC predicate and now calls\nisReconcileEligible with the resolved TZ. New `tz?: string` prop lets\ntests pin the TZ deterministically; default is the browser''s resolved\nTZ. Updated the LOCKED-eligible test to pass tz=\"UTC\" so the\n2026-05-01T00:00Z boundary still maps cleanly regardless of where the\ntest runner clock thinks it is.\n\n11 timezone vitest cases: thresholds before/at/after in\nAmerica/New_York + UTC, DST spring-forward (Mar 8 2026) + fall-back\n(Nov 1 2026) boundary weeks, formatInstant string + Date inputs,\ngetEmployeeTimezone override + browser fallback.\n\nAll checks green: 81/81 vitest, lint, typecheck, prettier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Xian Zheng <seeinplay@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7qvQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlaoQAF0rm1u8KIXhsjaF+TpJbroq\nJNGfeTjXQNxQo0PKyzknF3djNoq6bX/CM6Tew6je/NQpWXTMVK/MWW3DSV+Ln0R1\nCGGwm6vmXA7rnDNFKcXupUSyKAWa/1S2gMgqNgfVw4hcE/nfjjRZpo7Rq9vcutpc\nsf0TgpkDJmKlx7ooSHQD/PVyx8+VMqcJdmLu+Ocq5CGiojxLf7SXoYEtWHIwZ0s/\nZghvWgPvwYxFGMnjKD4q6Rb/HgEDUDxxZ0XojeoLIu7vlCiu3uil2Ox1z1yDvUBj\nir0zn4zIKSY+uU87U8eUFrfv8i18T5cDW39kNy/TdFF9SYktUVOCh0Ne0