ub.com/users/jthickma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jthickma/dynasty-hq/commits/0f45ea0f766a277af97f29147000e2a596bff082/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T07:12:01Z","email":"jthickma@ksu.edu","name":"jthickma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T07:12:01Z","email":"jthickma@ksu.edu","name":"jthickma"},"message":"Add OpenAI vision OCR with web-managed API key + model picker\n\nScreenshot OCR now flows through user-configurable credentials: a Setting\nKV table holds the OpenAI API key and chosen vision model, written via a\nnew /settings page. The Import tab gains a \"Screenshots (OCR)\" mode with\nmulti-file upload, dry-run preview, and target toggle for roster vs\nseason-stats. Model list is fetched live from /v1/models with a\nvision-capability filter. Env vars still take precedence for back-compat.\n\nSee docs/vision-ocr.md for the full architecture, API reference, and\nextension recipe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50f1528ab18f245c93f0afcd0ea1d843b99a31e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jthickma/dynasty-hq/git/trees/50f1528ab18f245c93f0afcd0ea1d843b99a31e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jthickma/dynasty-hq/git/commits/0f45ea0f766a277af97f29147000e2a596bff082","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181776265?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthickma/foll